                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      	India                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ú ú                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ía!5Å%#Ç% °95157243802026-10-23T03:04:48ZTiger Shroff firing: Four accused remanded to police custody till October 26mid-daymid-day.comhttps://www.mid-day.com/mumbai/mumbai-news/article/tiger-shroff-firing-court-extends-police-custody-of-four-accused-till-october-26-23656482engIndiaøÔøøøøø¿The four accused arrested for allegedly supplying weapons used in the firing at actor Tiger Shroffrsquos car were remanded to police custody till October 26 by an Esplanade magistratersquos court on ThursdayFour arrestedThey were arrested on October 20 and brought to Mumbai from Delhigtgt Kunal Singh 21 Rohana village Haryanarsquos Sonipat districtgtgt Sumit Suralia 19 Kharkhoda Sonipatgtgt Radha Verma 23 Sitapur Uttar Pradeshgtgt Babita Rao 23 Azamgarh Uttar PradeshPolice claimsThe prosecution sought police custody till October 31 saying the weapon used in the crime is yet to be recovered and the four were responsible for providing the firearms and ammunition Police told the court the accused were actively involved in the conspiracy along with those arrested earlier They claimed two of the accused travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons while the two women carried the firearms to Mumbai by train and handed them over to the shootersDefence objectionAdvocate Sachin Patil opposed remand arguing that police had not established pistolrsquos make He said no statement of a coaccused had been recorded before the arrests and police had sufficient time to questionArguing that arrest on mere suspicion was not a valid ground for custody Patil questioned what material linked the women to the case He said call detail records and electronic evidence would suffice and sought judicial custody He also pointed out that the custody of three other accused remanded on Wednesday had only just begunCourt roomThe magistrate granted police custody till October 26 after hearing both sides The accused made no complaints of illtreatment against the police though Kunal Singh appeared with a bandage on his headJuhu attackAt least two men fired at Shroffrsquos car in Juhu on the evening of October 18 before fleeing on a motorcycle The actor escaped relatively unhurt while his driver and a bystander were injured Ten people have been arrested so far On Wednesday the court remanded three of them mdash Rehan alias Sukka Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan and Phool Singh mdash to police custody till October 31    Ò  Ò                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       ê!5Å;1/Åg õ]95157185612026-10-23T02:57:44ZClass XI student shot dead in Chandigarh's Sector 22; auto driver injured, one detainedThe Indian Expressindianexpress.comhttps://indianexpress.com/article/cities/chandigarh/class-xi-student-shot-dead-chandigarh-sector-22-10933103/engIndiaø‡∞∞∞∞∞∞Thank you for your feedback.Your feedback has been reported succesfully.An alleged old enmity turned fatal for a Class XI student on Thursday evening when motorcycle-borne assailants opened fire at him and his friend while they were returning home in an auto, in Sector 22, Chandigarh.The student, Naitik, a Class XI student of SD School, was declared brought dead at a hospital.The incident took place near Sanatan Dharam Mandir in Sector 22. The auto driver was also injured in the firing, while another youth accompanying Naitik escaped unhurt.The UT Police has detained a suspect in connection with this case and is probing the circumstances leading to the shooting.According to the preliminary information, the suspect allegedly knew the victim since their school days, and investigators are examining whether the attack stemmed from an old personal dispute.A case under Section 103, which deals with murder, under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), has been registered.Speaking to The Indian Express, SHO Sudesh Kumar said initial probe suggested that the incident was linked to a fight the victim had with a group of youths in Sector 44 earlier in the day."There had been a fight in Sector 44 earlier in the day between Naitik, his friend and a group of youths. The dispute appears to be over an old issue, which we are verifying. The youths allegedly followed them on a motorcycle and opened fire in Sector 22. Naitik was taken to hospital, where he was declared brought dead. The auto-rickshaw driver was also injured, while the other youth accompanying him escaped unhurt," the SHO said.Police have initiated an investigation into the incident and are examining CCTV footage from the area.The victim's father works in the timber market.   Ö Ö                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           îx!5Å='1Ç% §}95157167922026-10-23T02:54:25ZMarriage prospects and job loss count in motor accident compensation, says Supreme CourtThe Telegraphtelegraphindia.comhttps://www.telegraphindia.com/india/supreme-court-raises-motor-accident-compensation-considers-jobs-and-marriage-prospects-prnt/cid/2185780engIndiaøÆ Two Kerala accident victims receive Rs 77.83 lakh and Rs 69.60 lakh after the court considers permanent disability, lifelong care costs and loss of earning capacityThe Supreme Court has held that the impact of a disability caused by a motor accident, including marriage prospects, earning capacity and the cost of keeping a lifelong attendant adjusted to inflation, must be considered while awarding compensation to victims.The apex court steeply enhanced the compensation amounts to be handed over to pillion rider Sunil Kumar and bike rider K.S. Sreejith to ‚Çπ77.83 lakh and ‚Çπ69.60 lakh, respectively. They had suffered grievous injuries when their bike was hit by another two-wheeler on the Thrissur-Kodara road in Keralam. These amounts are over ‚Çπ41 lakh more than the compensation fixed by the high court.The high court itself had enhanced the compensation amounts of ‚Çπ19.91 lakh and ‚Çπ16.03 lakh awarded to Sunil and Sreejith by the Motor Accidents Claims Tribunal.A Supreme Court bench of Justice S.V.N. Bhatti and Justice N.V. Anjaria said Sunil had suffered severe head injuries, an open diffuse axonal injury, a midbrain contusion with Weber's syndrome and a left knee penetrating injury."The functional effect of those injuries has to be estimated. They have grave consequences on the earning capacity of the appellant. The appellant would require an attendant and a bystander to look after him throughout his life. The appellant would be suffering from psychiatric disability of higher grade," the top court said."Therefore, even though the Medical Board certified the medical disability to be 75.5%, the functional effect can be said to be debilitating for the appellant to the extent of 100%," Justice Anjaria, who authored the judgment, added."...The appellant would not be able to do his own work, much less engage in earning activity for himself and his family, leading to total loss of working capacity".In the case of Sreejith, the bench said the medical board had certified a 62 per cent disability."...The appellant became permanently disabled and effectively lost his earning capacity.... The appellant... was an energetic, able-bodied youngster at the time of the incident. Therefore, the loss towards marriage prospects would have to be recognised while determining the amount of compensation," the court said.   õ õ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 íb!5Å+1Ç °95157071092026-10-23T02:40:51Z16 arrested in Lucknow gambling den raid, ‚Çπ1.27 lakh cash seizedHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/lucknow-news/16-arrested-in-lucknow-gambling-den-raid-1-27-lakh-cash-seized-101792696647328.htmlengIndiaøÃúúúúúùThe Bazaar Khala police arrested 16 men during a raid at a house in Nand Kheda Mill Area, where gambling was allegedly on, and seized ‚Çπ1,27,150 in cash, officials said on Thursday.Acting on a tip-off received during patrolling on October 21, a police team led by the assistant commissioner of police (Bazaar Khala) surrounded the house and conducted a raid. According to police, those present allegedly attempted to flee but were apprehended by the team.An FIR has been registered under Sections 3 and 4 of the Public Gambling Act at Bazaar Khala police station.Postal employee arrestedThe Sarojini Nagar police arrested a 24-year-old former branch postmaster, Raunak Shukla, on Thursday in connection with an alleged embezzlement of government and account holders' money, police said. According to police, an FIR (case number 122/2025) was registered against Shukla under Section 316(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita following a complaint filed on April 4, 2025, by Harihar Nath Tripathi, assistant superintendent of post offices. Shukla had been absconding since the case was registered, and a non-bailable warrant had been issued against him by a court.Man loses money after offering lift to strangerA 55-year-old man allegedly lost some of the ‚Çπ1.35 lakh he was carrying after a stranger asked him for a lift on his motorcycle near Vijaypur traffic signal in Vibhuti Khand on Thursday, police said.According to police, Gomti Prasad, a resident of Rahim Nagar, was carrying the cash from the glass shop where he had worked for around 15 years to AU Small Finance Bank in Husadiya's Patrakar Puram area. Around 1pm, a youth carrying a bag approached him and requested a lift. After getting on the motorcycle, the youth placed his bag across their thighs. Prasad became suspicious when the youth allegedly pressed the side where the cash was kept.The youth jumped off, causing Prasad to lose balance and fall. While Prasad collected the scattered cash with help from workers and a street vendor, the youth allegedly fled with some money. Police are gathering details for further action.   Ø Ø                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     îN!5Å+1Ç §m95157071142026-10-23T02:40:51ZAligarh road rage: Audi runs over injured motorcyclist, man diesHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/others/aligarh-road-rage-audi-runs-over-injured-motorcyclist-man-dies-101792696411793.htmlengIndiaøﬂ_____`In a suspected case of road rage, a man riding a motorcycle was killed after an Audi car allegedly rammed the two-wheeler from behind and then ran over him while he lay injured on the road in Aligarh on Tuesday night. Another man riding the motorcycle was injured. Police have registered cases of murder and attempt to murder after a video of the incident went viral.The case was registered at Banna Devi police station, and teams have been formed to arrest the absconding driver. According to reports, the car is registered in the name of Devraj Singh, a former BJP district unit president in Aligarh, and the absconding driver is said to be his nephew.Aligarh SP (City) Aditya Bansal said on Thursday evening that the police station received information on Wednesday about the incident, which took place on Tuesday night."According to the complaint, the occupants of an Audi car deliberately hit the motorcycle, leaving both riders injured. The motorcyclist, identified as Manoj Kumar, later died, while the other rider, Kanhaiya, was injured," Bansal said.A case was registered under relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), including Section 103 for murder and Section 109 for attempt to murder, he said.According to Bansal, the statement of Kanhaiya, an eyewitness and the injured survivor, was recorded. He told police that an altercation had taken place between the two parties over honking before the incident. The Audi driver allegedly rammed the moving motorcycle from behind and then drove over Manoj, who had fallen on the road."The CCTV footage has been preserved, the car has been seized, and the field unit has collected evidence. A technical inspection of the vehicle has also been conducted," Bansal said.He added that the Audi was registered in the name of Devraj Singh, a resident of Raghuveer Puri under Banna Devi police station limits. The driver has been identified as Singh's nephew, and police teams are working to arrest him.Manoj Kumar, who was in his late thirties, worked as a sweetmeat seller. He was married and had three children.The video of the incident, which has gone viral, purportedly shows the Audi hitting the motorcycle from behind and then running over one of the injured men. Some people at the scene are also seen throwing stones at the car as it drives away in the darkness.   	 	                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   çp!5S+1Åi ò95157067012026-10-23T02:40:09Z4 held with 10kg heroin in AmritsarHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/chandigarh-news/4-held-with-10kg-heroin-in-amritsar-101792695566040.htmlengIndiaøŒûûûûûûThe counter intelligence (CI) wing of Punjab Police busted a cross-border narcotics smuggling network by arresting four persons and recovering 10kg of heroin from their possession, director general of police (DGP) Gaurav Yadav said on Thursday.The arrested suspects have been identified as Sukhraj Singh of Hargobind Avenue, Ajitpal Singh, alias Mota, of Khandwala, Anmolpreet Singh of Jawahar Nagar and Robin Gill of Chogawan village, all residents of Amritsar district. Along with the contraband, police teams impounded a motorcycle and a scooter that the suspects were using to transport the illicit cargo.Sharing details of the operation, the DGP said that the CI Amritsar team acted on a reliable intelligence input. The report indicated that the associates were operating under the direct instructions of a foreign-based handler, from whom they had retrieved a consignment of heroin to deliver to another party.A police team intercepted all four suspects near Dera Baba Darshan Singh in Ghanupur Kale village while they were travelling on their two-wheelers. A subsequent search led to the direct recovery of the 10kg heroin consignment.Preliminary investigations reveal that the accused were functioning as a local distribution arm for international drug smugglers, aiming to supply the contraband across various parts of the state.A case has been registered under Sections 21, 25, and 29 of the Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances (NDPS) Act at the state special operations cell (SSOC) police station in Amritsar.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             óz !5i+1Å} ´{95157034522026-10-23T02:35:02ZMohali: Two dead in separate hit-and-run casesHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/chandigarh-news/mohali-two-dead-in-separate-hit-and-run-cases-101792700127641.htmlengIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿA 24-year-old government hospital pharmacist died five days after a hit-and-run on the Landran-Lakhnaur road. Police has registered a case against an unidentified driver of the car involved in the crash.Rohan Kumar, who worked as a pharmacist at Sub-Divisional Hospital (SDH), Kharar, was riding his Bajaj CT 100 motorcycle towards his home in Sekhan Majra after finishing his shift on October 14. His younger brother, Raman Kumar, a student, was driving behind him when a white Kia car allegedly hit Rohan near Balaji Marble Shop around 2.30 pm and fled.Raman said the collision threw his brother off the motorcycle. He alleged that the Kia's tyre punctured after the crash and that the driver changed it a few kilometres away before fleeing. Raman noted the car's registration number, PB-11CY-0450.Rohan suffered head injuries and remained under treatment for five days. He died around 6 pm on October 19, his family said.Raman said he witnessed the crash and followed his injured brother as the family sought medical care. He also alleged that the driver changed the car's punctured tyre a few kilometres from the collision site before fleeing.Sohana police registered a case against the unidentified driver under Sections 106(1) (causing death by negligence), 281 (rash driving) and 324(4) (mischief) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita.In another case, a 37-year-old plumber, Jaswinder Singh, died after a car hit his scooter from behind on the Rora-Bajheri road .Kharar police registered a case on a complaint by the victim's sister, Paramjit Kaur, under Sections 281(rash driving), 106 (causing death by negligence) and 125(a) (act endangering life) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. The collision occurred about 10 kilometres from the police station.According to the complaint, Paramjit and family members were walking from Rora towards Bajheri for work, while her brother Jaswinder Singh followed them on an Activa scooter, registration number PB 24 L 3657, to pick them up.When Jaswinder was about 100 metres behind the family, a car bearing registration number PB 65 P 8095 allegedly approached from behind and struck the scooter. The complaint states that the driver did not sound the horn or dip the headlights before the collision. The impact threw Jaswinder onto the road. He suffered head injuries, according to the complaint. The driver stopped ahead, allowing Paramjit to note the registration number, but then drove away.On receiving the information, police reached the spot and arranged an ambulance to take Jaswinder to Civil Hospital, Kharar. Doctors declared him brought dead. Hospital staff later moved his body to the mortuary at Civil Hospital, Phase 6, Mohali. Further investigation is underway to establish the circumstances of the collision and identify the driver.   s cs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       °5	!5Å%)Åy æM95157010002026-10-23T02:31:14ZInfosys, Adani Power and 8 Other Stocks Set to Announce Q2 Results TodayTrade Brainstradebrains.inhttps://tradebrains.in/indian-markets/infosys-adani-power-and-8-other-stocks-set-to-announce-q2-results-today-12719157engIndia?›]]]]][Stocks across IT, power, steel, automobiles, and pharmaceuticals are set to announce their Q2 FY27 results, with investors watching for earnings growth and business updates.Several listed companies are set to a   è!5Å-+1Ç= ô595157034502026-10-23T02:35:00ZChandigarh: Teen killed, friend hurt in Sector 22 shooting; 2 juveniles detainedHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/chandigarh-news/chandigarh-teen-killed-friend-hurt-in-sector-22-shooting-2-juveniles-detained-101792700609285.htmlengIndiaø‡ÒA 17-year-old boy was killed and another person injured after two juveniles allegedly opened fire outside Sanatan Dharam Temple in Sector 22 on Thursday night. Police have detained the two accused, who are said to be school students.This is the second murder involving juveniles in the city in a week.The deceased, identified as Naitik, a resident of Sector 22, was sitting inside an autorickshaw in the temple parking lot with two others when the assailants arrived on a motorcycle and opened fire around 9.30 pm, police said. One of the victims was declared dead after being taken to Government Multi-Specialty Hospital (GMSH), Sector 16.According to a senior police official, the accused allegedly had a dispute with the victims' group. The victims had reportedly recorded a video of themselves assaulting the accused and uploaded it on Instagram, following which the rivalry escalated.Police teams reached the spot soon after the incident and sealed the area. Around three shots were fired, according to preliminary information. Further investigation is underway.Earlier on October 15, a 17-year-old boy was stabbed to death following an altercation between two groups at a Ramlila event in Sector 41 on Thursday night. Police nabbed a 16-year-old boy for the crime while they are on a lookout for his five to six accomplices - also believed to be minors. A friend of the victim had objected to the other group's presence, questioning why boys from outside the locality had come there. The next day, the accused followed the victim to a nearby market, assaulted him before eventually stabbing him to death.    nnounce their quarterly results on October 23, covering sectors such as IT, banking, power, steel, automobiles, pharmaceuticals, and real estate. The results will give investors an update on how these companies performed during the September quarter.Investors can track revenue, profit, and margins, along with management commentary on future growth. These updates could influence share prices as the market assesses business performance and growth prospects for the coming quarters. Here are the stocks that are set to announce their quarterly results todayInfosys LtdInfosys is a global IT services and consulting company that provides software development, digital transformation, cloud computing, artificial intelligence, and business consulting services. It serves clients across industries, including banking, retail, manufacturing and healthcare, helping businesses improve their technology systems and operations. With a market capitalisation of Rs 4,67,270 crore, its share last traded at Rs 1,151 per share, down by 1.37 percent from the previous close.Coforge LtdCoforge is an IT services and consulting company that provides digital transformation, cloud, data analytics, artificial intelligence and software engineering solutions. It serves clients across industries such as banking, insurance, travel and transportation, helping them modernise technology systems and improve business processes. With a market capitalisation of Rs 84,310 crore, its share last traded at Rs 1,903 per share, down 2.61 percent from the previous close.Adani Power LtdAdani Power is a private sector power generation company that operates thermal power plants and supplies electricity to various states and industrial customers. The company focuses on expanding its generation capacity to meet rising electricity demand in India. With a market capitalisation of Rs 3,56,381 crore, its share last traded at Rs 185 per share, down by 1.20 percent from the previous close.JSW Steel LtdJSW Steel is one of India's leading steel manufacturers, producing products used in construction, infrastructure, automobiles and industrial applications. Its portfolio includes hot-rolled and cold-rolled steel, coated products and other value-added steel products. The company serves domestic and international markets through its manufacturing facilities and distribution network. With a market capitalisation of Rs 2,99,054 crore, its share last traded at Rs 1,223 per share, up by 0.10 percent from the previous close.Shriram Finance LtdShriram Finance is a non-banking financial company that provides commercial vehicle loans, passenger vehicle loans, two-wheeler finance, personal loans and other lending products. It has a strong presence in vehicle financing and serves individuals, transport operators and small businesses across India. With a market capitalisation of Rs 2,12,084 crore, its share last traded at Rs 901 per share, down by 0.85 percent from the previous close.Tata Motors LtdTata Motors is one of India's leading commercial vehicle manufacturers, producing trucks, buses, vans and small commercial vehicles for transportation, logistics and infrastructure needs. Following its demerger from the passenger vehicle business, the company operates as a separately listed entity focused on commercial mobility. With a market capitalisation of Rs 1,52,044 crore, its share last traded at Rs 413 per share, down 1.04 percent from the previous close.CG Power and Industrial Solutions LtdCG Power and Industrial Solutions manufactures electrical equipment used in power generation, transmission, distribution and industrial applications. Its product portfolio includes transformers, switchgear, motors and other electrical systems. The company serves utilities, infras                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ë|%5Å?)Åe üUb-95156938602026-10-23T02:18:28ZMinor boy shot dead by three motorcycle-borne assailants in ChandigarhBhaskar Live English Newsbhaskarlive.inhttps://bhaskarlive.in/others/minor-boy-shot-dead-by-three-motorcycle-borne-assailants-in-chandigarh-2156163engIndiaø«óóóóóòChandigarh, Oct 23 (IANS) A minor boy, identified as Natik, was shot dead by three motorcycle-borne assailants in Sector 22, Chandigarh late Thursday evening, police said.He was travelling in an autorickshaw with a friend when the incident took place. Two other people, including the autorickshaw driver, were also injured, and the driver was admitted to hospital for treatment.According to police, Natik and his friends had reportedly been involved in a rivalry with another group for the past two years. On Thursday, the two groups allegedly clashed in Sector 44. One of the accused reportedly uploaded a video of the altercation on Instagram.Police initially suspected a gang rivalry but later focused their investigation on a dispute between the two groups. The suspects have reportedly been identified.Further investigation into the incident is underway.Earlier in September, a Chandigarh Police Head Constable was shot dead at his residence in Sector 22, with police taking his son into custody in connection with the killing, officials said.The deceased was identified as Nitin, posted in the Accounts Branch of the Chandigarh Police, they said.The incident took place at the cop's official residence in Sector 22.Police received information about the shooting, following which a team from Sector 17 police station reached the spot and began an investigation.A country-made pistol was recovered from the scene, according to police. Forensic experts were also called in to collect evidence from the house.Nitin was taken to a hospital, where doctors declared him dead, reports said.Senior Superintendent of Police, Kanwardeep Kaur, told the media that the victim's wife and son were present at the time of the crime.In a similar incident earlier, Assistant Sub-Inspector Jaswant Singh, posted in Ajnala in Amritsar, had a providential escape when motorcycle-borne assailants attacked him on September 11, and the bullet passed through his turban.Created On : &nbsp 23 Oct 2026 7:46 AM IST   ü Õü                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   à+!5Å-3Ç å95156935112026-10-23T02:17:49ZKumuram Bheem Asifabad: Youth Dies, Another Injured in Bike AccidentDeccan Chronicledeccanchronicle.comhttps://www.deccanchronicle.com/southern-states/telangana/kumuram-bheem-asifabad-youth-dies-another-injured-in-bike-accident-1998053engIndiaøŸŸŸŸŸŸ⁄Kumuram Bheem Asifabad: A youth died and another sustained severe injuries after the motorcycle they were travelling on went out of control and skidded on a highway near Bodhampalli village of Chintalamanepally mandal in Kumuram Bheem Asifabad district.According to reports, the deceased was identified as Jade Ajay, a resident of Gangapur village in Chintalamanepally mandal. He died on the spot, while Durgam Prem Kumar suffered severe injuries in the accident.Locals who witnessed the accident immediately shifted the injured youth to a hospital for treatment.On receiving information, the police reached the spot and shifted the deceased's body to a government hospital for post-mortem examination.A case has been registered, and an investigation is underway.í0!5Åg1CÇm û_95156938252026-10-23T02:18:28Z'Supernatural powers, marry woman of choice': Rajasthan toddler kidnapped for 'sacrifice', rescued in MathuraThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/jaipur/supernatural-powers-marry-woman-of-choice-rajasthan-toddler-kidnapped-for-sacrifice-rescued-in-mathura/articleshow/135131661.cmsengIndiaø¿êêêêêèJAIPUR: Police have arrested a 34-year-old man for allegedly kidnapping a 22-month-old boy from the Neemrana area of Kotputli-Behror district, with investigators saying the accused intended to sacrifice the child to gain "supernatural powers, please gods, and marry a woman of his choice".The toddler, Krishna, was rescued from a Kali temple in Mathura district, Uttar Pradesh, within about 40 hours of the abduction, police said.Police identified the accused as Vivek Kumar Kushwaha, a native of Sasaram in Bihar's Rohtas district, and said he was arrested before he could allegedly carry out the human sacrifice.Police also said the accused told investigators he had been depressed for more than a year and that his wife had left him. Officials added there was a prior theft case against him in Bihar."The accused had become deeply influenced by superstition and believed that sacrificing the toddler would help him fulfil his personal desires," Superintendent of Police Satveer Singh said Thursday. "For almost four months he was thinking to kidnap and sacrifice an infant to please gods."Investigators said Kushwaha first planned to abduct an infant or toddler from the overcrowded Dargah Bazaar area in Ajmer but shifted plans after failing there.Police said he then stole a motorcycle from the Clock Tower area in Ajmer and travelled to Neemrana, allegedly stealing another bike en route when the first ran out of fuel. "The accused had visited Ajmer and other cities and randomly picked up the boy," the SP said.Krishna was allegedly kidnapped while playing outside his home in the Holi Tiba area of Neemrana on Oct 18, triggering a large search operation."We examined footage from more than 350 CCTV cameras and followed leads across several locations to track the accused's movements towards Uttar Pradesh," a police officer said. "The investigation eventually led police to a Kali temple in Kavar village near Kosi Kalan in Mathura, " he said.   Ù Ù                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          ö	!5Å7+1Ç9 Ø95156927212026-10-23T02:16:41ZMACT orders Serum institute, insurer to pay ‚Çπ16.72 lakh to accident victim's motherHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/pune-news/mact-orders-serum-institute-insurer-to-pay-16-72-lakh-to-accident-victim-s-mother-101792693768128.htmlengIndiaøÕùùùùùúPune: The Motor Accident Claims Tribunal (MACT), Pune, has directed Serum Institute of India Pvt Ltd and its insurer, New India Assurance Company Ltd, to jointly and severally pay ‚Çπ16.72 lakh in compensation, with 7% annual interest, to a 65-year-old woman whose 41-year-old son died after being run over by a car following a motorcycle accident near Golf Club Chowk in June 2024.In its judgment delivered on Wednesday, tribunal member SR Agrawal held that the evidence established negligence on the part of the car driver. Serum institute owned the vehicle involved in the accident."The material on record establishes that the accident was caused by the rash or negligent driving of the offending vehicle," the tribunal observed. It added that the motorcycle skidding and the victim falling on the road did not, by themselves, absolve the driver of the responsibility to exercise due care.The award was passed on a claim petition filed by the victim's mother, Lata Mohanrao Chavan, under Section 166 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988, on October 19, 2024.According to the petition, Kedar Chavan was riding towards Yerawada Jail Post Office from Golf Club Chowk around 1 pm on June 18, 2024, when his motorcycle skidded. The high-end car allegedly approaching from behind at high speed, hit the motorcycle and ran over him. He sustained multiple injuries and died during treatment at Sahyadri Hospital. Police registered a case against the driver and subsequently filed a chargesheet.The mother stated that her son worked as a delivery executive with a logistics firm and ran a tailoring business. She claimed he earned ‚Çπ37,000 a month from both occupations and sought ‚Çπ60 lakh in compensation, stating that she depended on his income.Serum institute admitted owning the car but denied its involvement in the accident. The insurer disputed the deceased's income and the mother's dependency, denied negligence and alleged that the driver lacked a valid licence and the owner had breached policy conditions.The tribunal noted that neither the driver nor any eyewitness was examined by the respondents to explain the collision. It said motor accident claims are decided on the preponderance of probabilities, rather than the stricter standard applicable in criminal trials.While accepting negligence, the tribunal assessed Chavan's monthly income at ‚Çπ15,000, citing gaps in the employment, income and tailoring-business records. Adding 25% for future prospects, deducting half towards personal expenses and applying a multiplier of 14, it calculated the loss of dependency at ‚Çπ15.75 lakh.The award includes amounts for funeral expenses, loss of estate, loss of consortium and medical expenses, taking the total to ‚Çπ16,72,210. Rejecting the insurer's policy-breach argument for want of evidence, the tribunal directed both respondents to pay the compensation with 7% annual interest from the date of filing the petition until realisation, along with ‚Çπ5,000 towards litigation costs.   a Qa                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ¢(!5Å'-Çw æM95156892852026-10-23T02:10:19ZTom Skerritt, star of 'Alien', 'Top Gun' and 'Picket Fences', dies in Seattle at 93 after more than 60 years in HollywoodThe Statesmanthestatesman.comhttps://www.thestatesman.com/entertainment/hollywood/tom-skerritt-star-of-alien-top-gun-and-picket-fences-dies-in-seattle-at-93-after-more-than-60-years-in-hollywood-1503654019.htmlengIndia?¢ He never had to raise his voice to run the room. A Detroit kid with four Air Force years behind h   ï,!5Å+1Ç/ •w95156918402026-10-23T02:15:13ZFour held for assaulting family over garbage dumping dispute in GurugramHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/gurugram-news/four-held-for-assaulting-family-over-garbage-dumping-dispute-in-gurugram-101792694248683.htmlengIndiaøŸŸŸŸŸŸ⁄Three men were arrested and a minor was apprehended on Thursday for allegedly assaulting a couple and their two minor children over repeated garbage dumping on a vacant private land in Behrampur, Sector 59, said police.According to police, the accused included a 45-year-old man, his 75-year-old father, both residents of Behrampur, Sector 65 and their 28-year-old relative from Faridabad's Bhaisrawali. The apprehended minor is the 45-year-old man's 16-year-old son. The incident took place on the evening of October 16.Police said the daughter suffered a head injury and a deep cut on her forearm, while the other three sustained multiple fractures in their forearms and legs.Investigators said the woman had repeatedly dumped kitchen waste on a vacant plot in front of their house. The plot belonged to the neighbouring family, leading to disputes between the two sides in the past.On October 16, the woman's son was on a motorcycle with her to deliver lunch to his father when their vehicle was involved in a minor collision with the neighbour's son, who was also riding a motorcycle. An argument followed between the two sides."Later that evening, the husband went to the neighbor's house to complain about his son. A heated argument broke out, following which the man returned home," said police.Police said the neighbours and others allegedly attacked him at the entrance of his house with rods and sticks. They also assaulted his wife and children when they tried to intervene before fleeing the spot.Neighbours rushed the injured family to a private hospital in Sector 57. They were discharged on Wednesday, police added.The injured man said he received six stitches on his head and suffered a fracture on his left forearm. "My son suffered fractures in both forearms and his right knee. My wife fractured her left leg, while my daughter sustained a severe head injury after being hit with a rod," he said."Our condition was critical and I could only give my statement to the police two days after the incident," he said.Sandeep Turan, spokesperson, Gurugram police, said the incident was captured on a CCTV camera. "The three arrested men would be kept in lock-up overnight and granted bail on Friday," he said.Based on the man's complaint, an FIR was registered against the suspects for assault, wrongful restraint, rioting and criminal intimidation at Sector 65 police station on Sunday.    im, Tom Skerritt built a career out of playing the person you would follow without a second thought. Sixty years later, that calm is exactly what people remember.Tom Skerritt has died at 93. His family said he passed away on Wednesday, October 21, 2026, in Seattle. The cause was natural.Skerritt worked for more than 60 years. Most people know him from 'Alien', 'Top Gun' and 'Picket Fences'. He had the jaw, the mustache and the crinkly eyes. He played captains, cops, dads and sheriffs. Audiences trusted him on sight. His family said, "We are heartbroken by his loss."A Detroit kidThomas Roy Skerritt was born on August 25, 1933, in Detroit. He was the youngest of three children. His mother, Helen, ran the household. His father, Roy, was a general businessman.Tom later called himself a blue-collar kid from the city. He graduated from Mackenzie High School in 1951. Acting was nowhere on his radar yet.Air Force yearsRight after graduation, he joined the US Air Force. He served a four-year tour. Part of that time was at Bergstrom Air Force Base in Texas.Service stayed with him for life. His family says veterans mattered a lot to him.Finding actingAfter the Air Force, he went to Wayne State University. Then he moved on to UCLA. He wanted to be a writer or a director. Acting began as a way to beat his shyness. He never thought it could be a real job.Then he landed a part in a stage production of 'The Rainmaker'. People noticed. He left UCLA without a degree and went after acting full time. His first film was 'War Hunt' in 1962.He did a ton of television. He guest-starred on shows like 'Combat!' and '12 O'Clock High'. In 1972 he played a young gambler on 'Cannon'. In 1975 he came back to that show as a crooked sheriff. Same actor, very different men.Over his career he logged more than 40 films. He also appeared in more than 200 TV episodes.MASH changes everythingHis big break came in 1970. Director Robert Altman cast him in 'MASH'. Skerritt was 37. Altman became a mentor to him.Work picked up fast after that. 'Wild Rovers' came in 1971. 'Fuzz' followed in 1972. 'Big Bad Mama' arrived in 1974. He also played a motorcycle cop in 'Harold and Maude'.In 1977 he played Shirley MacLaine's husband in 'The Turning Point'. That film earned 11 Oscar nominations. He closed out the decade with 'Up in Smoke' and 'Ice Castles' in 1978.Captain DallasIn 1979, Ridley Scott put him in space. Skerritt played Captain Dallas of the doomed ship Nostromo in 'Alien'.Here is the fun part. He first said no. He worried the budget would all go to special effects. Then he changed his mind, and the film became a sci-fi classic.Dallas does not make it to the end. Sigourney Weaver's Ripley takes over. But fans never forgot the captain who started the trip.Sheriffs and Top GunIn 1983 he played a small-town sheriff in 'The Dead Zone'. Then came 1986 and 'Top Gun'. He played Mike "Viper" Metcalf, the flight instructor with a calm voice and a firm hand. Tom Cruise's character looked up to him. So did a lot of moviegoers.That same year he appeared in 'SpaceCamp'. In 1988 he did 'Poltergeist III'. In 1989 he joined the big cast of 'Steel Magnolias'.This past May, 'Top Gun' returned to theaters for its 40th anniversary. Viper was back on the big screen.Cheers and Picket FencesTV gave him an even bigger stage. From 1987 to 1988 he had a six-episode run on 'Cheers' as Evan Drake.Then in 1992 came 'Picket Fences'. David E. Kelley created the CBS drama. Skerritt played Sheriff Jimmy Brock in the fictional town of Rome, Wisconsin. Brock was the calm one in a very strange place.The show ran four seasons, until 1996. It won 14 Emmy Awards. One of them went to Skerritt in 1993 for lead actor in a drama series. He also earned two Golden Globe nominations.A river and a causeIn 1992 he also appeared in Robert Redford's 'A River Ru                                                                                                                                                                                                & &                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ôW!5Å15Åm Ø95156889342026-10-23T02:09:41ZTiger Shroff firing: Two women among four accused sent to police custodyThe Shillong Timestheshillongtimes.comhttps://theshillongtimes.com/2026/10/23/tiger-shroff-firing-two-women-among-four-accused-sent-to-police-custody/engIndiaø·qqqqqrA court here on Thursday remanded four accused, including two women, held in Delhi in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff to police custody till October 26.They have been identified as Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh.The accused were produced before the magistrate court after being brought to the city from the national capital.Police sought their remand, saying they have active participation in the conspiracy along with the previously arrested accused.Police said these accused supplied weapons to the shooters, which were used in the crime.The defence, represented by Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi, opposed their remand, saying that there was no material against them and they have been arrested on the basis of mere suspicion.Hence, their custodial interrogation is unwarranted and the accused should be remanded to judicial custody, they said.After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused to custody till October 26.According to the police, two of these accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women smuggled the firearms by train to Mumbai, handing them over directly to the attackers.At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. A motorcycle, allegedly used by the shooters, was found abandoned in Andheri.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.A total of 10 persons have been arrested in the case so far.Of them, the court on Wednesday remanded three accused- Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, to police custody till October 31.Actor's team shares video of his injured armActor Tiger Shroff's team shared a video of his injured arms on Thursday, days after the Bollywood star narrowly survived a gun attack on his car.At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle.The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.Team Tiger Shroff, the official Instagram page managed by his team, shared the video along with the caption, "God is kind." The short clip shows several small, dot-like marks and red spots across his arm.Three accused, identified as Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, were detained at Kota railway station in Rajasthan.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act. (PTI)    ¬                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          ï)!5ÅI'+Ç •c95156796242026-10-23T01:56:52ZSchool student shot dead in Chandigarh's Sector 22, police probe rivalry angle - India TV NewsIndia TV Newsindiatvnews.comhttps://www.indiatvnews.com/news/india/school-student-shot-dead-in-chandigarh-s-sector-22-police-probe-rivalry-angle-2026-10-23-1057689engIndiaø››››››ﬁA firing incident was reported in Sector 22 of Chandigarh, leaving one person dead and another critically injured. The deceased has been identified as Naitik.As per initial reports, two groups who earlier studied in the same school engaged in a fighting at late night in Sector 34, following that, a group of three juvenile gunmen on a motorcycle attacked the another group of minors in Sector 22 when they are returning home in an autorickshaw. The alleged firing took life of one person and critically injured the other. The autorickshaw driver was also got injured.According to SHO Sudesh Kumar, "two boys and the auto-rickshaw driver were struck by gunfire. The auto-rickshaw driver has been admitted to the hospital. One person has lost his life. It appears there was a long-standing grudge between these boys, dating back to their school days. We have learned that a dispute broke out among a group of friends in Sector 44 today...The boy who died was a minor and the perpetrator is also of a similar age...The CFSL team has arrived, so it would be premature to comment further; the investigation is still in its initial stages."Similar incident: Class 9 student stabbed to death in Delhi's Pitampura over Instagram commentA Class 9 student was killed and a young man seriously injured in a stabbing incident during a Durga idol immersion procession in Delhi's Pitampura area on Wednesday evening. The attack allegedly involved masked assailants and is believed to have stemmed from a dispute over a comment on an Instagram post. Delhi Police have detained four minor boys in connection with the case. The injured man has been admitted to hospital, while police are investigating the circumstances surrounding the attack.What happened during the Durga idol immersion procession?The incident took place as a Durga idol immersion procession was passing through Pitampura on Wednesday evening. According to the initial account, the attackers were allegedly involved in a dispute with a young man named Ashu over a comment on an Instagram post.During the procession, the assailants allegedly found an opportunity to surround Ashu and attack him with knives. The stabbing left a Class 9 student dead and Ashu seriously injured. Further details about the sequence of events and the circumstances in which the school student was attacked have not been established in the information available so far.à;!5{Å? çG95156844832026-10-23T02:03:44ZMTC driver gets 4.5-year jail for double fatal incidentdtNext.indtnext.inhttps://www.dtnext.in/news/chennai/mtc-driver-gets-45-year-jail-for-double-fatal-incidentengIndiaøﬁ^^^^^^CHENNAI: Nearly a decade after a Metropolitan Transport Corporation (MTC) bus mowed down two youths, both aged 20, a court in Chennai sentenced the driver of the vehicle to four and half years' imprisonment. The fatal road accident happened in September 2017 in Ayanavaram.According to the prosecution, Mani, the bus driver, was driving the vehicle rashly and negligently from east to west at the junction of KH Road and Somasundaram Street in Ayanavaram. The bus hit a two-wheeler, and in the impact, the two people riding that vehicle, R Manikandan (20) and S Tamilarasan (20), died on the spot.The Kilpauk Traffic Investigation Wing (TIW) registered a case and conducted the inquiry, which revealed that Mani was responsible for the fatal accident. The police filed the final report before the magistrate. On Wednesday, the court held the charges proved.   ´ ´                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 îR%5Å9/Ås §b-95156791282026-10-23T01:55:37ZGuwahati city lanes pose accident risks amid poor streetlightingThe Sentinel Newspapersentinelassam.comhttps://www.sentinelassam.com/cities/guwahati-city/guwahati-city-lanes-pose-accident-risks-amid-poor-streetlightingengIndiaø÷÷÷÷÷÷◊GUWAHATI: While roads used by VIPs often receive priority attention, damaged internal roads and poorly lit neighbourhood lanes across Guwahati continue to pose safety risks to commuters. Residents have questioned the priorities of civic authorities as uneven surfaces and inadequate streetlighting make night travel hazardous.A stretch of an internal road, marked by broken interlocking pavement blocks, loose construction material and stagnant water, reflects the conditions residents say they regularly face. Sections of the surface have deteriorated, leaving uneven patches that could cause two-wheelers to skid and pedestrians to stumble. Without adequate streetlighting, these hazards become difficult to spot after sunset.Residents fear that the combination of damaged roads and poor visibility could lead to accidents, particularly involving motorcyclists, cyclists and elderly pedestrians. Water-filled depressions can conceal the extent of road damage, leaving commuters with little time to react."Roads should not become dangerous simply because they are inside residential areas. We also pay taxes and deserve safe roads and proper lighting," a resident said.Another citizen questioned the apparent disparity in road maintenance. "Whenever VIP movement takes place, roads on those routes appear to receive attention. But the condition of our neighbourhood lanes remains neglected. Who will take responsibility if someone meets with an accident at night?" the resident asked.A third resident said the absence of functional streetlights compounded the problem."After dark, it is difficult to see broken blocks and waterlogged patches. Two-wheeler riders can lose control, while pedestrians may fall. Authorities should act before an accident happens," the resident said.The situation raises questions about the regular monitoring of internal roads, the maintenance of streetlighting and accountability for civic infrastructure. While major routes are essential for citywide mobility, residential lanes are equally important for the daily movement of thousands of people.Residents have called for damaged stretches to be repaired, stagnant water to be cleared and non-functional streetlights to be restored. Without timely intervention, they fear, neglected neighbourhood roads will continue to expose commuters to preventable accidents.   ˙ Í˙                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              †n!5Q15Å! æM95156781272026-10-23T01:53:40ZOn Being Conrad Sangma: A CritiqueThe Shillong Timestheshillongtimes.comhttps://theshillongtimes.com/2026/10/23/on-being-conrad-sangma-a-critique/engIndiaø≥I write this knowing very well that I put my personal and professional reputation on the line. But what must be written has to be written else we become hypocrites unable to express our views for fear of adverse criticism.Meghalaya's Chief Minister, Conrad Sangma is the man for al   î!5Å71CÇ1 £95156790112026-10-23T01:55:37Z'God is kind': Tiger Shroff shares video showing gunpowder marks on arms after firingThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/mumbai/god-is-kind-tiger-shroffs-team-shares-video-showing-marks-on-actors-arms/articleshow/135131464.cmsengIndiaø¬íííííìTiger Shroff's team shared a video showing gunpowder marks on his arms on Thursday, days after the Bollywood star narrowly escaped a firing attack on his car in Mumbai.At least two men fired shots at Shroff's car in Juhu on Sunday evening before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander sustained injuriesTeam Tiger Shroff, the official Instagram page managed by his team, shared the video with the caption, "God is kind."The short clip shows several small, dot-like marks and red spots across his arm.ID@undefined Caption not available.ID@undefined Caption not available.ID@undefined Caption not available.ID@undefined Caption not available.ID@undefined Caption not available.Earlier, four accused arrested in connection with the firing on the actor were produced before Mumbai's Esplanade Court (Killa Court) on Thursday. Anil Pandit has been named as an absconding accused in the case, according to the police remand application submitted before the court.During the proceedings, Mumbai Police argued that the firing incident was carried out at the behest of Anil Pandit. The court remanded all four accused to police custody until October 26, rejecting the police request for custody until October 31.The four accused were brought to Mumbai from Kota, Rajasthan, and produced before the court after undergoing medical examinations.The incident took place around 7 pm on October 18 in Juhu when Shroff was leaving a football club. The actor escaped unhurt, while his driver sustained injuries.Meanwhile, on Tuesday, Tiger's team issued a stern warning against the circulation of fabricated stories, unauthorised statements and AI-generated videos falsely attributed to the actor. It urged media organisations and social media platforms to verify information before publishing it.The team also warned that legal action may be initiated against individuals and pages creating, promoting or circulating such content.In an official statement shared on social media, Team Tiger categorically clarified that the actor had not issued any statements, released any videos or authorised any communication concerning the recent firing incident or related developments.(With Agency Inputs)    l seasons. He seems to glide from meeting to meeting and then be on the ground to meet with real people. Hence he is able to feel the pulse of the people first hand and doesn't need to rely too much on his official channels. These channels are often peopled by those who believe they are selected to dress well, earn well, work from 10am to 5 pm and get rich quick from means foul or fair. This has been the trick of the trade for the longest time. Its no one's fault. Its the system that's broken or was intended to remain broken since it is copy-pasted from the British model.. the same British that once ruled us as sovereigns. That we adopted the playbook of the foreign rulers to then continue with the same kind of "rule" over our own people is in itself severely defective.Conrad Sangma entered politics after having observed his father, PA Sangma from close quarters. He was as affected as his parents were when on March 25, 1990, the government led by his father was toppled like nine-pins. He was then only 12 years of age, just about to enter the gawky teenage years. The night before the government fell, there were already signs of dissension within the cabinet since Sangma had drastically changed some of the rules of the game especially when it came to land acquisition for road making. I recall PA Sangma saying, "The Government is spending more on land acquisition than on the actual construction of roads." He saw "corruption" upfront in the Public Works Department (PWD) where engineers leaked state secrets to the business mafia who were informed about probable areas where land would need to be acquired for road projects. These business honchos then bought land for peanuts and sold it back to the government at a premium. PA Sangma wanted to end this culture of crony capitalism and nepotism. But PA Sangma did not bargain for the fact that many MLAs in his government ate out of the hands of the contractor caucus. And that was how Meghalaya lost a visionary CM who wanted to bring in several governance reforms.Some MLAs swore eternal loyalty to PA Sangma but hardly had they got out of his residence when they were called to another venue where the plan for formation of an alternative government was being hatched. This alternative team was aided and abetted by the leading moneybags of Meghalaya at the time (names cannot be mentioned; those who know, know who they are/were) end will who were discontented with PA Sangma's who they felt was a spoke on the wheels of their crony capitalist ventures particularly in land acquisition for road projects.Conrad's foray into electoral politics was in 2004 when he contested for the Garo Hills District Council elections. Interestingly he lost by 182 votes. But he learnt a critical lesson - grassroots connect was imperative if one was to win elections. He had been away from the state and country for a while for studies and people then did not know him enough to repose their faith in him. Since then, Conrad has learnt the electioneering game better than most politicians.In 2008 Conrad was first elected to the Meghalaya Legislative Assembly for the first time on a Nationalist Congress Party (NCP) ticket and even held the post of Finance Minister for a very brief period of a year. He also was Minister for Power, Tourism, GAD and IT. Sadly those were the days of frequent electoral earthquakes and from being in the government for one year, Conrad was pushed to playing the role of Leader of the Opposition during 2009-13. During that phase the CMs were DD Lapang, Donkupar Roy (with a brief stint of President's Rule in between), followed by Dr Mukul Sangma who lasted for nearly three years from April 2010 to March 2013. Afte                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                á{%5Å-)-Ç# ãb-95156559572026-10-23T01:12:05ZAre you planning to buy a Royal Enfield? These 5 upcoming bikes are worth a waitBusiness Todaybusinesstoday.inhttps://www.businesstoday.in/latest/photo/are-you-planning-to-buy-a-royal-enfield-these-5-upcoming-bikes-are-worth-a-wait-563106-2026-10-22engIndia?ø Planning to buy a Royal Enfield? Explore 5 upcoming bikes, including Himalayan 750, Continental GT 750, Interceptor 750, Scram 450 and electric Flying Flea S6, with key features and updates.Royal Enfield is preparing to unveil its biggest Himalayan yet! The Himalayan 750 is set for its global debut at EICMA 2026 in November, followed by an Indian showcase at Motoverse in Goa. Powered by a new 750cc parallel-twin engine, the adventure motorcycle is expected to produce around 55hp and 60Nm of torque. Built on the new R-platform, it could feature cruise control, a 19-inch front wheel and a more off-road-focused variant with a 21-inch wheel. Could this become Royal Enfield's ultimate touring machine?óp!5Å#1/Åg ´=95156698962026-10-23T01:37:44ZTiger Shroff firing: Accused shooters' jammed pistol misfired in hotel roomThe Indian Expressindianexpress.comhttps://indianexpress.com/article/india/tiger-shroff-firing-accused-shooters-jammed-pistol-misfired-10932870/engIndiaø◊WWWWWXThank you for your feedback.Your feedback has been reported succesfully.The two shooters arrested in connection with the firing incident at actor Tiger Shroff's residence allegedly practiced shooting in a forest near Mumbai before one of their pistols jammed. The weapon reportedly misfired when they attempted to remove a stuck bullet in their hotel room in Andheri (East), said a source.The two accused, Rehan Ansari and Phool Singh, were staying in room number 201 at RR Residency in Andheri (East). They allegedly checked in to the hotel at 11 am on October 14 using fake Aadhaar cards bearing the names Ankit and Mandeep Man.The accused booked the room and paid Rs 1,500 per day. However, they left the hotel on the afternoon of October 18 without informing the staff, a police officer said. The Crime Branch seized documents, the hotel's booking register, clothes and a small bag left behind by the accused, and sealed the room.According to police, the accused had stayed at different locations across Mumbai for nearly 20 days before the firing incident. They were also using a yellow motorcycle.Hotel staff told police they had not heard any gunshot from the room. CCTV footage showed the accused leaving the hotel through its rear exit at around 4:12 pm on October 18. Another accused Hritik Mehto alias Roshan was also seen at the hotel premises in CCTV footage; his yellow Pulsar was also seen on camera in the hotel premises, said a source.The hotel's manager Vikrant Paswan told media that at the time when the accused came to book the room, the establishment's staff asked for their documents. The accused said they had pictures of Aadhaar cards on their mobile phone and sent it to the hotel's WhatsApp number. The hotel staff took printouts, and the room was booked under a name mentioned on one of the Aadhaar cards, Paswan said. They left the room without informing the hotel staff. So, on the evening of October 18, the hotel staff tried to contact them by phone to confirm if they wanted to continue their stay, but their numbers were switched off, added Paswan.The Crime Branch was in the process of identifying the forest area where the two allegedly practiced shooting. Investigators suspect they may have visited Aarey Colony, but were verifying the same. The accused have so far been unable to recall the exact location or identify the spot where they allegedly went for practice.During the practice session, one of the pistols reportedly jammed. After returning to their hotel room, the accused allegedly tried to remove the stuck bullet, during which the weapon misfired and a bullet struck the wall, the officer said. The pistols have not yet been recovered. Police suspect the accused threw the weapons away while fleeing Mumbai.   * ı*                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              áH%5ÅA)-Ç5 ä b-95156453862026-10-23T00:52:20Z49 km claimed range, 436.5 km actual ride! How this electric bike stunned the record booksBusiness Todaybusinesstoday.inhttps://www.businesstoday.in/latest/photo/49-km-claimed-range-436-5-km-actual-ride-how-this-electric-bike-stunned-the-record-books-563083-2026-10-22engIndiaøÆ Zero Motorcycles' DS electric bike reportedly sets a Guinness World Record with a 436.5 km single-charge ride, beating the previous record by 125.82 km. Discover its battery secret.436.5 km on a single charge, and not on a closed test track! American manufacturer Zero Motorcycles' DS electric motorcycle has reportedly set a Guinness World Record after Belgian rider Jelle Verstraeten completed an extraordinary journey through France and Italy. The ride took him across public roads, mountain stretches and villages towards the Mediterranean coast, challenging the idea that electric motorcycles are only suitable for short commutes.í%5i-3ÅA †Kb-95156464342026-10-23T00:55:13ZFour killed in 2 days in A'bad-G'nagar mishapsAhmedabad Mirrorahmedabadmirror.comhttps://www.ahmedabadmirror.com/four-killed-in-2-days-in-abad-gnagar-mishaps/81924551.htmlengIndiaø“““““““Seven-year-old cyclist crushed under Fortuner in G'nagar; 3 others killed in separate accidents in Ahmedabad RuralFour lives, including that of a seven-year-old boy, were lost in separate road accidents in Gandhinagar and Ahmedabad Rural over two days.Seven-year-old Devansh Kadvatar, a Class 2 student of Radiant School, died after a Fortuner SUV allegedly knocked him off his bicycle in Gandhinagar's Sector 7 on Wednesday. The vehicle's left rear tyre ran over his head. Devansh had returned from school after an examination before stepping out to cycle. Accused driver Ghanshyamsinh Chauhan took him to Civil Hospital, where doctors declared him dead at 12.46 pm. Sector 7 police registered an FIR.Scrap dealer killed in a hit-and-runMahesh Devipujak (35), a Borsad-based scrap dealer and father of four, was killed in a hit-and-run accident near MP Pandya School on the Aslali-Jetalpur highway on Tuesday evening. Devipujak was returning home from a religious festival at his wife's parental home in Kadi when he parked his scooter and stepped onto the road to remove a sack of powder. An unidentified speeding vehicle struck him, causing fatal head injuries. The driver then fled the scene.Bolero hits bikeA woman, Kamla Parmar, died during treatment at LG Hospital after a Bolero pick-up allegedly collided head-on with a motorcycle near the pond curve ahead of Naz village on Pirana-Jetalpur Road on Wednesday. Her son Manoj, who was riding the motorcycle, sustained injuries to his right leg and other parts of his body. The duo were returning from Vasai after attending a condolence ritual. The Bolero driver allegedly abandoned the vehicle and fled.Fatal highway collisionAslali Police registered an FIR on Wednesday following a fatal hit-and-run near Jetalpur on October 20. According to complainant Sangeeta Devipujak, her husband Mahesh suffered severe head and left-leg injuries and died on the spot. Police booked the unidentified driver under BNS Sections 281, 125(a), 125(b) and 106(1), along with Sections 177 and 184 of the Motor Vehicles Act.   Q Q                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       á,%5Å/)-Ç/ âgb-95156430792026-10-23T00:47:01ZSmaller than a car! The world's tiniest plane made history before a tragic endingBusiness Todaybusinesstoday.inhttps://www.businesstoday.in/latest/world/photo/smaller-than-a-car-the-worlds-tiniest-plane-made-history-before-a-tragic-ending-563092-2026-10-22engIndiaøªMeet the Starr Bumble Bee II, the world's smallest aeroplane! Built by Robert H. Starr, it set a Guinness World Record in 1988 before a devastating crash ended its remarkable flying career.Why would anyone build an aeroplane barely longer than a motorcycle? For Robert Starr, it was a battle to claim aviation's most unusual record. He had previously worked with aircraft designer Ray Stits on the Stits Sky Baby, which first flew in 1952. Starr later built the original Bumble Bee in 1984, but when its record was surpassed, he returned with an even smaller creation. The Bumble Bee II was his answer to the challenge.    õ ã õ                                                                                                                                               °$!5})-Åq æM95156036842026-10-22T23:35:10ZViolence, counter-allegations mar local body nominationsThe Hans Indiathehansindia.comhttps://www.thehansindia.com/news/cities/amaravati/violence-counter-allegations-mar-local-body-nominations-1134850engIndiaø’’’’’’÷Police take away YSRCP MP Y S Avinash Reddy from his home in Pulivendula on ThursdayAmaravati: The second day of nominations for the MPTC and ZPTC elections in the state on Thursday witnessed widespread clashes, stone-pelting,     ör!5Å'#-Å[ ±Y95156266202026-10-23T00:17:17ZDelhi cops bust interstate heroin supply, manufacturing network - The TribuneThe Tribunetribuneindia.comhttps://www.tribuneindia.com/news/delhi/delhi-cops-bust-interstate-heroin-supply-manufacturing-network/engIndiaø€[[[[[\The Delhi Police busted an interstate heroin supply and manufacturing network spanning Delhi-NCR, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Jharkhand, arresting seven accused and recovering 8.128 kg of heroin worth around Rs 60 crore in the international market.The Special Staff of Rohini district also seized Rs 12.81 lakh in cash, three SUVs and a motorcycle. The police recovered chemicals, equipment and other materials allegedly used to manufacture heroin from an illicit facility in Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh.According to the police, the investigation uncovered links across the supply chain, from the alleged cultivation of opium poppy in Jharkhand and the supply of raw opium to the manufacturing of heroin in Uttar Pradesh and its distribution in Delhi-NCR.The operation began on September 16, when a team intercepted a car in Sector 32, Begumpur, and arrested Laxman Hooda, who had allegedly arrived to deliver heroin. The police recovered 300 grams of heroin and Rs 3 lakh from the vehicle.The next day, the alleged source supplier, Anil alias Bhola, was arrested from Sonipat, Haryana. The police recovered 501 grams of heroin from his vehicle. Anil has 12 previous cases registered against him, the police said.He was earlier arrested in an NDPS case registered at the Bhalswa Dairy police station in 2025 but allegedly failed to surrender after being granted interim bail. He was subsequently declared a proclaimed offender by a court.Further investigation, aided by technical surveillance and human intelligence, led the police to a suspected heroin manufacturing facility in Sita Colony, Jankipuram, Lucknow, on October 4. The police arrested Bablu and recovered 6.275 kg of freshly manufactured heroin.The raid also yielded 2.504 kg of sodium, 787 grams of acetic anhydride, a gas cylinder, a mixer grinder, a tub, utensils, polythene, an electronic weighing machine, a wooden basket and other materials allegedly used in the manufacturing process.Based on information provided by Bablu, the police traced and arrested Ruksar Ali, alias Raju, the alleged main supplier and owner of the manufacturing facility, from Bareilly, Uttar Pradesh.On October 6, the police arrested Ajaj Ahmed from Bareilly. He allegedly supplied crude opium to Ruksar Ali. The police said 501 grams of heroin and a motorcycle were recovered from him.The investigation subsequently led to the arrest of Mohammad Azhar from Badaun, Uttar Pradesh, on October 16. He allegedly supplied heroin and crude opium to Ajaj Ahmed. The police recovered 551 grams of heroin, Rs 9.81 lakh in cash and a SUV from him.On October 18, the police arrested Prakash Kumar from Jharkhand's Chatra district, a Naxalite-affected area. He allegedly supplied raw opium to other accused and was involved in the illegal cultivation of opium poppy on his agricultural land, the police said.The police said the arrests had exposed an interstate network involving alleged suppliers of raw opium, a heroin manufacturing facility and distributors operating across multiple states. Further investigation is underway to identify other associates and establish the full extent of the network and its operations.    allegations of nomination papers being torn up and police action in several districts, intensifying the political confrontation between the ruling NDA and the YSRCP.While the YSRCP accused the police of siding with the TDP and preventing its candidates from filing nominations, ruling alliance leaders alleged that the opposition was instigating disturbances and subsequently portraying itself as a victim.Incidents were reported from YSR Kadapa, Annamayya, Anantapur, Kurnool, Palnadu, Chittoor, Nellore, Prakasam and other areas. Reports included attacks on party workers, vehicles being set on fire, nomination documents being destroyed and police resorting to lathi-charges to disperse rival groups. Although nominations proceeded without major incidents in several other districts, the developments in Rayalaseema and Palnadu raised concerns about candidates' ability to participate freely.In Annamayya district's Thamballapalle constituency, clashes between TDP and YSRCP workers in Peddamandyam and Peddadippasamudram left several people injured. TDP leaders Narayana Reddy and Anand were among those injured in Peddamandyam, where police resorted to a lathi-charge. In Peddadippasamudram, stone-pelting and the burning of two-wheelers aggravated the situation.YSR Kadapa district witnessed clashes, stone-pelting and allegations of nomination papers being torn up at multiple locations.In Gundlakunta in Jammalamadugu constituency, a motorcycle belonging to YSRCP members was reportedly set on fire. Tension also prevailed near the residence of TDP MLC Ramasubba Reddy, while YSRCP MLA Dr Sudha and other leaders were arrested in Badvel.In Nandaluru, a factional clash within the TDP between supporters of Jaganmohan Raju and Meda Vijaya Sekhar Reddy resulted in two cars and some motorcycles being set on fire. TDP state spokesperson Balasubrahmanyam reportedly fired shots into the air.In Palnadu, clashes were reported at Nakarikallu, Dachepalli and Edlapadu. At Nakarikallu, rival groups accused each other of destroying MPTC nomination papers, prompting police to resort to a lathi-charge. A case was registered against former Macherla MLA Pinnelli Ramakrishna Reddy and other YSRCP leaders following a protest in Macherla over alleged obstruction of nominations.Anantapur district also witnessed confrontations. Police stopped former YSRCP MLA Thopudurthi Prakash Reddy at Vaddepalli while he was travelling towards Atmakur with a candidate, citing restrictions on people from outside the local area. In Guntakal, TDP and YSRCP leaders clashed amid allegations that nomination papers belonging to YSRCP candidates were torn up. Stone-pelting was reported near the Anantapur rural MPDO office, leaving a person named Ramanjaneyulu with a head injury.In Nellore district's Guduru, clashes followed allegations that TDP supporters obstructed YSRCP candidates.At the Eluru zilla parishad office, two persons allegedly snatched and tore the nomination papers of YSRCP candidate Maddula Ratnam before being apprehended by police. In Bestavaripeta in Markapuram district, TDP leaders were accused of tearing the nomination papers of a BJP MPTC candidate, triggering a confrontation.The YSRCP alleged that its candidates were being prevented from reaching nomination centres while several senior leaders were placed under house arrest. Those reportedly confined to their residences included MPs Gurumoorthy and Avinash Reddy, former MLAs Kethireddy Pedda Reddy, Thopudurthi Prakash Reddy and Kethireddy Venkatarami Reddy, former minister Sake Sailajanath, former Chittoor MLA Chevireddy Bhaskar Reddy and his sons, and former Pattikonda MLA Sridevi. Restrictions were also reported against YSRCP leaders in Tirupati and Nellore.Former minist                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    < <                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       