tha reaches out to road accident victimsThe Hans Indiathehansindia.comhttps://www.thehansindia.com/news/cities/visakhapatnam/hm-anitha-reaches-out-to-road-accident-victims-1134829engIndiaø€[[[[[\Home Minister Vangalapudi Anitha during shifting of the injured victims to the hospital in Visakhapatnam on ThursdayVisakhapatnam: Home Minister Vangalapudi Anitha demonstrated kindness by reaching out to accident victims.On Thursday, the Home Minister provided immediate help to two students who were seriously injured in a road accident along the BRTS road near Arilova Health City in Visakhapatnam.Anitha reached out to the accident victims while proceeding to Payakaraopeta via the BRTS road. When she noticed the accident where a four-wheeler hit a two-wheeler, injuring the students. She immediately stopped the convoy and took steps to shift the injured students to the hospital.Later, the Home Minister directed the doctors to provide quality treatment to the students and instructed the police to take legal action against the driver of the four-wheeler that caused the accident.Anitha's humanitarian gesture garnered appreciation from various quarters.   D D                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          õ9!5k#-Å' ≥Y95155663162026-10-22T22:25:56ZHeroin worth Rs 60 crore seized, seven arrestedThe Pioneerdailypioneer.comhttps://dailypioneer.com/delhi/heroin-worth-rs-60-crore-seized-seven-arrestedengIndiaø‡ÒThe Delhi Police has busted an alleged inter-State heroin manufacturing and supply network spanning Delhi, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Jharkhand, arresting seven persons and recovering more than 8 kg of the contraband worth around Rs 60 crore in the illicit market.The operation has led to the arrest of an alleged raw opium supplier from Jharkhand's Naxal-affected Chatra district, allegedly involved in illegal cultivation of poppy on his agricultural land, police said.Police have also seized nearly 3.3 kg of chemicals and other raw materials used in heroin manufacture, Rs 12.81 lakh in cash, three SUVs, a motorcycle and equipment allegedly used in production of the contraband.Investigation has revealed that raw opium was allegedly sourced from Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh, processed into heroin at an illicit manufacturing unit in Lucknow and supplied through a network operating across Delhi-NCR and other States, police said.The operation began on September 16 when a Delhi Police team, acting on specific inputs, intercepted an SUV in Sector 32 of north-west Delhi's Begumpur and apprehended Laxman Hooda, 58, who had allegedly arrived to deliver a heroin consignment. Police recovered 300 grams of heroin and Rs 3 lakh from the vehicle, which was seized.The next day, police apprehended an alleged supplier, Anil alias Bhola, 51, from Sonipat in Haryana and recovered 501 grams of heroin from his SUV.Anil has been previously involved in 12 criminal cases and was arrested in a narcotics case registered at Bhalswa Dairy police station in 2025. He allegedly failed to surrender after being granted interim bail and was subsequently declared a proclaimed offender by a court, police said.Further investigation, aided by technical surveillance and human intelligence, led the team to a heroin manufacturing facility in Lucknow, where Bablu, 35, was apprehended on October 4.The raid resulted in the recovery of 6.275 kg of freshly manufactured heroin, along with 2.5 kg of sodium, 787 grams of acetic anhydride and equipment, including a gas cylinder, mixer-grinder, tub, utensils, an electronic weighing machine and other material allegedly used in the manufacturing process.Acting on Bablu's disclosures, police traced and apprehended Ruksar Ali alias Raju, the alleged owner of the manufacturing facility, from Bareilly in Uttar Pradesh, officials said.On October 6, the team arrested Ajaj Ahmed, 38, from Bareilly with the help of technical surveillance. He allegedly supplied crude opium to Ruksar Ali. Police recovered 501 grams of heroin and a Royal Enfield motorcycle from him.The investigation subsequently led to the arrest of Mohammad Azhar, 20, from Badaun in Uttar Pradesh on October 16. He allegedly supplied heroin and crude opium to Ajaj Ahmed. Police recovered 551 grams of heroin, Rs 9.81 lakh in cash and an SUV from him.The final link was traced to Chatra district of Jharkhand, where Prakash Kumar, 31, was arrested on October 18. He allegedly supplied raw opium to the accused and was involved in illegal cultivation of opium poppy on his agricultural land, police said.With these arrests, police claimed to have dismantled the alleged network spanning raw opium cultivation, procurement of raw materials, heroin manufacturing and distribution.    u Ée u                                                                                                       †9!!5Y!] æM95155138222026-10-22T21:12:57ZAll Apps on GTA 6 Phone and Their UsesBeebombeebom.comhttps://beebom.com/all-gta-6-phone-apps/engIndia?ø In GTA 6, the phone is no longer an in-game menu to receive calls and messages. Rockstar Games is turning the phone into a physical device that Jason and Lucia pull out of their pockets and use in person. With a fully functional GTA 6 phone, you might wonder what apps are available on it.Well, GTA 6 previews shared with content crea   $ê !5Ç13ÇO öE95155377722026-10-22T21:45:32ZMumbai Western Express Highway Tragedy: Teenager Dies In Jogeshwari Motorcycle Crash, 31-Year-Old Killed In Bandra CollisionFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-western-express-highway-tragedy-teenager-dies-in-jogeshwari-motorcycle-crash-31-year-old-killed-in-bandra-collisionengIndiaø⁄⁄⁄⁄⁄⁄€Police are investigating two fatal motorcycle-related crashes on Mumbai's Western Express Highway that claimed the lives of a teenager and a 31-year-old man | AI Generated Representational ImageMumbai, October 22: Two people, including a 15-year-old boy, died in separate accidents on the Western Express Highway in Jogeshwari and Bandra.Teenager Dies In Jogeshwari CrashIn Jogeshwari East, Mohammad alias Shah, 15, died after a motorcycle carrying three people crashed into a divider between Metro pillars 720 and 721 near the southbound flyover around 12.15 am on Thursday, October 22.The Jogeshwari police said the 15-year-old rider allegedly lost control while speeding. He and another pillion rider, Ali Ayub, were injured. Following a bystander's call at 12.30 am, police reached the spot. The boys were taken to Trauma Care Hospital, where Shah was declared dead around 12.57 am.The police booked the minor rider and his father, Hayad Khanwani, for allegedly allowing the unlicensed teenager to take the motorcycle. The police said the boy would be produced before the Juvenile Justice Board, while a separate chargesheet would be filed against his father.Motorcyclist Killed In BandraIn Bandra East, Ketan Katariya, 31, died on Wednesday morning after another motorcycle allegedly hit his vehicle from behind near Teachers Colony, beyond the Vakola flyover.Also Watch:Katariya suffered a severe head injury and was declared dead before admission to Sion Hospital. His brother, Ashwin Walji Katariya, 34, identified the body. The Kherwadi police booked Noman Sayyad, 25, who sustained minor leg injuries, for alleged rash and negligent riding and served him a notice.äz!5Å'-Ås ëY95155384182026-10-22T21:46:56ZKite manja: Hubballi woman dies after sharp string slits throat on roadDeccan Heralddeccanherald.comhttps://www.deccanherald.com/india/karnataka/38-year-old-hubballi-woman-dies-after-kite-string-slits-throat-4191982engIndiaø¡ëëëëëëHubballi: A 38-year-old woman died after a kite manja cut her throat while she was riding a scooty near Shivashankar Colony on Karwar Road in Hubballi on Thursday.. The deceased, Vidya Manjunath Goudar, was working as a lab technician,police said..Intelligent traffic management at 14 junctions on cards in Hubballi-Dharwad. The incident occurred while she was on her way to work. The manja string got entangled around her neck, causing her to lose control of the two-wheeler and fall to the road.. She suffered excessive bleeding and died before she could be taken to a hospital, the police added.. Police Commissioner Bhushan Borase stated that those who use manja threads would be booked for endangering public life..Farmers reject CM D K Shivakumar's appeal to withdraw protest, to continue 'Hubballi Chalo'. Special teams have been formed to remove manja thread hanging from trees and electric poles, as they are a threat to the life of bike riders and pedestrians, he said.. Citizens are requested to inform '112' if they find hanging manja threads or someone flying kites with them, the commissioner said.    tors detailed apps for social media, vehicle theft, fast travel, fitness tracking, entertainment, and vehicle delivery. Yes, your in-game phone in GTA 6 does more things now. In this guide, learn about all the apps on the GTA 6 phone and what each does.Full GTA 6 Phone Apps ListPlenty of apps have already been revealed through the GTA 6 extended look, trailers, and creator previews. Some exclusive interviews also confirm certain mechanics, confirming the legitimacy of the apps.All Confirmed GTA 6 Phone AppsNow that you know about all the apps in brief, here is a full breakdown of each of them so you know what to look for in your GTA 6 phone:WAINK Vehicle ScannerWAINK is one of the most useful phone apps for players who enjoy stealing cars in GTA 6. When you approach a parked vehicle, WAINK can scan it and provide information before you decide whether to steal it. The app can identify whether the vehicle is locked, whether it has an alarm or tracker, and provide information about its value.It can also show the vehicle's registration cost and potential resale information. The app therefore gives players more information before committing to a car theft, especially when avoiding tracked or expensive vehicles.SnapmaticSnapmatic app from GTA 5 returns, but its role is different in GTA 6. Jason and Lucia can browse the feed and follow accounts, allowing them to keep up with activity happening around Leonida. The game also uses social media posts as part of the wider story.However, Jason and Lucia cannot publicly upload their own photos. Rockstar explained that the pair are hiding from authorities and do not want to leave a digital trail. They can still send photos to each other privately. It is important, given that you must work for that relationship in GTA 6.Ryde Me / RideMeFast travel in GTA 6 is possible thanks to the ride-hailing (taxi) service app on the phone. Players can book a ride and talk to the driver during the journey. Rides can also be shared, allowing other passengers to join the trip and interact with the player, including strangers.Fitness AppThe extended look at GTA 6 already showed how weight mechanics, gym, and food choices work. Looking at all the GTA 6 screenshots, we can understand that both Jason and Lucia will have to maintain their body fat for different types of attributes. That is where a fitness app comes into play.Confirmed through the creator previews, there will be a proper fitness app on the GTA 6 phone. It will also track how well the protagonists sleep. The information is also tied to the game's tiredness system.Rockstar explains that fatigue can affect how certain attributes regenerate. This gives the phone a practical role in tracking the characters' physical condition.On DemandOn Demand is an entertainment feature on the phone used for podcasts and shows. As per reports, Rockstar had a dedicated team working on the in-game entertainment content. These shows might be available through the On Demand app.It gives the characters access to entertainment while moving around the GTA 6 map. The same phone system also includes creator-safe music.Scooter BrosJust like a taxi app in GTA 6, the phone also includes a private car app called Scooter Bros. The service can deliver a personal vehicle to the player, giving Jason or Lucia another way to access their rides without manually searching for them.BuckMeBuckMe is the game's digital banking app. It is a part of the GTA 6 money system. It allows players to manage money that they deposit rather than carrying all of their cash physically.In GTA 6, money exists in separate forms, wi                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ◊ ◊                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ñ&"!5Åw13Ç= ¶{95155095922026-10-22T21:07:28ZMaharashtra Tragedy: Alibag Couple Found Dead In Khalapur Gorge After Scooter Plunges Off Mumbai-Pune Highway | VIDEOFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/maharashtra-tragedy-alibag-couple-found-dead-in-khalapur-gorge-after-scooter-plunges-off-mumbaipune-highway-videoengIndiaø——————“An Alibag couple, Chaitali Tandel, 23, and Prashant Tandel, 36, were found dead in a gorge nearly 20 feet below the Mumbai-Pune highway near Khalapur after going missing while returning from the Ekvira Devi temple. Police suspect a scooter malfunction may have caused the crash. An accidental death investigation is underway.Navi Mumbai, October 22: A couple from Alibag was found dead in a gorge in Khalapur on Thursday, a day after they went missing while returning from a visit to the Ekvira Devi temple.Their bodies, along with their scooter, were found in thick bushes nearly 20 feet below the road near the Saymal village turn in Khalapur taluka, Raigad district.Couple Went Missing After Temple VisitThe deceased have been identified as Chaitali Prashant Tandel (23) and her husband, Prashant Ravindra Tandel (36), residents of Sakhar Koliwada in Akshi, Alibag.According to preliminary information provided to the police, the couple left Lonavala on their Suzuki Burgman scooter around 10.30 am on October 21 after visiting the temple. However, they did not return home, prompting their family members to search for them.The family subsequently shared their last mobile phone location with the police. With assistance from the police and HELP Foundation, a search operation was conducted, leading to the discovery of the couple's bodies at the accident site on Thursday.Scooter Suspected To Have Plunged Into GorgeAccording to the police, Prashant was riding the scooter with Chaitali seated behind him when the vehicle is suspected to have developed a mechanical problem near the Saymal village turn on the Mumbai-Pune highway.He reportedly lost control of the scooter, which veered off the road and plunged into the gorge.Couple Declared Dead At HospitalBoth sustained serious injuries in the accident. They were taken by ambulance to the municipal hospital in Khopoli, where doctors examined them and declared them dead on arrival.The complaint was lodged by Chaitali's sister, Lina Waghmare (36), a staff nurse residing in Karanjade, Panvel.Also Watch:Khopoli Police Register Accidental Death Reports"We have registered an Accidental Death Report (ADR) in both the death cases, and further investigations are underway," said Sachin Hire, police inspector at Khopoli police station.The police registered the ADRs under Section 194 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, and are investigating the circumstances surrounding the accident.   2  ﬁ2                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      â)$!5Å #-ÅC é95154717342026-10-22T20:17:18ZMasked men shoot dead daily wager in Tarn Taran - The TribuneThe Tribunetribuneindia.comhttps://www.tribuneindia.com/news/amritsar/masked-men-shoot-dead-daily-wager-in-tarn-taran/engIndiaøÀõõõõõõA daily wager was shot dead by two masked men in Naushehra Pannuan town late last evening. The deceased has been identified as Kuldeep Singh (45).Kuldeep was returning home after work with his brother, Baj Singh, when he stopped at a shop on his way to his village to get a haircut.Two men arrived on a motorcycle. While one stayed beside the vehicle, the other went inside and asked who Manpreet Singh Batua's father was. Kuldeep Singh identified himself as Manpreet's father.After confirming his identity, the masked man opened fire at him with a pistol.The victim's brother, Baj Singh, could do nothing to save him. After the shooting, both accused fled on their motorcycle. The Sarhali police have registered a case under Sections 103(1) and 3(5) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) and Sections 25, 27, 54 and 59 of the Arms Act.Superintendent of Police (Investigation) Riputapan Singh said teams had been formed to identify the accused.ê#!5Å#-ÅW úE95154787542026-10-22T20:26:48ZChandigarh University student assaulted, bike taken away - The TribuneThe Tribunetribuneindia.comhttps://www.tribuneindia.com/news/chandigarh/chandigarh-university-student-assaulted-bike-taken-away/engIndiaø∑A second year MBA student of Chandigarh University was thrashed with baseball bats and sticks by a group of 15-16 assailants and his bike was taken away by them in full public view near Chai Aroma Cafe in front of Omega City in Kharar on Wednesday around 1am.The injured Ayush Dwivedi has sustained serious head injuries and is admitted to a hospital.The City Kharar police station have registered a case against the unknown youths who came in three vehicles and have started investigation.In his statement to the police, Ayush Dwivedi said that last night around 1 am, he along with his friends Ayush Rohela and Arnav Jain were standing near Chai Aroma Cafe on his Bullet motorcycle and were about to go towards the flat of his friend Yash who lives in GBP Crest. During this time, a black jeep passed by them at a high speed. After some time, a white coloured car without a number plate came and stopped there. Seven to eight youths got out of the car, armed with sticks and baseball bats, and attacked them.His friend Ayush Rohela fled the scene, while Arnav Jain stepped aside in fear.Ayush told the police that shortly after, two other vehicles arrived at the scene. One was a Thar and the other a black SUV. Eight to ten youth, armed with sticks, attacked him and threatened to kill him.According to the victim, the baseball hit his head during the attack, causing severe bleeding. To save his life, he abandoned his motorcycle and hid in a nearby building under construction. The attackers searched for him for a long time but then fled in their vehicles. The victim alleges the attackers also took his motorcycle.The police registered a case against unknown accused persons under Sections 115(2), 126(2), 351(2), 191(3), 190, and 303(2) of the BNS on October 21 and initiated further investigation.   © ©                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               úT%!5Å#-Å[ µ'95154651182026-10-22T20:09:22Z17-year-old boy shot dead in Chandigarh; revenge suspected - The TribuneThe Tribunetribuneindia.comhttps://www.tribuneindia.com/news/chandigarh/17-year-old-boy-shot-dead-in-chandigarh-revenge-suspected/engIndiaø‘TTTTTTPolice personnel at the crime scene in Sector 22, Chandigarh, on Thursday.A 17-year-old boy was shot dead at point-blank range by three motorcycle-borne assailants in full public view in Sector 22 on Thursday evening. The police suspect the killing was the result of an old rivalry between two groups of teenagers.The deceased, identified as Natik, a resident of Sector 22, was travelling in an auto-rickshaw with a friend when the incident took place. Two other persons, including the three-wheeler driver, were also injured.According to the police, the incident occurred around 9.28 pm near Sanatan Dharma Mandir in Sector 22-B. Natik was shot in the chest. Despite being injured, he ran towards the temple, but found its gate locked. He eventually collapsed near a shop. The injured were rushed to Government Multi-Speciality Hospital, Sector 16, where Natik was declared brought dead.Video 'triggers' attackAccording to the police, Natik and his friends had been involved in a rivalry with another group for the past two years. On Thursday, the two groups allegedly clashed in Sector 44. One of the accused reportedly uploaded a video of the altercation on Instagram.Following the clash, Natik's group took an auto-rickshaw and dropped off a friend before heading towards Sector 22. The rival group followed them and opened fire when the three-wheeler slowed down in traffic outside the temple.Onlookers alerted the police and called an ambulance. Two rounds were fired.The police initially suspected a gang rivalry but later focused their investigation on a dispute between two groups of school-going friends. Two minors, who were friends of Natik, were brought in for questioning at the Sector 22 dispensary. Their statements reportedly helped the police establish the background of the rivalry and the earlier clash in Sector 44.The weapon used in the crime had not been recovered till the filing of this report. No arrests had been made, although the police said they had identified suspects."The case clearly points towards teenage rivalry. The two groups have been fighting for the past two years, and they had an altercation in Sector 44 today. Thereafter, the rival group decided to take revenge. No arrests have been made so far, but we have narrowed down the suspects," a senior police officer said.The police said all those involved were reportedly minors. Investigators were also examining whether the group had contacted contract killers or gang members, although the police maintained that the incident appeared to stem from a personal rivalry among teenagers.Past shooting incidentsIn March, property dealer Charanpreet Singh, alias Chinni, was shot dead near a gym in Sector 9 by two motorcycle-borne men. The police subsequently alleged in a chargesheet that a woman had orchestrated the killing over a land deal.In June, Janki Das, a cashier at a medical store in Sector 11, was shot dead at point-blank range. Two masked men fired 13 rounds in broad daylight and fled the scene with an accomplice waiting on a motorcycle.Last December, Bishnoi gang associate Inderpreet Singh, alias Parry, was shot dead inside his car near the Sector 26 timber market. A Facebook post claimed responsibility for the killing.In September 2024, a bystander was killed near the Sector 17 market when four assailants opened fire about 100 metres from the police station.    R e R                                                                      ê'!5Å!1CÇ= õ95154565632026-10-22T20:00:42ZThree sentenced to 20 years for gang-raping woman on pretext of song shootThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/chandigarh/three-sentenced-to-20-years-for-gang-raping-woman-on-pretext-of-song-shoot/articleshow/135127151.cmsengIndiaøƒîîîîîïMohali: An additional district and sessions court has sentenced three men to 20 years' imprisonment for gang-raping a woman artist after allegedly luring her with the promise of a song shoot involving a Punjabi singer in 2022. The convicts were identified as Jaswinder Singh alias Jelly,Deepak Kumar and Gurwinder Singh alias Manna. Each was sentenced to 20 years' imprisonment and fined Rs 50,000 under Section 376D. The court also awarded them seven years' imprisonment and a fine of Rs 2,000 under Section 394, and five years' imprisonment and a fine of Rs 8,000 under Sections 366 and 120B. In case of non-payment of the fines, the convicts will undergo an additional three months' imprisonment.According to the complaint lodged with Majri police, the woman, an artist, received a message on Oct 12, 2022, asking if she would participate in the shooting of a Punjabi singer's song. She initially declined to travel to Sector 43, Chandigarh, but later agreed when the person who had contacted her arrived at her residence to pick her up.During the journey, she allegedly overheard him speaking on the phone about picking up other girls.When she asked about their destination, she was told they were going to collect more girls from Atipur.Near Atipur, two men on a motorcycle allegedly stopped their vehicle, took its keys and snatched her mobile phone. One of the accused allegedly threatened her with a knife before all three sexually assaulted her. She also alleged that the accused repeatedly choked her and covered her mouth during the assault.After examining the evidence and hearing arguments from both sides, the court convicted the three men and sentenced them to imprisonment under the relevant sections of law.è&!5Åe#-Ç ô%95154621322026-10-22T20:06:03ZSector 23 burglary case cracked in Chandigarh; 3 arrested with jewellery worth over Rs 25 lakh - The TribuneThe Tribunetribuneindia.comhttps://www.tribuneindia.com/news/chandigarh/sector-23-burglary-case-cracked-in-chandigarh-3-arrested-with-jewellery-worth-over-25-lakh/engIndiaø––––––œThe Chandigarh Police have arrested three persons, who were allegedly involved in a burglary at a Sector 23 house, and recovered gold and silver jewellery, besides cash and some documents from them.The accused have been identified as Basant, alias Bashu (27), a resident of Dadumajra Colony, Sector 38 (West); and Vikas (25) and Akash, alias Buchi (25), both residents of EWS Flats, Maloya.According to the police, the burglary took place at a Sector 23 house of Siddharth Gulati on October 20 night.The accused made off with gold jewellery, cash and documents. Gulati caught Basant on the spot, while Vikas and Akash fled with the loot, which was valued at over Rs 25 lakh.A case was registered at the Sector 17 police station on October 21 under Sections 305, 331(4), 3(5) and 317(2) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) following Gulati's complaint.A team led by sub-inspector Suneel Kumar, in-charge of Sector 22 police post, arrested Basant and recovered a part of the loot from him.Vikas and Akash were also arrested the same day.The recovered items include gold bangles, a ring, earrings, two pendants and a necklace set, besides five pairs of silver anklets, about Rs 6,200 cash, and documents such as a driving licence and an Aadhaar card. The police also seized a Pulsar motorcycle, a hammer and a pair of pliers allegedly used in the crime.Basant had a case against him in 2018 at the Sector 5 police station, Panchkula, under Sections 147, 148, 149 and 307 of the IPC. Vikas and Akash have no criminal record. All three have been sent to judicial custody. Further investigation is on.   } ©}                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 à))!5Å1'-Ç å 95154520092026-10-22T19:53:48ZBengaluru mob attack: Man beaten after being mistaken for phone thief in RT StreetDeccan Heralddeccanherald.comhttps://www.deccanherald.com/india/karnataka/bengaluru/bengaluru-man-mistaken-for-phone-thief-beaten-by-mob-at-rt-street-4192026engIndiaøΩ"Bengaluru: City Market police have registered a case after a 19-year-old man was allegedly mistaken for a mobile phone thief and beaten by a mob at RT Street on October 19, officials said on Thursday.. The incident occurred around 7 pm when the victim, Shahid, was riding a two-wheeler with his friend, Fardeen Pasha. According to the FIR, they hit an unidentified man..Bengaluru physicist Ashoke Sen becomes first Indian to win Oskar Klein Medal. When Pasha picked up a fallen mobile phone to return it to the man, those gathered at the spot mistook Shahid for a thief and assaulted him.. Someone then called the 112 emergency helpline. Police took Shahid to a hospital for treatment and subsequently registered a case. Investigation is ongoing, police said.íT(!5ÅS13Ç †95154536972026-10-22T19:56:11ZNavi Mumbai Tragedy: 17-Year-Old Boy Dies After Speeding Trailer Runs Over Scooter Near APMC MarketFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/navi-mumbai-tragedy-17-year-old-boy-dies-after-speeding-trailer-runs-over-scooter-near-apmc-marketengIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿThe APMC police have registered a case against a trailer driver after a collision near Annapurna Chowk claimed the life of a teenager travelling with his father | AI Generated Representational ImageNavi Mumbai, October 22, 2026: A 17-year-old boy was crushed under the rear wheels of a speeding trailer after it rammed into the scooter he was travelling on with his father near Annapurna Chowk in the APMC Market area on Wednesday evening. The boy's father was thrown onto the roadside in the impact, while the teenager died of his injuries.Teenager Identified As Mankhurd ResidentThe deceased has been identified as Ajay Jaggu Chavan, a resident of Sathe Nagar in Mankhurd. According to the police, Ajay was travelling to Vashi with his father, Jaggu Sardar Chavan, on a Honda Activa scooter.Trailer Rams Into Scooter From BehindThe two were heading from Orange Circle towards Turbhe Naka when the accident occurred near the Annapurna signal and traffic police chowky in the APMC Market area.A speeding trailer approaching from behind rammed into their scooter, throwing Jaggu Chavan onto the roadside. Ajay fell beneath the trailer's rear wheels and sustained critical injuries.Doctors Declare Boy Dead At HospitalPolice personnel rushed to the spot and took Ajay to the Navi Mumbai Municipal Corporation hospital in Vashi, where doctors declared him dead."The trailer rammed into the scooter from behind, causing the teenager to fall under its rear wheels. He sustained fatal injuries and was declared dead at the hospital. We have registered a case against the trailer driver, and further investigation is underway," a police officer said.Heavy Vehicles Raise Safety ConcernsThe incident has once again raised concerns over the safety risks posed by heavy vehicles moving at high speeds in the busy APMC Market area.Also Watch:APMC Police Begin InvestigationThe APMC police have registered a case against the trailer driver under relevant sections of law. Assistant Police Inspector Sunil Mohite is investigating the case.    Ö  Ö                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           êx*!5Å%Åu ùo95154509272026-10-22T19:52:24ZPromising Indian sprinter Dondapati Jayaram dies in road accidentThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/sport/promising-indian-sprinter-dondapati-jayaram-dies-in-road-accident/article71612145.eceengIndia?¿êêêêêèJayaram along with Malay Barik, another athlete, was going to Kataka for Dussehra celebration by bike on Wednesday evening when the accident occurredIn a tragic road accident, Dondapati Mrutyum Jayaram, a promising athlete who brought laurels to the country at the national and international levels, died in a road accident near Cuttack late on Wednesday (October 21, 2026) evening.Jayaram, along with Malay Barik, another athlete, was travelling to Cuttack to celebrate Dussehra when they reportedly lost control of their motorcycle and crashed into a road median. Doctors at SCB Medical College and Hospital in Cuttack declared both of them brought dead.Originally hailing from Kakinada, Andhra Pradesh, he lived in Bhabanipatna, Kalahandi district, Odisha. He trained at the Odisha Reliance Foundation Athletics High Performance Centre in Bhubaneswar under coaches Rohit Mane and Martin Owens.A promising talent in the 100-metre and 200-metre sprints and the 4√ó100-metre relay, Jayaram has represented Odisha's junior and senior teams and India's Under-20 men's team. The departed athlete won one silver and one bronze medal in the 4√ó100m relay and the 100m sprint, respectively, in the 4th South Asian Junior Athletics Championship, held at the Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium in Chennai from September 11-13, 2024.Besides, he was part of the Indian men's 4√ó100m relay team that won the bronze medal with a national record of 40.01 seconds in the 21st Asian Junior (U-20) Athletics Championships at the Dubai Police Stadium in Dubai on April 27, 2024.Recently, he had won one silver and one bronze medal in men's 200m and 100m run respectively at the 6th Indian Open U-23 athletics competition held Sawai Mansingh Stadium, Jaipur, October 16-18, 2026.Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi condoled death athletes saying their untimely passing was a profound loss to Odisha's sporting fraternity.    ∆  ∆                                                                                                                                                                                            û7+!5Å)EÉS ∂]95154449152026-10-22T19:44:00ZUltraviolette launches X-47 Venom electric motorcycle at Rs 2.65 lakhEconomic Timeseconomictimes.indiatimes.comhttps://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/auto/two-wheelers-three-wheelers/ultraviolette-unveils-revolutionary-x-47-venom-electric-motorcycle-priced-at-rs-265-lakh-with-cutting-edge-vx-100-platform/articleshow/135126899.cmsengIndia?∆ñññññöUltraviolette has launched the X-47 Venom electric motorcycle at an introductory price of Rs 2.65 lakh. Bookings for the motorcycle began on October 22, with expected deliveries starting in November 2026. The X-47 Venom features advanced battery technology and motor capabilities for enhanced performance and safety. Additionally, it comes with innovative rider safety vests that offer significant protection.Electric two-wheeler maker Ultraviolette on Thursday launched the X-47 Venom electric motorcycle at an introductory price of Rs 2.65 lakh, while unveiling its new VX-100 100V platform.Bookings for the motorcycle opened on October 22 at 4 pm, with deliveries scheduled to begin in November 2026. The introductory price applies to the first 5,000 customers, the company said in a press release.The X-47 Venom is the first motorcycle built on the new VX-100 architecture and features the company's newly developed UV LIGHTFURY motor and SRB-11 battery technology.The motorcycle has an IDC range of 343 km, a peak power output of 30 kW (40 hp) and a top speed of 155 kmph. It can accelerate from 0 to 60 kmph in 2.7 seconds and from 0 to 100 kmph in 5.9 seconds. The company said the motorcycle weighs 180 kg, up to 20 kg less than the previous generation.The X-47 Venom supports 12 kW DC fast charging, which Ultraviolette described as a first for an Indian electric two-wheeler. It also features a 1.6 kW onboard charger, cruise control and a seven-inch TFT LCD touchscreen.Its safety and rider-assistance features include UV Hypersense radar intelligence, blind-spot monitoring, lane-change assistance, overtake alerts and rear-collision warnings. The motorcycle also comes with an integrated front and rear dashcam, park assist and upgraded navigation integrated with Mappls.The newVX-100 platform incorporates SRB-11 battery technology, which the company said offers up to 20% higher energy density and twice the cooling performance. Its thermal management system is designed to dissipate heat up to 50% faster.The battery pack includes a pyro-fuse designed to isolate the circuit within microseconds when a critical fault is detected, alongside a battery management system that monitors cell voltage, temperature and current.The motorcycle's UV LIGHTFURY motor is designed to reduce weight and energy losses while improving power density. Its next-generation motor control unit is twice as compact and offers three times the power density, according to the company.Alongside the motorcycle, Ultraviolette introduced B-MAX, a reusable rider safety vest designed to provide protection to the collar, back, chest, sides and hips. The company said the vest offers 86% force attenuation and can be reused up to five times.The X-47 Venom also features VIOLETTE A.I. connectivity functions, including movement, fall and towing alerts, remote lockdown and crash alerts. Ultraviolette said the motorcycle offers extendable warranty coverage of up to 8 lakh km.The company plans to launch the X-47 Venom in Europe on November 3 at EICMA 2026 in Milan, Italy.Narayan Subramaniam, CEO and co-founder of Ultraviolette, said the VX-100 platform would provide a technology foundation for a new generation of products across segments and markets.Niraj Rajmohan, CTO and co-founder of the company, said the new architecture, battery technology, motor and motor control unit had been developed together to improve power delivery, efficiency, thermal performance and safety.   £ 	*£                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       â-!5Å1CÇ çC95154439172026-10-22T19:42:43Z33-year-old scooterist killed as taxi hits him from behindThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/gurgaon/33-year-old-scooterist-killed-as-taxi-hits-him-from-behind/articleshow/135126950.cmsengIndiaø‘‘‘‘‘‘‘Gurgaon: A 33-year-old private company employee died after a commercial taxi hit his scooter from behind near Maharana Pratap Chowk late Wednesday. The driver fled after the crash, police said.The deceased, Praveen, who was a resident of Ashok Vihar in the city, was critically injured in the accident and was taken to a hospital by the cops where doctors declared him dead.Police said they received a call around 9:30pm and a team from Sector 17/18 police station reached the spot and found the man was already dead.Police found a card on the body with his personal details. "We are trying to contact the family," an officer said.A case would be registered after the family is contacted and an autopsy is conducted. Police said they are working to identify the taxi and its driver and analysing CCTV footage from the surrounding area to zero in on the man.çS,!5q1CÇ ó95154439242026-10-22T19:42:43ZTwo men fire shots at retired Sub-Inspector's homeThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/gurgaon/two-men-fire-shots-at-retired-sub-inspectors-home/articleshow/135126931.cmsengIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿGurgaon: Two men fired shots at the house of a retired Haryana Police sub-inspector in Nagla Enclave Part-II, Faridabad around 2am Thursday, while his family was asleep inside.CCTV footage of the incident shows the two men approaching the house on foot, opening fire and fleeing on a motorcycle. It recorded one of the men, wearing a blue T-shirt with a yellow cotton towel wrapped around his head, pulling out a gun and firing first towards the house. The other man, dressed in a white shirt, then took out a firearm and attempted to fire. After a brief pause, the man with the towel steps back and fires again before discharging a third shot into the air.One bullet hit the wall, and a windowpane was shattered. CCTV footage also shows the man in the white shirt picking up spent bullet casings from the ground and putting them in his pocket before the duo fled.The house belongs to Surjeet Bainsla, a retired sub-inspector of Haryana Police, who lives with his family. Bainsla retired in 2023. "In the CCTV footage installed at the house, he found two men firing outside and did not recognise either of the men and had no knowledge of who they were or why they targeted his house," he said.The incident has raised questions about the motive behind the firing, particularly as the retired officer has denied knowing the attackers.Police have registered a case. "Efforts are being made to identify the two men and establish the reason behind the firing," they said.   Ê ÜÊ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          è/!5Å#1CÇ; ô/95154439142026-10-22T19:42:39ZSchoolkids shoot rivals in Sec-22 after brawl; one killed, another criticalThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/chandigarh/schoolkids-shoot-rivals-in-sec-22-after-brawl-one-killed-another-critical/articleshow/135126955.cmsengIndiaø‹\\\\\]Chandigarh: Three juvenile gunmen on a motorcycle fired at a group of minors in Chandigarh's Sector-22 late Thursday night, killing one of them and critically injuring the other. An autorickshaw driver was also injured.SSP Kanwardeep Kaur said everyone involved -- victims and shooters -- are school students. Three suspects were detained less than an hour after the shooting, said the SSP. The deceased was identified as 17-year-old Naitik, a resident of Sector 22.According to police, both groups earlier studied in the same school but the victims had recently joined a school in Sector-32. The two groups brawled in Sector 34 around 10.15pm. Some of them took videos of the bashed up boys and put it on Instagram to humiliate them.The ones who ended up facing the brunt of the fistfight returned armed with pistols and went looking for the other group. They found some of them driving home in an autorickshaw around 11.15pm, and chased them through traffic, say police.At Sector 22, the trio caught up with the auto and started shooting at the boys at point-blank range just outside a temple. Devotees and passersby scattered in panic and the gunmen sped away amid the chaos.Two teenagers and the auto driver lay slumped, struck by bullets.A police patrol rushed to the spot and took the duo to PGIMER, where one of them died. He had been shot in the chest.Police cordoned off the area and collected forensic evidence. Checkpoints were set up and police teams fanned out looking for the assailants. Around midnight, police rounded up three suspects. An old rivalry is believed to have triggered the violence.äw.!5s1CÇ ëE95154439222026-10-22T19:42:43ZSnatchers target two; flee with gold chain, earringThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/chandigarh/snatchers-target-two-flee-with-gold-chain-earring/articleshow/135126935.cmsengIndiaø∆ñññññöChandigarh: Two snatching incidents were reported in the city over the past 24 hours, with two-wheeler-borne miscreants fleeing after targeting pedestrians in Sector 37 and Mauli Jagran.In the first incident, a woman was targeted while on an evening walk near a gurdwara in Sector 37. An unidentified man riding a Honda Activa snatched a gold earring from her right ear before escaping. The Sector 39 police station team responded to a call from the victim's son, Harsimran Singh of Sector 37-C. The victim told police that the snatcher had covered his face, preventing her from noting the scooter's registration number.In the second case, Surjit Kumar of Vikas Nagar, Mauli Jagran, was walking near mandi ground when two youth on a motorcycle forcibly intercepted him. The duo threatened him at knifepoint, snatched his gold chain along with a locket, and sped away. Kumar was also unable to record the bike's licence plate.Mauli Jagran police arrived at the scene after receiving a call and recorded the victim's statement. Investigators are scanning CCTV footage from both crime scenes to identify the suspects.   ! •!                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ç1!5Å=%Ç? ï	95154314982026-10-22T19:26:39ZMTC bus driver sentenced to four years in prison for causing two deaths in 2017 accidentThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/chennai/mtc-bus-driver-sentenced-to-four-years-in-prison-for-causing-two-deaths-in-2017-accident/article71612162.eceengIndiaø‘TTTTTTA court has sentenced a 56-year-old Metropolitan Transport Corporation (MTC) bus driver to four years in prison and imposed a fine of ‚Çπ11,000 for causing the deaths of two 20-year-old men in a road accident in Ayanavaram in 2017.On the night of September 24, 2017, one Mani was driving an MTC bus at high speed and in a rash and negligent manner from east to west at the junction of K.H. Road and Somasundaram Street in Ayanavaram. The bus rammed into a two-wheeler that was proceeding in the same direction on the road.The two-wheeler riders, R. Manikandan, 20, and S. Tamil Arasan, 20, died on the spot. A case was registered at the Kilpauk Traffic Investigation Wing police station in connection with the accident.After completing the investigation, the police filed a final report before the Sixth Metropolitan Magistrate Court in Egmore, where the case came up for trial.Following the conclusion of the trial, the court delivered its verdict on Wednesday holding Mani guilty of the charges.The court sentenced him to six months' imprisonment and imposed a fine of ‚Çπ1,000 under Section 279 of the Indian Penal Code (IPC) for rash driving. Under Section 304(A) of the IPC, he was sentenced to four years' imprisonment for each of the two deaths and fined ‚Çπ10,000.The court ordered that all the sentences run concurrently.ÜX0%5Å+/ÅY â=b-95154421862026-10-22T19:40:14ZOdisha: Two athletes die as bike hits road divider on NH-16Millennium Postmillenniumpost.inhttps://www.millenniumpost.in/nation/odisha-two-athletes-die-as-bike-hits-road-divider-on-nh-16-680691engIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿBhubaneswar: Two promising young athletes from Odisha have died after their motorcycle hit a road divider on NH-16 between Cuttack and Bhubaneswar, police said on Thursday.The deceased have been identified as Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati (21) and Malaya Barik (20).They were returning to the Kalinga Stadium in Bhubaneswar after witnessing Durga Puja celebrations in Cuttack when the accident took place around 11 pm on Wednesday, police said.The two athletes were rescued by police and locals and taken to SCB Medical College and Hospital in Cuttack, where doctors declared them dead, they added.   µ µ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           íH2!5Å''Åc °95154263212026-10-22T19:20:00ZHarley Davidson stock hits 52-week high at 28.87 USD By Investing.comInvesting.cominvesting.comhttps://www.investing.com/news/company-news/harley-davidson-stock-hits-52week-high-at-2887-usd-93CH-4967217engIndia?·ÒÒÒÒÒÚHarley Davidson stock reached a new 52-week high, climbing to $28.87, reflecting a positive momentum in the market. The stock's performance has been particularly strong in recent months, with a year-to-date gain of 36.81% and a six-month return of nearly 21%. According to InvestingPro analysis, the stock remains undervalued relative to its Fair Value, placing it among opportunities on the platform's most undervalued stocks list. This milestone underscores investor confidence in Harley Davidson's strategic initiatives and market performance, despite the challenges faced in the broader economic landscape. InvestingPro Tips highlight that management has been aggressively buying back shares, further demonstrating confidence in the company's future. The company's ability to achieve this 52-week high is a testament to its resilience and adaptability in a competitive industry. For investors seeking deeper insights, HOG is among the 1,400+ US equities covered by comprehensive Pro Research Reports, offering expert analysis and actionable intelligence.In other recent news, Harley-Davidson reported second-quarter 2026 results that surpassed expectations, with notable achievements in both profit and revenue. The company announced that North America retail sales increased by 3%, while global retail sales saw a 1% rise. Despite a 6% decline in consolidated revenue to $1.227 billion, Harley-Davidson's core motorcycle business experienced a 6% revenue increase, reaching $1.1 billion. The firm also raised its full-year operating income guidance for its motorcycle and financial services divisions. DA Davidson responded to these strong results by raising its price target for Harley-Davidson shares from $30 to $33, maintaining a Buy rating. Meanwhile, Raymond James estimated a 5% year-over-year increase in U.S. retail sales for the third quarter of 2026, marking the fourth consecutive quarter of positive growth. Additionally, a regulatory filing revealed that Director Daniel Nova purchased nearly $1 million worth of Harley-Davidson stock, further signaling confidence in the company's prospects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          ìm3!5Å 1CÇ £95154252682026-10-22T19:18:12ZTeen tortured, stripped, tonsured over car damage; 6 arrestedThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/hyderabad/teen-tortured-stripped-tonsured-over-car-damage-6-arrested/articleshow/135126639.cmsengIndiaø‚222222Hyderabad: The Golconda police have arrested six people for allegedly harassing, assaulting, humiliating and attempting to kill a 19-year-old, after he failed to pay for damage to a rented car.The prime accused, Ibrahim Ali Khan, and the five others were remanded in judicial custody on Oct 21, said Syed Faiz, assistant commissioner of police (Golconda).Police said they received a complaint on Oct 18 from Arbaz Khan, an intermediate student, who alleged that he had rented a self-drive car for a day about five months ago. When the vehicle was returned, its owner, Ibrahim Ali Khan, found minor damage to the car's body."Ibrahim demanded that Arbaz get the damage repaired. When he failed to do so even after a week, Ibrahim began pressuring him to get the work done and also demanded that he pay rent for using the car for another week," a Golconda police official said.On Oct 18, after Arbaz failed to meet Ibrahim's repeated demands, two men on a motorcycle -- identified as Fardeen and Khurram, alleged accomplices of Ibrahim -- intercepted him around 2 am, while he was on his way to a medical store.. "They first forced Arbaz to transfer Rs 1,500 to Ibrahim and then took him to Ibrahim's office in Gulshan Colony, where he was threatened and tortured," the official said.In his complaint, Arbaz alleged that the accused initially beat him with sticks and then forced him to strip and dance naked.He was further humiliated when the accused allegedly measured his penis and cut his hair. He was subsequently taken to a salon, where his head was shaved, police said.The teenager also alleged that the accused attempted to attack him with a stone.Police said the accused confined Arbaz at Ibrahim's office throughout the night before releasing him at around 11 am on Oct 18."On reaching home, Arbaz's family members asked him about his absence and the injuries he had sustained. He then narrated how the car owner had tortured him for failing to pay for the vehicle's repairs," the police official said.Based on Arbaz's complaint, police registered a case under Sections 109 (attempt to murder), 308(5) (extortion) and 351(2) (criminal intimidation) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS). Further probe in underway, cops said.   f 	éf                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          ä%5!5{1CÇ	 ê95154205352026-10-22T19:12:05ZDaily-wage worker run over by road roller, dies in PuneThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/pune/daily-wage-worker-run-over-by-road-roller-dies-in-pune/articleshow/135126559.cmsengIndiaøﬁﬁﬁﬁﬁﬁ›Pune: A 32-year-old daily-wage worker died after being run over by a road roller at Kharabwadi in Khed taluka on Tuesday afternoon.Police identified the deceased as Kailas Kokare, a native of Hingoli district. The North Mahalunge police have registered a case of causing death by negligence against the road roller operator.An officer from North Mahalunge police said Kokare was working as a helper to the road roller operator. "On Tuesday afternoon, the operator had brought the road roller to a construction site in Kharabwadi to perform a puja on the occasion of Dussehra. While turning it, the operator failed to notice Kokare, who was standing behind it, and ran over him. Kokare died on the spot."In another accident, 44-year-old Ankush Pandhare of Alandi died after an unidentified vehicle hit his motorcycle. The accident occurred on Wednesday afternoon while Pandhare was riding towards Sarkar Chowk from PCM Chowk. The Alandi police have registered a case of causing death by negligence against the unidentified driver.åo4!5y1CÇ ï-95154205412026-10-22T19:12:08ZYouth flees after taking lift, man suspects cash theftThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/lucknow/youth-flees-after-taking-lift-man-suspects-cash-theft/articleshow/135126514.cmsengIndiaøƒîîîîîïLucknow: A 55-year-old employee of a glass shop allegedly lost part of Rs 1.35 lakh he was carrying to deposit in a bank after giving a lift to an unidentified youth on his motorcycle near the Vijaypur traffic signal in Vibhuti Khand on Thursday, police said.The complainant, Gomti Prasad, a resident of Rahim Nagar, told police he was heading to the AU Small Finance Bank branch at Husadiya in Patrakar Puram with the cash on behalf of his employer. Prasad said he has worked at Dream Beavers, a glass shop, for around 15 years.According to the complaint, around 1 pm an unknown youth with a bag approached Prasad near the Vijaypur signal and asked for a lift, calling him "uncle". Prasad agreed and the youth rode pillion, placing his bag across both their laps during the ride.Prasad alleged the youth repeatedly pressed the side of the bag in which the cash was kept, prompting him to cover the pocket containing the money. Shortly after, the youth allegedly jumped off the moving motorcycle, causing Prasad to fall and the cash to scatter on the road.Prasad said labourers and a nearby street vendor helped him collect the notes. He later suspected a portion of the money was missing and reported the matter to police. Vibhuti Khand police have begun inquiries and are trying to identify the suspect. The amount allegedly stolen is yet to be determined.   8 ≠8                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            är7!5Å%Ç ë;95154202612026-10-22T19:11:53ZTwo men returning from Mysuru Dasara die as bike hits electric poleThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/bangalore/two-men-returning-from-mysuru-dasara-die-as-bike-hits-electric-pole/article71613037.eceengIndiaø∆ñññññöTwo men returning from Mysuru after attending the Dasara festivities died after their motorcycle allegedly rammed into a roadside electric pole near Mylasandra Junction in east Bengaluru's Kengeri on Friday.The deceased have been identified as Rajath, 21, a resident of Goraguntepalya who ran a grocery shop, and Nagendra, 20, a native of Shivamogga. Nagendra, a friend of Rajath, had come to Bengaluru in search of a job.The incident unfolded around 2.30 a.m., according to the police. A preliminary police probe revealed that eight people on four two-wheelers had travelled to Mysuru to watch the Dasara festivities.While returning home around 2.40 a.m., Rajath, who was riding the motorcycle, allegedly lost control, hit the pavement and crashed into the electric pole near Mylasandra Junction.Overspeeding suspectedPolice said that Rajath died on the spot, while Nagendra, who was riding pillion, sustained severe injuries. Although the latter was rushed to a nearby hospital, doctors declared that he was brought dead. Kengeri police suspect that they were overspeeding. A case has been taken up.éP6!5]1CÅk ô-95154205402026-10-22T19:12:05Z4 held, minor detained for Baner robberyThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/pune/4-held-minor-detained-for-baner-robbery/articleshow/135126508.cmsengIndiaø–PPPPPPPune: The Baner police have arrested four youths and detained a minor on the charge of robbing a cybersecurity analyst of cash and gold jewellery, collectively worth Rs 1.22 lakh, on Pan Card Club Road in Baner on Oct 1.Four days later, members of the gang robbed a cab driver of cash and a cellphone, together worth Rs 12,000, under Pashan-Sus bridge. A case has been registered with the Bavdhan police.Police said the 32-year-old analyst had arrived in the city from Kolhapur in the early hours of Oct 1, when four men intercepted him on two-wheelers. They snatched his gold chain and a gold-plated bracelet worth Rs 1.03 lakh, forced him to transfer Rs 19,000 via UPI to two bank accounts, and fled the spot.After he approached the police, assistant inspector Ganesh Raikar launched an investigation. "We examined CCTV footage and noticed the suspects fled through Katraj-Dehu Road bypass, which doesn't have very good CCTV coverage," Raikar said.They combed through 225 CCTV recordings and traced the suspects' movements to an eatery in Khed-Shivapur. A minor was seen accompanying the four men. The police subsequently took Parage, a Dhayari resident, into custody in Bavdhan. Under questioning, he revealed the names of his accomplices -- Dhayari residents Aditya Kolkar (18) and Vishal Zodge (18), and Sahil Margale (19) of Kolhewadi. "We have taken all of them into custody," Raikar said. Margale has a criminal record.Raikar said the two bank accounts were held in other states and that the suspects transferred the money to a gaming app. They have recovered some cash and a two-wheeler from the suspects.    ‹ Ã ‹                                                                                                                                                                                                                èm9!5Å!1CÇ1 ö[95154065082026-10-22T18:56:44ZSpeeding SUV rams parked sedan, injures newspaper vendor; owner flees spotThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/bhopal/speeding-suv-rams-parked-sedan-injures-newspaper-vendor-owner-flees-spot/articleshow/135126287.cmsengIndiaø⁄ZZZZZZBhopal: A 36-year-old newspaper vendor suffered a severe fracture in his left leg after a speeding SUV rammed into a parked sedan, pushing it into his scooter while he was arranging newspapers in DK-2 Danish Kunj under Kolar police station limits around 5am on Thursday. The collision also damaged another scooter parked alongside his vehicle.The incident was captured on CCTV footage from a shop opposite the accident spot. The footage purpotedly shows the SUV driver, two men and a woman passenger getting out of the vehicle and leaving the scene after the crash.According to the complaint, the driver abandoned the black SUV and fled. The injured hawker also alleged that the driver was under the influence of alcohol.Around 5am on Thursday, he was loading newspapers onto his scooter when the SUV approached from the Jain temple side at high speed and allegedly rammed into a parked sedan. The impact pushed the sedan into Malviya's scooter and another two-wheeler parked beside it, damaging both and injuring his leg under the left knee badly.Malviya's colleague, Gaman, took him to a private hospital, where he was undergoing treatment when police recorded his statement in the emergency ward around 9am.His associate Amit told TOI that Malviya underwent a surgery at another private hospital.Kolar police registered a case under section 281 and 125 (a) of the BNS for rash and negligent driving and an act endangering life and public safety. Police are investigating the crash and the allegations against the driver.Kolar SHO Sanjay Soni said that the damaged SUV was seized by police. Search was on to nab the SUV driver who fled the spot after the incident. Further investigations are on.é18!5Å9%Ç= óo95154130872026-10-22T19:03:45Z21-year-old arrested for murdering wife, dumping body in stormwater drain in BengaluruThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/bangalore/21-year-old-arrested-for-murdering-wife-dumping-body-in-stormwater-drain-in-bengaluru/article71613005.eceengIndiaø÷÷÷÷÷÷◊The police have arrested a 21-year-old man for allegedly murdering his wife and disposing of her body near a stormwater drain off Gopalapura Main Road in West Bengaluru.The accused has been identified as Mohammad Izar, a native of Bihar, who allegedly killed his wife, Ruksana Khatun, 25. The incident came to light on October 13, when a beat police officer found Ruksana's decomposed body near the drain.An investigator in the case said that they launched investigations to identify the body. "When we were inquiring about any possible missing persons in the locality, a resident revealed that Izar's wife had not been seen in the area for some time. When Izar was questioned, he lied, saying that she had gone to her native place," the officer said.However, when asked to contact her, Izar gave various reasons, raising suspicions. Subsequent investigations revealed that he had allegedly murdered Ruksana.According to the police, the incident occurred on October 10. Izar reportedly suspected that his wife was having an affair with another person. The couple allegedly fought over the issue at their house, and the argument escalated, ending with Izar smashing Ruksana's head with a stone."He then wrapped her body in plastic covers, transported it on his work scooter to a spot near a stormwater drain and disposed of it," the officer said.Police investigations revealed that Ruksana had divorced her previous husband and met Izar in Bihar. The couple got married about a year ago and moved to Bengaluru.   g ûg                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           í4;!5Å)1CÇ9 üY95153932192026-10-22T18:41:19ZMLC's PA sent to jail after drunk driving spree, delivery boy battles for lifeThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/nagpur/mlcs-pa-sent-to-jail-after-drunk-driving-spree-delivery-boy-battles-for-life/articleshow/135125921.cmsengIndiaø◊◊◊◊◊◊◊Nagpur: The personal assistant (PA) of an MLC known for his influence in eastern Vidarbha, was sent to prison on Wednesday for driving drunk and triggering a series of high-speed collisions, hours after midnight on Dussehra.A 28-year-old delivery boy, Raheel Shakeel Sheikh, suffered critical head injuries in the crash and is battling for life at a private hospital and two vehicles were wrecked in the impact. The neta's PA was driving back to his Godhani home after attending a party, when he rammed a two-wheeler near Samvidhan Chowk. Sheikh, who was on his way to Yashodhara Nagar, was tossed in the air, before falling with a thud near a roadside tree. The family's sole bread earner, Sheikh was rushed to hospital, where doctors say his condition is critical.Instead of pressing on the brakes to help the injured man, the allegedly drunk man drove away at top speed and swerved towards the flyover near Kasturchand Park, where his car crashed into a pickup van, before coming to a halt. The politician's PA was nabbed from the accident spot.The twin collisions could have caused more casualties as the roads were crowded with people and vehicles in the early hours of Dussehra and Dhammachakra Pravartan Din.Rohit Chinchmalkar, the complainant and an eyewitness, told police he too had a narrow escape when the car brushed past him before crashing into Raheel's two-wheeler. Police rushed to the spot and nabbed the accused, who was so intoxicated that he could barely stand. Sitabuldi police took him to a govt hospital, where doctors confirmed alcohol in his blood.A case of rash and negligent driving endangering life, causing injuries through a dangerous act, and failing to stop and assist after an accident was registered along with charges of drunk driving under Motor Vehicle Act.The accused was produced in court on Wednesday and remanded in judicial custody. Sources hinted at political pressure, but presence of multiple eyewitnesses at the accident site and police action put the case back in focus.ä_:%5q+/ÅI ëob-95154051552026-10-22T18:55:06ZSuspicious car parked on Jessore Road sparks alarmMillennium Postmillenniumpost.inhttps://www.millenniumpost.in/bengal/suspicious-car-parked-on-jessore-road-sparks-alarm-680649engIndiaøªKolkata: Tension gripped the Duttapukur area on the night of Vijay Dashami after the state police seized an abandoned vehicle packed with a massive cache of suspected explosives and banned chemicals along Jessore Road in the Tetultala area.The white car that was parked outside a local two-wheeler showroom for two days raised suspicions among local residents who eventually alerted the police. A high-level joint operation was immediately launched, bringing in the state's Special Task Force (STF), the National Investigation Agency (NIA), the National Security Guard (NSG) and the Bomb Disposal Squad. According to police, after inspection of the suspicious substances kept inside the car, the NSG reported that they found no signs of any explosive material so far. Superintendent of Police (SP), Barasat Police District, J Mercy, said they had received the NSG report and were awaiting the results of the forensic examination.The inquiry is ongoing, the SP added. Meanwhile, police are questioning the car's owner, identified as Rakibul Islam, who reportedly owns the two-wheeler showroom in front of which the vehicle was parked.   Ñ Ñ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          öy<!51CÇ ±795153882872026-10-22T18:35:00ZWoman arrested with 32g of synthetic drug in MuvattupuzhaThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kochi/woman-arrested-with-32g-of-synthetic-drug-in-muvattupuzha/articleshow/135125671.cmsengIndiaø’UUUUUWKochi: A 50-year-old woman was arrested with 32g of synthetic drug during an investigation carried out as part of Operation Toofan on Thursday. The arrested person, Minimol of Kothamangalam, had been staying in a rented house in Muvattupuzha.An electronic weighing scale and other materials were recovered from the house. The drug had allegedly been packed and stored in separate packets.Investigators are also probing the person who had been staying with her, as well as the source of the drug and the financial transactions linked to the operation. They are also looking into those who allegedly bought drugs from her.The operation was conducted by a team led by Muvattupuzha circle inspector M S Faisal at the directive of Muvattupuzha DSP K R Manoj. The team included Muvattupuzha SHO Subin Biju, SI R B Roshni, ASIs P S Salim, K M Aneesh and K A Anas and senior civil police officers Varghese Venatt, K Girish Kumar, C A Shiyas, Dayesh, Sreeju Rajan, Sijas and Mithu Mohan.The accused was produced before a court and remanded in custody.Man arrested for chain snatchingVarapuzha Police on Thursday arrested Umesh, 45, of Cheranalloor for allegedly snatching the gold chain of an elderly woman after approaching her on the pretext of asking for directions.The accused, who was staying in a rented house in the Karinngathuruthu area of Alangad, allegedly targeted the 68-year-old woman on Monday morning. Lathika was walking home after visiting a temple when Umesh arrived on a scooter, stopped near her and asked for directions. He then allegedly snatched her two-and-a-half-sovereign gold chain and fled.The police examined CCTV footage while also focusing on people recently released from prison after serving sentences in chain-snatching cases. Officers said Umesh is an accused in chain-snatching cases registered at Hill Palace, Kalady, Mulanthuruthy, Paravur and Elamakkara police stations. He reportedly told investigators that he committed the theft to fund gambling.The stolen chain was recovered from a financial institution in Paravur, where it had allegedly been pledged for Rs 1.5 lakh. The accused was produced before a court and remanded in custody.Police intensify inspections as part of Operation GripKochi City Police intensified inspections and legal action across the city as part of Operation Grip against gangsters and anti-social elements.On Wednesday, the police checked 125 people within the city limits and initiated further action as per law. Twenty people listed under Operation Grip were checked and legal action, including preventive detention, was initiated against seven of them. The police also checked 85 people allegedly involved in anti-social activities or included in the rowdy lists maintained by various police stations. Preventive action, including arrests, was taken against 52 of them.Man arrested for stealing liquor bottles from Bevco outlet in MuvattupuzhaMuvattupuzha Police on Thursday arrested Arun Babu, 31, of Muvattupuzha, for allegedly stealing liquor bottles from the premium counter of the Bevco outlet at Vazhappilly on Tuesday. The accused was produced before a court and remanded in custody.   ﬂ Áﬂ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   å>!5Å)!Ç	 ìe95153851872026-10-22T18:31:49ZMasked men set bike on fire in Delhi's Azadpur village; CCTV captures incidentNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/agency-feeds/masked-men-set-bike-on-fire-in-delhis-azadpur-village-cctv-captures-incident-10393586.htmlengIndiaø—QQQQQRNew Delhi, Oct 22 (PTI) Two masked men allegedly set a motorcycle on fire in Azadpur village here around 5 am, with the blaze spreading to a nearby shop and a house, and CCTV cameras captured the sequence, police said on Thursday.The footage purportedly shows the two accused covering their faces with masks and sheets to conceal their identities. While one of them allegedly kept watch, the other approached the parked motorcycle, took out an inflammable substance from a bag, sprinkled it on the vehicle and set it on fire before fleeing with his accomplice."The fire intensified, and a loud explosion was heard as flames engulfed the motorcycle. The fire spread to a nearby grocery shop, setting sacks kept outside ablaze, and also damaged four outdoor air-conditioning units and electrical wires at an adjoining house," a senior police officer said.Northwest Delhi residents rushed out after hearing the explosion and tried to douse the flames with buckets of water. Police were subsequently informed.Officials are analysing footage the victim and residents handed over to identify and trace the accused. Police registered a case. Preliminary investigation suggests that the incident may have stemmed from personal enmity, a source said. PTI BM ASDé=!5Å	1CÇ ó[95153882782026-10-22T18:34:58ZBiker killed in road crash on highway, Mumbai police file caseThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/mumbai/biker-killed-in-road-crash-on-highway-mumbai-police-file-case/articleshow/135125863.cmsengIndiaø‰ÙÙÙÙÙıMumbai: A 31-year-old motorcyclist died after another motorcycle allegedly hit his vehicle from behind on Western Express Highway near Teachers Colony in Bandra East on Wednesday morning. A police constable who was conducting a roadblock with other personnel on the southbound carriageway after Vakola flyover said members of the public alerted them to the accident. Kherwadi police said the deceased was found with a severe head injury and another motorcyclist with minor leg injuries has been booked for death due to negligence.The accused biker Noman Sayyad (25) allegedly told police that he was travelling from Vakola towards Bandra when his motorcycle struck Ketan Katariya's motorcycle from behind. "Katariya suffered head injury and died at the hospital. Sayyad, who suffered injuries, has been served notice after charges of death due to negligence has been filed against him," said the Kherwadi police officer.Police constable Sunil Bhanudas Nagmal, who was conducting a roadblock with other personnel on the southbound carriageway after Vakola flyover, said members of the public alerted them to the accident.Police found Katariya with a severe head injury and another motorcyclist, Sayyad, with minor leg injuries. Katariya was taken by ambulance to Sion Hospital, where doctors declared him dead before admission. His brother, Ashwin Walji Katariya (34), later identified the body.A complaint was lodged against Sayyad for allegedly riding rashly and negligently and causing Katariya's death.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                ôg?%5Ç1++Ç ≠}b-95153815382026-10-22T18:27:20ZSuspected explosives, banned chemicals found in car in Bengal's Duttapukur; owner arrested | Indiablooms - First Portal on Digital News ManagementIndiablooms.comindiablooms.comhttps://www.indiablooms.com/news/suspected-explosives-banned-chemicals-found-in-car-in-bengals-duttapukur-owner-arrested/detailsengIndiaø”SSSSSTSuspected explosives and banned chemicals were recovered from a car on Jessore Road in Duttapukur, North 24 Parganas, late Wednesday night, prompting a search operation involving the National Investigation Agency (NIA), National Security Guard (NSG), forensic experts and local police.The car's owner, Rakibul Islam, who runs a motorcycle showroom business, has been arrested and is being questioned as investigators examine whether the materials were intended for subversive activities.A senior officer of the Barasat Police District said explosive-like substances and banned chemicals had been found in the vehicle.Officials are conducting further tests to establish the exact nature and potency of the suspected explosives.STF acts on intelligence, vehicle interceptedThe Times of India, citing sources, reported the Special Task Force (STF) had received intelligence about suspicious materials inside a car parked in the Tetultala area of Duttapukur.The STF subsequently kept the vehicle under surveillance before intercepting it on Wednesday night. Rakibul was detained for questioning and later arrested.Investigators suspect the materials may have been intended for transportation to Kolkata, although their intended destination and purpose have not yet been established.The recovered items reportedly included explosive-like substances and iron mesh rods. Forensic examination is expected to determine the composition of the materials and whether they posed an immediate threat.Probe into source of materials, possible linksInvestigators are trying to establish where the materials came from, who may have instructed Rakibul to transport them and whether other individuals were involved.Barasat Police District Superintendent J. Mercy confirmed that the investigation was underway and that the suspected explosives were being examined."The investigation is underway. The nature of the explosives is being examined. The accused has already been arrested. Further details can be provided after the investigation progresses," she said.Past showroom blast under scrutinyPolice sources said Rakibul had reportedly left his car-repair business around a decade ago and subsequently entered the motorcycle showroom business.He currently operates four showrooms in areas including Tetultala and Bira in Duttapukur, as well as Berachampa in Deganga.Investigators are also expected to examine reports of an explosion at a motorcycle showroom in Amdanga, allegedly owned by Rakibul, a few years ago.Whether that incident has any connection to the latest recovery remains unclear.According to Times of India's sources, the car had been parked beside the Road King showroom on Tetultala Road in Duttapukur for the past two days before the operation.The investigation is ongoing, and officials have yet to establish the intended use of the recovered materials or whether the case involves a wider network.   P P                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ì-@!5ÅC1CÇ[ °95153777312026-10-22T18:22:40ZFriend-turned-rival chases, runs over, then beats man to death in Chhatrapati SambhajinagarThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/aurangabad/friend-turned-rival-chases-runs-over-then-beats-man-to-death-in-chhatrapati-sambhajinagar/articleshow/135125503.cmsengIndiaø‹‹‹‹‹‹‹Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar: A friendship that allegedly soured into a professional rivalry ended in a gruesome murder in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar on Thursday, with a man allegedly running over and bludgeoning his friend to death before surrendering to police.The victim, Devesh alias Bunty Dixit (36), died on the spot. The accused, Pawan Parashar (22), a resident of Wankhedenagar, later drove to the Cidco police station and surrendered, police said.Preliminary investigation revealed that Dixit was returning home after a gym session when Parashar allegedly began pursuing him in a car. The chase ended near Mangesh Gas Agency in N-7 Cidco. Police said Parashar allegedly rammed Dixit's two-wheeler from behind with enough force to fling him onto the road. His two-wheeler was thrown nearly 150 feet away.Citing eyewitness accounts, police said the accused took a U-turn after the collision, drove back towards the injured Dixit, stepped out of the car and repeatedly struck him on the head with a stick and an iron rod he had carried with him."After the collision, the accused took a U-turn, drove back to the injured man, got out of the car and repeatedly attacked him on the head with a stick and an iron rod," said Cidco inspector Atul Yerme.Dixit succumbed to the injuries on the spot before any medical help could reach him. The killing triggered panic in the locality, with passersby and shopkeepers gathering at the scene. Senior police officers, including deputy commissioner of police (Zone II) Ratnakar Navale, visited the spot.Police suspect the crime stemmed from a fallout between the two men."The accused, after surrendering before the police, claimed that he and the victim used to work as bouncers for different bars. He was upset due to their friendship turning into a rivalry," Navale told TOI.He said police teams were cross-verifying the accused's version and probing the exact motive behind the murder.Inspector (Crime) Gajanan Kalyankar said investigators were questioning Parashar to establish the complete sequence of events and ascertain the circumstances that led to the killing.   ‰ ‰                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          òA!5Å95Åo ¨95153774762026-10-22T18:22:28ZUltraviolette makes a dent in premium EV motorcycle segmentThe New Indian Expressnewindianexpress.comhttps://www.newindianexpress.com/business/2026/Oct/22/ultraviolette-makes-a-dent-in-premium-ev-motorcycle-segmentengIndia?¢ Niraj Rajmohan, founder and CTO of the company, says the technologies being developed by the Bengaluru-based company were designed to have a lifespan of nearly 10 yearsUltraviolette Automotive Pvt Ltd has made a dent in the premium electric motorcycle segment with its technology, which is designed to last nearly a decade, said Niraj Rajmohan, founder and CTO of the company.Speaking to TNIE on Thursday, Rajmohan said the company was the world's fastest-growing premium motorcycle manufacturer and expected the electric motorcycle market in India to continue expanding rapidly."In Europe, I was asked about our strategy to grow overall sales because we have now become the biggest manufacturer of premium motorcycles. Over the past few years, electric motorcycles have grown more than twofold in India. I expect similar growth over the next 36 months, and we are geared up to be a frontrunner in this space. We have been able to make a dent in the premium EV motorcycle segment because of our cutting-edge technology," he said.Rajmohan said the technologies being developed by the Bengaluru-based company were designed to have a lifespan of nearly 10 years.Founded in 2015, Ultraviolette has invested nearly Rs 500 crore in research and development and sold more than 7,000 electric motorcycles globally, he said.The company will showcase its latest motorcycle, the X-47 Venom, at the EICMA International Motorcycle Exhibition in Milan, Italy, in November 2026, and launch it in global markets.Ultraviolette has also begun construction of a manufacturing plant in Hosur, Tamil Nadu, as part of its global expansion plans. The facility, involving an investment of Rs 779 crore, is expected to have an annual production capacity of 2.5 lakh electric motorcycles, which the company plans to scale up to 5 lakh units over the next five years. Southern Europe and South America are among its target markets.The company recently introduced the VX-100, its new 100V platform, and unveiled the X-47 Venom, the first motorcycle built on the architecture. The platform will also underpin future products, including the Tessaract and Shockwave.Powered by the VX-100 architecture and SRB-11 battery technology, the X-47 Venom is designed to offer higher speeds, greater range, faster charging, lighter subsystems and quicker acceleration. It also supports 12 kW DC fast charging.Ultraviolette CEO and co-founder Narayan Subramaniam had previously told TNIE that the company's ability to develop advanced technology was strengthened by its talent pool, which includes professionals from the aviation industry and companies such as Tesla and Rivian Automotive.Bookings for the X-47 Venom opened on Thursday, with the motorcycle priced at Rs 3 lakh. The first 5,000 customers will receive a discount of Rs 35,000.   ˝ ˝                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ö B!5a75ÅQ ∞+95153756802026-10-22T18:20:07ZAther faces capacity test as rivals expandThe Financial Expressfinancialexpress.comhttps://www.financialexpress.com/business/news/ather-faces-capacity-test-as-rivals-expand/4367372/engIndia?Æ Ather Energy's ability to keep pace with the fast-growing electric two-wheeler market will depend on how quickly it can expand production, as rising demand and longer delivery times create an opportunity for established rivals to gain ground.The company's market share fell to 14.8% in September from 18.2% in January, even as electric two-wheeler penetration rose to 11.6%, pointing to the challenge of converting demand into sales in an increasingly competitive market.Ather's immediate constraint appears to be production rather than a lack of demand. The company produced 31,000 units in June against a monthly capacity of around 35,000 units. Chief Executive Tarun Mehta had said during the Q1 investors' call that the company was approaching full capacity utilisation even as demand exceeded supply. Ather estimated that it could have sold an additional 13,000-15,000 scooters a month during the quarter if production had been sufficient. Dealer inventory has fallen from 14 days to just three days, while waiting periods have stretched to two months or more in some markets.The company is expanding its manufacturing operations through its Aurangabad Industrial City facility in Maharashtra, which is expected to take its total annual installed capacity to 920,000 units. The facility, however, is scheduled to become operational towards the end of 2026. This could limit Ather's ability to capitalise fully on the festive-season demand, when customers typically prefer immediate deliveries.Industry experts said some buyers may turn to alternatives if waiting periods remain long, although the extent of any customer shift will depend on how quickly supply improves.Competitors are expanding capacity to meet the growing market. TVS Motor is raising its electric two-wheeler production capacity from around 40,000 units a month to more than 50,000, while Bajaj Auto has reached 50,000 units for its Chetak scooter and is working towards 60,000. Hero MotoCorp has increased its electric vehicle capacity to nearly 30,000 units a month and is targeting 45,000 by the end of FY27. In September, TVS and Bajaj accounted for 26.1% and 23.4% of electric two-wheeler registrations, respectively. Hero, which holds a 32.8% stake in Ather, accounted for another 11.7%."Today, nobody waits. There are dozens of products from established players. A supply shortage at this point means Ather will lose more market share," an industry expert said.Beyond capacity, Ather's supplier base and product mix could influence how quickly it responds to demand. Smaller vendors may offer less scale in procurement than the established manufacturers, while the company has discontinued three variants of its 450 range as it prioritises production of its higher-volume Rizta scooter. Such choices could help streamline production, though a narrower range may limit options for some buyers. Ather's challenge is to improve supply without losing the product differentiation that has helped it build demand. A query sent to the company remained unanswered till the time of going to the press.   q q                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       èC!5Å)#'Ç ô[95153722142026-10-22T18:15:58ZMan crushed to death by ex-BJP leader's Audi after argument over honking in UPIndia Todayindiatoday.inhttps://www.indiatoday.in/cities/other-cities/story/up-aligarh-audi-incident-man-run-over-after-honking-dispute-3023136-2026-10-22engIndiaøﬂﬂﬂﬂﬂﬂ‡A man died after an Audi allegedly struck his motorcycle and ran over him following a honking dispute in Aligarh. Police seized the car and began examining CCTV footage as the family alleged a deliberate attack.An alleged dispute over honking and passage on the road took a deadly turn in Uttar Pradesh's Aligarh, where a man named Manoj died after an Audi car allegedly rammed his motorcycle and ran over him. The incident took place at around 11 pm on October 20 in the Bannadevi police station area. The victim's family has alleged that Manoj was deliberately run over following the argument, while an injured eyewitness has also described the collision as intentional.According to Manoj's family, an argument broke out between the occupants of the Audi and the motorcycle riders over honking and the passage of vehicles. The family alleged that the Audi subsequently hit Manoj's motorcycle from behind. After Manoj fell on the road, the car allegedly ran over him, killing him.Kanhaiya, who was riding pillion on Manoj's motorcycle, was injured in the incident. According to Aligarh SP City Aditya Bansal, Kanhaiya told the police that the collision was deliberate and that the Audi ran over Manoj after he fell.POLICE EXAMINE CCTV FOOTAGE, SEIZE AUDIThe police have secured CCTV footage related to the incident and seized the Audi for a technical examination. A field unit has also collected evidence as part of the investigation.The victim's family has claimed that the Audi belongs to Chaudhary Devaraj Singh, a former BJP district president. The police have identified the driver and formed teams to arrest the accused.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ô^D!5w1CÇ# Æw95153620112026-10-22T18:04:41ZUltraviolette eyes Europe expansion with Venom launchThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/ultraviolette-eyes-europe-expansion-with-venom-launch/articleshow/135124737.cmsengIndia?∆ñññññöBengaluru: Ultraviolette on Thursday launched its X-47 Venom electric motorcycle as it prepares to expand its European presence and increase monthly motorcycle sales from around 700 to 1,000 in the first quarter of 2027.The Bengaluru-based company will introduce the Venom in Europe on Nov 3 at the EICMA motorcycle exhibition in Milan. It already exports to 20 European countries, including Germany, France, Italy and the UK. Europe accounts for roughly 10% of its current sales, the company said.The Venom is priced at Rs 2.6 lakh, ex-showroom Bengaluru, for the first 5,000 customers. The starting price will rise to Rs 3 lakh thereafter. Bookings opened on Thursday. The model is an updated version of the X-47 Crossover.The launch comes as Ultraviolette broadens its product portfolio, expands its distribution network and adds manufacturing capacity. Beyond Europe, it plans to enter the US in 2027 and is exploring opportunities in Latin America and Southeast Asia.Domestic expansion will accompany the overseas push. CEO and co-founder Narayan Subramaniam told reporters on Thursday that the company plans to expand its retail network from around 50 locations to 100 by the first quarter of 2027.With additional products, including the Shockwave motorcycle and Tesseract scooter, it is targeting sales of around 10,000 vehicles a month by this time next year.This broader target goes beyond the near-term increase expected from its motorcycle business as the company prepares to enter the electric scooter market. The planned additions will expand its portfolio across sports, crossover and street-and-dirt motorcycles, as well as scooters.Ultraviolette raised $85 million in September in a funding round led by Yali Capital and TDK Ventures, with participation from Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan. The funds are intended to support manufacturing capacity, new electric vehicle platforms and international expansion.The company has also announced plans to invest Rs 779 crore over five years in a new factory in Hosur, Tamil Nadu. The facility is designed to ramp up to an annual capacity of 2.5 lakh vehicles in phases. It will manufacture the Tesseract scooter and future products, alongside the company's existing Bengaluru operations.The Venom is the first motorcycle built on Ultraviolette's VX-100 platform, which combines new battery, motor and control systems. The architecture can accommodate different battery capacities and power outputs, allowing the company to extend it across future models and markets.Subramaniam described VX-100 as establishing "a technology foundation for a new generation of products across segments and markets". The company developed the platform as it prepared to expand beyond its existing motorcycle portfolio.Founded in 2016 by Subramaniam and Niraj Rajmohan, Ultraviolette counts TVS Motor, Qualcomm Ventures, Zoho and Lingotto among its investors. Its existing motorcycle portfolio includes the F77 range and X-47 Crossover.(With inputs from agencies)    ¶ Ä ¶                                                                                                                                                          èWF!5Å 1CÇ ö]95153620082026-10-22T18:04:39ZExtortion bid behind firing at immigration firm, shooter heldThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/ludhiana/extortion-bid-behind-firing-at-immigration-firm-shooter-held/articleshow/135124781.cmsengIndiaøÂuuuuuvLudhiana: Less than two weeks after bullets were fired at an immigration consultancy in the upscale Model Town Extension area, Ludhiana police have arrested one of the alleged shooters and claimed the attack was linked to an extortion bid orchestrated from abroad.Police said the firing was allegedly carried out on the directions of Varinder Charan, a Rajasthan resident, and Jagjit Singh alias Gandhi of Butahari village, both of whom are currently based overseas. Investigators claim the duo had demanded extortion money from the owner of the immigration firm and ordered the attack after their demand was allegedly refused.The case was registered at Model Town police station on Oct 11 on the complaint of Bhanu Ahuja, a resident of Haibowal Kalan, after two unidentified assailants opened fire at the office.Police said the investigation led to the identification of Deepak Kumar and Gagandeep, a resident of Seelampur in Delhi, as the alleged shooters. Deepak has now been arrested, while Gagandeep remains absconding.Police said Deepak was produced before a court and remanded to police custody. The motorcycle allegedly used in the attack has also been recovered.Officials added that raids are being conducted to apprehend the second accused and that further action is being initiated against the alleged masterminds operating from abroad.Investigators said Deepak, who studied up to Class X, does not have any previous criminal record.The firing had triggered concern among immigration consultants in the city, a sector that has increasingly come under the scanner amid extortion and gangster-linked threats in recent years. Police maintain that the remaining accused would be arrested soon.é}E!5y1CÇ ôE95153620012026-10-22T18:04:39ZMan wanted in assault case held after police encounterThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/varanasi/man-wanted-in-assault-case-held-after-police-encounter/articleshow/135124879.cmsengIndiaø‚222222Varanasi: Azamgarh police on Thursday arrested a wanted accused after an encounter in the Jiyanpur police station area near a culvert on the Amma Aima Mor-Dhanchhula road.The accused, identified as Ankit Yadav, a resident of Mau district, was wanted in connection with a murderous assault case reported at Chauko Bazaar.According to reports, Ankit opened fire on a police team after being surrounded during a checking and search operation.In retaliatory firing by police, he sustained a bullet injury in his left leg. He was arrested and taken to the district hospital for treatment.Police recovered a .315-bore illegal country-made pistol, two spent cartridges and one live cartridge from his possession.The case relates to an incident reported on Oct 19. Ramprasad Yadav lodged a written complaint at Jiyanpur police station, alleging that due to enmity over refusal to compromise in an old case, 11 named accused, including Satyam Yadav and Ankit Yadav, rammed the motorcycle of Ramprasad and his brother Prashant Yadav, causing them to fall. The accused then allegedly attacked them with sticks and rods with intent to kill. Ramprasad sustained serious injuries.A case under Sections 3(5) and 109(1) of the BNS was registered at Jiyanpur police station.During questioning, Ankit allegedly told police that he had been living in Azamgarh city while preparing for the Army. He said he went to Chauko Bazaar on October 19 after being called by Satyam Yadav, where he and others attacked Ramprasad and Prashant over resentment linked to the old case.CO Sagari Deshraj Singh said further legal action is underway.-- Binay Singh    L  L                                                                  ü1G!5q1CÇ ∫E95153588192026-10-22T18:02:21ZWoman dies after falling off joyride, man criticalThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/delhi/woman-dies-after-falling-off-joyride-man-critical/articleshow/135125040.cmsengIndiaøÕùùùùùúNew Delhi: On Monday evening, 25-year-old Guriya Kumari headed to the Dussehra Ground in Vikaspuri with her family members, excited to try out the new 'mixer ride' at the fair. The joyride, however, turned fatal as the gate gave way while it was in operation, hurling Guriya first onto a generator and then to a metal staircase. While Guriya died, a man was seriously injured.Late Thursday, police arrested Mandeep, owner and operator of the ride, and Ramesh, the supervisor.The incident took place around 1.30am early Tuesday. Guriya's sister, Rinki Devi, alleged the ride kept spinning even after the gate broke, as the operator had gone to watch a Ramlila performance. "They kept stuffing people into the ride and started it before we could even stand properly. After four-five rotations, as the ride started gaining speed, the gate suddenly opened and my sister fell off," she said.Claiming there were no ambulances at the fair, Rinki said she and her other sister, Gunja Devi, rushed Guriya to a private hospital in an e-rickshaw. "She had to sit curled up in a fetal position during the journey due to pain. She pinched my palms and even broke my bangles, begging me to stop the agony," she recalled.Guriya had a fractured neck, blood clots in the chest and a deep wound that split open her forehead, her family said.Rinki claimed the private hospital quoted Rs 6 lakh for treatment, following which they took Guriya to Ram Manohar Lohia Hospital, where no bed was available. Two days later, Guriya succumbed to her injuries at Lady Hardinge Hospital.Originally from Bihar's Darbhanga, Guriya had come to Delhi barely six months ago in search of work and was employed as a domestic help. She was a resident of Kaali Basti in Uttam Nagar."My daughter used to support us by sending money back home. I wanted her to get married this year, but she wanted to save money for us before looking for a husband," said her father, Suresh Mahto, who suffers from heart disease and is unemployed.During their last conversation, on a video call, Guriya told her father about the "perfect girl" for her younger brother. "She kept telling me, 'we'll discuss this when I come back home for Chhath'," he added.After her death, Guriya's family marched to the fair and demanded that the organiser stop the event. They were allegedly driven out of the fair as a dandiya programme was about to begin. A video circulating on social media shows the fair's organiser, Sunil Jindal, claiming the victims suffered minor injuries and were fine."While I was receiving my daughter's dead body, people were singing, dancing and enjoying themselves at the fair. How can the organiser continue to run programmes at the same place even after such an incident?" said Mahto.Ravi, the other person who fell from the ride, sustained injuries to his head, neck and waist, and remains critical. According to his family, he was discharged from RML Hospital after doctors said he was fine, despite being unable to walk or speak. Ravi has since been admitted to the ICU of a private hospital, they said.Ravi, who runs a small motorcycle repair shop alongside his family's departmental store, had gone to the fair on the insistence of a friend. He had taken the same ride a day before the accident as well.The injuries have left his family in distress. Ravi's repair shop, which is now shut, supported his three children and his wife, who has been admitted to RML Hospital for the past two weeks due to paralysis on the left side of her body."He couldn't even recognise us after being hospitalised as he was injured in the head," said his mother, Madhu Devi. Ravi has shown some signs of responsiveness since then, she added, saying he now nods his head and moans in pain.   + +                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 õRH!5Å91CÇG ±w95153588242026-10-22T18:02:21ZStopped 42 times for no PUCC, BMW top violator; 2-Wheelers Among Main Repeat OffendersThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/delhi/stopped-42-times-for-no-pucc-bmw-top-violator-2-wheelers-among-main-repeat-offenders/articleshow/135124731.cmsengIndiaø»òòòòòóNew Delhi: Despite GRAP-I curbs invoked and a valid pollution under control certificate (PUCC) made mandatory, some motorists in the city have been keeping the challan printers busy, turning repeat offending into a remarkably persistent habit.The top violator is a 2019-model BMW, whose compliance record is far from premium. Since 2019, its driver has received 42 challans for driving without a valid PUCC, including 24 this year alone. The vehicle's PUCC has remained expired since 2024.With the capital struggling to breathe, one would imagine that at some point the owner might have driven to an authorised pollution-testing centre instead of risking another penalty. Apparently, that thought has yet to catch on.The law, meanwhile, is crystal clear. Section 190(2) of Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 mandates that every vehicle must meet prescribed emission standards and carry a valid PUCC issued by an authorised testing centre under Central Motor Vehicles Rules, 1989. New vehicles are required to get a PUCC one year after registration. Older vehicles must renew it every six months -- or even every three months in the case of high-polluting vehicles, depending on fuel type and local rules.The BMW that piled up 42 PUCC breaches is not alone in this dubious race. The next four spots on Delhi's repeat-offender list belong to two-wheelers, showing that the problem is not restricted to luxury cars or their owners.A 2023-model Suzuki motorcycle has accumulated 33 PUCC challans, 29 of them this year. It finally has a valid certificate, but only after repeated reminders from the enforcement system. An Activa has clocked 32 challans, including 26 in 2026, yet its PUCC remains expired. A 2012-model Ace has been challaned 28 times while a 2025-model TVS Raider has 24 challans, all recorded this year. Both still have expired certificates.While compliance eventually arrives, for some, it seems to take a remarkable number of nudges.Delhi Traffic Police said repeated violations were treated as habitual rather than accidental. "Vehicle owners are equally responsible for ensuring valid PUCC. Cases with more than 10 pending PUCC challans reflect a clear disregard for the law. Cases where an immediate challan is not possible are pursued through courts," a traffic police officer said.The pollution check certificate confirms that emissions meet applicable limits. Yet, the scale of repeat violations raises questions about whether issuing challans alone is enough to get motorists to comply.According to transport expert Anil Chhikara, awareness of vehicle-related legal requirements remains uneven. He argued that some owners were unfamiliar with PUCC and insurance obligations, and that govt messaging about pollution prevention had not reached everyone on the ground. The 'no PUCC, no fuel' policy, he said, could force more motorists to obtain certificates.Chhikara also cautioned against treating the absence of a valid certificate as proof that a vehicle's emissions exceed prescribed limits. "A physical emissions test is needed to establish whether exhaust emissions breach the standards," he said, adding that testing and enforcement need to be effective on the ground.   Á Á                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             úI!5Å'-Åo ¥/95153522172026-10-22T17:55:00ZUltraviolette unveils VX-100 platform, launches X-47 VenomDeccan Heralddeccanherald.comhttps://www.deccanherald.com/business/companies/ultraviolette-unveils-vx-100-platform-launches-x-47-venom-4191963engIndia?¿êêêêêèUltraviolette on Thursday unveiled VX-100, its new 100V platform, and launched the X-47 Venom, the next-generation X-47 Crossover motorcycle and the first model built on the new platform. Going ahead, the Bengaluru-headquartered e-mobility firm plans to expand its portfolio with the Tesseract scooter, Shockwave motorcycle, and a new F77 model.. The X-47 Venom is powered by the VX-100 architecture and SRB-11 battery technology, engineered to deliver higher speed, greater range, faster charging, lighter subsystems and quicker acceleration. The motorcycle is available across India at an introductory ex-showroom price of Rs 2,65,000 for the first 5,000 customers..Ultraviolette Automotive announces five-year investment plan to expand manufacturing base in Karnataka. With an IDC range of 343 km, peak power of 30 kW (40 hp), torque of 550 Nm at the wheel and a top speed of 155 kmph, the motorcycle accelerates from 0-100 kmph in 5.9 seconds. At a kerb weight of 180 kg, it is up to 20 kg lighter than the previous generation. It also features cruise control and UV Hypersense radar-based rider assistance technology.. "At Ultraviolette, design, engineering and technology have always evolved together, each pushing the other to unlock new possibilities. We constantly challenge ourselves to deliver greater performance, build more intelligence into our motorcycles and make every component lighter and more efficient," said Narayan Subramaniam, CEO and Co-founder of Ultraviolette.. "VX-100 is the outcome of that approach, establishing a technology foundation for a new generation of products across segments and markets. The X-47 Venom brings these advances to life," he added.. Niraj Rajmohan, CTO and Co-founder of Ultraviolette, said the motorcycle's architecture, battery technology, lighter motor and next-generation motor control unit had been developed as an integrated system to improve power delivery, efficiency and thermal performance. It supports 12 kW DC fast-charging and features multi-tiered electro-mechanical protection, including a pyro-fuse.. "The X-47 Venom reflects our approach to engineering the entire motorcycle as one integrated system. Each subsystem has been developed in conjunction with the others to improve power density, optimise packaging and reduce weight," Rajmohan said.He added that the company had invested more than Rs 500 crore in R&D efforts over the course of its existence, with most of its technology developed in-house.Ultraviolette plans to introduce new products every quarter, with the Tesseract scooter and Shockwave motorcycle targeted for launch in the first quarter of next year. A new F77 model is also in development, Rajmohan told DH ..Electric bikemaker Ultraviolette secures $45 million capital from Zoho, Lingotto. The company has added a vehicle assembly line and expanded its battery line at its existing Jigani plant in Bengaluru, which can manufacture 50,000-60,000 units annually. It is also investing in a new facility in Hosur, Tamil Nadu, with a planned annual capacity of 5 lakh units. The first phase will have a capacity of 2.5 lakh units. Both plants can manufacture all its vehicles.. Ultraviolette currently operates 55 showrooms and plans to expand its network to 100 by the first quarter of next year, covering major cities and tier-2 towns.   m m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   áJ!5Å 1CÇ# âI95153502572026-10-22T17:52:38Z6 injured as truck rams 4 vehicles on Una-Dharamshala highwayThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/chandigarh/6-injured-as-truck-rams-4-vehicles-on-una-dharamshala-highway/articleshow/135124570.cmsengIndiaø€[[[[[\Shimla: Six people were injured after a truck rammed into four vehicles on the Una-Dharamshala national highway at Kuthiyari in Himachal Pradesh's on Thursday morning.Police said the truck, travelling from Una, first hit a car before colliding with a pickup, motorcycle and scooter, triggering panic at the spot.Police rushed to the scene and shifted the injured to hospital. One person, whose condition was serious, was referred to Regional Hospital, Una, while the remaining injured are being treated at Civil Hospital, Amb. Police have registered an FIR at Amb police station against the truck driver.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      õqK%5ÅY?)Ç# ≤Ab-95153443332026-10-22T17:45:36ZBihar couple's marital dispute ends in murder; husband dumps wife's body in Bengaluru stormwater drainBhaskar Live English Newsbhaskarlive.inhttps://bhaskarlive.in/national/bihar-couples-marital-dispute-ends-in-murder-husband-dumps-wifes-body-in-bengaluru-stormwater-drain-2156138engIndiaø»òòòòòóBengaluru, Oct 22 (IANS) A 22-year-old Bihar native has been arrested on Thursday for allegedly murdering his 25-year-old wife and dumping her body in a stormwater drain on Magadi Road in Bengaluru following frequent quarrels over suspicions of an extramarital relationship. The accused, Mohammed Irfaz, allegedly killed his wife, Ruksana, on October 10. Her body was recovered from the drain on October 13.Both Irfaz and Ruksana hailed from Bihar and had married a year ago. Ruksana had been married earlier and had a child from her previous marriage, but had separated from her first husband.According to the police, the couple fell in love while selling balloons in Bihar. They moved to Bengaluru around six months ago, where Irfaz began working at a garment factory. Ruksana was also employed, but the couple frequently quarrelled.Irfaz allegedly suspected that his wife was involved in an extramarital relationship because she frequently spoke on the phone. The dispute escalated on October 10, when he allegedly picked up a stone and killed her before stuffing a scarf into her mouth.After the murder, the accused allegedly broke the handle lock of an unidentified person's motorcycle and used it to transport the body. He reportedly placed the body in a bag between the motorcycle's handles and pushed the vehicle to the location where he dumped the body in the stormwater drain.The body was discovered on October 13. Initially, the police had no leads, and the woman's identity could not be established.The Magadi Road police subsequently formed more than 10 teams and conducted door-to-door inquiries while gathering information about missing persons.During the investigation, residents informed the police that a man from Gopalapura had reported his wife missing. The police questioned Irfaz, who allegedly claimed that his wife had returned to her native place in Bihar and was not using her mobile phone.Suspecting his account, the police took him into custody for further questioning. During interrogation, he allegedly confessed to murdering his wife, helping investigators crack the case.It can be recalled that Bengaluru Police arrested 32-year-old Sagar Chandra Rawat for the murder of his 28-year-old wife, Anusuya Behara, on August 11.Anusuya Behara (28) and Sagar Chandra Rawat (32) were from Odisha and lived in a rented house near Sampigehalli / MS Nagar in northeast Bengaluru. The couple had a heated argument over financial matters and salary. Rawat allegedly assaulted and strangled Anusuya to death at their home.Rawat kept the body inside the house for three days, wrapped it in a bed/bedsheet, tied it with a rope, and dumped it in an overgrown vacant plot in Agrahara Layout, M.S. Nagar around midnight. He then shifted to stay at the hotel where he worked as a kitchen supervisor.On September 2, 2026, workers clearing the vacant plot under a Greater Bengaluru Authority (GBA) directive found the highly decomposed body. As the body was badly decomposed, identification was difficult. Police traced a clothing tag on the victim to a shopping complex in Bhubaneswar, Odisha, which led them to identify Anusuya and arrest Rawat.Created On : &nbsp 22 Oct 2026 11:14 PM IST                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         õ^L!5S-3ÅW ≥{95153418532026-10-22T17:42:49ZPadmaraonagar Road Remains UnusableDeccan Chronicledeccanchronicle.comhttps://www.deccanchronicle.com/southern-states/telangana/padmaraonagar-road-remains-unusable-1997989engIndiaø¢Residents of Padmaraonagar have sought urgent road repairs after civic works left nearly half the stretch behind Gandhi Hospital damaged and unsafe for commuters.Nearly half of the road along the rear gate of Gandhi Hospital at Padmaraonagar, connecting Secunderabad to Musheerabad, remains damaged months after civic works, causing inconvenience to motorists, particularly two-wheeler riders.Residents alleged that the road was not properly restored after the repair works, leaving a significant portion of the stretch unusable. They sought permanent repairs, usable footpaths and regular maintenance, particularly along the route towards Musheerabad crossroads.Sriharsha Tulasi, an IT employee and a Secunderabad resident, said several roads in the locality required immediate attention, including Musheerabad Road towards Gandhi Hospital, Padma Rao Nagar T-junction and the road behind the hospital."Following municipal works carried out a few months ago, the road was not properly carpeted or restored, leaving approximately 50 per cent of the road surface unusable. This has made commuting difficult and poses safety risks, especially for two-wheeler riders," he said.Sriharsha said potholes and damaged road surfaces were affecting commuters across the locality. "Safe road infrastructure is as important as responsible driving. This is not about blaming any individual or department, but about highlighting a genuine public concern that requires timely intervention. Residents of Secunderabad deserve safe, motorable roads," he said.Another resident, Aravind Ramchander, said he had repeatedly raised complaints about damaged roads at Prajavani meetings and submitted photographs and videos highlighting their condition."I've been posting videos and pictures and lodging complaints at Prajavani meetings. I was even added to a WhatsApp group with engineers. GHMC and HMWSSB are in a troubled relationship," he said, referring to the lack of coordination between the civic body and the water board.Expressing concern over the delay in repairs, Aravind said, "The road here will take a miracle to get done by this year."Resident Naresh Raghavan offered to contribute '1 lakh from his personal funds towards road development. He said the locality, once known for its well-maintained residential surroundings, required better civic infrastructure and cooperation between residents and government agencies.Residents also complained about dust, garbage dumping and inadequate pedestrian facilities in parts of Padma Rao Nagar. They sought regular cleaning of public spaces and measures to prevent indiscriminate dumping.They urged the Greater Hyderabad Municipal Corporation (GHMC) and other departments concerned to inspect the damaged stretches, restore roads following civic works and improve coordination to avoid repeated inconvenience to commuters.When contacted, GHMC officials said the works had been undertaken by the Hyderabad Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (HMWSSB).A HMWS&SB officials said the road had been dug up for underground sewerage repairs. They acknowledged receiving complaints about improper restoration and said the agency responsible for the works had been terminated. An official source said GHMC had proposed laying a new road on the affected stretch.    i  i                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ëM%5Å3)y üb-95153345232026-10-22T17:34:35ZTiger Shroff firing case: Family claims accused is innocentD A I J I W O R L Ddaijiworld.comhttps://daijiworld.com/news/newsDisplay?newsID=1332209engIndiaøîDaijiworld Media Network - BegusaraiBegusarai, Oct 22: The family of Hritik Kumar alias Roshan, one of the key accused in the firing case involving Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff, has confirmed his arrest by Mumbai police but maintained that he is innocent.Hritik's mother, Sanyukta Devi, who runs a tea-cum-cosmetics shop in Begusarai, said the family had received information about his arrest in connection with the case. "My son is innocent. He can't do this," she said.She said the last information she received from Hritik was that he was working as a cook with a catering agency in Delhi. According to her, he wanted to marry a woman from Rajasthan and had travelled to Surat in Gujarat for wedding shopping.Begusarai Superintendent of Police Maneesh confirmed that police had questioned Hritik's parents at their residence and gathered information about his background. "We also collected information about Hritik's credentials," the SP told the media.According to his family, Hritik left his village about two years ago in search of employment. He initially worked as a cook with a catering agency in Delhi before moving to Mumbai around three months ago. In Mumbai, he reportedly worked at a restaurant as a cook and also as a bike-taxi driver.Hritik studied up to Class 12 at a local college before leaving home for work. A neighbour said his lifestyle had changed significantly after he moved to Delhi.The 22-year-old, a native of Begusarai district in Bihar, was arrested in Kota, Rajasthan, and subsequently brought to Mumbai for interrogation in connection with the firing incident. He is allegedly accused of riding the two-wheeler used during the attack, in which his accomplice reportedly opened fire at Shroff in Mumbai's Juhu area.Shroff escaped unhurt, but his driver and a bystander sustained injuries in the firing. Anil Pandit and Harman Sandhu, alleged operators of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang, later claimed responsibility for the attack on the actor.   ç ç                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   òpN!5Å''ÅW ≠o95153344352026-10-22T17:34:34ZRajasthan Police Recover Israeli Tourist Moshaiof Noam's Lost PouchnewKerala.comnewkerala.comhttps://www.newkerala.com/news/a/rajasthan-police-recover-israeli-tourists-lost-passport-cash-540.htmengIndia?Ω"Israeli tourist Moshaiof Noam lost her belt pouch while riding from Pushkar to Ranthambore on October 19 and reported it at Malpura Police Station. A team led by SHO Chainaram Beda used CCTV footage and local intelligence to trace the pouch to Mumana village, questioning seven people who had travelled the route that day. All her belongings, including her passport and Rs 20,000 in cash, were returned on Thursday, and Noam thanked the Rajasthan Police in a video.Rajasthan Police recover Israeli tourist's lost passport, cash and valuablesJaipur, Oct 22In a swift operation, the Rajasthan Police have recovered a belt pouch containing an Israeli tourist's passport, driving licence, four credit cards, electronic gadgets, Rs 20,000 in cash and other important documents within two days of it going missing.The belongings were safely returned to the tourist on Thursday, following a coordinated investigation by Malpura Police and the District Special Team (DST).The Israeli national, Moshaiof Noam, was travelling with friends from Pushkar to Ranthambore on a motorcycle on October 19 for a wildlife safari when she discovered that the belt pouch she was wearing around her waist was missing.After searching extensively along the route without success, she and her companions approached Malpura Police Station to report the loss.The police promptly registered the complaint and launched an investigation to trace the missing belongings.The operation was conducted under the supervision of Tonk Superintendent of Police Roshan Meena.A special team was formed under the leadership of Malpura Station House Officer Chainaram Beda to locate the pouch.Police used a combination of technical and human intelligence, examining CCTV footage from locations along the suspected route and gathering information through local sources.During the investigation, the team received a lead indicating that the missing belongings might be in Mumana village, which falls under the jurisdiction of Peeplu Police Station in Tonk district.Investigators identified and questioned seven individuals who had travelled between Malpura and Mumana on October 19.The investigation led to the recovery of the entire pouch, including the tourist's passport, driving licence, four credit cards, electronic gadgets, Rs 20,000 in cash and other essential documents.Police subsequently informed the tourist and returned all her belongings on Thursday.Relieved by the recovery, Noam expressed her gratitude to Rajasthan Police for its prompt response and assistance.She also released a video thanking the Rajasthan Police for their efforts.Assistant Sub-Inspector Narayan Lal Sharma and Head Constable Ramraj of DST Malpura played key roles in the operation.The successful recovery highlights Rajasthan Police's efforts to assist foreign tourists through timely intervention, coordinated investigation and professional service.      ˜                  èWP!5ÅS13Ç ö#95153306762026-10-22T17:31:06ZMan Allegedly Kills Wife Over Money For Paralysed Son's Treatment, Fakes Road Accident In MP's DharFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/indore/man-allegedly-kills-wife-over-money-for-paralysed-sons-treatment-fakes-road-accident-in-mps-dharengIndiaø‰¥¥¥¥¥¥Police in MP's Dhar arrested Rajesh Mandor for allegedly killing his wife, Sannubai, following an argument over money for their paralysed son's treatment. The accused reportedly claimed she died in a motorcycle accident, but post-mortem findings revealed severe internal injuries. Witness statements contradicted his account, prompting police to arrest him.Dhar (Madhya Pradesh): A man allegedly killed his wife after an argument over money for their paralysed son's treatment in Bandikhali village of Dhar district.The suspect, Rajesh Mandor, allegedly assaulted his wife, Sannubai, on Oct 16 and later tried to mislead the police by claiming that she had fallen from a motorcycle.According to police, Sannubai had asked her husband for money to pay for their son Sahil's treatment. When Rajesh said he had no money, an argument broke out.In a fit of rage, he allegedly grabbed her from behind, slammed her against a wall and repeatedly kicked her in the chest and abdomen. She lost consciousness following the assault.Family members rushed Sannubai to Kanchan Hospital in Rajgarh, where doctors declared her dead.The post-mortem report revealed that her liver and spleen had ruptured, causing severe internal bleeding. The medical findings and witness statements contradicted the suspect's claim of a motorcycle accident.Following an investigation, Sardarpur police arrested Rajesh. A team led by SHO Anil Kumar Jadhav inspected the crime scene and collected evidence.Police said they would produce the suspect before the court after completing the investigation. Meanwhile, Sannubai's death has left her paralysed son without his parents in police custody.êO!5Å!Åe ú395153319672026-10-22T17:32:18ZTwo Odisha athletes die as bike hits road divider on NH-16News18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/agency-feeds/two-odisha-athletes-die-as-bike-hits-road-divider-on-nh-16-10393554.htmlengIndiaø––––––œBhubaneswar, Oct 22 (PTI) Two promising young athletes from Odisha have died after their motorcycle hit a road divider on NH-16 between Cuttack and Bhubaneswar, police said on Thursday.The deceased have been identified as Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati (21) and Malaya Barik (20).They were returning to the Kalinga Stadium in Bhubaneswar after witnessing Durga Puja celebrations in Cuttack when the accident took place around 11 pm on Wednesday, police said.The two athletes were rescued by police and locals and taken to SCB Medical College and Hospital in Cuttack, where doctors declared them dead, they added.Dondapati was emerging as one of India's fastest under-23 sprinters, while Barik was a promising 400-metre runner.Both were undergoing professional training at the Kalinga Stadium High-Performance Centre in Bhubaneswar.Their deaths have sent shockwaves through Odisha's sporting fraternity.Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi and Leader of Opposition Naveen Patnaik mourned the deaths of the two athletes."Deeply saddened by the tragic demise of athletes Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malaya Barik in a road accident. Their untimely passing is a profound loss to Odisha's sporting fraternity. My heartfelt condolences to their bereaved families. May Mahaprabhu Shri Jagannath grant them strength in this difficult time and eternal peace to the departed souls," Majhi wrote in a post on X.Patnaik also expressed grief over the deaths."The news of the untimely demise of talented young athlete Mrityunjay Jaya Ram Dandapati and Malay Barik in a road accident is heartbreaking. This is an irreparable loss for the sports world. While praying for the eternal peace of their immortal souls, I convey my deepest condolences to their grieving families," he said in a post on X. PTI AAM AAM MNB   Q Q                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       è,Q!5Å11CÇG ô395153282062026-10-22T17:28:26ZPetrol-bomb attacks near pandals fail to dampen Shillong's Durga Puja celebrationsThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/guwahati/petrol-bomb-attacks-near-pandals-fail-to-dampen-shillongs-durga-puja-celebrations/articleshow/135123863.cmsengIndiaøπShillong: Durga Puja celebrations remained grand and enthusiastic across Meghalaya despite a series of petrol-bomb attacks near govt offices and puja pandals in Shillong.Security was tightened after a petrol bomb was hurled outside Mawbah Durga Puja pandal on Saturday and an attempt was made to set fire to the welcome gate of Kench's Trace Puja Committee in Laban early on Monday.On Tuesday evening, Meghalaya state skill development society office on Keating Road, which also houses Employment Exchange, came under attack. The building is opposite Civil Hospital and near PWD and Keating Road Durga Puja pandals.Following a request from Central Puja Committee, Meghalaya, the chief secretary convened a meeting on Monday attended by the director general of police and other senior civil and police officials. The meeting discussed measures to strengthen security and prevent further incidents. Additional plainclothes personnel were deployed to improve surveillance.Puja committees were advised to increase the number of volunteers to help manage crowds and maintain vigilance.A total of 237 Durga Pujas were held across Meghalaya from Oct 16 to 21, with Garo Hills accounting for the highest number at 142.Early Thursday, Oct 22, two masked men on a two-wheeler allegedly hurled a petrol bomb at the building housing Enforcement Directorate office in Shillong's Langkyrding area. The incident came a day after an attack on the health department office in Laitumkhrah.East Khasi Hills SP Vivek Syiem said the building suffered no structural damage and no injuries were reported. Police investigations are underway.   X X                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ï%R%5Å%?)Åm ¶b-95153245762026-10-22T17:24:37ZRajasthan Police recover Israeli tourist's lost passport, cash and valuablesBhaskar Live English Newsbhaskarlive.inhttps://bhaskarlive.in/others/rajasthan-police-recover-israeli-tourists-lost-passport-cash-and-valuables-2156132engIndia?≥Jaipur, Oct 22 (IANS) In a swift operation, the Rajasthan Police have recovered a belt pouch containing an Israeli tourist's passport, driving licence, four credit cards, electronic gadgets, Rs 20,000 in cash and other important documents within two days of it going missing.The belongings were safely returned to the tourist on Thursday, following a coordinated investigation by Malpura Police and the District Special Team (DST).The Israeli national, Moshaiof Noam, was travelling with friends from Pushkar to Ranthambore on a motorcycle on October 19 for a wildlife safari when she discovered that the belt pouch she was wearing around her waist was missing.After searching extensively along the route without success, she and her companions approached Malpura Police Station to report the loss.The police promptly registered the complaint and launched an investigation to trace the missing belongings.The operation was conducted under the supervision of Tonk Superintendent of Police Roshan Meena.A special team was formed under the leadership of Malpura Station House Officer Chainaram Beda to locate the pouch.Police used a combination of technical and human intelligence, examining CCTV footage from locations along the suspected route and gathering information through local sources.During the investigation, the team received a lead indicating that the missing belongings might be in Mumana village, which falls under the jurisdiction of Peeplu Police Station in Tonk district.Investigators identified and questioned seven individuals who had travelled between Malpura and Mumana on October 19.The investigation led to the recovery of the entire pouch, including the tourist's passport, driving licence, four credit cards, electronic gadgets, Rs 20,000 in cash and other essential documents.Police subsequently informed the tourist and returned all her belongings on Thursday.Relieved by the recovery, Noam expressed her gratitude to Rajasthan Police for its prompt response and assistance.She also released a video thanking the Rajasthan Police for their efforts.Assistant Sub-Inspector Narayan Lal Sharma and Head Constable Ramraj of DST Malpura played key roles in the operation.The successful recovery highlights Rajasthan Police's efforts to assist foreign tourists through timely intervention, coordinated investigation and professional service.Created On : &nbsp 22 Oct 2026 10:52 PM IST   ™ ™                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                íSS!5Å 1CÇ †U95153192732026-10-22T17:18:50ZWoman dies after manja slits throat; top cop orders crackdownThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/hubballi/woman-dies-after-manja-slits-throat-top-cop-orders-crackdown/articleshow/135123645.cmsengIndiaø√ìììììíHubballi: A 38-year-old woman riding a motorcycle died after a manja (kite string) slit her throat near Shivankar Colony on Karwar Road in Hubballi on Thursday afternoon.Police identified the deceased as Vidya Goudar, a resident of Beeraband oni, Old Hubballi and a lab technician. She was riding home for lunch when a manja string hanging from a tree got entangled around her neck, causing a deep cut. She fell from the motorcycle and died from severe bleeding, police said.The incident comes days after a person suffered a neck injury due to manja, while a 19-year-old student died after his throat was slit by kite string in Belagavi.Following Thursday's death, Hubballi-Dharwad police have decided to intensify action against the sale and use of manja. Police said cases would be registered against sellers as well as those found flying kites using the string. Parents could also face action if minors are caught using manja.The incident has renewed concerns among motorists, particularly as kite flying has been reported in several parts of the twin cities.Hubballi-Dharwad police commissioner Bhushan Borase said police had conducted an awareness campaign against manja last week, but would now focus on enforcement."We are extremely shocked. I have instructed crime branch officers and other staff to raid shops or houses where manja is being sold secretly and register cases against sellers," he said.Borase said police would also keep a watch on people flying kites with manja and initiate action against violators. Cases could be registered even if minors were found using the string, with parents also being held responsible, he added.The commissioner said he would hold talks with corporation officials to remove kites and strings hanging from trees and electricity cables to prevent further incidents.Police have also learnt that some people are procuring manja online and are exploring measures to curb such purchases, Borase said. He appealed to residents to inform police about manja use in their localities, assuring them that their identities would be protected.   Ñ 	8tÑ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      °pV!5Å]%-Ç% æS95153183452026-10-22T17:17:29ZJapan's ageing business owners have no successors. Young entrepreneurs are stepping in- Moneycontrol.comMoneyControlmoneycontrol.comhttps://www.moneycontrol.com/news/trends/japan-s-ageing-business-owners-have-no-successors-young-entrepreneurs-are-stepping-in-14057972.htmlengIndia?√ìììììèYoung entrepreneurs in Japan are taking over cafes, guesthouses and farms from older owners who want to retire but have no one to succeed them. With the cou   KãAU!5ÅC1CÇM ëE95153192632026-10-22T17:18:46ZMotorcyclist dies after luxury car runs over him 'twice' in Aligarh; murder case registeredThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/agra/motorcyclist-dies-after-luxury-car-runs-over-him-twice-in-aligarh-murder-case-registered/articleshow/135123758.cmsengIndiaø›]]]]]]Aligarh: A 40-year-old confectioner died and his associate was injured after a luxury car allegedly hit his motorcycle and reversed before running over him again near Sarasoul crossing in Aligarh's Bannadevi area on Tuesday night. Police registered a murder case after the horrific incident was partly caught on CCTV camera.Kanhaiya, who was injured, told police that an argument broke out between them and car occupants over "excessive honking". The driver then deliberately rammed into them from behind and ran the car over (confectioner) Manoj, he added.According to police, the white Audi car, bearing a Uttarakhand registration number, has been seized and the driver detained. But, investigators are yet to establish who was behind the wheels at that time.SP city Aditya Bansal said: "An FIR was registered under BNS 103 (1), 352, 351 (3) and 109 (1) on a complaint by Manoj's uncle, Chhotelal."According to locals, the incident took place when Manoj was riding his bike towards the city after closing the shop at night. Some locals threw bricks at the car to make it stop, but the driver allegedly sped away.çET!5Å!1CÇ7 ñ95153192672026-10-22T17:18:46ZGMCH records 82 road accident admissions during Durga Puja; 9 brought deadThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/guwahati/gmch-records-82-road-accident-admissions-during-durga-puja-9-brought-dead/articleshow/135123749.cmsengIndiaø öööööúGuwahati: Gauhati Medical College and Hospital (GMCH) recorded 82 road accident admissions during Durga Puja, with nine victims brought dead, between Oct 16 and 21.Two-wheeler riders accounted for most cases, while young people formed the majority of those affected.Of the 82 victims, 67 were men, and 15 were women. Eight of the nine victims brought dead were men, and one was a woman, hospital superintendent Dr Devajit Choudhury said.Most victims were from Guwahati and neighbouring areas and were brought to the hospital by police. Others were referred from districts, including Darrang, Nalbari and Barpeta, and reached GMCH by ambulance.Dr Choudhury said the numbers were around 15% lower than last year during the Puja period. However, the severity of the injuries remained a concern."Around 20% of the admitted patients are still in serious condition and are in the intensive care unit (ICU)," he said. "Head injuries were among the most common serious injuries, with several patients requiring neurosurgical intervention. Doctors were also treating patients with internal injuries, including ruptured spleens and intestinal perforations," Dr Choudhury said.Young people accounted for a significant share of the victims. Thirty-seven patients were aged between 15 and 30 years, while 11 victims were children aged between five and 15 years. Two-wheeler accidents accounted for 70% of all cases.    ntry's ageing population creating a growing business succession problem, online platforms are connecting retiring owners with people willing to take their businesses forward. Kengo Ohama, 31, and his wife took over Country Road, a cafe and coffee roastery in Mihara, Hiroshima, in April after finding it listed on Relay, a business succession platform. Ohama now rides his motorcycle for about an hour to reach the cafe, arriving by 6am. The previous owners were preparing to retire and wanted someone to preserve the business rather than see it close. "Their biggest wish was simply for someone to take good care of the shop and keep it a lively place," Ohama said. The deal cost him nothing upfront. For a monthly rent of ¬•50,000 (Rs 30,157 approximately), he took over the cafe's brand, furniture, kitchen equipment, recipes and supplier information for ¬•0. He was also allowed to redesign the interiors while keeping the business running. "That flexibility made the opportunity very attractive," he said. Relay has listed about 900 businesses, around 350 of which are currently active. Many owners are in their 60s and 70s, while prospective successors tend to be in their 30s and 40s. Another platform, BATONZ, had listed more than 42,000 businesses and matched 3,421 buyer-seller pairs as of March 2026. Japan's falling birth rate and ageing population have left many small businesses without obvious successors. Owners' children may live elsewhere, have established careers or simply not want to take over the family business. A 2023 Japan Finance Corporation survey found that 57.4% of small and medium-sized enterprises expected to close when their owners stepped away, up from 52.6% in 2019. A separate Teikoku Databank survey found that 52.1% of companies had no identified successor in 2024, highlighting the scale of the challenge despite a gradual improvement in the rate. For some buyers, taking over an existing business offers a way to become an entrepreneur without starting entirely from scratch. From a guesthouse to a new career Akitaka Mitsui, 67, opened Mori to Mizu Backpackers in Nagano in 2011 after working as an outdoor guide. The Covid-19 pandemic forced the guesthouse to close temporarily. When it reopened, Mitsui scaled down operations and reduced staff. As visitor numbers began recovering in 2022, Mitsui suffered a stroke and reconsidered his future in the business. "It was not severe, but I had to be hospitalized," he said. "The cause of the stroke was never identified, which meant it could happen again. I began to think it would be better to stop running the business." Mitsui turned to BATONZ to find a successor. He did not want his children to feel obliged to inherit the guesthouse. "I never intended to make my children take over the business," he said. "I wanted them to do what they wanted to do with their own lives." Kota Fujisawa, 29, a Nagano native who had moved to Tokyo for university and worked in consulting, was looking for a way to contribute to his home region. He took over the guesthouse with two childhood friends in May 2024, although one later left. They renamed it Local Knot Backpackers. Fujisawa paid less than ¬•10 million (Rs 60,35,470 approximately) for the business, including its website, booking systems and staff. The building was not part of the deal, and the rent was not disclosed. "My previous work was mainly desk-based, but I now spend much more time on-site and have more opportunities to communicate directly with a wide range of tourists," he said. He has retained much of the guesthouse's original character rather than completely remaking it. "If we changed everything, it would become a completely different place," Fujisawa said. Leaving government work to grow cacao In Miyazaki, 29-year-old Takayuki Otawara left a civil service job to pursue farming aft                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ⁄  ⁄                                                                                                                                                                                                              í@X!5q+1Åu ° 95153142322026-10-22T17:12:39ZPune's festive vehicle registrations dips by 25.6%Hindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/pune-news/punes-festive-vehicle-registrations-dips-by-256-101792688662797.htmlengIndia?¶ During the festive season, new vehicle registrations in Pune dropped by 25.6%, according to data from the Pune Regional Transport Office (RTO). Registrations fell to 10,534 in October 2026, down from the 14,168 vehicles recorded in October 2025.Motor car registrations witnessed the steepest decline among the major vehicle categories, dropping 46.1 per cent from 4,813 to 2,595, while two-wheeler registrations fell 12 per cent from 8,007 to 7,046.According to Pune RTO data, motorcycle registrations dropped by 961. Registrations of auto-rickshaws fell sharply from 183 to 41, while tourist taxi registrations declined from 423 to 229. Goods vehicle registrations decreased from 577 to 507, and tractor registrations fell from 100 to 42. Bus registrations, however, increased marginally from 33 to 36, while the category listed as 'others' rose from 32 to 38.Swapnil Bhosale, deputy regional transport officer, Pune RTO, said, "The registration figures show a decline in the overall number of vehicles registered during the period under comparison. Purchasing decisions can be influenced by several factors.""I had planned to buy a car this Dussehra, but the drought has affected our farming income, and we are not getting a good price for our produce. With uncertain earnings and expenses to manage, I felt it was not the right time to take on a big financial commitment," said Bhagwandas Bhadale, a farmer from rural Pune.The data also reveals a contrasting trend in electric vehicle registrations. Electric motorcycle registrations increased from 1,152 to 1,182, while electric car registrations rose from 355 to 382. Total registrations in the electric vehicle category increased from 1,566 to 1,638, a rise of approximately 4.6 per cent. Electric goods vehicle registrations also climbed from 16 to 44, while electric auto-rickshaw registrations increased from 5 to 14. Tourist taxi registrations in the electric category, however, fell from 38 to 12. The figures suggest that the overall decline in vehicle registrations has not been accompanied by a fall in every electric vehicle category.ã`W!5Å-3Ç ì95153159192026-10-22T17:14:51ZHubballi Woman Killed By Kite String, Police Warn Of Strict ActionDeccan Chronicledeccanchronicle.comhttps://www.deccanchronicle.com/southern-states/karnataka/hubballi-woman-killed-by-kite-string-police-warn-of-strict-action-1997975engIndiaø◊WWWWWXCity Police Commissioner Bhushan Gulabrao Borase expressed regret over the incident: ReportsHUBBALLI: A 38-year-old woman died after a kite string (manja) slit her throat while she was riding a two-wheeler on Karwar Road in Hubballi on Thursday afternoon.The deceased, Vidya Manjunatha, was passing near Shivashankar Colony when the hanging string caught her neck and cut her throat, leading to her death.City Police Commissioner Bhushan Gulabrao Borase expressed regret over the incident and warned that the police would take strict action against those using and selling manja."We have registered a case of culpable homicide not amounting to murder at Old Hubballi police station. We will investigate the incident and identify those responsible," he told reporters.The commissioner said the police had already warned people against using the banned kit string and would intensify checks following the death."I want to send a clear message to the people of Hubballi-Dharwad that criminal cases will be registered against anyone found using it. We will deploy our crime staff to check for its use," he said.Borase added that action would also be taken against those selling the banned kite string.   r r                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        èY!5Å-!ÅK ö995153112972026-10-22T17:09:28ZAP couple held in Hyderabad for chain snatching to fund weddingThe Siasat Dailysiasat.comhttps://www.siasat.com/ap-couple-held-in-hyderabad-for-chain-snatching-to-fund-wedding-3562376/engIndiaøÀõõõõõõHyderabad: A couple from Andhra Pradesh was arrested for chain snatching in Hyderabad on Wednesday, October 21. They committed the offence to fund their wedding.Initially, the couple moved to Hyderabad and planned to get jobs and save up for their wedding. However, they turned to chain-snatching and were arrested. The accused, Annapu Reddy Durga Ramana Reddy, 23, and Tenka Varalaxmi, 24, were arrested by Vanasthalipuram police for allegedly snatching a gold chain weighing around 30 grams from an elderly woman at a temple in Hasthinapuram.According to the police, the couple took to chain snatching after failing to get jobs in Hyderabad. Addressing the media, the police said that the incident occurred at 6:04 AM on October 18, at the Raja Rajeshwari Temple in Venkata Ramana Colony, Hasthinapuram.The victim, 65-year-old Rmuluamma, was cleaning the temple premises when Reddy and Varalaxmi approached her. According to the police, Varalakshmi caught hold of the victim and covered her mouth, while Reddy pulled the mangalsutra from her neck.The couple fled the place on a two-wheeler. No devotees were present at the temple during the incident. Based on a complaint, the Vanasthalipuram police registered a case of theft and launched an investigation. After scanning the closed-circuit television cameras, they arrested the couple on Wednesday from near a jewellery shop.During interrogation, the couple revealed that they were in a relationship for 1.5 years and planned to get married. They were living in the Gurramguda area of Hyderabad. The investigation revealed that Reddy and Varalakshmi were first-time offenders.The couple was remanded to judicial custody.   L L                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ô1Z!5s1CÇ	 Æ;95153046512026-10-22T17:03:52ZHelmetless riding deaths double in Madurai districtThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/madurai/helmetless-riding-deaths-double-in-madurai-district/articleshow/135123316.cmsengIndiaøú!MADURAI: Deaths linked to riding without helmets doubled to 64 in Madurai district during January-June, up from 32 in the corresponding period last year, according to official data, raising questions about the effectiveness of enforcement.The rise contrasts with Madurai city police's claims of tighter checks and safer roads. The commissionerate set a target of reducing accidents by 15% this year and conducted a week-long special drive, booking 3,300 cases against motorcycle riders and pillion riders for not wearing helmets.Resident-activist G Hari Shankar alleged that helmet checks were largely conducted to meet monthly targets. "Police checks were often held for namesake during the first few days of every month to show enforcement records to senior officers, while violations went unchecked for the rest of the month," he said.A senior traffic police officer rejected the criticism, blaming riders for ignoring the law. "We conduct special drives and regular awareness programmes, but cannot deploy police at every street corner. Many riders put on helmets when they spot us and remove them immediately after crossing the checkpoint," the officer said.Hari Shankar said predictable checkpoints made it easy for riders to evade checks. He called for frequent changes to interception points instead of relying on personnel stationed at shaded locations near Iyer Bungalow, Mattuthavani and the railway junction.Motorists familiar with these spots simply took diversions, he said.School zones have also emerged as hotspots for helmet violations. Activist S Kamal said parents routinely dropped off or picked up children without helmets, sometimes carrying three people on a motorcycle, with little visible policing. He questioned the example set by parents who appeared to disregard traffic rules in front of their children.A 2024 civic survey found that only 242 of 2,034 adult two-wheeler users observed in Madurai wore helmets. Helmet use among children was negligible.On March 22, two motorcyclists who were not wearing helmets died when their speeding bikes collided head-on outside Nirmala Girls Higher Secondary School near Teppakulam. The accident occurred shortly after midnight, not during school hours, but highlighted the risks on roads near educational institutions.Kamal also attributed weak enforcement to the February-May election period. "Authorities avoided stringent checks to prevent voter resentment," he said.Statewide data showed that driving licences suspended for six major offences fell 14% during the first half of 2026, when police personnel were deployed for election duty.Police have also raised concerns about riders using cheap, substandard helmets merely to avoid fines. Officials have called for stronger action against traders selling helmets with fake or absent ISI certification. The Bureau of Indian Standards, which regulates mandatory helmet certification, can seize non-compliant helmets and prosecute sellers.   Ì Ì                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ä[!5Å1CÇ# è?95153045772026-10-22T17:03:44ZYouth critically injured as truck hits bike in Ajmer, driver fleesThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/jaipur/youth-critically-injured-as-truck-hits-bike-in-ajmer-driver-flees/articleshow/135123454.cmsengIndiaø“““““““Ajmer: A 25-year-old man was critically injured after a truck hit his motorcycle from behind at Budda Pushkar Thursday morning. Police are on the lookout for the truck driver, who fled after the accident.He was taken to Jawaharlal Nehru (JLN) Hospital in Ajmer, where he is undergoing treatment.Police identified the injured man as Hariram Kumawat, a resident of Pisanghan village who works as a supervisor at a private company in Ajmer. After spending three days on leave in his village, he was returning to work on his motorcycle when the accident occurred.According to police, the truck was travelling from Pushkar towards the highway when it hit Hariram from behind and sped away.As Hariram was not carrying any identification documents, police uploaded his photograph on social media to establish his identity. They also called the last number on his mobile phone, through which his brother, Deepak Kumawat, identified him and reached the hospital.Police have registered a case.   è è                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ñn\!5Å-'-Ç ©95152971732026-10-22T16:59:54ZThree men sentenced to 20 years each in Mohali gang rape case, fined Rs 1.8 lakhThe Statesmanthestatesman.comhttps://www.thestatesman.com/india/three-men-sentenced-to-20-years-each-in-mohali-gang-rape-case-fined-rs-1-8-lakh-1503653993.htmlengIndiaø“RRRRRSA court in Punjab's Mohali district has sentenced three men to 20 years in prison each for gang-raping a young woman after luring her with the promise of a role in a Punjabi singer's music video, nearly four years after the crime took place.Additional District and Sessions Judge Vikrant Kumar convicted Jaswinder Singh, alias Jelly, Deepak Kumar and Gurwinder Singh, alias Manna, and imposed fines totalling Rs 1.80 lakh on the three convicts.The court awarded each convict 20 years' imprisonment and a fine of Rs 50,000 under Section 376D of the Indian Penal Code (IPC), dealing with gang rape.Each was also sentenced to seven years in prison and fined Rs 2,000 under Section 394, relating to robbery involving hurt, besides five-year prison terms and fines of Rs 8,000 each under Sections 366 and 120B, concerning abduction and criminal conspiracy.The convicts will face an additional three months' imprisonment if they fail to pay the fines, according to details of the judgment. Deputy District Attorney Hardeep Singh Rumana represented the prosecution.The case dates back to October 2, 2022, when the woman, who worked as an artist, received a message offering her an opportunity to participate in the shooting of a Punjabi singer's music video.According to her complaint to Majri police, she initially agreed to the offer but declined when asked to reach Sector 43 in Chandigarh. The person who contacted her subsequently arrived outside her residence and persuaded her to accompany him.During the journey, she allegedly overheard the man discussing arrangements to pick up other girls. When she questioned him about their destination, he claimed they were travelling to Abhipur to collect two more women.Near Abhipur, two motorcycle-borne men intercepted their vehicle, removed the car keys and snatched her mobile phone, according to the complaint.The woman alleged that one of the men entered the vehicle and sat beside her while another threatened her with a knife.The three accused subsequently sexually assaulted her after threatening to kill her if she resisted, the prosecution said.In her complaint, the survivor alleged that the attackers repeatedly covered her mouth and pressed her throat to prevent her from raising an alarm.The accused fled after the assault.Following the investigation and trial, the court found all three men guilty of gang rape and other offences, including robbery, abduction and criminal conspiracy.The prosecution's case centred on allegations that the men had used a fabricated professional opportunity to lure the woman before carrying out the assault.   ™ 	®™                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              è{^!5Å1CÇ3 öw95152947042026-10-22T16:57:53ZThree shooters had a practice session before firing at actor Tiger ShroffThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/mumbai/three-shooters-had-a-practice-session-before-firing-at-actor-tiger-shroff/articleshow/135122557.cmsengIndiaø⁄ZZZZZZMumbai: Investigation into the Tiger Shroff firing case has revealed that the three shooters allegedly had a practice session in a remote location before carrying out the attack on the actor on Oct 18.Police sources said Phool Singh and Rehan Ansari from Sonipat, Haryana, along with aggregator cab driver Rithik Kumar alias Roshan (22) from Begusarai, Bihar, who had moved to Mumbai a year ago, stayed in a budget hotel at Chakala in Andheri from Oct 14 to 18 using fake identities.Inside the room, while they were checking whether the weapons were functioning properly, one of the firearms accidentally went off, with a bullet hitting the bed, said the sources.Ansari and Singh allegedly checked into the hotel at 11 am on Oct 14 under the names Ankit and Randeep after arriving on a yellow motorcycle. They allegedly booked the room using a forged Aadhaar card, which police seized along with the booking register on Oct 19.Hotel employee Dheeraj Yadav told the police that the teenagers usually left around 1 pm and returned three hours later, claiming they were sightseeing.On Sunday, they allegedly left through the hotel's rear exit around 4.10 pm, carrying a small bag without informing the staff that they were checking out.Police later found their clothes in two bags left in the room.Police seized CCTV footage that allegedly showed the accused leaving with a blue bag reportedly containing firearms before heading towards Juhu on a motorcycle. Hotel staff identified them from photographs provided by the police but said they had not seen the third suspect at the hotel.On Wednesday, crime branch officials took the accused to the hotel where they had allegedly tested the firearm before the attack.åU]!5q1CÇ ï95152947082026-10-22T16:57:53ZMother arrested in 2023 murder of 8-month-old babyThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kochi/mother-arrested-in-2023-murder-of-8-month-old-baby/articleshow/135123144.cmsengIndiaøÕùùùùùúKottayam: Police have arrested the mother of an eight-month-old girl whose body was found in a marsh at Valanjavattam in Pulikkeezh in Aug 2023, saying the case has been established as murder.The body was found around 6pm on Aug 12. A special investigation team led by Thiruvalla DSP P R Santhosh, formed at the directive of Pathanamthitta district police chief R Anand, traced and arrested Manju (38) of Chemmanampathi Colony, Palakkad. She is the third accused.Police said Manju left home in 2023 after a quarrel with her husband. At Kalarkode in Alappuzha, a man named Sivan allegedly offered to look after her and the child, and they began living on a shop veranda in Changanassery. Sivan allegedly killed the baby by pressing her neck after she cried at night.Sivan and Manju then allegedly summoned his younger brother Shakthi and carried the body on a scooter to the marsh at Valanjavattam, where they dumped it.The case came to light after Manju returned to her colony in Palakkad without the child. A tribal promoter who grew suspicious informed Meenakshipuram police. Manju allegedly confessed during questioning there, police said. The special team took her into custody and questioned her at Pulikkeezh.Manju was produced in court and remanded on Tuesday. Police are searching for Sivan and Shakthi, the first and second accused.   , D,                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                à`!5Å%Ç å95152811072026-10-22T16:43:38ZMother and one-year-old daughter killed in road accident in TheniThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Madurai/mother-and-one-year-old-daughter-killed-in-road-accident-in-theni/article71612961.eceengIndiaø”SSSSSTA woman and her one-year-old daughter were killed in a road accident in Theni district on Thursday. The woman's husband sustained serious injuries.According to police, Manoj, a resident of Moonandipatti near Thevaram, was returning home on his two-wheeler with his family after purchasing new clothes for Deepavali.When they were travelling on the Dindigul-Kumily highway near Muthudevanpatti, a goods vehicle coming from the opposite direction collided with the two-wheeler and Manoj's wife, Shakila and their one-year-old daughter sustained serious injuries, and died on the spot.Manoj who sustained serious injuries was rushed to Theni Government Medical College Hospital for treatment. Veerapandi police are questioning the driver of the goods vehicle Gopal.ì9_!5Å5+1Ç3 °u95152855732026-10-22T16:48:16ZGangster who claimed responsibility in Tiger Shroff firing case named wanted accusedHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/gangster-who-claimed-responsibility-in-tiger-shroff-firing-case-named-wanted-accused-101792678206481.htmlengIndiaø‚rrrrrrGangster Anil Pandit, who had claimed responsibility for the firing on Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff has been named as a wanted accused in the case, police told a court on Thursday as it remanded four arrested persons to police custody till October 26.Pandit, a member of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang who is said to be operating from the US, had allegedly claimed responsibility for the October 18 attack on Shroff in a social media post.The Crime Branch of Mumbai Police on Thursday produced Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both hailing from Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh, before the Esplanade Magistrate's court here.The firing on Shroff was carried out at Pandit's instructions, and he has been named as a wanted accused in the case, the police told the court.The investigators sought police custody of the four arrested accused, stating that they had actively participated in the conspiracy with those held earlier in the case.These four accused had supplied a weapon to the shooters, the police said.Kunal and Sumit collected a pistol and 20 rounds from Amritsar on Anil Pandit's instructions, while Radha and Babita travelled to Mumbai and handed over the weapon to other conspirators, the police said.Defence lawyers Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi opposed the demand for custody, arguing that there was no material against these four accused and they had been arrested on mere suspicion.After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused in police custody till October 26.At least two men fired shots at Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on the evening of October 18 before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.The motorcycle was later found abandoned in suburban Andheri.Mumbai Police have registered a case of attempt to murder and arrested a total of 10 persons so far.On Wednesday, the court remanded Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana to police custody till October 31.   O O                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ì/b!5ÅEÇ ¢95152734582026-10-22T16:36:01ZWATCH | Tiger Shroff's Team Shares Video Of Bruises, Pellet Marks After Juhu Firing IncidentNewsXnewsx.comhttps://www.newsx.com/entertainment/watch-tiger-shroffs-team-shares-video-of-bruises-pellet-marks-after-juhu-firing-incident-286213/engIndiaø±Tiger Shroff's team has shared a video showing bruises and reddish marks on his arm, four days after gunshots were fired at his car in Mumbai's Juhu area. The footage comes amid online speculation about his injuries.Tiger Shroff's team has shared a video showing reddish marks and bruises on the actor's arm, four days after gunshots were fired at his car in Mumbai's Juhu area on October 18. The video was posted on the team's official Instagram account on Thursday, October 22, with the caption, "God is kind."The video comes amid questions on social media about the actor's injuries after he was seen wearing bandages shortly after the incident but appeared without them in photographs shared later. The newly shared footage offers a closer look at the marks on his arm.What Happened During The Firing Incident?The firing took place on October 18 when Tiger was reportedly returning from a football ground in Juhu. According to reports, three men arrived on a motorcycle and opened fire at his car before fleeing the scene.The actor did not sustain any gunshot injuries, although he suffered minor abrasions. His driver and an autorickshaw driver were also injured in the incident, according to reports.Watch VideoWhy Did Tiger Shroff's Team Share The Video?The footage surfaced after photographs of Tiger without visible bandages prompted speculation online about the extent of his injuries. His team had earlier issued a statement warning against fabricated stories, AI-generated videos and unauthorised statements falsely attributed to the actor. It urged media outlets and social media users to verify information and said it reserved the right to take legal action against those circulating misleading content.What Is The Latest Update On The Investigation?Mumbai Police are investigating the firing incident. Reports on Thursday said 10 people had been arrested in connection with the case, with investigators examining the alleged roles of the accused and their links to the attack.Tiger has not publicly commented on the incident so far. His team's video is the latest development following the firing and the speculation surrounding his injuries.â|a!5i1CÇ èa95152771862026-10-22T16:39:27ZTwo youngsters die as bike rams pole in MysuruThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/bengaluru/two-youngsters-die-as-bike-rams-pole-in-mysuru/articleshow/135123001.cmsengIndiaø◊◊◊◊◊◊◊Bengaluru: A trip to Mysuru to witness the grand Dasara Jamboo Savari ended in tragedy for two youngsters after their motorcycle crashed into an electric pole on Mysuru Road early Thursday.The accident occurred around 2.30am near Mylasandra Junction, within the jurisdiction of Kengeri traffic police station, when the two were were returning home after watching Dasara procession.The victims, Rajath (21) and Nagendra (20), were relatives. Rajath ran a grocery store, while Nagendra, a diploma holder, had come to Bengaluru from Shivamogga for internship and was staying at Rajath's house in Goraguntepalya.The two had travelled to Mysuru on a motorcycle to witness Jamboo Savari. However, they lost control of the bike and rammed the pole, throwing both onto the road.Rajath, who was riding, died on the spot, while Nagendra succumbed to injuries while being taken to hospital.A senior Kengeri traffic police officer said, "We are not sure if both were wearing helmets. We will check CCTV footage."   _ _                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ìc!5Å-3Ç/ °[95152691192026-10-22T16:32:12ZTiger Shroff Firing: Gangster Anil Pandit Wanted, 4 Get Police CustodyDeccan Chronicledeccanchronicle.comhttps://www.deccanchronicle.com/entertainment/tiger-shroff-firing-case-gangster-anil-pandit-named-wanted-accused-4-held-in-police-custody-1997957engIndiaø·qqqqqrMumbai: Gangster Anil Pandit, who had claimed responsibility for the firing on Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff, has been named as a wanted accused in the case, Mumbai Police told a court here on Thursday while securing the custody of four freshly arrested people.The Esplanade Magistrate's Court remanded the four accused, Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both hailing from Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh, in police custody till October 26.Pandit, a 32-year-old alleged associate of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang believed to be operating from the US, had claimed responsibility for the October 18 attack on the actor in a social media post.Producing the four accused before the magistrate, the Crime Branch of Mumbai Police said that the firing was carried out at Pandit's behest and that the four had actively participated in the conspiracy with three people arrested earlier from Kota.These four accused had supplied a weapon to the shooters, the police said, seeking their custody.Kunal and Sumit collected a pistol and 20 rounds from Amritsar on Anil Pandit's instructions, while Radha and Babita travelled to Mumbai and handed over the weapon and ammunition to other conspirators, the police said.Defence lawyers Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi opposed the demand for custody, arguing that there was no material against these four accused and they had been arrested on mere suspicion.After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused in police custody till October 26.At least two men fired shots at Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on the evening of October 18 before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.The motorcycle was later found abandoned in suburban Andheri.Mumbai Police have registered a case of attempt to murder and arrested a total of 10 persons so far.On Wednesday, the court remanded Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana in police custody till October 31.   » »                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ñ5d!5o1CÇ ®K95152668232026-10-22T16:30:06ZShowroom owner held after explosives found in carThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kolkata/showroom-owner-held-after-explosives-found-in-car/articleshow/135122928.cmsengIndiaø öööööúKolkata: Suspected explosives and banned chemicals were recovered from a car on Jessore Road at Duttapukur late on Wednesday night. The NIA, NSG, forensic experts and local police conducted a search operation at the spot. Investigators are probing whether the materials were intended for subversive activities. The car owner, Rakibul Islam, owner of a local motorcycle showroom, has been arrested and is being questioned by the police."Explosive-like substances and banned chemicals were recovered from the car going along Jessore Road. The National Investigation Agency (NIA), National Security Guard (NSG), forensic experts and Barasat District police conducted a search operation at the spot. The car owner has been arrested. Police are probing whether the materials were intended for subversive activities," a senior police officer of the Barasat District police said.According to cops, the Special Task Force (STF) had received prior intelligence about suspicious materials inside a car parked in the Tetultala area of Duttapukur. Acting on the information, the STF had been keeping the vehicle under surveillance.The car was intercepted on Wednesday night, and its owner, Rakibul, was detained for questioning.Investigators suspect that the explosives and chemicals were intended to be transported to Kolkata. However, the exact destination and purpose of the consignment remain unclear.Police sources said the recovered materials included explosive-like substances and iron mesh rods. The nature and potency of the suspected explosives will be determined through further tests. Investigators are trying to establish the source of the materials, who instructed Rakibul to transport them and whether others were involved in the incident.Barasat Police District Superintendent J. Mercy said, "The investigation is underway. The nature of the explosives is being examined. The accused has already been arrested. Further details can be provided after the investigation progresses."Rakibul reportedly left his car-repair business around 10 years ago and subsequently opened a motorcycle showroom. He currently operates four showrooms in different areas, including Tetultala and Bira in Duttapukur and Berachampa in Deganga.According to sources, a motorcycle showroom in Amdanga, reportedly owned by Rakibul, had been rocked by an explosion a few years ago. Investigators will also examine whether that incident has any connection with the latest recovery.Local sources said the car had been parked beside the Road King showroom on Tetultala Road in Duttapukur for the past two days.   f f                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ôe!5Åu%ÇU ¨q95152426632026-10-22T16:07:31ZCalliope Capital Ola Electric Investment: How many rights entitlements has the firm applied for? | Stock Market Newsmintlivemint.comhttps://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/calliope-capital-ola-electric-investment-how-many-rights-entitlements-has-the-firm-applied-for-11792681740296.htmlengIndia?ŒûûûûûûMotilal Oswal Financial Services and Calliope Capital Advisors applied for about 2.39 crore shares in Ola Electric's ‚Çπ1,000 crore rights issue after receiving transferred rights entitlements. The offer is priced at ‚Çπ27 per share and will issue 37.03 crore partly paid-up shares.Motilal Oswal Financial Services and Calliope Capital Advisors, an investment vehicle associated with the Motilal Oswal group, have applied for a combined 2.39 crore shares in Ola Electric's ‚Çπ1,000 crore rights issue on the first day of the offer, which opened on Thursday.The electric two-wheeler maker said in an exchange filing that ANI Technologies Private Limited, a member of Ola Electric's promoter group and the parent company of Ola Cabs, renounced 1,28,33,054 rights entitlements in favour of Motilal Oswal Financial Services. The financial services company applied for all the entitlements it received.Separately, Indus Trust, acting through its trustee Ankush Agarwal, renounced 1,10,22,422 rights entitlements in favour of Calliope Capital Advisors. Calliope Capital also applied for all the entitlements transferred to it.Calliope Capital Advisors LLP is an investment vehicle owned by Navin Agarwal, group managing director of Motilal Oswal Financial Services. Together, the two investors applied for 2,38,55,476 rights entitlements, equivalent to approximately 2.39 crore shares. The filing confirmed the applications but did not specify the investors' reasons for applying.Renouncing a rights entitlement means transferring the right to subscribe to new shares to another investor. Earlier this month, Agarwal pledged a 4.32% stake in Ola Electric to fund his participation in the rights issue.Earlier this month, Ola Electric approved the rights issue at ‚Çπ27 per equity share, including a premium of ‚Çπ17 per share. This represents a 26% discount to the stock's Wednesday closing price of ‚Çπ36.32, with the amount payable in two instalments.The latest fundraising comes just three months after Ola Electric raised ‚Çπ780 crore through a qualified institutional placement (QIP) in June.The rights issue price of ‚Çπ27 per share will be payable in two installments. On application, eligible shareholders will have to pay ‚Çπ16.20 per share, comprising ‚Çπ6 towards the face value and ‚Çπ10.20 towards the premium. This represents 60% of the total issue price.The first and final call will require an additional payment of ‚Çπ10.80 per share, comprising ‚Çπ4 towards the face value and ‚Çπ6.80 towards the premium. This represents the remaining 40% of the issue price, the company said in its earlier filings.Ola Electric had 4,62,84,08,313 outstanding equity shares before the rights issue. Assuming full subscription and payment of all call monies, the number of outstanding equity shares will increase to 4,99,86,80,978 following the issue.   %  ”„%                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       á;h!5%Ç  äu95152387242026-10-22T16:04:30ZDeath toll in accident involving TNSTC bus rises to threeThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Coimbatore/death-toll-in-accident-involving-tnstc-bus-rises-to-three/article71612627.eceengIndiaø„333333A 46-year-old man, who was hit by a TNSTC bus that went out of control after its driver suffered a cardiac arrest on Wednesday (October 21, 2026), succumbed to injuries on Thursday (October 22, 2026), taking the death toll to three.The police said that Abbas, a resident of Tipu Sultan Colony near Kuniyamuthur, died without responding to treatment on Thursday.According to the police, Abbas was hit by the bus when he was sitting on his two-wheeler on the side of the road and talking to a person over the phone. He suffered grievous injuries.The two others who died in the accident are driver of the bus T. Martin (54) and Noor Muhammed (46), an autorickshaw driver from Kuniyamuthur.¢g!5Åc%Çi æM95152418132026-10-22T16:06:54ZUnderage driving, non-adherence to helmet rule back in focus after death of a man in accident in PuducherryThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/puducherry/underage-driving-non-adherence-to-helmet-rule-back-in-focus-after-death-of-a-man-in-accident-in-puducherry/article71611028.eceengIndiaø·qqqqqrThe tragic incident highlights how irresponsible decisions by parents and vehicle owners in allowing their minor wards to ride   Xê*f!5ÅA1CÇS õ95152420342026-10-22T16:07:04ZTiger Shroff firing case: Shooters had practice session in Mumbai hotel room before attackThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/mumbai/tiger-shroff-firing-case-shooters-had-practice-session-in-mumbai-hotel-room-before-attack/articleshow/135122557.cmsengIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿMumbai: Investigation into the Tiger Shroff firing case has allegedly revealed that the three shooters allegedly had a practice session in a hotel room in Andheri before carrying out the attack on Oct 18.Police sources said Phool Singh and Rehan Ansari, along with aggregator driver Rithik Kumar alias Rosha (22), stayed in a budget hotel at Chakala from Oct 14 to 18 using fake identities. One of the accused allegedly fired two rounds in the room while another fired one round to check whether the weapon was functioning properly. Investigators also found that one of the firearms accidentally went off while the accused were testing it inside the hotel room, with a bullet hitting the bed.Ansari and Singh allegedly checked in at 11 am on Oct 14 under the names Ankit and Randeep after arriving on a yellow motorcycle. They allegedly booked the room using a forged Aadhaar card, which police seized along with the booking register on Oct 19. Hotel employee Dheeraj Yadav told police that the teenagers usually left around 1 pm and returned three hours later, claiming they were sightseeing. On Sunday, they allegedly left through the hotel's rear exit around 4.10 pm, carrying a small bag without informing the staff that they were checking out.Police later found their clothes in two bags left in the room.Police seized CCTV footage that allegedly showed the accused leaving with a blue bag reportedly containing firearms before heading towards Juhu on a motorcycle. Hotel staff identified them from photographs provided by the police but said they had not seen the third suspect at the hotel. On Wednesday, Crime Branch officials took the accused to the hotel where they had allegedly tested the firearm before the attack.     motor vehicles could result in devastating and irreversible consequences, says Senior Superintendent of Police D. Divya. Wearing a helmet would have significantly reduced the risk of fatal head injuries and saved the victim's precious life, the police officer addsThe recent death of a 52-year-old person in an accident has once again brought to fore the dangers of motor vehicles being driven by underage children and riding of two-wheelers without wearing a helmet in Puducherry.Early this month, a family of three travelling in a scooter along Ambedkar Salai near Uppalam was hit by a high-performance sports bike ridden by a minor. Varadaraj, 52, who was riding the scooter sustained head injuries while two others who were travelling with him suffered bruises.Mr. Varadaraj, after receiving initial treatment at the Puducherry Government General Hospital, was shifted later to a private healthcare facility in Chennai. Despite the efforts of the doctors at the private hospital, he succumbed to his injuries a few days ago. His death has now prompted the police to alter the criminal sections charged against the minor boy from 125(a) and 281 of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), 2023, to sections 281 and 106(1) of the BNS, 2023.Police said the rider of the high-end motorcycle was only 17 years of age and was driving the vehicle in a rash and negligent manner when the accident occurred. The minor has been arrayed as the first accused (Juvenile in Conflict with Law) and his mother, the registered owner of the motorcycle, as second accused for allegedly permitting her minor son to ride the vehicle."The tragic incident highlights how irresponsible decisions by parents and vehicle owners in allowing their minor wards to ride motor vehicles could result in devastating and irreversible consequences. The accident could have been averted if the minor was not permitted to ride the bike. Further, wearing a protective helmet could have significantly reduced the risk of fatal head injuries and might have saved the victim's precious life," Senior Superintendent of Police D. Divya said.She further said the incident served as a painful reminder that both responsible parental supervision and strict adherence to basic road safety measures were essential to prevent avoidable loss of life. Parents and vehicle owners should recognise that handing over a vehicle to a minor could have grave legal consequences and might result in preventable accidents, permanent disabilities and loss of precious lives, Ms. Divya pointed out.Concurring with the views of the police officer on the need to follow traffic rules, Additional Professor and Head, Department of Neurosurgery, Jawaharlal Institute of Postgraduate Medical Education and Research, Manoranjitha Kumari Mani said adhering to road safety rules for protecting lives was a collective responsibility. Road discipline, adherence to traffic rules, responsible driving and respect for traffic police must become an integral part of commuting culture, she added."In India, approximately 19 individuals die every hour due to road traffic injuries, with head injuries accounting for a substantial proportion of these deaths. In Puducherry, data indicate that 15 out of every 100 patients admitted with head injuries die in hospital. In severe cases, even those who survive may never regain their pre-injury functional status. Much of the sufferings could be prevented by wearing a good quality helmet with the chin strip securely fastened, both for rider and pillion rider," the doctor said.Advising road users to follow traffic rules for their personal and common good, the SSP said stern action would be initiated against violators. The minors involved in traffic offences would be strictly dealt with under the Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2015 and owners of the vehicle woul                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ° Zë°                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   °*k!5ÅC'=ÇA Ω395152260142026-10-22T15:54:42ZBKT ties up with Pirelli for premium car tyres as rivals commit ‚Çπ8,600 crore to expansion@businesslinethehindubusinessline.comhttps://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/bkt-ties-up-with-pirelli-for-premium-car-tyres-as-rivals-commit-8600-crore-to-expansion/article71611103.eceengIndia?«óóóóóòRising SUV sales, premiumisation and demand for larger tyres are reshaping India's passenger-vehicle tyre market. Established manufacturers have a   ZèFj!5o1CÇ öe95152293312026-10-22T15:57:12Z2 athletes riding without helmets die in accidentThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/bhubaneswar/2-athletes-riding-without-helmets-die-in-accident/articleshow/135122312.cmsengIndiaøpˇCuttack: Two budding Indian sprinters died after their motorcycle skidded and crashed into an iron barricade on NH-16 near Phulnakhara between Bhubaneswar and Cuttack late on Wednesday night. Police said both were riding without helmets. The deceased were identified as Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati (21) and Malaya Barik (20). They were travelling to Cuttack for Durga Puja festivities when the accident occurred around 10.30 pm near a Toyota showroom at Telengapentha.Police said the motorcycle, allegedly travelling at high speed, skidded and threw the riders against a highway barricade on the left side of the road. Residents alerted police. "On reaching the spot, we found the two lying near the NH barricade. We rescued them and rushed them to SCB Medical College and Hospital, where doctors declared them brought dead," said DCP Khilari Rishikesh Dnyandeo.A case was registered at Sadar police station. Postmortems were conducted on Thursday and the bodies handed over to their families. Further investigation is on, police said.Mrutyam from Kalahandi district had won gold medals in the men's 100m and 200m events at the Indian Open U-23 Athletics Competition in 2025. Barik, from Bargarh district, was a 400m runner who represented Odisha in state and national-level competitions. Both trained at the High Performance Centres at Kalinga Stadium Sports Complex in Bhubaneswar.Forum for Prevention of Road Accidents president Bikash Mohapatra said stricter enforcement of helmet rules could have averted the tragedy. Chief minister Mohan Charan Majhi expressed grief over the deaths on X, describing them as a profound loss to Odisha's sporting fraternity and extending condolences to their families.â#i!5Å31CÇC ç#95152293282026-10-22T15:57:12ZRoutine motor accident not ground for disqualification from temple panel, Kerala HCThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kochi/routine-motor-accident-not-ground-for-disqualification-from-temple-panel-kerala-hc/articleshow/135122390.cmsengIndiaø‹\\\\\]Kochi: The high court has held that the mere registration of a routing vehicle accident criminal case that does not involve moral turpitude allegations, cannot be a valid ground for disqualifying a person from membership of a temple advisory committee.A bench of Justices V Raja Vijayaraghavan and K V Jayakumar was considering a petition by Radhakrishnan R of Karunagappally in Kollam, elected as a member of the temple advisory committee of Adinad Sakthikulangara Sree Durga Bhadra Bhagavathy Temple.The petitioner challenged the proceedings of the Travancore Devaswom Board sub group officer disqualifying him for the motorcycle accident case registered at the Karunagappally police on May 2, 2025.The bench noted that it was only a rash and negligent driving case. Accordingly, it allowed the petition and set aside the disqualification.    nnounced ‚Çπ8,600 crore in capacity expansion, while BKT is seeking to diversify beyond off-highway tyres through assured orders, technical expertise and a future manufacturing venture with Pirelli.Balkrishna Industries (BKT) on Thursday announced a partnership with Italian tyre maker Pirelli to manufacture premium passenger car and SUV tyres at its Bhuj plant in Gujarat, targeting annual production of up to 8 lakh Pirelli-branded tyres by 2030. The companies have not disclosed when production will begin.Rajiv Poddar, BKT's Joint Managing Director, said the partnership would accelerate its existing plans to enter new tyre categories, describing Pirelli's decision as "a recognition of the manufacturing strength, quality and expertise we have built over decades".Under three agreements signed on October 22, the companies plan a 50:50 joint venture to establish a new tyre factory in India, sharing manufacturing capacity equally. BKT will separately pay Pirelli in euros for testing and technical services covering its own passenger-car, SUV and two-wheeler tyres. The venture's incorporation is targeted by December 31, 2030, although investment, capacity and commissioning details remain undisclosed.The partnership comes as Bridgestone, Michelin, CEAT and Apollo Tyres have announced combined investments of approximately ‚Çπ8,600 crore to expand Indian production. Apollo accounts for ‚Çπ5,810 crore, CEAT ‚Çπ1,314 crore, Bridgestone approximately ‚Çπ750 crore ($85 million) and Michelin nearly ‚Çπ686 crore.BKT has separately outlined a ‚Çπ6,800 crore investment programme through FY29 covering off-highway and on-highway tyres, carbon black and infrastructure. Whether the Pirelli venture requires additional investment remains unclear.India's premium tyre opportunity extends beyond luxury cars. SUVs account for more than half of passenger-vehicle sales, driving demand for larger 17-inch to 22-inch tyres. Electric vehicles require tyres designed for greater weight, higher torque and reduced noise, while the expanding vehicle population supports replacement demand.Manufacturing orders, technology supportUnder the initial offtake agreement, Pirelli has committed to minimum annual purchases, although year wise quantities, contract value and margins remain undisclosed. Pricing will reflect actual raw-material and conversion costs, providing demand visibility without guaranteeing profitability.The arrangement gives BKT, traditionally an off-highway tyre specialist serving agriculture, mining and construction, an established premium customer while it develops its own passenger-car brand. Pirelli's trademark and specified know-how can be used only for tyres supplied to Pirelli and its affiliates.Marco Tronchetti Provera of Pirelli, said India's economic development and growing demand for technologically advanced tyres made it important to the company's international strategy.BKT targets ‚Çπ23,000 crore in revenue by FY30, with on-highway tyres contributing approximately 20 per cent, or ‚Çπ4,600 crore.Competition builds capacityBridgestone, which reported around 20 per cent of India's passenger-vehicle replacement tyre market in 2024, plans to add 11 lakh tyres annually at Pune by 2029. CEAT plans another 35 lakh annually at Chennai by FY28, while Michelin is expanding premium-car tyre production and Apollo is adding passenger-car and commercial-vehicle capacity.BKT and Pirelli expect India's premium car-tyre market to grow almost fivefold between 2025 and 2030, without disclosing its starting size.For Pirelli, the partnership offers Indian manufacturing capacity; for BKT, the challenge is building a profitable passenger-car tyre business against established competitors.Published on October 22, 2026                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              - -                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   âPl!5}1CÇ éc95152116622026-10-22T15:41:24Z60-year-old man killed in motorcycle collision in CacharThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/guwahati/60-year-old-man-killed-in-motorcycle-collision-in-cachar/articleshow/135122157.cmsengIndiaøﬁ^^^^^^Silchar: A 60-year-old man was killed after an allegedly speeding motorcycle hit him on National Highway 306 at Uttar Krishnapur near Silchar in Assam's Cachar district on Thursday.The deceased was identified as Zakir Hussain Mazumdar of Barohali in Sonai. Police said the motorcyclist fled after abandoning the vehicle, leaving Mazumdar critically injured.Mazumdar, who worked as a night guard at a nearby workshop, was reportedly walking along the highway when the motorcycle struck him.Police recovered the body and sent it to Silchar Medical College and Hospital for autopsy.The incident triggered tension in the area, with residents demanding the immediate arrest of the absconding rider. A team from Sonai police station faced protests from locals after reaching the scene.Residents urged the police to identify the motorcyclist and take stringent legal action. Mazumdar's death has left his family and the local community shocked.   9 9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               óDm!5Å+1/Åa ™c95152008112026-10-22T15:32:27ZAudi owned by ex-Aligarh BJP chief runs over biker; police yet to arrest driverThe Indian Expressindianexpress.comhttps://indianexpress.com/article/cities/lucknow/aligarh-audi-hit-and-run-sweetshop-owner-killed-10932715/engIndiaøªThank you for your feedback.Your feedback has been reported succesfully.A 38-year-old sweetshop owner was killed after a speeding Audi hit his motorcycle from behind and ran over him in Aligarh's Banna Devi area in the intervening night of Tuesday and Wednesday. The car, owned by former Aligarh BJP district president Devraj Singh, fled the spot.Two days after the incident, police have not arrested anyone. A murder case has been registered against an unidentified driver, and the investigation is focused on establishing who was behind the wheel.Circle Officer Dhananjay confirmed to The Indian Express that the Audi belonged to Devraj Singh. He said no one had been taken into custody as police were still trying to identify the driver.According to police, the incident took place between midnight and 12.30 am when Manoj, a resident of Gabhana, was riding towards Aligarh city. The car hit his motorcycle from behind, throwing him off. It then ran over him before speeding away.Passers-by and residents allegedly pelted stones at the car in an attempt to stop it, but the driver escaped. Manoj was taken to a hospital, where he died during treatment on Wednesday morning.Superintendent of Police (City), Aligarh, Aditya Bansal, said police received information that around 11 pm on October 20, an Audi car deliberately rammed into a motorcycle from behind, killing the rider, Manoj, and injuring the pillion passenger, Kanhaiya."Kanhaiya told police that an argument and verbal altercation had taken place with the occupants of the Audi over honking. The Audi driver then deliberately rammed into the motorcycle from behind and ran over Manoj," Bansal said.He said CCTV footage has been secured, and the vehicle has been taken into custody as per rules. "The field unit has collected technical evidence, and the vehicle's technical inspection has been completed. The identity of the driver has been established. Teams have been formed to arrest the accused, and further legal action will be taken based on the evidence," he added.Police examined CCTV footage from the area, which showed an Audi hitting the motorcycle from behind. The footage appeared to show the car slowing down after the collision, reversing slightly and then running over Manoj and his motorcycle before driving away. Some passers-by who approached the injured man were seen running to the sides of the road as the car sped away.Police have taken the car into custody. Current Aligarh BJP district president Krishnapal Singh alias Lala confirmed to The Indian Express that Devraj Singh served as the party's district president from 2013 to 2016. He does not hold any party post at present but remains a senior BJP leader, Singh said.   • •                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           éXn!5Å)!Ç ô	95151991732026-10-22T15:30:55ZTwo arrested for firing at retired Haryana police officer's house in FaridabadNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/agency-feeds/two-arrested-for-firing-at-retired-haryana-police-officers-house-in-faridabad-10393474.htmlengIndiaø—QQQQQRFaridabad, Oct 22 (PTI) Two men were arrested after they allegedly opened fire at the house of a retired Haryana Police sub-inspector in Faridabad in the early hours of Thursday, police said.The incident took place around 2.30 am in Nagla Enclave Part-2 when the family of retired sub-inspector Sarjeet Bainsla was asleep, they said.The accused allegedly fired three shots at the house before fleeing on a Bullet motorcycle. The incident was captured on CCTV cameras installed at the residence, police said.A windowpane was shattered during the firing, while one bullet hit a wall. The third shot was fired into the air, according to police.Bainsla, who retired from the Haryana Police in 2023, said he did not recognise the attackers. He learnt about the incident after a neighbour informed him, following which he checked the CCTV footage, police said.A 59-second CCTV clip purportedly shows two men approaching the house on foot and opening fire. One of them was wearing a blue T-shirt with a cloth tied around his head, while the other was dressed in a white shirt.The footage also purportedly shows one of the men picking up an empty cartridge casing before the duo fled on a motorcycle, police said.The accused have been identified as Harsh and Ranjit. They are being questioned to ascertain the motive behind the firing, police added."A case has been registered based on a complaint from the family. We have arrested two suspects and are questioning them to determine the motive behind the firing," said Inspector Hukum Singh, SHO of Saran police station. PTI COR SMV SMV SKY   € €                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ò"o!5Å7!Åm ¨395151909662026-10-22T15:23:12ZTwo Arrested For Firing At Retired Haryana Cop's House In FaridabadRediff.com India Ltd.rediff.comhttps://www.rediff.com/news/report/two-arrested-for-firing-at-retired-haryana-police-officers-house/20261022.htmengIndiaøÿXXXXXXDiscover the details of the Faridabad firing incident where two men were arrested for allegedly opening fire at a retired Haryana Police sub-inspector's home, with CCTV footage playing a crucial role in their apprehension.IMAGE: This is an AI-generated image and has been used only for representational purposes.Key Points* Two men were arrested in Faridabad for allegedly opening fire at a retired Haryana Police sub-inspector's house in the early hours of Thursday.* The incident occurred around 2.30 am in Nagla Enclave Part-2 while the family of Sarjeet Bainsla was asleep.* Three shots were fired, shattering a windowpane and hitting a wall, with the entire incident captured on CCTV cameras.* The accused, identified as Harsh and Ranjit, fled on a Bullet motorcycle and are currently being questioned to determine their motive.* Retired sub-inspector Bainsla, who left the force in 2023, did not recognise the attackers.Two men were arrested after they allegedly opened fire at the house of a retired Haryana Police sub-inspector in Faridabad in the early hours of Thursday, police said.The incident took place around 2.30 am in Nagla Enclave Part-2 when the family of retired sub-inspector Sarjeet Bainsla was asleep, they said.Details Of The Firing IncidentThe accused allegedly fired three shots at the house before fleeing on a Bullet motorcycle. The incident was captured on CCTV cameras installed at the residence, police said.A windowpane was shattered during the firing, while one bullet hit a wall. The third shot was fired into the air, according to police.Bainsla, who retired from the Haryana Police in 2023, said he did not recognise the attackers. He learnt about the incident after a neighbour informed him, following which he checked the CCTV footage, police said.