                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  àzp!5Å%Ç çO95151908852026-10-22T15:23:12ZAndhra Pradesh Home Minister rushes injured students to hospitalThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Visakhapatnam/andhra-pradesh-home-minister-rushes-injured-students-to-hospital/article71612319.eceengIndiaøø Andhra Pradesh Home Minister V. Anitha came to the rescue of two students who sustained serious injuries in a road accident on the BRTS Road near Health City in Arilova, on Thursday.The Minister was travelling from Visakhapatnam towards Payakaraopeta via the BRTS Road, when she noticed a vehicle colliding with a scooter carrying the two students. On seeing the injured students, Ms. Anitha immediately intervened and arranged for them to be shifted to a hospital for medical treatment.The Minister instructed the doctors concerned to provide the injured students with the best possible medical care. She also directed the police to take appropriate legal action against the driver of the vehicle responsible for the accident, in accordance with the law.The Home Minister expressed concern over the incident and wished the injured students a speedy recovery.   ò ò                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              òeq!5Å3+1ÇE ¨=95151884092026-10-22T15:20:55Z{Godara gang link surfaces} One nabbed for Oct 11 firing at visa consultancy officeHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/chandigarh-news/godara-gang-link-surfaces-one-nabbed-for-oct-11-firing-at-visa-consultancy-office-101792681825046.htmlengIndiaø››››››ﬁ(Blurb) Associate at large; no prior criminal record found, say police- The firing took place at the office of Brightway Immigration on October 11. The owner had been receiving extortion calls for ‚Çπ1 crore.- As he didn't pay, two persons committed the crime. Deepak, who has been arrested, says his cousin from Delhi accompanied him during the firing.- The accused got directions for the firing from two persons linked to Godara gang operating from abroad, say police. The weapon is yet to be recovered.Ten days after two motorcycle-borne men opened fire at a visa consultancy office in Model Town Extension, the police have arrested one of the accused. According to investigators, the accused are linked to the Rohit Godara gang through two foreign-based operatives. The gang had demanded a ‚Çπ1 crore extortion from the immigration consultant, and the attack was the result of the victim's refusal to pay.The arrested accused has been identified as Deepak Kumar, 22, a resident of Hazuri Bagh Colony, while his cousin Gagandeep, a resident of Seelampur, Delhi, is on the run. During interrogation, Deepak told police that he and Gagandeep opened fire at the visa consultancy office on the directions of Varinder Charan from Jhunjhunu, Rajasthan, and Jagjit Singh from Butaheri, Ludhiana. The police have also booked Varinder Charan and Jagjit Singh based on the information provided by the arrested accused. Both Charan and Singh are linked to the Godara gang and are currently operating from abroad.The police have recovered the motorcycle used in the crime, though the weapon is yet to be traced. Deputy commissioner of police (investigation) Harpal Singh stated that Varinder Charan and Jagjit Singh paid ‚Çπ40,000 to Deepak and Gagandeep for the task. The weapon used in the crime was also provided by the gang.The DCP added that no prior criminal record of the accused was found. Deepak, a matriculate, is jobless. The incident occurred late on the night of October 11, when two men arrived on a motorcycle outside Brightway Immigration. One of them allegedly fired two to three rounds at the building while his accomplice recorded the act on a mobile phone, before both fled.The incident came to light the following morning when employees found a shattered windowpane and informed the police. Investigators recovered spent bullet shells and live rounds from outside the premises and examined CCTV footage to identify the suspects.The consultancy owner, Bhanav Ahuja, stated that he had been receiving extortion calls and threats for around four months. Following his statement, the Model Town police registered an FIR under Sections 125 (act endangering life or personal safety), 324(4) (mischief) and 3(5) (common intention) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, along with Sections 25, 27, 54 and 59 of the Arms Act.    C  C                                                         ü:r!5Å7%Å{ ∫G95151816012026-10-22T15:16:23ZUltraviolette launches X-47 Venom electric motorcycle, introduces new VX-100 platformEntrackrentrackr.comhttps://entrackr.com/news/ultraviolette-launches-x-47-venom-electric-motorcycle-introduces-new-vx-100-platform-12739314engIndia?ø Bengaluru-based electric mobility startup Ultraviolette Automotive has launched the X-47 Venom electric motorcycle alongside a new 100V VX-100 platform. The motorcycle is priced at Rs 2.65 lakh under an introductory offer, with deliveries scheduled to begin in November 2026.The X-47 Venom is the first motorcycle built on Ultraviolette's new VX-100 architecture. The company said the platform is designed to improve performance, energy efficiency, charging speed and safety while reducing vehicle weight.Bookings for the motorcycle open on October 22, with the introductory price applicable to the first 5,000 customers. The vehicle will be available across India through Ultraviolette's UV Space Stations.The X-47 Venom offers an IDC-certified range of 343 km, a peak power output of 30 kW (40 hp) and a top speed of 155 kmph. It can accelerate from 0 to 60 kmph in 2.7 seconds and from 0 to 100 kmph in 5.9 seconds. The motorcycle delivers 550 Nm of torque at the wheel and has a kerb weight of 180 kg, which is up to 20 kg lower than that of the previous-generation platform, according to the company.The motorcycle supports 12 kW DC fast charging and comes with a 1.6 kW onboard charger. Ultraviolette claims it is the only electric two-wheeler in India to support 12 kW DC fast charging."The X-47 Venom brings these advances to life, combining distinctive design with deeper engineering capabilities and technology that enhances the riding experience," said Narayan Subramaniam, CEO and co-founder of Ultraviolette.The VX-100 platform integrates the company's SRB-11 battery technology, UV LIGHTFURY motor and a next-generation motor control unit. Ultraviolette said the battery technology offers up to 20% higher energy density and twice the cooling performance. An optimised thermal management system is designed to dissipate heat up to 50% faster.The battery pack also features a pyro-fuse designed to isolate the electrical circuit within microseconds when a critical fault is detected. It works alongside a battery management system that monitors cell-level voltage, temperature and current, as well as individual cell fuses.The motorcycle features a 77 GHz rear radar system under the company's UV Hypersense technology. The system supports blind-spot monitoring, lane-change assistance, overtake alerts and rear-collision warnings.Other features include a seven-inch TFT touchscreen, cruise control, park assist with a rear-camera feed, Mappls-integrated navigation and connectivity through the VIOLETTE A.I. system.Alongside the motorcycle, Ultraviolette has introduced B-MAX, a reusable rider safety vest designed to extend its safety features beyond the vehicle. The company claims the vest provides 86% force attenuation and can be reused up to five times.Commenting on the motorcycle's engineering, Niraj Rajmohan, CTO and co-founder of Ultraviolette, said the VX-100 architecture, battery technology, lighter motor and motor control unit had been developed as an integrated system to improve power delivery, efficiency, thermal performance and safety.The modular VX-100 platform is also designed to support different battery capacities, vehicle configurations and power levels across Ultraviolette's future product portfolio.Founded in 2016 by Narayan Subramaniam and Niraj Rajmohan, Ultraviolette develops electric vehicle platforms and battery technologies. The company is backed by investors including Lingotto, TDK Ventures, Qualcomm Ventures, Zoho Corporation, TVS Motor Company, Yali Capital and Speciale Invest.Ultraviolette said it has expanded its presence to 20 countries across Europe. The company plans to launch the X-47 Venom in Europe on November 3 at EICMA 2026 in Milan, Italy.   • •                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           íXs!5ÅS95ÇE üq95151800002026-10-22T15:13:51ZTiger Shroff firing case: Family of key accused Hritik Kumar pleads innocence in Bihar after arrestThe New Indian Expressnewindianexpress.comhttps://www.newindianexpress.com/states/bihar/2026/Oct/22/tiger-shroff-firing-case-family-of-key-accused-hritik-kumar-pleads-innocence-in-bihar-after-arrestengIndiaøΩ"PATNA: Family members of Hritik Kumar alias Roshan, one of the key accused in the Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff firing case, on Thursday admitted that he had been arrested by Mumbai police. They, however, pleaded Hritik's innocence.Hritik's mother, Sanyukta Devi, who runs a tea-cum-cosmetics shop in Begusarai, said, "The family got information about Hritik's arrest by Mumbai police in connection with the Bollywood actor's firing case. My son is innocent. He can't do this."She said that the last information she received from her son was that he was working as a cook in a catering agency in Delhi. He wanted to marry a girl from Rajasthan and had gone to Surat (Gujarat) for wedding shopping, she revealed.Begusarai Superintendent of Police (SP) Maneesh confirmed that the police interrogated Hritik's parents at their residence. He has two younger brothers and sisters. "We also collected information about Hritik's credentials," the SP told the media.The family told the interrogators that Hritik left his village in search of a job about two years ago. He first started working as a cook in a catering agency in Delhi. About three months ago, he shifted to Mumbai, where he worked as a cook at a restaurant and as a bike-taxi driver.He studied up to Class 12 (Intermediate) at a local college before leaving home in search of a job. Locals recall that Hritik was very particular about his lifestyle even in his native village. "His lifestyle has completely changed after shifting to Delhi," his neighbour said.The 22-year-old suspect from Bihar's Begusarai was arrested in Kota, Rajasthan, and subsequently taken to Mumbai for interrogation in the Tiger Shroff firing case. He was allegedly riding the two-wheeler when his accomplice fired shots at Shroff in Mumbai's Juhu area.Though Shroff escaped unhurt, his driver and a bystander were injured in the firing. Two alleged operators of the notorious Lawrence Bishnoi gang, Anil Pandit and Harman Sandhu, later claimed responsibility for the attack on the actor.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       ïpt!5Å]S%Ç= ¶95151775442026-10-22T15:11:43ZTiger Shroff firing case: Anil Pandit named absconding accused, 4 sent to police custody till October 26Daily News and Analysis (DNA) Indiadnaindia.comhttps://www.dnaindia.com/bollywood/report-tiger-shroff-firing-case-anil-pandit-named-absconding-accused-4-sent-to-police-custody-till-october-26-3222824engIndiaø››››››ﬁMumbai's Esplanade Court has remanded four accused in the Tiger Shroff firing case to police custody until October 26. Police allege the accused supplied weapons on gangster Anil Pandit's instructions. With 10 arrests so far, the investigation into the October 18 attack continues.Four accused arrested in connection with the firing incident targeting actor Tiger Shroff were produced before Mumbai's Esplanade Court on Thursday. The court remanded them to police custody until October 26, rejecting the Mumbai Police's request to extend their custody until October 31. Gangster Anil Pandit, a member of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang who is believed to be operating from the US, has been named as an absconding accused in the case. According to the police remand application, the firing was carried out at his behest. Pandit had allegedly claimed responsibility for the October 18 attack in a social media post.The four accused were identified as Kunal, 21, and Sumit, 19, both from Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha, 23, and Babita, 23, from Uttar Pradesh. They were brought to Mumbai from Kota, Rajasthan, and produced before the court after undergoing medical examinations. According to the police, Kunal and Sumit collected a pistol and 20 rounds from Amritsar on Pandit's instructions. Radha and Babita allegedly travelled to Mumbai and handed over the weapon to other conspirators. Investigators told the court that the four had actively participated in the conspiracy and supplied the weapon used by the shooters.The defence lawyers opposed the police custody plea, arguing that there was insufficient material against the accused and that they had been arrested on suspicion. After hearing both sides, the court granted police custody until October 26. Mumbai Police have registered a case of attempt to murder and arrested a total of 10 persons so far. On Wednesday, the court remanded three suspected shooters - Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Bihar and residing in Mumbai; and Phool Singh, from Haryana - to police custody until October 31.The firing took place around 7 pm on October 18 in Mumbai's Juhu area, when Shroff was leaving a football club. At least two men allegedly opened fire at his car before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped unhurt, while his driver and a bystander sustained injuries. The motorcycle was later found abandoned in suburban Andheri.   ‹ "‹                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                àCv!5Å)EÇ/ å95151666952026-10-22T15:03:43ZE-bike startup Ultraviolette targets 10,000 monthly sales by 2027-endEconomic Timeseconomictimes.indiatimes.comhttps://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/startups/e-bike-startup-ultraviolette-targets-10000-monthly-sales-by-2027-end/articleshow/135121554.cmsengIndia?±E-scooters account for close to 20% of new scooter sales in India, while electric motorcycles make up less than 1% of new motorcycle sales, he added. He expects electric motorcycle adoption to pick up as more manufacturers introduce products, similar to the increase seen in e-scooter penetration over the past three years.Bengaluru-based electric two-wheeler startup Ultraviolette expects monthly sales to reach 10,000 units by the end of 2027, driven by a slate of launches next year, including its first e-scooter, Tesseract, cofounder and chief technology officer Niraj Rajmohan told ET."From a volume perspective, all three motorcycles put together -- - the X-47, the F77, and the Shockwave (upcoming) -- will be equivalent to the scooter volumes," Rajmohan said. Theè[u%5Å#Å'#Åi ö!b-95151720602026-10-22T15:07:30ZMan steals gold worth Rs 5 lakh from in-laws house in Bhubaneswar, arrestedLatest Odisha News, Breaking News Today | Top Updates on Corona - OTV Englishodishatv.inhttps://odishatv.in/odisha/man-steals-gold-worth-rs-5-lakh-from-in-laws-house-in-bhubaneswar-arrested-12739308engIndiaø––––––œA newly married man was arrested on Thursday by Nayapalli Police for allegedly stealing gold jewellery from his in-laws' house in Bhubaneswar.The accused has been identified as Rajesh Kumar Nayak, a native of Nayagarh, who was staying in a rented accommodation in Unit-8 locality of the State Capital.According to police sources, Rajesh had married a young woman from the Unit-8 area a few days ago. After visiting his in-laws' house for the first time, he allegedly noticed gold ornaments kept inside an almirah.Police said the accused allegedly took advantage of a time when no one was present at the house and stole gold jewellery worth around Rs 5 lakh.The alleged theft came to light after the family discovered that the ornaments were missing.The accused allegedly went a step further and took his father-in-law's motorcycle as well. The motorcycle was reportedly pledged elsewhere.Following a complaint lodged at Nayapalli Police Station, police began an investigation into the alleged theft. The accused, Rajesh Kumar Nayak, was subsequently arrested by Nayapalli Police.The case has drawn attention as the accused allegedly targeted his in-laws' house shortly after marrying into the family.The police action followed the complaint regarding the missing gold ornaments and motorcycle.No comments were received from the local police in this regard.Worth mentioning, earlier, some looters allegedly took advantage of the festive rush in Bhubaneswar, targeting homes and people attending Dussehra celebrations.In the previous incident, a government quarter in VSS Nagar under Sahid Nagar police limits was burgled during the daytime on Wednesday.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ïjw%5Å_Å#'Åg ¶b-95151646292026-10-22T15:02:34ZPetrol Bomb Hurled at ED Office in Shillong, Second Attack on Govt Building in Two Days - Yes Punjab NewsYesPunjab ‚Äì No.1 News-Portal. Latest News from Punjab, India & the World.yespunjab.comhttps://yespunjab.com/petrol-bomb-hurled-at-ed-office-in-shillong-second-attack-on-govt-building-in-two-days/engIndiaøŒûûûûûûShillong, October 22, 2026 (Yes Punjab News)Two unidentified men allegedly riding a motorcycle hurled petrol bombs at a building housing the Enforcement Directorate (ED) office in Meghalaya's capital, Shillong, early Thursday, police said. The incident marks the second suspected petrol bomb attack on a government establishment in the city in two days.The attack took place in the Langkyrding area of East Khasi Hills district. No structural damage to the building was reported, Superintendent of Police Vivek Syiem said.According to the police officer, the security guard stationed inside the building became aware of the incident only on Thursday morning. Police are examining CCTV footage to identify the suspects, and a case is being registered in connection with the attack.Patrolling has been intensified in the area as authorities step up security measures, Syiem said.The latest incident comes a day after a similar attack was reported at the Health Department office in Shillong's Laitumkhrah area, raising concerns over the safety of government establishments.The attacks follow a series of suspected petrol bomb incidents and arson cases reported across the city in recent months. On October 20, three suspected petrol bomb incidents were reported at Kench's Trace, Keating Road and Laitumkhrah, prompting authorities to strengthen security arrangements and increase surveillance.In September, several government offices, police facilities and vehicles were targeted in suspected petrol bomb attacks and arson incidents. The affected locations included the Directorate of Mineral Resources, Lumdiengjri police station, the Directorate of Health Services and a police booth at Nongmynsong.Those incidents prompted the state government and police authorities to review security arrangements, intensify patrolling and examine CCTV footage to identify those responsible.Earlier, in August, suspected miscreants allegedly hurled petrol bombs at a National People's Party office in Shillong and a police outpost at Nongmynsong amid heightened tensions following violence during a Khasi Students' Union rally.Police have not established whether the latest attacks are connected to the earlier incidents, and no common motive has been publicly confirmed.Investigations are continuing as authorities work to identify the perpetrators and prevent further attacks on government establishments in the city.   ô –ô                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ä4y!5Å/M+ÅI ê?95151488652026-10-22T14:49:14ZTwo Arrested in Nilagiri for Alleged Gang Rape of Woman After Offering Her a LiftPragativadi: Leading Odia Daillypragativadi.comhttps://pragativadi.com/two-arrested-for-alleged-gang-rape-of-woman-after-offering-her-a-lift/engIndiaø“RRRRRSPolice have arrested and forwarded to court two youths from Kunchibania village under Garadihi panchayat on charges of gang-raping a woman from the Berhampur police station area in Nilagiri block.According to reports, the incident occurred last Sunday evening. The woman had just returned by bus from Baripada and was purchasing groceries at the Kalakad market. The two accused, identified as Litu alias Abhijit Singh (23) and Sipun Singh (20) of Kunchibania village, approached the woman and offered to drop her home on their motorcycle.Trusting them, the woman accepted the ride. However, instead of taking her home, the accused drove her to a deserted quarry area where they allegedly gang-raped her before fleeing the scene.Following the ordeal, the victim managed to inform her family about the incident, prompting them to file a formal complaint at the Brahmapur police station.Acting swiftly on the complaint, Inspector-In-Charge (IIC) J Patnaik registered a case, arrested both accused individuals, and forwarded them to court today.é-x!5w1CÇ	 ò/95151636952026-10-22T15:01:53ZCourt rejects plea to shift Mini Cooper crash accusedThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/kochi/court-rejects-plea-to-shift-mini-cooper-crash-accused/articleshow/135121637.cmsengIndiaø◊◊◊◊◊◊◊Kochi: Judicial first class magistrate court, Angamaly, on Thursday dismissed a petition filed by the superintendent of Borstal School, Kakkanad, seeking to transfer the prime accused in the Nedumbassery Mini Cooper accident case to a central prison over security concerns.The petition was filed by the superintendent of the facility, which houses prisoners aged between 18 and 21. After examining the plea, the magistrate rejected the request for the accused's transfer.Suhail Sajeev (19), the key accused, was allegedly driving the Mini Cooper that rammed into a scooter from behind on the airport road at Nedumbassery on Oct 11, killing three youths. He was under the influence of alcohol and the car was reportedly travelling at high speed the time of the crash.The victims were Gopika (21) of Mannarkkad, Devika (21) of Kalpetta and Iyas (21) of Karnataka.Suhail's admission to Borstal School had triggered allegations on social media that he was receiving preferential treatment. Police subsequently clarified that he was lodged at the facility in accordance with norms applicable to his age. Three others who were travelling in the car were also arrested and booked for abetment.They are also lodged at Borstal School.The magistrate court had earlier rejected the bail petitions of the accused. They have since approached the Ernakulam principal sessions court seeking bail.Meanwhile, the investigation into the accident is continuing. As part of the probe, an investigation team visited the house of Devika in Wayanad, on Thursday morning.    ˛ ` ˛                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ä_{!5g1CÇ ë)95151458422026-10-22T14:46:26Z3 killed in separate road crashes in north APThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/vijayawada/3-killed-in-separate-road-crashes-in-north-ap/articleshow/135121487.cmsengIndiaø◊WWWWWXVisakhapatnam: Three persons were killed in two separate road accidents in north Andhra Pradesh.In the first incident, two youngsters were killed after their motorcycle went out of control and rammed into an electric pole between Papayyavalasa and Mulakayyavalasa villages under Makkuva mandal in Parvathipuram Manyam district.The deceased were identified as Y Giri (18), a polytechnic student, and S Ravu (17), a second-year Intermediate student. Both were friends and natives of Chappabuchipeta.According to police, the duo had gone to Papayyavalasa village to witness the ongoing Dasara celebrations. While returning home on Wednesday, the rider reportedly lost control of the motorcycle and crashed into a roadside electric pole, killing both on the spot.In another incident, one person died on the spot and another sustained injuries after two motorcycles collided near Ponduru in Srikakulam district.The deceased was identified as B Narayana Rao (42), a carpenter and a native of Rapaka village. Police said the accident occurred when Rao was travelling towards Jawam village on his motorcycle.ìz!5o%Åy ¢W95151466802026-10-22T14:47:09ZStolen jewellery recovered, two held in CuddaloreThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/stolen-jewellery-recovered-two-held-in-cuddalore/article71611555.eceengIndiaø«óóóóóòThe Cuddalore district police on Wednesday arrested two men allegedly involved in a series of burglaries across Tamil Nadu and recovered 38 sovereigns of gold jewellery from their possession.The accused were identified as Manickaraj, 41, of Kolathur, Chennai, and Baranidarane, 30, of Perambalur district. The search is under way for another suspect in connection with the case.According to police, the accused broke into the house of Saraswathi, 55, a government school teacher residing at Gandhi Nagar in Vriddhachalam. She had gone to Shirdi on August 26 and found the house burgled on her return.The duo broke open the front gate, turned away the CCTV camera installed at the entrance and gained access into the house. They stole 30 sovereigns of gold jewellery, five kg of silver articles and drove away in the car parked in the house.Following a complaint, a special police team was constituted by Superintendent of Police Vivekananda Shukla.On October 21, the police team was on patrol when they intercepted a car on the Vriddhachalam-Karuveppilankurichi Road. After preliminary enquiry, the police found that the duo was linked to the burglary reported in Vriddhachalam.Police said Manickaraj and Baranidarane had become acquainted while they were lodged in Puzhal prison. Manickaraj was released on bail from Coimbatore prison on August 10, and Baranidarane was released from Salem prison on August 8.According to police, more than 50 cases were pending against Manickaraj and 30 against Baranidarane in various police stations across Tamil Nadu. Police suspect their involvement in burglaries reported over the past two months in Perambalur, Chennai, Red Hills, Tiruchi, Dharapuram and Vadalur.The police recovered 18 sovereigns of gold jewellery linked to the burglary reported at Vriddhachalam and another 20 sovereigns linked to a theft in Vadalur.They also seized ‚Çπ1.04 lakh from the sale of silver articles stolen from the teacher's house, the stolen car, two other cars allegedly purchased with the proceeds from the sale of stolen jewellery, a motorcycle suspected to have been used in the offences and three mobile phones from their possession. Further investigations are on.   i 	Yi                                                                                                   