ent. He then placed her body in a bag and dumped it in the drain.The couple had married about a year ago and moved to Bengaluru around six months ago, where they worked in garment factories, police said.Ruksana, who had a child from her previous marriage, had met Irfaz in Bihar after separating from her first husband, and the two subsequently fell in love, according to police.Motive Behind The MurderPolice said Irfaz allegedly suspected his wife of having an illicit relationship because she frequently spoke to people over the phone, which led to regular arguments between them.On October 10, an argument allegedly escalated, following which Irfaz attacked her with a stone, police said.To dispose of the body, the accused allegedly broke the handle lock of a motorcycle belonging to an unidentified person, placed the body inside a bag on the vehicle and pushed it before dumping the body in the drain, police said.Investigation Leads To ConfessionAfter the body was discovered on October 13, police formed a special team to establish the woman's identity and trace the accused.During the investigation, police received information from local residents that a man from Gopalapura had reported his wife missing.When questioned, Irfaz allegedly told police that Ruksana had returned to her native place in Bihar and was not using a mobile phone. However, suspecting inconsistencies in his account, police took him into custody for further questioning.During interrogation, he allegedly confessed to the murder, police said.The Magadi Road police are continuing their investigation into the case.Disclaimer: News content is sourced from the stated source. Headlines, summaries, section headers, and images are automatically generated or selected using AI/algorithms and may not always be fully accurate. Readers are advised to refer to the full article for complete context.   9 9                                                                                       