heir clothes in two bags left behind in the room.Yadav said the teenagers typically left the hotel around 1 pm and returned about three hours later, claiming they had gone sightseeing.Police seized CCTV footage that allegedly showed the two leaving with a blue bag containing firearms before heading towards Juhu on a motorcycle. Hotel staff identified the teenagers from photographs shown to them by police but said they had not seen the third suspect at the hotel.Gun accidentally discharged in roomA Crime Branch officer said the suspects had brought weapons into their hotel room. According to the officer, a gun accidentally discharged while they were attempting to clear a jammed bullet or test-fire it, and the bullet struck either the bed or a wall.The suspects also allegedly travelled by autorickshaw to a forested area on Mumbai's outskirts on October 17, where they paid Rs 400 to conduct target practice, according to the investigation.    re also eagerly awaiting for the Fauzi glimpse and are also hoping that the makers of Kalki 2898 AD 2 and Spirit will surprise them with new updates.On the other hand, we Hans India have listed down the powerful dialogues of Darling Prabhas from his 10 best movies. Take a look!1. Mr. Perfect:* "Gelavalante longali vongali ante nenu nammanu...Mundu manalo matter undali".* "Premante iddariki oke brand coffee nachadam kadu, iddaru kalsi oka manchi coffee thayaru cheskovadam...Neeku gelupu guest lantidi appudapudu mathrame vasthundi, But naku mathram frnd lantidi eppudu naathone untadi...".* "Ela ante cheppalekapovachu Entha ante chupinchalekapovachu But e gunde kottukunnantha kalam ninnu premisthune unta...".* "Abhiprayalu kalisthene premanukunnanu, but manasulu kuda kalavalani thelsukunnanu...".* "Aata lo gelavadam mukyam kadu ra aata ni enjoy cheyadam mukhyam...".2. Varsham:"Shailu kosam padi saalu chastaanu nenu, nuvvu okkasaari chaavagalava..nenu ready nuvvu ready na?"3. Chatrapathi:"Vaadupothe veedu, veedupothe nenu, nenu pothe naa amma mogudantu evadaina adhikaaram kosam egabadithe... Appalanaidu.. dadagirikochina, dhouryanjaayinikochina... goondayijaanikochhina, group lu kattadaanikochhinaa... raajakeeyamtho vachinaa, rowdyizam tho vachhina potuko shavam lekkana portuku balavthaayi theeram lo kerataalu erupu rangu poosukoni pothetthuthaay."4. Bujjigadu:* "Tipper lorry velli scooter ni guddhithe ela untado telusa..ala untadi nenu guddhithe...".* "Bavunnaavra... Volvo bus laa maanchi dhittangaa unnav... ee bandi chusava...naa chaasi number chussthava..chupinchana...ne taravatha model nenu.. Isuzi engine... rye rye rye horse pwoer ekkuva..."* "Ila kodithe naraalu kanabadathaayata, itta pattesukunte dorikesthaay, ee naraannitta patti laagithe vanda meetarla thaadosthadi...laageskundhaareti...".* "Endi evanna matlaadande..o paata paadande...".5. Billa:"Trust no one, kill anyone, be only one..Asthala vistha baby...".6. Mr Perfect:"Edhagaalante maraali, longaali, vangaali ante nenu nammanu.. manalo matter undaali...".7. Rebel:"Meeru aakalitho vetaade puli ni chusuntaru...aaveshamtho vetaade puli ni chusuntaaru.. nenu rendellu upavaasam tarvatha vetaade Puli ni..daaniki aahaaram ippude fix ayindi...".8. Mirchi:* "Cutout chusi konni konni nammeyaali dude...".* "Veelaithe premiddam dude, poyedhemundi...maha aithe thirigi premisthaaru...".* "Collar pattukodavam emundra, nenu mee oorochhi ne mede pattukunna... aa oori meedaki ravaalante nuvvu sketch eskoni ravaali...nenu hanger kunna shirt eskonochhestha..."* "katthi vaadatam modhaledithe naakanna baga evadu vaadaledu... kani chivaraku katthule migulthay.. manushulu migalaru...".8. Baahubali - The Beginning:"Edi maranam.. mana gunde dhairyam kanna shatru balagam peddadi anukodam maranam.. ranarangamlo chaavukanna pirikithanamtho bathikundadam maranam.. mana thallini avamaaninchina neechudu kalledurugaa nilabadi navvuthu chusthunte... vaadi thala nariki amma padhaala kinda paathakunda, vennu chupi paaripovadam maranam... aa maranaanni jayinchadaaniki nenu velthunnanu... naa thallini, naa nelani ye neechudu, nikrushtudu muttukoledani rommu cheelchi, netthuru thaagu cheppadaaniki velthunna... naatho vachedevaru...naatho chachhedevaru...aa maranaanni dhaati naatho bathikedevaru.. Jai mahishmathi...".9. Baahubali - The Conclusion:* "Thappu chesaav Devasena... aadadaani vonti mida cheyyi vesthe narakaalsindi velu kadu..thala...".* "Nuvvu naa pakkanundagaa nannu champe magaadinka puttaledu mama".10. Saaho:* "Galli lo six evadaina kodathaadu... kani stadium lo kottevaadike, oka range untadi...".* "evaru vaallu.. na fans antha violent gaa unnaru die-hard fans".                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ˝ û˝                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 çÅ"!5Å713Ç ïc95149948772026-10-22T12:53:04ZTwo Brothers Among Three School Students Killed As Truck Hits Motorcycle In MP's DharFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/indore/two-brothers-among-three-school-students-killed-as-truck-hits-motorcycle-in-mps-dharengIndiaø‘‘‘‘‘‘‘Three school students, including two brothers, were killed after a trailer truck hit their motorcycle on Mahendra Bridge in Madhya Pradesh's Pithampur on Thursday. The victims, identified as Priyansh Rajak (13), Moksh Rajak (10) and Ayushi Rajak (10), were returning home from Saint Francis School. Priyansh was riding the motorcycle. Police reached the spot and informed their families.Dhar (Madhya Pradesh): Three school students, including two brothers, were killed after a trailer truck hit their motorcycle in Madhya Pradesh's Pithampur industrial town in Dhar district on Thursday, police said.The accident occurred on Mahendra Bridge on the Mhow-Neemuch road under the jurisdiction of the Sector-1 police station in Pithampur, about 50 km from the Dhar district headquarters.The three students were returning home from Saint Francis School on a motorcycle when they came under the truck and died, Pithampur police Station House Officer Sunil Sharma told PTI.After being alerted about the accident, police immediately dispatched a team to the spot, he said.The deceased were identified as Priyansh Rajak (13), a Class 9 student, his younger brother Moksh Rajak (10), a Class 5 student, and Ayushi Rajak (10), also a Class 5 student, police said. Priyansh was riding the motorcycle.Police completed the identification process and informed the families about the tragedy.ä^Å!!5y1CÇ ë95149949342026-10-22T12:53:10ZBody of missing youth recovered from well in HazaribagThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/ranchi/body-of-missing-youth-recovered-from-well-in-hazaribag/articleshow/135119657.cmsengIndiaø—QQQQQRHazaribag: The body of a 24-year-old man who had been missing for four days was recovered from a well under Mufassil police station limits on Thursday morning. The deceased, identified as Ujjwal Paswan, was a resident of Odia village under Sadar block.According to family members, Paswan left home on his motorcycle on the evening of Durga Puja Ashtami and did not return. His phone was found switched off, prompting the family to search for him before lodging a missing person complaint with the police.Locals spotted his motorcycle parked near Bocho Bridge at Babhanway village on Thursday morning. A search of the area led to the discovery of his body in a nearby well.A police team led by Mufassil OC Mukesh Singh reached the spot, recovered the body and sent it to Sheikh Bhikhari Medical College and Hospital for post-mortem examination.Singh said, "The exact cause of death would be known only after the post-mortem report is received. Police have launched an investigation and are examining all possible angles to establish the sequence of events leading to the youth's death."   Ü Ü                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            îvÅ#!5Å%%Åy •S95149929042026-10-22T12:51:29ZUltraviolette X47 Venom Price in India, Specifications and Features RevealedLatestLYlatestly.comhttps://www.latestly.com/auto/ultraviolette-x47-venom-price-in-india-specifications-and-features-revealed-7653417.htmlengIndia?Ãúúúúú°Ultraviolette launched the X47 Venom electric motorcycle in India at an introductory price starting at INR 2,65,000. Based on the new VX-100 platform, it features up to an 11 kWh battery with a 343 km IDC range, 39.5 bhp output, radar-based ADAS, and 12 kW DC fast-charging capabilities.Ultraviolette Automotive has launched its new high-performance electric motorcycle, the Ultraviolette X47 Venom, in India with introductory prices starting at INR 2,65,000. Built on the company's next-generation VX-100 architecture, the motorcycle debuts as a lighter and more technologically advanced platform designed to enhance daily riding dynamics and track capabilities.The electric sportbike adopts an aggressive aerodynamic fairing layout complemented by a sharp front cowl design and a streamlined tail section. Alongside its revised physical profile, the vehicle brings notable upgrade features, including a lightweight structural chassis, a high-capacity SRB-11 battery pack supporting rapid DC charging, a integrated dual-camera setup, and an advanced radar-based driver assistance safety system. Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP Price in India, Specifications and Features Revealed.Ultraviolette X47 Venom Specifications and FeaturesThe Ultraviolette X47 Venom is built on the new VX-100 platform with a kerb weight of 180 kg and is powered by an electric motor generating 39.5 bhp and 550 Nm of peak wheel torque. It offers two battery configurations utilising the SRB-11 battery system, including a 7.5 kWh unit providing a claimed IDC range of 227 km and an 11 kWh pack delivering up to 343 km of IDC range.The flagship variant accelerates from 0 to 100 km/h in 5.9 seconds and achieves a top speed of 155 km/h, with the battery supporting DC fast charging up to 12 kW. Equipment includes a 7-inch TFT touchscreen display, front and rear cameras, and an Advanced Driver Assistance Systems (ADAS) suite featuring Blind Spot Monitoring, Lane Change Assist, Rear Collision Warning, and Overtake Alert. Ducati Hypermotard V2 Price in India, Specifications and Features Revealed.Ultraviolette X47 Venom Price in IndiaThe Ultraviolette X47 Venom starts at an introductory price of INR 2,65,000 for the base 7.5 kWh variant, while the X47 Venom+ is priced at INR 3,15,000. The higher-range 11 kWh variants are offered as the X47 Recon at INR 3,75,000 and the top-spec X47 Venom Recon+ at INR 3,99,900.   	I 	I                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ç3Å$%5Å)9/Ç# ïub-95149919702026-10-22T12:50:52ZTiger Shroff's Team Reveals Gunpowder Burn Marks, Warns Trolls of Legal ActionThe Sentinel Newspapersentinelassam.comhttps://www.sentinelassam.com/north-east-india-news/assam-news/tiger-shroffs-team-reveals-gunpowder-burn-marks-warns-trolls-of-legal-actionengIndiaø öööööúTeam releases proof of injuries following the Juhu shooting incident and addresses online skepticismDays after surviving a terrifying shooting attempt, Bollywood action star Tiger Shroff's representation has shared visual proof of his injuries to counter growing online skepticism.On Thursday, Team Tiger Shroff posted an Instagram video captioned "God is Kind," revealing small, red, dot-like gunpowder burn marks scattered across the actor's arm.The post comes after internet trolls questioned the authenticity of the attack, pointing to recent pictures where Shroff appeared seemingly unmarked just two days after heavily bandaged photos went viral.Addressing the malicious rumors, the actor's team issued a stern warning: "Those creating or circulating misleading content could face legal consequences." They added that they are actively taking cognisance of these instances and reserve the right to pursue full legal remedies, urging the public to rely strictly on verified updates.The underlying incident transpired on October 18 when three motorcycle-borne assailants opened fire on Shroff's car outside a Juhu football ground.While the actor escaped gunshot wounds -- sustaining minor injuries from gunpowder and shattered glass -- his driver and a fan were injured.Kota Police in Rajasthan have since arrested three suspects, who have been handed over to the Mumbai Police.   1 1                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       óKÅ%15ÅÅY ´-2026-10-13191450032026-10-22T12:40:56ZUltraviolette X-47 Venom Launched At Rs 2.65 Lakh; Gets 343 Km RangeNDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/auto/ultraviolette-x-47-venom-launched-at-rs-2-65-lakh-gets-343-km-range-12220636engIndia?¿êêêêêèUltraviolette X-47 Venom is lighter, is based on a new platform, and now offers a range of up to 343 km on a single charge.Ultraviolette has launched the X-47 Venom electric motorcycle in India at an introductory price of Rs 2.65 lakh for the first 5,000 units, with the regular starting price set at Rs 3 lakh. Bookings open today, October 22, with deliveries scheduled to begin in November 2026.New VX-100 PlatformThe X-47 Venom is the first motorcycle built on Ultraviolette's new VX-100 100V architecture, which will also underpin future products. The platform brings changes to the battery, motor and controller aimed at improving efficiency and reducing weight.The motorcycle weighs 180 kg, making it up to 20 kg lighter than the previous generation. The new battery pack is 15 per cent lighter with 25 per cent higher energy density, while an axial cooling arrangement replaces the earlier radial setup, offering twice the cooling performance.Battery And PerformanceThe X-47 Venom will be available with 7 kWh and 11 kWh battery packs. The larger SRB-11 pack offers 11 kWh of usable capacity and a claimed IDC range of 343 km, though range for the entry-level 7 kWh version hasn't been detailed yet.The motor produces 30 kW (about 40 bhp) and 550 Nm of torque at the wheel. Ultraviolette claims 0-60 kmph in 2.7 seconds, 0-100 kmph in 5.9 seconds and a top speed of 155 kmph. The platform supports DC fast charging at up to 12 kW, alongside a 1.6 kW onboard charger.Safety And FeaturesThe X-47 Venom features Ultraviolette's Hypersense system, using a 77 GHz rear radar with a claimed monitoring distance of up to 200 metres. Functions include blind-spot monitoring, lane-change assistance, overtake alerts and rear-collision warnings, with hazard lights activating when a threat is detected from behind.A new 7-inch touchscreen running Interface X forms the centre of the cockpit, with onboard Mappls navigation, rear-camera park assist and cruise control. Connected features include software updates and VIOLETTE AI alerts for movement, falls, towing and crashes.ColoursThe X-47 Venom will be offered in Afterburner Yellow, Turbo Red, Cosmic Black and Stellar White. Ultraviolette has also announced extendable warranty coverage of up to 8,00,000 km, with detailed terms and eligibility still to be clarified. Alongside the motorcycle, the company showcased its B-MAX safety vest, claiming 86 per cent force attenuation and reusability up to five times, though pricing hasn't been specified.Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the worldUltraviolette X-47 Venom, Ultraviolette, Electric Vehicle    ñ  ñ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       