pprehended a juvenile in connection with the attack.The incident took place on October 16. According to police, the complainant, who works as a village watchman, alleged that his wife and son were on their way to their plot when Sachin, a resident of the village, parked his motorcycle in front of them and started arguing with them."When the watchman went to Sachin's house to raise the issue, another argument broke out between them, police said. Later, when the complainant and his family reached near their house, Sachin and some of his associates allegedly arrived there and assaulted the four family members with sticks. They also threatened to kill them, according to the complaint," a police officer said.Police received information about the fight on October 16 and reached the spot, but neither party was present. The team later learnt that some injured people had been admitted to a hospital.Doctors initially declared them unfit to give statements, following which the police recorded the complainant's statement on October 18 and registered a case at Sector 65 police station.During the investigation, police found that the accused had a plot opposite the complainant's house, where he allegedly dumped garbage. An argument over the dumping of waste is suspected to have triggered the assault, police said.A police team arrested Hemu (45) and Tal Singh (75), both residents of Naya Behrampur, and Rinku (28), a Faridabad resident currently living in Naya Behrampur, along with a juvenile, from Sector 65 on October 22.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              èhÅ'!5Å913Å} ö}95149756722026-10-22T12:40:03ZAligarh Hit-And-Run: Audi Runs Over Confectioner Twice, Murder Case Registered - VIDEOFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/india/aligarh-hit-and-run-audi-runs-over-confectioner-twice-murder-case-registered-videoengIndiaø’UUUUUWA man was killed in Uttar Pradesh's Aligarh on Tuesday after a white Audi car rammed a bike and ran over two men while fleeing the spot after the accident. The accident was captured on CCTV cameras, and footage of the fatal accident has gone viral on social media.The footage purportedly shows a speeding Audi car hitting the victim's motorcycle before running over him and the two-wheeler again while driving away.Driver allegedly flees after collisionThe incident took place under the jurisdiction of Bannadevi police station. Following the collision, the driver allegedly attempted to flee the spot as local residents tried to stop the car. Some people reportedly threw stones at the vehicle in anger, but the driver managed to escape.Police have registered a case under the murder charge in connection with the incident and launched an investigation into the circumstances surrounding the death.Police trace Audi with Uttarakhand registrationDuring the investigation, police traced a white Audi bearing a Uttarakhand registration number on Thursday morning. The vehicle was subsequently brought to the police station after its identity was established.According to the investigation, the car is registered in the name of Chaudhary Devraj Singh, a BJP leader and former district party president.Vehicle seized, driver's identity under investigationPolice have seized the vehicle and taken into custody a person reported to be its driver. However, authorities have not yet confirmed who was behind the wheel at the time of the fatal incident.Investigators are examining CCTV footage and other technical evidence to establish the identity of the person driving the car when the confectioner was hit.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     óaÅ(!5Åa%Ç? ™/95149721252026-10-22T12:37:26ZIs Honda Motra making a comeback? Patent hints at petrol and electric versions of iconic 1980s bike | Mintmintlivemint.comhttps://www.livemint.com/auto-news/is-honda-motra-making-a-comeback-patent-hints-at-petrol-and-electric-versions-of-iconic-1980s-bike-11792671058992.htmlengIndia? öööööòHonda may revive its 1982 CT50 Motra, with patent drawings showing petrol and electric versions featuring its signature boxy design, chunky tyres and luggage racks. However, Honda has not confirmed a comeback or a production launch.Could Honda revive one of its most unusual motorcycles, the CT50 Motra, more than four decades after it first went on sale? Yes, if reports are to be believed.According to a recent patent drawings, the Japanese manufacturer may be exploring a modern interpretation of the 1980s model, although Honda has not officially confirmed a comeback.According to Australian Motorcycle News (AMCN), which reported on the patent designs, the proposed motorcycle could be offered with either a petrol engine or an electric powertrain.First launched in Japan in 1982, the CT50 Motra was designed as a recreational motorcycle with a rugged, utilitarian appearance. It was powered by a 49cc Super Cub-derived engine and featured a three-speed gearbox alongside a separate high/low range selector, giving it six effective gear ratios.Production ended in 1983, according to reports.The drawings show that the design is starkly similar to the classic two-wheeler from the 1980s. It shows the compact, boxy design associated with the original Motra and include chunky tyres and luggage racks at the front and rear.It depicts three possible configurations: a petrol-powered version, an electric version with a removable battery and another electric version with a fixed battery.The petrol-powered design features a single-cylinder engine and transmission layout resembling the units used in Honda's C125 Super Cub, Monkey and MSX125/Grom motorcycles.However, the patent does not specify the proposed Motra's final engine capacity, power output or gearing.The electric version adopts a different design, with a battery pack placed where the petrol model's engine would sit. It also uses a swingarm with an integrated electric motor, unlike the conventional swingarm depicted in the combustion-engine version.Honda has not confirmed whether the designs will enter production or whether any eventual model would be marketed under the Motra name.Why was the original Honda Motra discontinued?The Motra was designed to carry loads at low speeds rather than prioritise speed. According to reports, it was typically used in camping areas and for practical transport over uneven terrain.The original Motra reportedly fell well short of Honda's sales expectations. Motra, which could only sold around a tenth of projected sales targets of around 45,000 per year.Despite its limited commercial run, the Motra has since developed a following among enthusiasts and collectors.   Â Â                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           äÅ)!5Å!Ç ê95149622892026-10-22T12:30:51Z2 brothers among 3 school students killed as truck hits motorcycle in MPNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/agency-feeds/2-brothers-among-3-school-students-killed-as-truck-hits-motorcycle-in-mp-10393258.htmlengIndiaø€€€€€€€Dhar (MP), Oct 22 (PTI) Three school students, including two brothers, were killed after a trailer truck hit their motorcycle in Madhya Pradesh's Pithampur industrial town in Dhar district on Thursday, police said.The accident occurred on Mahendra Bridge on the Mhow-Neemuch road located under the Sector-1 police station limits in Pithampur, about 50 km from the Dhar district headquarters.The three students were returning home from their Saint Francis School on a motorcycle when they came under the truck and died, Pithampur police station house Officer Sunil Sharma told PTI.After the police were alerted about the accident, a team was dispatched to the spot immediately, he said.The deceased were identified as Priyansh Rajak (13), a Class 9 student, his younger brother Moksh Rajak (10), a Class 5 student, and Ayushi Rajak (10), also from Class 5, the police said, adding that Priyansh was riding the motorbike.Police completed the identification process and informed the families about the tragedy. PTI COR LAL NP                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    ôbÅ*!5Ç %-Çc ≠O95149586882026-10-22T12:27:32ZTiger Shroff firing case: New CCTV shows accused leaving Andheri hotel with blue bag allegedly carrying gun- Moneycontrol.comMoneyControlmoneycontrol.comhttps://www.moneycontrol.com/entertainment/tiger-shroff-firing-case-new-cctv-shows-accused-leaving-andheri-hotel-with-blue-bag-allegedly-carrying-gun-article-14057856.htmlengIndiaø’’’’’’÷Fresh CCTV footage has reportedly emerged in the Tiger Shroff firing case, showing three alleged attackers leaving a hotel in Mumbai's Andheri area on October 18. According to footage, one suspect was seen carrying a blue bag believed to contain a pistol, while two others departed on a yellow Pulsar motorcycle. The footage could provide important clues about the preparations made before the attack. A new development has emerged in the investigation into the firing at Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area. Exclusive CCTV footage obtained by news portals eportedly shows three accused leaving an Andheri hotel hours before the October 18 shooting. The footage is believed to capture the suspects' movements before they allegedly travelled towards the football ground where Tiger was targeted. According to the CCTV footage was recorded outside an Andheri hotel on Sunday, October 18. The recording reportedly shows one of the accused leaving the premises at approximately 4:12 pm, carrying a blue bag suspected to contain a pistol. A minute later, at around 4:13 pm, two other accused were allegedly seen departing on a yellow Pulsar motorcycle. Investigators are examining the footage to establish the suspects' movements and determine whether the bag contained a firearm. The exact contents of the bag have not yet been independently confirmed. According to the report, the three individuals travelled towards a football ground in Juhu, where the firing occurred later that evening. The attack took place when Tiger was reportedly leaving after playing football. Also Read: Salman Khan arrives amid heavy security at IIFA press conference in Mumbai, hugs Kareena Kapoor Khan as duo poses together Unidentified gunmen opened fire at his vehicle, injuring his driver and another person present nearby. Tiger escaped without a gunshot wound. The latest CCTV footage could help police reconstruct the events leading up to the shooting and verify the route allegedly taken by the attackers. Meanwhile, three key accused arrested in connection with the firing were brought to Mumbai from Kota, Rajasthan, on Wednesday, October 21. They have been identified as Rehan alias Sukka from Sonipat, Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai, Bihar; and Phool Singh from Haryana. A Mumbai magistrate's court remanded the three accused to police custody until October 31. During the hearing, investigators sought 14 days' custody to recover the firearms allegedly used in the attack and establish the motive behind the shooting. Police also informed the court that two mobile phones had reportedly been destroyed. Investigators are working to recover call records and other electronic evidence. The Mumbai Crime Branch is examining the CCTV footage, alleged weapons trail and communications between the suspects to determine whether others were involved in planning the attack. &nbsp;   T ET                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        †IÅ,!5s'-ÅM ΩG95149545832026-10-22T12:24:34ZUltraviolette X-47 Venom launched from Rs 2.65 lakhAutocar Indiaautocarindia.comhttps://www.autocarindia.com/bike-news/ultraviolette-x-47-venom-launched-from-rs-265-lakh-441111engIndia?»òòòòòóFirst UV product to be powered by the new high voltage architecture VX100 platform.Bengaluru-based Ultraviolette Automotive, has revealed the brand-new VX100 platform that will power all of its future vehicles. The company has also launched the very f   ìó7Å+%5Å{Å#'Ç ®eb-95149569502026-10-22T12:26:25ZSupriya Sule Questions How Jailed Lawrence Bishnoi Could Claim Responsibility for Tiger Shroff Firing - Yes Punjab NewsYesPunjab ‚Äì No.1 News-Portal. Latest News from Punjab, India & the World.yespunjab.comhttps://yespunjab.com/supriya-sule-questions-how-jailed-lawrence-bishnoi-could-claim-responsibility-for-tiger-shroff-firing/engIndiaø◊WWWWWXMumbai, October 22, 2026 (Yes Punjab News)Nationalist Congress Party (Sharadchandra Pawar) MP Supriya Sule on Thursday questioned how jailed gangster Lawrence Bishnoi could plan an attack and claim responsibility for it on social media following the firing incident targeting Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff in Mumbai.Sule said it was difficult to understand how a person lodged in jail could publicly claim responsibility for a crime through social media posts. She called for an inquiry into the matter, expressing concern over the alleged intimidation of people."I was surprised because your news channels and newspapers say that Lawrence Bishnoi is in jail. Yet, he is tweeting himself and declaring, 'I take responsibility for this.' It is hard to comprehend how a person inside a jail can take responsibility like this. It is very confusing. Given how everyone is being intimidated, we will demand an inquiry into how someone sitting inside a jail can do all this," Sule said.Meanwhile, the Mumbai Police Crime Branch on Thursday brought four more accused -- two women, Radha and Babita, and two men, Kunal and Sumit -- to Killa Court on transit remand in connection with the case.According to police sources, the accused had allegedly practised shooting at a location near Mumbai before the attack. A misfire reportedly occurred while they were testing the weapon in their hotel room in Andheri.Reports also suggested that the accused had initially considered targeting another Bollywood celebrity. However, when they allegedly found it difficult to reach their intended target, they decided to target Tiger Shroff instead.The accused reportedly learnt through social media reels shared by the actor's fans that he did not have police protection at the time. They allegedly took this into account while planning the attack. Preliminary questioning also indicated that the firing was intended to spread fear within the film industry.On the evening of October 18, Tiger Shroff narrowly escaped injury after three motorcycle-borne men allegedly opened fire at him in Mumbai's Juhu area. The actor was unharmed, but his driver sustained injuries in the incident.Within hours of the firing, a video clip circulated on social media in which a man identifying himself as Anil Pandit and claiming links to the Lawrence Bishnoi gang took responsibility for the attack. The message allegedly warned Shroff to stop working with Bollywood superstar Salman Khan.The three accused were arrested at Kota railway station in Rajasthan within hours of the incident. The investigation is continuing.    irst motorcycle to be powered by said platform, the X-47 Venom at an introductory price of Rs 2.65 lakh for the entry-level variant with 7.5kWh battery. The highest variant with the 11kwh battery in the new Afterburner Yellow colour costs Rs 4.12 lakh (also introductory).All prices mentioned are ex-showroom, Bengaluru.* Gets a new SRB-11 battery with 11kWh capacity* Cruise control and 7-inch TFT display are other noteworthy features* Introductory prices are applicable only to the first 5,000 buyers; will increase by Rs 35,000 after that* Bookings open now, deliveries starting in NovemberNew platform saves weight and improves range, among othersThe major upgrade on the latest X-47 compared to before has come in the form of weight savings thanks to the improved platform, followed by the range. The base, 7.5kWh variant now weighs 180kg, which is a substantial 17kg lower than the previous X-47 with the 7kWh battery. The top Recon variant with an 11kWh battery, on the other hand, weighs 195kg, 13kg lower than the outgoing X-47 Recon with its 10.3kWh battery. Ultraviolette also claims an additional 20km range, taking the top-variant's claimed range to 343km now. The base variant sees a 16km increase, with a claimed 227km range.The noteworthy improvements are thanks to the new VX100 platform which improves the battery, motor and motor controller. All three are lighter than before, while packing in more energy and also cool down faster as well. The improvements show up in two other areas as well, claims UV, sustained high performance and regen. Ballistic, UV's fastest ride mode, is now available till 10 percent battery charge, as opposed to 30 percent earlier. Regenerative braking, on the other hand, is now available from 99 percent battery charge, as opposed to 90 percent earlier.Elsewhere, the performance figures largely hover around the same numbers. On the Recon variant, peak power is 40hp (0.2hp lower) while peak torque is 90Nm (10Nm lower). Rear wheel torque has gone to 550Nm from 610Nm before. While that sounds like a significant drop, UV's claimed acceleration times have remained unchanged, or improved. The X-47 Venom can accelerate 0-60kph in 2.7s (same as before) and 0-100kph in 5.9s (2.2s faster than before). These claimed performance gains are likely to be down to the weight savings on the latest X-47. Charging times see marginal increases as well, with the standard portable charger (1.3kW) now taking 5 hours and 30 minutes for a 20-80 percent top-up; previously, that would have taken 5 hours. The figures see such marginal increases across all available charging options for the X-47 Venom.On the features front, the X-47 Venom gets three new, noteworthy features: cruise control, camera-powered parking assistance and a larger 7-inch TFT display. Do bear in mind that all three are limited to the top three variants. UV continues to offer rider aids like dual-channel ABS, traction control and dynamic stability control as standard. Higher variants add four levels of traction control, radar-powered UV Hypersense assistance system and an integrated dashcam, among others.Except for the weight, all the other dimensions stay where they were earlier, which means a 820mm seat height, 200mm ground clearance and 1385mm wheelbase. No changes to the brakes or suspension either. The now lighter X-47 Venom is stopped by the same 320mm front disc and 230mm rear disc. Suspending the motorcycle are a 41mm, preload adjustable USD fork and preload adjustable monoshock. Tyre sizes remain the same as well, 110/70R17 at the front and 150/60R17 at the rear. The motorcycle continues to utilise a steel trellis frame.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               	˙ 	˙                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       