silver anklet, Rs 25,000 in cash, around 25 kg of brass and bronze utensils, two LPG cylinders, besides two motorcycles, three mobile phones, and tools used in the crime cases have been seized, police added.   4 4                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          óHÅ.!5Åg13Ç; ©Q95149544482026-10-22T12:24:21ZTiger Shroff's Team Shares Video Of Red Spots On Injured Arms Days After Firing Incident, Posts 'God Is Kind'Free Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/entertainment/tiger-shroffs-team-shares-video-of-red-spots-on-injured-arms-days-after-firing-incident-posts-god-is-kindengIndiaø öööööúTiger Shroff's team shared a video showing marks and red spots on his arms on Thursday, days after gunshots were fired at his car in Mumbai's Juhu. The post carried the caption, "God is kind." Ten people have been arrested so far. The Mumbai Police have named alleged Lawrence Bishnoi gang operative Anil Pandit as a wanted accused in the caseActor Tiger Shroff's team shared a video showing marks on his arms, days after gunshots were fired at his car in Mumbai's Juhu area. The video was posted on Thursday (October 22) on the team's official Instagram page, Team Tiger Shroff, with the caption, "God is kind."The short clip shows several small, dot-like marks and red spots across the actor's arm. The post comes days after the firing incident on Sunday evening, when the actor narrowly escaped a suspected attack while leaving a football ground in Juhu.At least two men allegedly fired at Tiger's car before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped direct gunshot injuries, while his driver sustained a bullet wound and a bystander was also injured.Tiger Shroff Firing Case: Ten Arrested So FarThe Mumbai Police have arrested 10 people in connection with the case so far. Three accused -- Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and residing in Mumbai; and Phool Singh, from Haryana -- were detained at Kota railway station in Rajasthan.Investigators are examining the alleged recruitment network, the movement of weapons and suspected links between the accused and the Lawrence Bishnoi gang.Anil Pandit Named As Wanted AccusedGangster Anil Pandit, an alleged operative of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang who is reportedly based in the United States, has been named as a wanted accused in the case.On Thursday, the Mumbai Police told the Esplanade court that the firing was allegedly carried out at Pandit's behest. Pandit, a native of Haryana's Panipat district, is suspected of operating a criminal network from the US and coordinating with shooters in India. He is also wanted in several alleged extortion and firing cases in Delhi and other locations.An audio clip that surfaced earlier featured a man identifying himself as Pandit and claiming responsibility for the attack on Tiger. The speaker also allegedly threatened people associated with actor Salman Khan.In the purported recording, the man claimed that Tiger had been warned against working with Salman, suggesting that their association was the reason behind the attack. The speaker also issued threats against members of the film industry who work with Salman and those who speak against the Bishnoi gang.   á á                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             öuÅ/!5Å'-Å{ ±_95149497762026-10-22T12:20:30ZDuttapukur showroom owner sent to three days police custodyThe Statesmanthestatesman.comhttps://www.thestatesman.com/cities/kolkata/duttapukur-showroom-owner-sent-to-three-days-police-custody-1503653838.htmlengIndiaøÃúúúúúùA motorcycle showroom owner arrested in connection with the recovery of explosives and suspected prohibited chemicals from a vehicle at Duttapukur in Bengal's North 24-Parganas district was remanded by the Barasat court on Thursday and sent to three days of police custody.The arrest followed a joint operation involving the state police's Special Task Force (STF), the National Investigation Agency (NIA), the National Security Guard (NSG) and forensic personnel at Tentultala on Jessore Road on Wednesday night, when a suspicious vehicle was intercepted.Investigators reportedly recovered around 3 kg of suspected explosive material, approximately 10 kg of splinter material and other suspicious substances from the vehicle.The investigating agencies are examining the nature of the recovered materials, their intended destination and whether there was any plan to use them for a subversive activity. Investigators are also trying to establish their source, identify those who may have been involved in transporting them and determine whether the case has any wider or international links.According to police sources, the STF had prior information about suspicious items being carried in a vehicle in the Tentultala area.Acting on the tip-off, officers kept the vehicle under surveillance before intercepting it on Wednesday night and questioning its owner, Rakibul Islam. Investigators suspect that the materials might have been intended for transportation towards Kolkata, although their precise destination and intended use remain unclear.The recovered articles reportedly included explosive material and metal mesh or rods. Their exact composition and explosive capability will be established through forensic examination.Following Islam's arrest, investigators searched his residence at Bamungachhi and his motorcycle showrooms as part of the probe. The searches are aimed at gathering evidence about the origin of the recovered materials and identifying possible links to other individuals or incidents.Islam reportedly gave up vehicle repair work around a decade ago to set up a motorcycle showroom business. He currently operates four showrooms in areas including Tentultala and Bira in Duttapukur, and Berachampa in Deganga.Investigators are also expected to examine whether there is any connection between the present recovery and an explosion reported several years ago at a motorcycle showroom in Amdanga, whose owner was reportedly Islam. No link between the two incidents has been established so far.Barasat police district superintendent M. Marcy said the investigation was under way and that the recovered material was being examined to determine its nature. Further details, she indicated, would emerge as the investigation progressed.The three-day custody is expected to provide investigators an opportunity to question the accused and pursue leads concerning the source, transportation and intended use of the recovered materials.Meanwhile former BJP state president and state minister Dilip Ghosh said that no subversive activist will be allowed to spread terrorist network as they use to spread during the Trinamool Congress tenure.   ß ß                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             íUÅ0!5ÅE1CÇ[ ü]95149494232026-10-22T12:20:07ZMan kills wife over infidelity suspicion, dumps body in Bengaluru stormwater drain; arrestedThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/bengaluru/man-kills-wife-over-infidelity-suspicion-dumps-body-in-bengaluru-stormwater-drain-arrested/articleshow/135118574.cmsengIndiaø⁄ZZZZZZBENGALURU: Bengaluru police have arrested a 22-year-old migrant labourer fromBihar for allegedly murdering his 25-year-old wife and dumping her body in a stormwater drain over suspicions of infidelity, officials said on Thursday.The accused has been identified as Mohammad Irfaj, while the victim was identified as Ruksana. Both were natives of Bihar, news agency ANI reported.According to police, the couple had married around a year ago. Ruksana was previously married and had a child from her first marriage.The two reportedly fell in love while selling balloons in Bihar and moved to Bengaluru around six months ago, where Irfaj found work at a local garment factory.Police said their relationship had become strained in recent months, with Irfaj suspecting Ruksana of having an affair because she allegedly spoke frequently to someone over the phone. The couple often quarrelled over the issue, ANI reported.The dispute allegedly turned violent on October 10, when Irfaj attacked Ruksana with a stone, killing her on the spot, investigators said. He then allegedly stuffed a piece of cloth into her mouth.To conceal the crime, the accused allegedly broke the handle lock of an unattended motorcycle parked nearby.He stuffed Ruksana's body into a bag, placed it between the handlebars, pushed the vehicle to the Gopalapura drainage area and dumped the body into the stormwater drain.On October 13, the body, wrapped in a plastic cover, was found in the drain. Police were initially unable to identify the victim.The Magadi Road police subsequently formed more than 10 teams to conduct extensive door-to-door verification and cross-check recent missing person complaints in the locality, ANI reported.During the inquiry, local residents informed police that a woman living in Gopalapura had been missing for several days. This led to Irfaj being questioned.According to police, the accused allegedly confessed during interrogation.Further investigation is underway, and more details are awaited.(With agency inputs)   Ó ﬂÓ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  °?Å2%5kÅ'#Å? æMb-95149467042026-10-22T12:18:04ZForget futuristic, This EV is busy being usefulLatest Odisha News, Breaking News Today | Top Updates on Corona - OTV Englishodishatv.inhttps://odishatv.in/business/auto/forget-futuristic-this-ev-is-busy-being-useful-12738852engIndia?∑Discover the E-Went Foxy electric scooter, featuring a 160 km claimed range, 36-litre boot, 60 km/h top speed and long-term battery coverage.160 km range. 36litre boot. 150 kg load capacity. 60 km/h.    ôîÅ1!5Ç	%-Çu ¢195149473352026-10-22T12:18:17ZTiger Shroff's team shares video of his injured arms after firing attack amid trolling, writes 'God is kind'- Moneycontrol.comMoneyControlmoneycontrol.comhttps://www.moneycontrol.com/entertainment/bollywood/tiger-shroff-s-team-shares-video-of-his-injured-arms-after-firing-attack-amid-trolling-writes-god-is-kind-article-14057825.htmlengIndiaøƒîîîîîïActor Tiger Shroff's team released a video of his injured arms on Thursday, days after the Bollywood star narrowly survived a gun attack on his car. At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before running off on a motorcycle. The actor managed to escape relatively unhurt, but his driver and a bystander were injured. Team Tiger Shroff, the official Instagram page run by his team, shared the video showing the actor's injured hands. Sharing the video, the team penned in the caption, "God is kind." View this post on Instagram A post shared by Team Tiger Shroff (@teamtigershroff) The short video shows several small, dot-like marks and red spots on his arm. Tiger's injury video came just a day after several social media users alleged that he was faking the injuries. The actor was spotted without a bandage in the photos with minister Ashish Shelar just a few days after the shooting incident. Critics raised doubts about the quick recovery of Tiger Shroff, questioning how his bandages were removed and his injuries healed in just one day. However, the actor's team has now shared a new video showing Tiger's injuries, debunking all the allegations and speculation. Three people have been picked up at the Kota railway station in Rajasthan. They have been identified as Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, who is from Begusarai in Bihar but is staying in Mumbai; and Phool Singh, from Haryana. The Mumbai Police have registered a case against the three in light of an attempt to murder and the Arms Act. For the unversed, Tiger Shroff was targeted in a firing incident on Sunday at around 7 pm when he was heading home after playing a football match. The actor managed to escape the attack, but his driver and an autorickshaw driver sustained injuries. Also Read: Tiger Shroff firing case: Shooters allegedly conducted recce of Ranbir Kapoor's Bandra residence As per preliminary information, three men came on a motorcycle, and while two of them allegedly opened fire, the third waited to help them escape the scene. Videos that have since gone viral apparently show the suspects escaping on the motorcycle.    And a price proposition that makes the usual "premium EV" formula look a little unnecessary.The Indian EV market has a fascination with extremes. Longest range. Fastest acceleration. Biggest screen. Most futuristic design. But somewhere between all those headline numbers, a rather important question gets lost:What does the scooter actually do for you every day? Enter the E-Went Foxy. And it may be interesting precisely because it isn't trying too hard to impress.160 Km Isn't The Only Number HereThe Foxy claims an IDC range of up to 160 km. But E-Went also publishes an ERM -- E-Went Real Mileage -- figure of 130 km, specified for an 80-kg rider at 45 km/h under Indian road conditions.That distinction is important. Because brochure range tells you what a scooter can achieve under a defined test cycle. Real-world range tells you something much closer to what a rider wants to know:"How far can I actually go?"Then E-Went Foxy Does Something Unexpected: It Has A 30-Litre BootThink about the last time you bought groceries on a scooter. Or carried a laptop. Or squeezed a backpack, shopping bags and everyday essentials onto a two-wheeler.Suddenly, boot space doesn't sound like a specification. It sounds like freedom.The Foxy gets 36 litres of boot space and more than 380 mm smart foot space, turning it into something more useful than a simple commuter.It is a small detail with a big implication the scooter is designed around your life not the other way around.India Doesn't Ride On Perfect Roads. Neither Does FoxyPotholes. Monsoon water. Dust. Heat. Stop-start traffic. Uneven surfaces. India doesn't exactly make life easy for a two-wheeler.Foxy responds with a steel tubular chassis, hydraulic front and rear suspension, while its motor and smart controller carry an IP67 rating and the lithium battery an IP67 rating.The message is straightforward don't build an EV for the showroom. Build it for the road outside it.Practical Doesn't Have To Mean BoringUnderneath the Foxy sits a 12-inch BLDC hub motor, producing 2.8 kW peak and 2 kW continuous power. It has a claimed 60 km/h top speed, three riding modes Eco, Ride and Power and more than 250 kg loading capacity.Then come the details riders actually notice Reverse mode.Dual LED projector headlamps with a claimed 35 metre illumination distance.Individually, none of these is revolutionary. Together, they reveal something more interesting Someone has been thinking about what happens after you leave the showroom.And Then There's The BatteryThis might be the most important part of the story. E-Went treats the battery as a Complete Power System, combining premium Samsung Lithium Cells, Smart BMS technology and Bluetooth diagnostics designed to monitor battery health and cell status.And then comes the number worth noticing 1,300 CHARGE CYCLESE-Went's 2.5 kWh battery is specified with a 4-year/55,000-km warranty and 1,300 charge cycles. The 1.8 kWh battery carries a 3-year/45,000-km warranty and 1,100 cycles, with the applicable milestone being whichever comes first.That shifts the EV conversation. Not just: "How far can it go today?"But "How confidently will the battery keep performing tomorrow?"The Biggest Surprise May Be What Happens After You Buy ItE-Went says it now has 20,000+ vehicles on Indian roads, a 250+ dealer network across seven states, and a warranty claim rate below 1.5% over three years.For Foxy specifically, the listed warranty package includes coverage for the motor, controller, chassis, rusting and battery, subject to their respective time, kilometre or cycle limits.That matters because the most expensive part of buying an EV isn't always the scooter. It's the uncertainty of owning one. And that's exactly what E-Went is tryi                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         O XO                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ÜÅ4%5Å+%%ÅG àb-95144344192026-10-22T12:16:43ZSeptember 2026: Indian Motorcycle & Scooter Sales Figures & Analysis | Team-BHPTeam-BHP.comteam-bhp.comhttps://www.team-bhp.com/news/september-2026-indian-motorcycle-scooter-sales-figures-analysisengIndiaø™!Only bikes that sell 500+ units (and thus, the relevant ones) have been included in the gainers & losers chart.NOTES:1: Thanks to the team at Auto Punditz for sharing these sales numbers with us!2: Only bikes that sell 500+ units (and thus, the relevant ones) have been included in the gainers & losers chart.3. These manufacturer-reported sales numbers are factory dispatches to dealerships. They are NOT retail sales figures to end customers.Check out BHPian comments for more insights and information.ì$Å3%5Å?)Åg ¢b-95149454382026-10-22T12:17:00ZThree schoolchildren killed as trolley hits motorcycle in MP's PithampurBhaskar Live English Newsbhaskarlive.inhttps://bhaskarlive.in/others/three-schoolchildren-killed-as-trolley-hits-motorcycle-in-mps-pithampur-2155982engIndiaø””””””’Dhar, Oct 22 (IANS) Three schoolchildren, including two brothers and their cousin sister, were killed after a speeding trolley hit their motorcycle in Madhya Pradesh's industrial town Pithampur on Thursday, police said.The accident occurred on the Mhow-Neemuch Highway near Mahendra Bridge, close to St. Francis School, under the Sector-1 police station area.The deceased were identified as Priyansh, a Class 9 student, his younger brother Moksh, who studied in Class 5, and their cousin sister Aarushi, a Class 7 student.All three were residents of Utkarsh Angan Colony in Pithampur.According to preliminary police information, Priyansh had not attended school on Thursday.However, he went on his motorcycle in the afternoon to bring his younger brother and cousin sister home after their classes ended.The three were returning home on motorcycle number MP 40 ML 4037 when a speeding trolley hit their vehicle near St. Francis School.All three died on the spot due to the impact, police said.Following the accident, family members and local residents staged a protest by placing one of the deceased children's bodies on the road.The protest disrupted traffic in the area as people gathered at the accident site.Local residents told the police about the accident, following which a team reached the spot.The bodies were sent to Pithampur Civil Hospital for post-mortem examination, and the families were informed about the deaths.The trolley driver fled from the spot after the accident, police said, adding that a case had been registered against him under relevant provisions of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita and the Motor Vehicles Act.Efforts were underway to trace and arrest him.Traffic on the Mhow-Neemuch Highway was disrupted for some time following the accident and the gathering of residents.It was restored after the damaged motorcycle was removed from the road, police said.Further investigation is underway, and statements of eyewitnesses are being recorded.The deaths of the three children have left their family and residents of Utkarsh Angan Colony and surrounding areas in shock and mourning.Created On : &nbsp 22 Oct 2026 5:42 PM IST    π  π                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               êCÅ5%5Å%ÅE ù3b-95149341992026-10-22T12:09:07ZHonda CBR500R FOUR Arrives In Europe: Key Highlights - OverdriveOverdriveoverdrive.inhttps://www.overdrive.in/news-cars-auto/honda-cbr500r-four-arrives-in-europe-key-highlights/engIndia?ø After its debut in the Chinese market, the Honda CBR500R FOUR has now made its way to Europe, as its newest inline four middleweight super sport class motorcycle. It packs in a brand new engine that revs up to 11,000 rpm, features a sharp design, and comes loaded with tech. Here are its five key highlights:Honda CBR500R FOUR EngineThe biggest talking point of the new Honda CBR500 R FOUR is its brand new 502 cc inline four engine. This mill produces 72 PS at a whopping 11,000 rpm, and 47.4 Nm at 9,750 rpm. The engine comes mated to 6-speed gearbox, and it will work in tandem with Honda's E-clutch technology, which will allow for clutchless operation.Honda CBR500R FOUR FeaturesThe new CBR500 R FOUR comes equipped with a 5-inch TFT display with the Honda RoadSync smartphone connectivity available as standard. There are three ride modes on offer: Standard, Sport and Urban, along with two custom modes as per the rider's preference wherein one can control parameters like engine power, engine braking, and traction control.Honda CBR500R FOUR SpecificationsHonda has gone for a relatively simpler, and conventional, diamond-type steel frame chassis with the CBR500 R FOUR. Suspension duties are carried out by a non-adjustable 41 mm USD fork, and a pre-load adjustable rear monoshock, both from KYB. It rides on 17-inch wheels shod with Pirelli Diablo Rosso IV tyres.Honda CBR500R FOUR DesignThe Honda CBR500R looks like a typical CBR, but with an added flair. The fairing is sharper now, and upping its appearance are those sleek LED projector headlamps. It will be available in two shades: Ignition Red and Mat Ballistic Black Metallic.Honda CBR500R FOUR India LaunchThe Honda CBR500R FOUR is priced at ¬£6,999 in the UK, which translates to Rs 8.89 lakh in Indian Rupees. However, it is highly unlikely that Honda would bring this bike to India.    ä  ä                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                êrÅ6%5ÅIO)g ûb-95149311432026-10-22T12:06:54ZNagpur Records 2,021 Vehicle Registrations in 22 Days; AK Gandhi Auto Tops Two-Wheeler DealersNagpur Today - Its Where You Livenagpurtoday.inhttps://www.nagpurtoday.in/?p=140737488904888engIndia?ƒîîîîîòNagpur: Nagpur recorded 2,021 vehicle registrations between October 1 and October 22, according to dealer-wise data from the Nagpur Regional Transport Office (RTO), MH-31. The report shows that 1,851 vehicles were registered with e-KYC, while 170 registrations were completed without e-KYC.The data covers multiple vehicle categories, including motorcycles and scooters, motor cars, tractors, mopeds and construction equipment vehicles, providing a snapshot of the city's vehicle registration activity during the first 22 days of October.AK Gandhi Auto Leads Two-Wheeler RegistrationsAK Gandhi Auto Private Limited emerged as the leading two-wheeler dealer in the report, recording 126 registrations. Blue Mobility Ventures Private Limited followed with 109, while Saidynamic Autowheels LLP secured third place with 64 registrations.The top three dealers together accounted for 299 two-wheeler registrations, highlighting their strong presence in Nagpur's two-wheeler market during the period.Province Automobiles Tops Motor-Car DealersIn the motor-car category, Province Automobiles Co. recorded 40 registrations, followed by Jaika Motors Pvt. Ltd. with 34. Aryodaya Autostar Pvt. Ltd. ranked third with 24 registrations.The three dealers together recorded 98 motor-car registrations during the period.E-KYC Accounts for Most RegistrationsOf the 2,021 registrations recorded, 1,851 were completed with e-KYC, accounting for approximately 91.6% of the total. The remaining 170 registrations, or around 8.4%, were recorded without e-KYC.The dealer-wise report offers a glimpse into the competitive landscape of Nagpur's automobile market, with two-wheeler dealers accounting for substantial volumes among the listed businesses.The figures relate to registrations recorded by the RTO between October 1 and October 22, 2026, and should be distinguished from independently measured vehicle sales.   ¬ ¬                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        î:Å7!5i1CÅ{ §e95149299822026-10-22T12:06:11ZCouple running tea shop shot dead in BhagalpurThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/patna/couple-running-tea-shop-shot-dead-in-bhagalpur/articleshow/135118444.cmsengIndiaø‘TTTTTTPatna: A couple running a tea and snacks shop was shot dead by unidentified assailants in Bhagalpur district early Thursday.The incident took place in Hatia area under Ismailpur police station. The deceased, identified as Ranjan Mandal (40) and his wife, Kiran Devi (35), were found dead at their shop on Thursday morning.The couple is survived by two children, aged around 16 and 14 years. The motive behind the killings remains under investigation, police said.According to their son, Madan Kumar, three men arrived on a motorcycle late at night and asked his father for snacks. When Ranjan refused, citing the late hour, the assailants allegedly opened fire."The criminals fired around 10 rounds. One bullet hit my father in the eye, while two bullets struck my mother," Madan alleged.He further alleged that the family called Dial-112, but the police arrived nearly half an hour later. "When we reached the police station, my parents were still breathing. We requested an ambulance, but the policemen told us to take them to hospital in an e-rickshaw," he claimed.Naugachia SDPO Saiyam Raza, however, dismissed the allegations of police negligence as baseless.He said he had personally arranged an ambulance to transport the bodies.There were discrepancies in the accounts of the timing of the incident and the injuries sustained by the couple. Madan placed the incident between 3 am and 3:30 am, while the SDPO said it occurred between 4:10 am and 4:25 am.According to the SDPO, Ranjan sustained two bullet injuries, one in the eye and another below the shoulder, while Kiran was shot in the lower abdomen.The case has taken another turn with the reported disappearance of the couple's two-and-a-half-year-old niece, Pallavi Kumari, who has been missing for two days. The family lodged a police complaint on Oct 19 and had been searching for the child. Police are yet to establish whether her disappearance is connected to the killings.Police teams from Ismailpur and Gopalpur inspected the spot, and a forensic science laboratory team was called to collect evidence."One suspect, identified as Saurabh Mandal, has been arrested and is being questioned, while efforts are underway to trace the other assailants," the SDPO said.Angry villagers initially refused to allow the bodies to be taken away but relented after police intervention.   N N                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    ì.Å8!5Å-3Ç ¢#95149297122026-10-22T12:05:58ZFour Accused in Tiger Shroff Car Firing Case Remanded to Police CustodyDeccan Chronicledeccanchronicle.comhttps://www.deccanchronicle.com/nation/crime/four-accused-in-tiger-shroff-car-firing-case-remanded-to-police-custody-1997876engIndiaø·qqqqqrA Mumbai court remands four accused, including two women, till October 26 over allegations of procuring and transporting firearms used in the Juhu shooting.A magistrate court in Mumbai on Thursday remanded four accused, including two women, to police custody till October 26 in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff's car in the Juhu area, officials said.The accused, identified as Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh, were apprehended in Delhi and brought to Mumbai before being produced in court.Seeking their custody, Mumbai Police told the court that the accused had allegedly played an active role in the conspiracy alongside those arrested earlier. According to the police, they supplied firearms used in the crime.The prosecution further alleged that two of the accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women allegedly transported the firearms to Mumbai by train and handed them over to the attackers.Opposing the police remand, defence lawyers Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi argued that there was no material evidence against the accused and that they had been arrested on mere suspicion. They contended that custodial interrogation was unwarranted and sought their judicial custody.After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused to police custody till October 26.Firing at JuhuThe incident occurred on Sunday evening when at least two men allegedly fired at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander sustained injuries.According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the vehicle. A motorcycle allegedly used by the shooters was later found abandoned in Andheri. Police have registered a case under provisions relating to attempt to murder and the Arms Act.With the latest arrests, the total number of people arrested in the case has reached 10. On Wednesday, a court remanded three other accused -- Rehan alias Sukka, Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan and Phool Singh -- to police custody till October 31.    ı ¢ ı                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         â)Å:!5Å'Åu éI95149241142026-10-22T12:02:25ZMeghalaya: ED office targeted in fresh petrol bomb attack in ShillongNORTHEAST NOWnenow.inhttps://nenow.in/north-east-news/meghalaya/meghalaya-ed-office-targeted-in-fresh-petrol-bomb-attack-in-shillong.htmlengIndiaøœüüüüü°Guwahati: Two masked men riding a motorcycle allegedly threw a petrol bomb at the building housing Meghalaya's Enforcement Directorate (ED) office in Shillong early Thursday, October 22.Police said this was the second reported attack on a government establishment in the city in two days.The incident occurred at the ED premises in Shillong's Langkyrding area.Superintendent of Police Vivek Syiem confirmed that the building sustained no structural damage and that the security guard inside discovered the incident on Thursday morning.Investigators are analysing local CCTV footage to identify the perpetrators and trace the motorcycle used in the attack as a formal case is registered.The strike follows similar petrol bomb incidents targeting government facilities in Laitumkhrah, Keating Road, and Kench's Trace.Security patrols and citywide surveillance have been intensified as police investigate the pattern.îZÅ9!5Å#)ÇC £m95149288192026-10-22T12:05:20ZNot Possible For Jailed Person To Plan Attack And Claim Responsibility On Social Media: Supriya Sule On Tiger Shroff CaseOmmcom Newsommcomnews.comhttps://ommcomnews.com/india-news/not-possible-for-jailed-person-to-plan-attack-and-claim-responsibility-on-social-media-supriya-sule-on-tiger-shroff-case/engIndiaø“RRRRRSMumbai: Responding to the firing incident targeting Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff, for which jailed gangster Lawrence Bishnoi has claimed responsibility, Nationalist Congress Party (SP) MP Supriya Sule said on Thursday that no jailed person can plan an attack and then take responsibility and post it on social media.Sule said, "I was surprised because your news channels and newspapers say that Lawrence Bishnoi is in jail. Yet, he is tweeting himself and declaring, 'I take responsibility for this.' It is hard to comprehend how a person inside a jail can take responsibility like this. It is very confusing. Given how everyone is being intimidated, we will demand an inquiry into how someone sitting inside a jail can do all this."On Thursday, Mumbai Police Crime Branch brought in four more accused, two women, Radha and Babita, and Kunal and Sumit, to Killa Court on transit remand in connection with the case.Meanwhile, police sources revealed that the accused practised shooting at a location near Mumbai before the attack. A misfire also reportedly occurred while they were testing the weapon in their hotel room in Andheri.Reportedly, the accused actually had another Bollywood celebrity in mind. However, as per the reports, when the accused were unable to easily reach their initially planned target, they decided to target Tiger Shroff instead.The accused reportedly learned through social media reels shared by Tiger's fans that he did not have police protection at that time, and keeping this in mind, they decided to target him.During the preliminary questioning, it has also been revealed that the attack on Tiger was intended to spread fear in the industry.On 18 October evening, Tiger had a narrow escaped after three motorcycle-borne men opened fire at him in the Juhu area of Mumbai. While the actor did not suffer any injury in the attack, his driver was injured in the incident.Within hours of the incident, a video clip was circulating on social media in which a man claiming to be Anil Pandit from the Lawrence Bishnoi gang took responsibility for the firing and claimed that it was a warning to the actor to stop working with superstar Salman Khan.The three accused were arrested at Kota railway station in Rajasthan within hours of the incident.   M 	M                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 â8Å<!5ÅÅ)ÅK é%95149148562026-10-22T11:55:29ZTiger Shroff's team shares video of his injured arm, says 'God is kind'Odisha News, Odisha Latest news, Odisha Daily - OrissaPOSTorissapost.comhttps://www.orissapost.com/tiger-shroffs-team-shares-video-of-his-injured-arm-says-god-is-kind/engIndiaøƒîîîîîïMumbai: Actor Tiger Shroff's team shared a video of his injured arms Thursday, days after the Hindi film star narrowly survived a gun attack on his car.At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.Team Tiger Shroff, the official Instagram page managed by his team, shared the video along with the caption, "God is kind."The short clip shows several small, dot-like marks and red spots across his arm.Three accused, identified as Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, were detained at Kota railway station in Rajasthan.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.èsÅ;%5Å+5Å úb-95149178662026-10-22T11:57:52ZBengaluru: Bihar man arrested for killing wife, dumping body in drainWebindia123.comnews.webindia123.comhttps://news.webindia123.com/news/articles/India/20261022/4513812.htmlengIndiaø“RRRRRSThe accused has been identified as Mohammad Irfaj, while the victim has been identified as his wife, Ruksana. Both are natives of Bihar.According to police, the couple had married approximately a year ago. Ruksana was previously married and had a child from her first marriage. The duo reportedly fell in love while selling balloons in Bihar and relocated to Bengaluru around six months ago, where Irfaj secured employment at a local garment factory.Police said the marital relationship had turned strained in recent months, as Irfaj suspected Ruksana of having an affair, alleging she was frequently talking to someone on the phone. The couple frequently quarrelled over the same.The dispute reached a violent flashpoint on October 10, when Irfaj allegedly attacked Ruksana with a stone, killing her on the spot, before stuffing a piece of cloth into her mouth, investigators said.To conceal the crime, the accused allegedly broke the handle lock of an unattended motorcycle parked nearby. He then stuffed the victim's body into a bag, placed it between the handlebars, pushed the vehicle to the Gopalapura drainage area, and dumped the body into the stormwater drain.On October 13, the bodywrapped in a plastic coverwas discovered in the drain. Initially, police were unable to identify the victim.The Magadi Road police then constituted more than 10 teams to conduct extensive door-to-door verifications and cross-reference recent missing person complaints in the locality.During the inquiry, local residents alerted the police that a woman residing in Gopalapura had been missing for several days, leading to Irfaj's questioning.As per the police, during the interrogation, the accused allegedly confessed.Further investigation is underway, and more details are awaited. (ANI)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                èvÅ=!5ÅW13Ç öY95149130042026-10-22T11:53:51ZTiger Shroff Firing Case: CCTV Shows Accused Leaving Andheri Hotel 3 Hours Before Juhu Attack | VIDEOFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/tiger-shroff-firing-case-cctv-shows-accused-leaving-andheri-hotel-3-hours-before-juhu-attack-videoengIndiaø‘TTTTTTCCTV footage from RR Residency in Andheri East reportedly shows three accused leaving the hotel around 4.12 pm on October 18, about three hours before the firing incident in Juhu. One allegedly carried a blue bag containing a pistol, while two others left on a Pulsar motorcycle. Their stay in Room No. 201 is now part of the investigation.Mumbai, October 22, 2026: CCTV footage from RR Residency in Andheri East shows the accused in the firing case involving actor Tiger Shroff leaving the hotel about three hours before the attack in Juhu on October 18.The footage, recorded between 4.12 pm and 4.13 pm, shows one of the accused leaving the hotel with a blue bag allegedly containing a pistol. Shortly afterwards, two other accused are seen leaving on a Pulsar motorcycle.According to the information available, the three men left the hotel in the Chakala area of Andheri East and headed towards a football ground in Juhu, where the firing took place at around 7 pm the same day.Accused Stayed In Room No. 201The accused had stayed in Room No. 201, which was reportedly booked under the names Ankit and Mandeep Nain. However, the two men were allegedly identified as shooters Phool Singh and Rehan.The accused reportedly kept to themselves during their stay and usually went outside to eat.Also Watch:CCTV Footage May Provide Investigative CluesThe hotel is located around eight kilometres from the spot where the firing took place. The CCTV footage could provide investigators with important clues about the accused's movements in the hours leading up to the attack.Their stay at this hotel has now become an important part of the investigation into the Tiger Shroff firing case.   e e                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           óÅ>%5Å''Å1 ™ob-95149112022026-10-22T11:52:10ZUltraviolette X-47 Venom Launch Price Rs 2.65 Lakh in IndiaBikeAdvice.inbikeadvice.inhttps://bikeadvice.in/ultraviolette-x-47-venom-launch-price-rs-2-65-lakh-in-india/engIndia?«óóóóóòThe X-47 Venom becomes the first company model to come with the all-new VX-100 platform, SRB-11 battery technology and UV LIGHTFURY electric motorUltraviolette X-47 Venom has been launched at an introductory price of Rs 2.65 lakh (ex-showroom, India) in the Indian market. However, the price mentioned before will be applicable to the first 5000 customers. The X-47 Venom bookings have commenced from today at the brand's official website while the first deliveries are promised by Nov 2026. Based on the all-new VX-100 100V architecture, it will be be launched in Europe on November 3 at EICMA 2026 in Milan, Italy. The next-gen electric motorcycle comes with an extendable warranty coverage of up to 8 lakh km.First things first, the Venom X-47 is the first company model to use the newly-developed 100V platform which will be later seen with the Shockwave and Tesseract as well. The Bengaluru-based EV start-up claims that the new architecture ensures higher speed, greater range, faster charging, and quicker acceleration with lighter and more compact subsystems.Featuring the SRB-11 battery technology, Ultraviolette X-47 Venom returns an IDC range of 343 km on a single charge. In addition, it delivers top power of 40.2 bhp and peak wheel torque of 550 Nm. The all-electric motorcycle also establishes a new benchmark in e2w industry with the capability to support 12 kW DC fast charging. The company is offering a 1.6 kW On-board Charger as standard on the purchase of the electric motorcycle.It does the 0-60 kmph sprint in just 2.7 secs while taking around 5.9 secs for a 0-100 kmph sprint. Ultraviolette claims that the X-47 Venom is capable of outperforming all the 200-450cc ICE-powered bikes currently on sale in India. It can clock a top speed of 155 kmph due to the introduction of the UV LIGHTFURY Motor, which is lighter and faster while equipped with advanced Soft Magnetic Composite (SMC).Tipping the weighing scale at 180 kg, it is nearly up to 20 kg lighter than the previous generation platform. Some of the notable features onboard the X-47 Venom are a new 7-inch TFT LCD touchscreen, UV Hypersense Radar intelligence (World's first-in-segment), Integrated front and rear Dashcams, Battery Management System (BMS) with pyro-fuse, and Cruise Control.Ultraviolette X-47 Venom's SRB-11 battery technology is designed with up to 20 percent greater energy density and 2X cooling performance. The battery housing is carried out in cast-aluminium for impact protection and reduced mass. The battery pack gets IP67 certification to ensure protection against dust and water. The X-47 Venom features a next-generation motor control unit (MCU) engineered to be twice as compact while delivering 3X power density.   Ω Ω                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ñ?Å?!5Åk13Ç7 ß?95149094442026-10-22T11:50:46ZTiger Shroff Firing Case: Mumbai Court Sends 4 More Accused Including 2 Women To Police Custody Till October 26Free Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/tiger-shroff-firing-case-mumbai-court-sends-4-more-accused-including-2-women-to-police-custody-till-october-26engIndiaø‡ppppppA Mumbai court remanded four accused, including two women, to police custody until October 26 in the Tiger Shroff firing case. Police alleged their involvement in procuring and transporting firearms used in the Juhu shooting. Ten people have been arrested so far, while investigators continue probing the conspiracy.Mumbai, Oct 22: A court here on Thursday remanded four accused, including two women, held in Delhi in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff to police custody till October 26.They have been identified as Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh.The accused were produced before the magistrate court after being brought to the city from the national capital.Police seek custody over conspiracyPolice sought their remand, saying they have active participation in the conspiracy along with the previously arrested accused.Police said these accused supplied weapons to the shooters, which were used in the crime.The defence, represented by Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi, opposed their remand, saying that there was no material against them and they have been arrested on the basis of mere suspicion.Hence, their custodial interrogation is unwarranted and the accused should be remanded to judicial custody, they said.Court grants police remandAfter hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused to custody till October 26.According to the police, two of these accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women smuggled the firearms by train to Mumbai, handing them over directly to the attackers.Gunfire in Mumbai's Juhu areaAt least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. A motorcycle, allegedly used by the shooters, was found abandoned in Andheri.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.Also Watch:Ten arrested in firing caseA total of 10 persons have been arrested in the case so far.Of them, the court on Wednesday remanded three accused -- Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana -- to police custody till October 31.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ùuÅ@!5Å1/Åw ∑C95149067642026-10-22T11:48:22ZRs 30 lakh, 2 houses and revenge: Inside Gujarat's garba murder probeThe Indian Expressindianexpress.comhttps://indianexpress.com/article/cities/ahmedabad/gujarat-vadodara-garba-murder-revenge-plot-four-arrested-10932311/engIndiaø’’’’’’÷Thank you for your feedback.Your feedback has been reported succesfully.A 24-year-old Vadodara resident left home to watch a garba event. Minutes later, while sitting outside the venue, he was repeatedly stabbed by a masked man, who fled the scene. Two days later, on Wednesday, the police said Nilesh Vanzara's murder was part of a revenge plot.The incident occurred outside Swagat Party Plot on Monday. Nilesh, 24, left his Gujarat Housing Board home in Kishanwadi on Ajwa Road to attend a garba event. After arriving at the venue on his motorcycle, he was sitting outside when he was attacked.After receiving news of a man being attacked, police officials reached the spot and found Nilesh critically injured. The police rushed him to SSG Hospital, where he was declared dead on arrival. A murder case was lodged, following which teams from Kapurai police station and the Zone 3 Local Crime Branch spread out to identify and arrest the assailant.Deputy Commissioner of Police (DCP), Zone 3, Abhishek Gupta said that the police scanned footage from more than 100 CCTV cameras in and around the crime scene and questioned people present at the venue. The probe identified Poonam Vanzara as the suspected attacker. Technical analysis and human sources eventually led the police teams to Mahisagar district, where Poonam was tracked near Lunawada and arrested.During questioning, Poonam allegedly told the police that Vikram Vanzara regularly helped him financially, including paying his rent and providing money for household expenses. The police said Poonam allegedly revealed that Vikram had offered him Rs 30 lakh and two houses in return for killing Nilesh.The revenge plotAccording to the police, Vikram allegedly offered Poonam money and "two houses" to kill Nilesh to avenge the murder of his son, Sumit, who was allegedly murdered by Nilesh's brother, Ajay, three months ago. Ajay is currently lodged in the Vadodara Central Jail.The police arrested four people on Wednesday, including Vikram and Poonam.According to the police investigation, the accused had been monitoring Nilesh's movements. After learning that he was likely to attend the garba event at Swagat Party Plot, they allegedly decided to execute their plan. "On the day of the crime, Poonam called the victim and got him to come outside while the garba event was underway, where he was stabbed," DCP Gupta said."All the accused involved in hatching the conspiracy, assisting in its execution and carrying out the murder have been arrested. We will seek their remand for detailed questioning and conduct a reconstruction of the crime scene as part of the further investigation," Gupta added.How the murder was executedThe police said that Poonam and Vikram allegedly purchased two knives from a hotel near Jambuva Bridge days before the crime. On October 18, they allegedly met Vijaykumar alias Viju alias Brijesh Vanzara and Satish alias Gallo to finalise the plan. Vijaykumar was allegedly assigned to keep watch and identify Nilesh.On the day of the attack, Vikram allegedly provided Poonam with a knife and a motorcycle without a number plate, while Satish followed in a hired autorickshaw. When Nilesh arrived at the party plot, Vijaykumar allegedly signalled to Poonam, who then allegedly approached Nilesh and stabbed him three to four times.The police said Poonam then escaped in the autorickshaw and further on a motorcycle. The police have recovered the knife allegedly used in the murder from the vehicle and seized two mobile phones.   b b                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        óÅA!5Åk'+Ç ®?95149061172026-10-22T11:47:59ZFour accused held from Delhi sent to police custody till October 26 in Tiger Shroff firing case - India TV NewsIndia TV Newsindiatvnews.comhttps://www.indiatvnews.com/maharashtra/two-women-among-four-accused-held-from-delhi-sent-to-police-custody-till-october-26-in-tiger-shroff-firing-case-latest-updates-2026-10-22-1057644engIndiaø„333333At least two men fired gunshots at Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on the evening of October 18 before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.A Mumbai court on Thursday (October 22) remanded four accused, including two women arrested in Delhi in connection with the firing incident involving actor Tiger Shroff, to police custody until October 26. The accused were produced before the Esplanade Court, also known as Killa Court, in Mumbai.The arrested accused have been identified as Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh.The accused were produced before the magistrate court after being brought to the city from the national capital.Accused supplied weapons to shootersPolice had sought nine days of custody, saying that the four accused were actively involved in the conspiracy along with those arrested earlier in the case.According to the police, the accused supplied weapons to the shooters that were allegedly used in the crime.The defence lawyers, Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi, opposed the remand plea, arguing that there was no material evidence against the accused and that they had been arrested on mere suspicion.The defence submitted that custodial interrogation was unwarranted and sought judicial custody for the accused.After hearing arguments from both sides, the court remanded the four accused to police custody until October 26.According to the police, two of these accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women smuggled the firearms by train to Mumbai, handing them over directly to the attackers.Tiger Shroff firing caseAt least two men allegedly opened fire at actor Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening (October 18) before fleeing on a motorcycle. The actor escaped unhurt, while his driver and a bystander sustained injuries.According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. The motorcycle allegedly used by the shooters was later found abandoned in Andheri.Police have registered a case under charges of attempt to murder and provisions of the Arms Act.Police have arrested 10 people in connection with the case so far.On Wednesday, a court remanded three accused--- Rehan alias Sukka, from Haryana's Sonipat; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Bihar's Begusarai and currently residing in Mumbai; and Phool Singh, from Haryana --- to police custody until October 31.   	 	                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ç_ÅB!5Å'-Ç ó 95149056582026-10-22T11:47:39ZFive killed in two road accidents in Purba Bardhaman on Vijaya DashamiThe Statesmanthestatesman.comhttps://www.thestatesman.com/cities/kolkata/five-killed-in-two-road-accidents-in-purba-bardhaman-on-vijaya-dashami-1503653820.htmlengIndiaø“““““““Five people died in two seperate road accidents in Bengal's Purba Bardhaman district on Vijaya Dashami, on Monday.Three family members from Bajitpur village died after their motorcycle was hit by a loaded truck on State Highway 7 (Burdwan-Arambagh) near Mirepota crossing under Raina police station limits.The deceased have been identified as Kamakhya Roy (61), Narugopal Roy (45) and Srikanta Roy (41), all residents of Bajitpur village under Sehara Gram Panchayat in Raina.According to district police, the three were heading towards a refuelling station at Mirepota when a speeding truck bound for Bardhaman suddenly approached and hit their motorcycle as they were crossing the road.Police from Raina police station soon rushed to the spot and shifted the critically injured men to Burdwan Medical College and Hospital, where all three were declared dead. The truck has been seized, though its driver was still absconding, police said.The deaths on the day of festivities have cast a pall of gloom over Bajitpur and neighbouring villages, including Bendua, Bujrukdighi, Bodehar and Mirepota.In another incident, two youths died after being hit by an unidentified vehicle while returning home after pandal-hopping late on Monday evening near a cremation ground in Patna village under Bhatar police station limits.The deceased have been identified as Jeet Majhi (19) and Manoj Pal (30). Both were residents of the Mahachanda area in Bhatar, police said.    Ë æ Ë                                                                                                                                                                                                                            âRÅD!5Å!Åc èM95149046252026-10-22T11:47:03ZSix hurt as truck hits multiple vehicles in Himachal's UnaNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/agency-feeds/six-hurt-as-truck-hits-multiple-vehicles-in-himachals-una-10393188.htmlengIndiaø◊◊◊◊◊◊◊Una, Oct 22 (PTI) Six people were injured when a truck collided with multiple vehicles on the Una-Dharamshala National Highway in Himachal Pradesh's Una district on Thursday, police said.The accident occurred in Kuthiadi, within the jurisdiction of the Amb police station, an official sapokesperson said.According to police, the truck, coming from the Una side, first collided with a car and then hit a pickup truck, a motorcycle and a scooter.One of the injured, whose condition is critical, has been referred to the Regional Hospital in Una, while the others are undergoing treatment at the Civil Hospital in Amb.After receiving information about the accident, police reached the spot and ensured that the injured were shifted to hospital for treatment.The Amb police inspected the scene, registered a case and initiated further action.The exact circumstances leading to the accident will be established after the investigation is completed, police said. PTI COR BPL SMV SMV APLî>ÅC!5ÅÅc •95149046292026-10-22T11:47:05ZVideo: Speeding Audi Hits Bike, Reverses, Drives Over Riders. 1 KilledNDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/india-news/video-speeding-audi-hits-bike-reverses-drives-over-riders-1-killed-12220390engIndiaø…ôôôôôöThe incident happened on Tuesday, October 20Aligarh:One motorcyclist was killed and another was injured after a speeding Audi crashed into them in Aligarh, and then ran them over in Uttar Pradesh's Aligarh. The incident was captured on CCTV.The footage, accessed by NDTV, shows the two men riding on a motorcycle when a white-coloured sedan approaches from behind at high speed and crashes right into the two-wheeler. One of the men is flung into the air as both of them fall to the ground. Instead of getting out of the car or speeding away, the Audi driver reverses the vehicle and runs over the riders again as eyewitnesses run to the scene to take action.A speeding Audi rammed a motorcycle from behind on GT Road in Aligarh. The footage shows one of the riders being flung into the air.Instead of stopping, the driver reversed the car and ran over the victims again before fleeing the spot. The incident killed one man, identified as Manoj Kumar.The crash happened on October 20 around 11:10 pm near Bannadevi police station area. #Aligarh #UttarPradesh #CCTV -- NDTV (@ndtv)October 22, 2026He then speeds away as the locals attempt to throw stones at the car and stop it.The incident happened on Tuesday, October 20, at around 11:10 pm. It was reported from the Bannadevi police station area near Sarsaul on GT Road in Aligarh.The accident killed one of the motorcyclists, who has been identified as Manoj Kumar, a resident of Mahrawal village under the Gabhana police station area.The injured person, who has not been identified yet, has been hospitalised and is undergoing treatment.While there was no revelation about the Audi owner's identity at the time of the incident, a senior police official later confirmed to NDTV that it belongs to Devraj Singh, a former BJP district president.Police arrived at the scene soon after receiving reports about the hit-and-run and sent the body for post-mortem examination.An investigation has been launched into the case, and information about the driver's arrest, as well as subsequent legal action, is awaited.(With inputs from Adnan Khan)Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the worldMotorcyclist Death Aligarh, Speeding Audi Crash, Hit And Run Incident                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        ó^ÅE!5Å1%Ç ´95148992632026-10-22T11:43:39ZIndia News | Bengaluru: Bihar Man Arrested for Killing Wife, Dumping Body in DrainLatestLYlatestly.comhttps://www.latestly.com/agency-news/india-news-bengaluru-bihar-man-arrested-for-killing-wife-dumping-body-in-drain-7653345.htmlengIndiaø“““““““Get latest articles and stories on India at LatestLY. The Bengaluru police have arrested a 22-year-old migrant labourer from Bihar for allegedly murdering his 25-year-old wife and dumping her body in a stormwater drain over suspicions of infidelity, officials said on Thursday.Bengaluru (Karnataka) [India], October 22 (ANI): The Bengaluru police have arrested a 22-year-old migrant labourer from Bihar for allegedly murdering his 25-year-old wife and dumping her body in a stormwater drain over suspicions of infidelity, officials said on Thursday.The accused has been identified as Mohammad Irfaj, while the victim has been identified as his wife, Ruksana. Both are natives of Bihar.According to police, the couple had married approximately a year ago. Ruksana was previously married and had a child from her first marriage. The duo reportedly fell in love while selling balloons in Bihar and relocated to Bengaluru around six months ago, where Irfaj secured employment at a local garment factory.Police said the marital relationship had turned strained in recent months, as Irfaj suspected Ruksana of having an affair, alleging she was frequently talking to someone on the phone. The couple frequently quarrelled over the same.The dispute reached a violent flashpoint on October 10, when Irfaj allegedly attacked Ruksana with a stone, killing her on the spot, before stuffing a piece of cloth into her mouth, investigators said.To conceal the crime, the accused allegedly broke the handle lock of an unattended motorcycle parked nearby. He then stuffed the victim's body into a bag, placed it between the handlebars, pushed the vehicle to the Gopalapura drainage area, and dumped the body into the stormwater drain.On October 13, the body -- wrapped in a plastic cover -- was discovered in the drain. Initially, police were unable to identify the victim.The Magadi Road police then constituted more than 10 teams to conduct extensive door-to-door verifications and cross-reference recent missing person complaints in the locality.During the inquiry, local residents alerted the police that a woman residing in Gopalapura had been missing for several days, leading to Irfaj's questioning.As per the police, during the interrogation, the accused allegedly confessed.Further investigation is underway, and more details are awaited. (ANI)(The above story is verified and authored by ANI staff, ANI is South Asia's leading multimedia news agency with over 100 bureaus in India, South Asia and across the globe. ANI brings the latest news on Politics and Current Affairs in India & around the World, Sports, Health, Fitness, Entertainment, & News. The views appearing in the above post do not reflect the opinions of LatestLY)   º º                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ñ@ÅF!5ÇÇQ ß=95148989722026-10-22T11:43:24ZHigh-Speed Scorpio Collides With Bike on New Madhubani Four-Lane, Incense-Stick Businessman Dies on the Spot in MuzaffarpurNewsXnewsx.comhttps://www.newsx.com/regionals/high-speed-scorpio-collides-with-bike-on-new-madhubani-four-lane-incense-stick-businessman-dies-on-the-spot-in-muzaffarpur-286116/engIndiaø‰ÙÙÙÙÙıA deadly midnight collision on Muzaffarpur's Madhubani Four-Lane claimed the life of incense-stick businessman Ashok Kumar. The Scorpio caught fire after the crash, while locals raised concerns over the absence of an underpass.A midnight collision on the Madhubani Four-Lane in Bihar's Muzaffarpur turned fatal when a speeding Scorpio collided head-on with a motorcycle, killing an agarbatti trader on the spot. The impact was so severe that the SUV caught fire and was soon engulfed in flames, triggering panic among people near the accident site. The accident occurred around 12:30 am on Wednesday night along the Madhubani Four-Lane stretch of the Muzaffarpur-Patna New Bypass under the Sadar police station area.Scorpio-Bike Collision on Muzaffarpur Four-Lane Turns FatalAccording to the available information, a new Scorpio travelling at high speed collided head-on with a motorcycle. The biker suffered fatal injuries and died at the spot. The deceased was identified as Ashok Kumar, a resident of Madhubani village who worked in the agarbatti business. The collision sparked chaos in the area as locals gathered at the scene.Scorpio Catches Fire After Impact, Occupants Jump to SafetyThe crash took a more alarming turn when the Scorpio caught fire immediately after the collision. As flames spread through the vehicle, its occupants reportedly jumped out to save themselves.The police and fire brigade were alerted and rushed to the spot. However, the Scorpio had already been completely gutted by the time the fire engine arrived. Most of the vehicle was destroyed in the blaze.Villagers Raise Safety Concerns Over Missing UnderpassThe fatal accident has also sparked anger among local residents, who raised concerns about road safety on the busy stretch. Local resident Pankaj Kumar said the absence of an underpass makes crossing the road difficult for people and exposes them to the risk of accidents. Residents expressed concern over the lack of a safe crossing facility and the danger faced by people who need to cross the four-lane road.Police Send Ashok Kumar's Body for PostmortemSadar police station SHO Navlesh Kumar Azad reached the accident site with a police team after receiving information about the crash. The police took custody of Ashok Kumar's body and sent it to Shri Krishna Medical College and Hospital (SKMCH) for a postmortem examination. Officials said they were gathering further details about the Scorpio involved in the accident. Further legal action is underway.   $ 6$                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        äÅH!5ÅW#-Ç è#95148970412026-10-22T11:41:51ZTiger Shroff firing case: Actors team shared video of his injured arm, says God is kind - The TribuneThe Tribunetribuneindia.comhttps://www.tribuneindia.com/news/entertainment/tiger-shroff-firing-case-actors-team-shared-video-of-his-injured-arm-says-god-is-kind/engIndiaø∆ñññññöMaharashtra Deputy CM Eknath Shinde with Tiger Shroff in Mumbai.Actor Tiger Shroff's team shared a video of his injured arms on Thursday, days after the Bollywood star narrowly survived a gun attack on his car.At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.Team Tiger Shroff, the official Instagram page managed by his team, shared the video along with the caption, "God is kind."The short clip shows several small, dot-like marks and red spots across his arm.Three accused, identified as Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, were detained at Kota railway station in Rajasthan.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.ìFÅG!5Å='-Ç1 ¢95148989512026-10-22T11:43:12ZTiger Shroff firing: Two women among four accused sent to police custody till October 26Deccan Heralddeccanherald.comhttps://www.deccanherald.com/elections/maharashtra/tiger-shroff-firing-two-women-among-four-accused-sent-to-police-custody-till-october-26-4191376engIndiaø÷÷÷÷÷÷◊Mumbai: A court here on Thursday remanded four accused, including two women, held in Delhi in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff to police custody till October 26.. They have been identified as Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh.. The accused were produced before the magistrate court after being brought to the city from the national capital..Tiger Shroff case: Arrested UP women transported firearms to shooters in Mumbai; kin says innocent. Police sought their remand, saying they have active participation in the conspiracy along with the previously arrested accused.. Police said these accused supplied weapons to the shooters, which were used in the crime.. The defence, represented by Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi, opposed their remand, saying that there was no material against them and they have been arrested on the basis of mere suspicion.. Hence, their custodial interrogation is unwarranted and the accused should be remanded to judicial custody, they said.. After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused to custody till October 26.. According to the police, two of these accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women smuggled the firearms by train to Mumbai, handing them over directly to the attackers.. At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.. According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. A motorcycle, allegedly used by the shooters, was found abandoned in Andheri.. The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.. A total of 10 persons have been arrested in the case so far.. Of them, the court on Wednesday remanded three accused- Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, to police custody till October 31.    h Y h                                                                                            °RÅJ!5ÅG!)Ç æM95148957872026-10-22T11:40:47ZSix 160 cc Bikes For City Commutes And Weekend Highway Riding: Unicorn, Pulsar, Apache & Morecarandbikecarandbike.comhttps://www.carandbike.com/news/six-160-cc-bikes-for-city-commutes-and-weekend-highway-riding-unicorn-pulsar-apache-more-3222435engIndia?◊◊◊◊◊◊◊While a basic 100 cc or 125 cc commuter motorcycle may be fuel efficient, it runs out of breath quickly on open roads for longer excursions. On the other hand, larger 250 cc machines    ¨õ#ÅI%5s'Å/ ≥#b-95148963712026-10-22T11:41:13ZUltraviolette X-47 Venom Launched At Rs. 2.65 LakhsMotorBeammotorbeam.comhttps://www.motorbeam.com/ultraviolette-x-47-venom-launched-price-range-features/engIndia?à Ultraviolette has introduced the X-47 Venom in India at an introductory ex-showroom price of Rs. 2.65 lakhs. The electric motorcycle is the first product based on the company's new VX-100 100V platform and brings a claimed range of 343 km, a top speed of 155 km/hr and a range of rider assistance features.Bookings for the X-47 Venom will open on October 22, 2026, while deliveries are scheduled to begin in November. The introductory price is limited to the first 5000 customers. Ultraviolette will also display the motorcycle at EICMA 2026.Ultraviolette X-47 Venom: Motor And PerformanceThe X-47 Venom uses a new UV LIGHTFURY electric motor rated at 30kW, equivalent to around 40 BHP. The company claims a wheel torque figure of 550 Nm, with acceleration from 0-60 km/hr taking 2.7 seconds and the 0-100 km/hr sprint completed in 5.9 seconds.Its claimed maximum speed stands at 155 km/hr, placing it among the higher-performance electric motorcycles in the market. Actual performance and range may vary depending on riding conditions, speed and other factors.The motorcycle weighs 180 kg, which Ultraviolette says makes it up to 20 kg lighter than the X-47 Crossover.Battery, Range And ChargingPower comes from an 11kWh SRB-11 battery pack. Ultraviolette claims an IDC-certified range of 343 km on a full charge, although real-world range is likely to differ based on riding style, traffic and operating conditions.For charging, the X-47 Venom gets a 1.6kW onboard charger and supports DC fast charging at up to 12kW. The combination of a large battery and fast-charging capability is intended to improve its usability for longer journeys, though charging times will depend on the charging equipment and conditions.The new VX-100 platform also incorporates an updated motor control unit alongside the revised motor and battery setup.Ultraviolette X-47 Venom: Features And TechnologyThe electric motorcycle comes equipped with a seven-inch TFT touchscreen instrument console. It also gets integrated front and rear dashcams, cruise control and navigation powered by Mappls.A park assist function uses the rear-camera feed to help riders manoeuvre the motorcycle backwards in confined spaces. This feature could be useful given the bike's 180 kg kerb weight.The X-47 Venom also incorporates radar-based rider assistance systems. These include blind-spot monitoring, lane-change assistance, overtake alerts and rear-collision warnings. Such systems are designed to provide additional information about surrounding traffic, although riders must continue to exercise caution and remain attentive to road conditions.Ultraviolette X-47 Venom: Price And AvailabilityThe Ultraviolette X-47 Venom is priced at Rs. 2.65 lakh (ex-showroom) for the first 5000 buyers under the introductory offer. The regular price has not been specified in the provided details.Bookings begin on October 22, 2026, with deliveries expected to start in November. With its performance figures, large battery and technology-focused equipment list, the X-47 Venom expands Ultraviolette's electric motorcycle portfolio. Its real-world range, charging experience and the long-term usability of its electronic assistance systems will be important factors for prospective buyers.    offer strong highway pace, but their heavier kerb weight and thirstier engines can make daily office commuting in city traffic far more demanding.A good 160 cc bike, on the other hand, is light enough to handle congested city bottlenecks, and it also packs enough mid-range punch to cruise comfortably at 85 to 95 kmph when needed. There are many capable, practical choices in India's 160 cc segment today, some of which we have mentioned here.1. Honda UnicornPrice Starting From: Rs. 1.16 Lakh onwards (ex-showroom) | Base Variant: Unicorn (Only one option)While younger riders might dismiss the Honda Unicorn's conservative design and chrome accents as old-fashioned, five minutes in the saddle truly reveals why it's always been an Indian favourite. At the heart of this bike is a 162.7 cc single-cylinder engine that produces 13 bhp and 14.58 Nm of torque, linked to a five-speed gearbox. The highlight of the Unicorn is the engine with its refined performance, producing near-zero vibrations at the handlebar or footpegs between 40 and 70 kmph.It offers generous low-end torque as well, meaning you can move the bike in third gear alone at 25 kmph throughout the city, without any engine knocking. And on the highway, the Unicorn sits happily at 80 to 85 kmph. The long, flat seat is thickly padded, with high levels of comfort for the rider and pillion alike. But note that its soft suspension can float gently over high-speed undulations.Key Features:* Single-channel ABS with front disc brake* Reliable fuel efficiency of around 50 to 52 kmpl* Upright, fatigue-free commuting handlebar position* Long, cushioned single-piece seat for rider and pillion* Smooth 162.7 cc engine with counterbalancer technologyWho should buy it: Mature commuters and daily office-goers who value engine smoothness, plush seating comfort and low maintenance bills much more than aggressive styling.2. TVS Apache RTR 160 4VPrice Starting From: Rs. 1.15 Lakh onwards (ex-showroom) | Base Variant: Single-Channel ABSThe TVS Apache RTR 160 4V is one of the most complete all-rounders in the 160 cc space. Its 159.7 cc oil-cooled, four-valve engine pumps out around 17.3 bhp and 14.73 Nm of torque in Sport mode, which makes it arguably one of the most powerful motorcycles in its displacement class. But what actually makes the Apache truly special is how adaptable it feels. It comes with three dedicated riding modes: Urban, Rain, and Sport.In Urban mode, throttle response is tuned low to keep fuel consumption in mind, while Sport mode sharpens up the bike's acceleration for open highways. TVS has also fitted it with Glide Through Traffic (GTT) technology, which allows the bike to crawl forward in first or second gear in city traffic without needing any throttle input. Meanwhile, on the highway, the Apache feels eager and quick as well, accelerating cleanly to 100 kmph with an addictive, throaty exhaust note. The riding position is slightly sporty with a mild forward lean, yet it's still comfortable enough for long weekend highway rides.Key Features:* Four-valve engine that produces a potent 17.3 bhp* Three unique riding modes (Urban, Rain, and Sport)* Available upside-down front forks and dual-channel ABS* Glide Through Traffic (GTT) technology for easy city commuting* Slipper clutch that prevents rear wheel hop on aggressive downshifts* TFT display with Google Maps mirroring in latest top-spec variantWho should buy it: Riders who want high-revving performance, cutting-edge riding electronics and agile handling without giving up everyday city usability.3. Bajaj Pulsar N160 SPrice Starting From: Rs. 1.34 Lakh onwards (ex-showroom) | Base Variant Pulsar N160 SThe Bajaj Pulsar N160 isn't built on the foundations of the older Pulsars; it actually has a ne                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      E E                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           ù7ÅK!5Åm-Ç ¥95148941832026-10-22T11:39:15ZTiger Shroff Firing Case Accused Moved To Mumbai 3 Months Ago To Work As Cook, Bike-Taxi Driver - Details InsideTimesNowtimesnownews.comhttps://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/tiger-shroff-firing-case-accused-moved-to-mumbai-3-months-ago-to-work-as-cook-bike-taxi-driver-details-inside-article-156385574engIndiaø‹‹‹‹‹‹‹Tiger Shroff Was Attacked By Three Men In Mumbai. (Credit: Instagram)Tiger Shroff's firing incident left the entire film industry in shock. For the unversed, the Bollywood star was attacked by three men on October 18. The trio came on the bike, and two of them fired seven rounds of bullets at the actor's car. He escaped the attack with minor injuries, but his driver and one more person got injured in it. Mumbai Police immediately started scouting for the accused and arrested three of them in Kota with the help of Rajasthan Police. Now, two attackers are from Haryana's Sonipat, while the other one is from Bihar's Begusarai. As per the latest statement by the Bihar Police, a 22-year-old Hrithik Kumar aka Roshan left the state two years ago to work with a catering agency in Delhi. He moved to Mumbai three months ago and worked as a cook before becoming a driver with an app-based bike-taxi.Bihar Police Reveals Details About Tiger Shroff's AttackerAccording to a statement released by the Bihar Police, the 22-year-old accused, Hrithik, studied in Bihar till the intermediate level and left his house in Begusarai two years ago in search of work. He did his first job with a food catering agency in Delhi. Three months ago, he moved to Mumbai, where he worked at a restaurant as a cook. After a few weeks, he started working as a bike-taxi driver and delivery partner.The officials further revealed that Hrithik Kumar was allegedly riding a two-wheeler when his accomplice fired shots at Tiger Shroff in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening. Lawrence Bishnoi's gang, the Anil Pandit and Harman Sandhu, claimed responsibility for the attack. A day later, the accused were nabbed at Kota station.While revealing more about Kumar, the Begusarai SP, Maneesh said that the accused has two younger brothers and sisters. His family and friends revealed Kumar is very particular about his appearance and fitness. He had also gained attention on social media with his intense workout and tattoo videos.Hrithik Kumar's mother Sanyukta said, "Last I knew, he was working with a catering agency in Delhi and also wanted to marry a woman from Rajasthan. He had even visited Surat to purchase wedding-related items along with the woman's father. We know that he last visited Surat railway station with the woman on October 17 and last spoke to him at around 2pm that day. His mobile phone went off after that."Kumar's parents run a tea-cum-cosmetic stall at Pipra Chowk. His mother further said, "My son is innocent. I cannot believe he is a criminal and was part of the firing at the actor." On the other hand, his uncle revealed the family had not been in touch with him for the last few days.Hrithik Is Very Aggressive, Reveals Accused's Mumbai NeighbourHrithik Kumar aka Roshan's neighbours at Mumbai's Gilbert Hill, revealed that he rented a room for around six months. They said he would often get into fights over parking his electric scooter or water spilling near his doorway. Mohammed Azhar, a construction site worker who stays close to Hrithik in Mumbai, said, "Roshan was extremely aggressive and was always ready to pick fights."The three accused were sent to police custody till October 31. Tiger Shroff has not yet addressed the incident publicly. His team shared a video of minor pellet injuries on his hand on social media. Stay tuned for more updates!    on Thursday launched the X-47 Venom at an introductory price of Rs 2.65 lakh for the sale of first 5,000 motorcycles, expanding its premium electric motorcycle portfolio with a new platform that offers higher range, improved performance and reduced weight.The motorcycle has a regular starting price of Rs 3 lakh and is built on Ultraviolette's newly developed VX100 architecture. It offers a claimed Indian Driving Cycle (IDC) range of up to 343 km on a single charge, compared with 323 km on the earlier X-47 Crossover.The company opened bookings for the motorcycle today, with deliveries scheduled to begin in November 2026. The company also plans to launch the motorcycle across 20 European countries, with an international unveiling scheduled for November 3 at the EICMA motorcycle exhibition in Milan.The X-47 Venom will be offered with battery options of around 7 kWh and 11 kWh. The motorcycle will come equipped with the SRB11 battery pack, developed under the new VX-100 architecture. Ultraviolette claims the new battery offers 25% higher energy density while being approximately 15% lighter than the previous-generation pack.According to the company, improvements in battery cooling and thermal management have also enabled twice the cooling performance and faster charging. The new battery system supports DC charging at up to 12 kW.Niraj Rajmohan, Co-founder and Chief Technology Officer, said the company focused on increasing battery capacity without adding weight, a major challenge in electric motorcycle development."Today, I'm going to say that India's largest battery pack got even bigger. And not just bigger, it even got 15% lighter than the current model," he said.The new platform incorporates a lighter electric motor and an in-house-developed motor controller using silicon carbide power electronics. Ultraviolette said these changes have helped reduce the motorcycle's overall weight by approximately 20 kg compared with the previous platform."We've reduced 10% on the platform, now we've reduced 20 kgs from the motorcycle platform," Narayan Subramaniam, Co-founder and CEO of Ultraviolette Automotive said, highlighting the engineering changes.The X-47 Venom develops a claimed 40 hp and 550 Nm of torque at the rear wheel. It has a claimed top speed of 155 km/h and can accelerate from zero to 100 km/h in 5.9 seconds.The motorcycle also offers nine levels of regenerative braking, with the company claiming improved energy recovery across a wider range of battery charge levels. The revised thermal management system allows regenerative braking to remain active even when the battery is close to zero or fully charged.In terms of safety, Ultraviolette has introduced a pyrofuse protection system designed to rapidly disconnect the battery's high-voltage electrical circuit when an abnormal condition is detected. The company said the system can respond within two to three milliseconds.The X-47 Venom also carries forward Ultraviolette's radar-based rider-assistance technology, which provides blind-spot monitoring, rear collision warnings, lane-change assistance and overtake alerts.Other equipment includes integrated front and rear dashcams, a seven-inch touchscreen instrument cluster, cruise control, four levels of traction control, switchable dual-channel ABS, hill-hold assist and an onboard charger that allows the motorcycle to use a standard 16-amp power socket.The company has also introduced a lithium-ion auxiliary battery in place of the conventional lead-acid unit, aimed at reducing failures associated with auxiliary battery discharge. It announced a battery and motor warranty programme of up to eight years or 8 lakh km, subject to applicable terms.Alongside the motorcycle, Ultraviolette unveiled the B-Max airbag vest, an ac                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    °JÅL%5ÅI5'Åe æMb-95148934222026-10-22T11:38:34ZUltraviolette Launches X-47 Venom on New VX100 Platform at Rs 2.65 Lakh | Autocar ProfessionalAutocar Professionalautocarpro.inhttps://www.autocarpro.in/news/ultraviolette-launches-x-47-venom-on-new-vx100-platform-at-rs-265-lakh-135402engIndia?Ω"The electric crossover motorcycle comes with an 11 kWh battery, which offers a range of 343 km on a single charge.Bengaluru-based electric two-wheeler manufacturer Ultraviolette Automotive    Æ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ùiÅM!5Å5#'ÇG ∂S95148861322026-10-22T11:32:56ZIndian National Car Racing Championship 2026 to commence in Coimbatore on October 24India Todayindiatoday.inhttps://www.indiatoday.in/auto/latest-auto-news/story/indian-national-car-racing-championship-2026-to-commence-in-coimbatore-on-october-24-3022811-2026-10-22engIndia?ﬁ^^^^^`The 29th season of the Indian National Car Racing Championship begins in Coimbatore on October 24, featuring 17 races across six categories, including Formula 4 and touring car championships.The 29th season of the CTR-JK Tyre FMSCI Indian National Car Racing Championship 2026 will begin at Kari Motor Speedway in Coimbatore on October 24 and 25. The opening weekend will feature 17 races across six categories, bringing together established racers and emerging talent in Indian motorsport.The championship is backed by a partnership between JK Tyre and Chennai Turbo Riders (CTR), with the aim of providing a competitive platform for drivers across different levels of circuit racing. The opening round will feature single-seater racing, touring car competition and single-make championships, with competitors looking to secure an early advantage in the season.The races will be streamed live on JK Tyre Motorsport's Facebook and YouTube channels from 10am on Saturday and 9.45am on Sunday.Indian National Car Racing Championship 2026: CategoriesThe opening round will feature LGB Formula 4, the JK Tyre Novice Cup, Super Saloon, Indian Touring Car (ITC), Indian Super Touring Car (ISTC), the JK Tyre Levitas Cup and the Royal Enfield Continental GT Cup presented by JK Tyre. The programme covers both car and motorcycle racing, with separate grids for different classes.LGB Formula 4LGB Formula 4, now in its 29th year, remains an entry point into single-seater racing in India. The cars use a 1,298cc carburetted Suzuki Swift engine, an Esteem five-speed gearbox and a chrome-molybdenum tubular frame. The category will feature three races over the weekend.JK Tyre Novice CupThe JK Tyre Novice Cup provides a pathway for karting drivers moving into single-seater formula racing. The category will feature two races during the opening weekend, giving newcomers an opportunity to gain experience in full-scale circuit competition.Super Saloon, ITC and ISTCThe touring car programme will feature production-based racing cars across multiple classes. Super Stock and Indian Junior Touring Cars (IJTC) will provide close competition, with technical regulations and vehicle modifications varying across the classes.The ITC and ISTC categories will feature production-based cars prepared for circuit racing, with ISTC allowing more extensive modifications. Two races are scheduled for the ITC/ISTC category during the weekend.JK Tyre Levitas CupThe JK Tyre Levitas Cup enters its second season with lightweight, race-prepared Maruti Suzuki Ignis cars. The single-make series uses a naturally aspirated 1.2-litre K-Series engine producing 92bhp, with headers and a straight-pipe exhaust.The category will feature two races, with competitors divided into Rookie and Pro/Gentlemen's classes. The series focuses on car control, braking, cornering and overtaking, offering drivers a platform to develop their circuit racing skills.Royal Enfield Continental GT CupThe Royal Enfield Continental GT Cup, presented by JK Tyre, enters its sixth edition with a revised format. Amateur and Professional riders will compete on separate grids, using the GT-R650 and GT-R750 platforms, respectively.The Amateur grid will feature 20 riders, while the Professional category will have 15. Three races are scheduled for each class.With 17 races scheduled across the two days, the Coimbatore opener will set the early championship standings across the participating categories.   ∆ ∆                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            î6ÅN!5Å)/Å} §K95148855812026-10-22T11:32:27ZBihar Man Kills Wife and Dumps Body in Drain in Bengaluru; ArrestedRepublic Worldrepublicworld.comhttps://www.republicworld.com/india/bihar-man-kills-wife-and-dumps-body-in-drain-in-bengaluru-arrested-2026-10-22-139447engIndiaø¡ëëëëëëAccording to police, the couple (Irfaj and Ruksana) had married approximately a year ago. Ruksana (the wife) was previously married and had a child from her first marriage. The duo reportedly fell in love while selling balloons in Bihar and relocated to Bengaluru around six months ago.Bengaluru, Karnataka: The Bengaluru police have arrested a 22-year-old migrant labourer from Bihar for allegedly murdering his 25-year-old wife and dumping her body in a stormwater drain over suspicions of infidelity, officials said on Thursday.The accused has been identified as Mohammad Irfaj, while the victim has been identified as his wife, Ruksana. Both are natives of Bihar.According to police, the couple had married approximately a year ago. Ruksana was previously married and had a child from her first marriage. The duo reportedly fell in love while selling balloons in Bihar and relocated to Bengaluru around six months ago, where Irfaj secured employment at a local garment factory.Police said the marital relationship had turned strained in recent months, as Irfaj suspected Ruksana of having an affair, alleging she was frequently talking to someone on the phone. The couple frequently quarrelled over the same.The dispute reached a violent flashpoint on October 10, when Irfaj allegedly attacked Ruksana with a stone, killing her on the spot, before stuffing a piece of cloth into her mouth, investigators said.To conceal the crime, the accused allegedly broke the handle lock of an unattended motorcycle parked nearby. He then stuffed the victim's body into a bag, placed it between the handlebars, pushed the vehicle to the Gopalapura drainage area, and dumped the body into the stormwater drain.On October 13, the body -- wrapped in a plastic cover -- was discovered in the drain. Initially, police were unable to identify the victim.The Magadi Road police then constituted more than 10 teams to conduct extensive door-to-door verifications and cross-reference recent missing person complaints in the locality.During the inquiry, local residents alerted the police that a woman residing in Gopalapura had been missing for several days, leading to Irfaj's questioning.As per the police, during the interrogation, the accused allegedly confessed.Further investigation is underway, and more details are awaited.   ì ì                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         òiÅO!5Å!Ås ≠]95148852212026-10-22T11:32:18ZUltraviolette plans to double retail network to 100 stores by MarNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/agency-feeds/ultraviolette-plans-to-double-retail-network-to-100-stores-by-mar-10393136.htmlengIndia?√ìììììèNew Delhi, Oct 22 (PTI) Electric two-wheeler maker Ultraviolette Automotive plans to nearly double its retail footprint to 100 locations by the first quarter of 2027 and boost monthly sales to 10,000 units by the end of next year, its co-founder and CEO Narayan Subramaniam said.The company currently has around 50 retail stores in India and is clocking monthly volumes of around 700 units. The automaker expects the volume to increase to over 1,000 units per month in the first quarter of 2027, Subramaniam told PTI on the sidelines of unveiling its VX100 high-voltage architecture and launching the X47 Venom model."Starting Q1 2027, we should be targeting very good volumes. Volume is not only a factor in product development, but also a factor of distribution; by Q1 2027, we should be at 100 locations in India. Now, we are at around 50," he said.The retail expansion comes as the company plans to expand its product range.Ultraviolette is targeting to launch four models over the next year.These include the existing F77 sports motorcycle, the X47 Venom, the new Shockwave entry-level street-and-dirt motorcycle and the new Tesseract electric scooter.By this time next year, we should be at about 10,000 vehicles a month, Subramaniam said.He noted that demand is coming for electric motorcycles across tier-one and tier-two cities.The X47 Venom, which comes at an introductory ex-showroom price of Rs 2.65 lakh, is the first motorcycle built on the new VX100 architecture, which operates on a 100-volt architecture.Subramaniam said the platform was under development for two to three years and would be used for the upcoming models.He said the new platform is engineered to deliver greater energy density, improved thermal performance and better safety with higher energy density than the previous reference configuration.Ultraviolette is also expanding production capacity to support its growth plans. At the existing facility, it is ramping up capacity to up to 50,000 units, while a new plant is being set up.The new plant, BIGGA (Big Global Ambition) Factory, is coming up in Hosur, Tamil Nadu, with a capacity of 2.5 lakh units in the first phase, at an investment of Rs 779 crore over five years. The company is targeting a total capacity of 3 lakh units by 2028.Most of the capital raised has gone into product development. Now, serious capital is going into production, expansion and marketing, Subramaniam said.International markets are another part of the company's growth strategy.Ultraviolette said about 15 per cent of its volumes come from overseas markets and aims to increase that share to 20-25 per cent by 2028.The startup is backed by investors like Lingotto, TDK Ventures, Qualcomm Ventures, Zoho Corporation, TVS Motor, Yali Capital and Speciale Invest.It has recently raised USD 85 million in a funding round led by Yali Capital and TDK Ventures. PTI KMM BAL   û û                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    ú^ÅP%5Å'Å; µkb-95148825432026-10-22T11:30:28ZBenelli TRK 552 Range Launched in India at Rs 7.22 Lakh | MotoroidsMotoroidsmotoroids.comhttps://www.motoroids.com/news/benelli-trk-552-range-launched-in-india-at-rs-7-22-lakh/engIndia?™!Benelli backed by Hyderabad-based Adishwar Auto Ride India (AARI) in India, has launched the new TRK 552 and TRK 552X adventure touring motorcycles. The new range is powered by a 554cc twin-cylinder engine and comes equipped with premium standard features including a 5-inch TFT display, heated grips, and a heated seat.Prices for the lineup start at Rs 7.22 lakh (ex-showroom). The street-focused TRK 552 is built primarily for highway touring, while the rugged TRK 552X features spoke wheels and higher ground clearance for off-road riding. A special Limited Edition of the TRK 552X is also available. Bookings for all three versions officially opened on October 22, 2026, across all authorized Benelli-Keeway dealerships.Benelli TRK 552 Range: Price in IndiaThe TRK 552X costs Rs 52,000 more than the standard TRK 552. The Limited Edition carries a further premium of Rs 16,000 over the regular TRK 552X.554cc Engine Produces 52 bhpAll three versions use the same 554cc, liquid-cooled, DOHC parallel-twin engine. It produces 52 bhp at 8,500 rpm and 49 Nm of torque at 6,500 rpm. A six-speed gearbox and slipper clutch are standard.The engine is housed in a tubular steel trellis frame, paired with an aluminium swingarm. Both motorcycles also share the same suspension and braking hardware. Key mechanical details include:* 554cc parallel-twin engine* 52 bhp at 8,500 rpm* 49 Nm at 6,500 rpm* Six-speed gearbox with slipper clutch* 50mm Marzocchi upside-down front fork* Rear monoshock with adjustable preload* Twin 320mm front discs and a 260mm rear disc* Bosch dual-channel ABSBenelli TRK 552 vs TRK 552X: What's Different?The main differences are in the wheels, tyres, ground clearance and seat height. These changes give the two motorcycles different characteristics for touring.Benelli TRK 552The standard TRK 552 gets 17-inch aluminium alloy wheels at both ends. It uses Pirelli tyres, with a 120/70ZR17 front tyre and a 160/60ZR17 rear tyre.Its 190mm ground clearance and 835mm seat height suit its road-oriented setup. The motorcycle is available in Black and White.Benelli TRK 552XThe TRK 552X gets a 19-inch front spoke wheel and a 17-inch rear spoke wheel. The tyres are from Metzeler, measuring 110/80R19 at the front and 150/70R17 at the rear.Ground clearance increases to 210mm, while the seat height rises to 860mm. The taller front wheel and extra clearance make this version better suited to uneven roads and light off-road riding.The regular TRK 552X is available in Green and White. The Limited Edition gets a Yellow finish.Features and Touring EquipmentBoth motorcycles receive a 5-inch TFT instrument display with Bluetooth connectivity and navigation functions. The system supports route planning, turn-by-turn directions, offline navigation and trackback functionality.Other features include:* Tyre Pressure Monitoring System (TPMS)* Navigation screen mirroring* Gear position indicator* USB charging port* Illuminated switchgear* Optional T-BOX connectivityHeated grips and a heated seat are standard on both motorcycles. Benelli has also redesigned the seats with additional padding and added an adjustable handlebar to help riders find a comfortable riding position. New hand guards provide extra protection while riding.Both versions have a 20-litre fuel tank and a kerb weight of 235kg.Benelli TRK 552 Range: Dimensions and Specifications   Ë Ë                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ñÅQ!5Å3))ÅY ®95148825792026-10-22T11:30:28ZUltraviolette X47 Venom Launched At Rs 2.65 Lakh - New VX-100 Platform, 343km Rangedrivespark.comdrivespark.comhttps://www.drivespark.com/two-wheelers/2026/ultraviolette-x47-venom-launched-rs-2-65-lakh-088401.htmlengIndia?¶ The Ultraviolette X47 Venom has been launched in India at Rs 2.65 lakh (ex-showroom). It's the first motorcycle on the brand's new VX-100 platform and claims an IDC range of 343 km. That price is introductory and applies to the first 5,000 customers. Bookings opened at 4 pm today (October 22), with deliveries starting in November 2026.Ultraviolette X47 Venom - Battery, Motor and PerformanceThe Ultraviolette X47 Venom's SRB-11 battery pack offers 11 kWh of usable capacity. The motor makes 39.5 bhp (30 kW) and 550 Nm of torque at the wheel. Top speed is claimed at 155 km/h, and 0-100 km/h takes 5.9 seconds.At 180 kg, the Ultraviolette X47 Venom is 20 kg lighter than before. The battery pack is 15 per cent lighter and claimed to be 25 per cent more energy-dense, while axial cooling replaces the radial arrangement and doubles cooling performance.DC fast charging goes up to 12 kW. Ballistic mode now works until the battery falls to 10 per cent, and regenerative braking is available from the start instead of only below a 90 per cent charge level.The Light Fury motor spins at up to 9,000 rpm and uses soft magnetic components. Rare-earth metal use is down 50 per cent and motor weight is down 25-30 per cent, with power output maintained or improved. The motor controller is twice as compact and 40 per cent lighter than the current-generation unit. The VX-100 is a 100V platform, and Ultraviolette says it will also support future products.Ultraviolette X47 Venom - Safety, Features and ColoursA pyro-fuse isolates the battery circuit within microseconds if a critical fault is detected. It works alongside the battery management system and cell-level fuses, and the battery enclosure has IP67 protection against dust and water ingress.UV Hypersense uses a 77 GHz rear radar with a claimed monitoring range of up to 200 metres. It enables blind-spot monitoring, lane change assist, overtake alert and rear collision warning, and the hazard lights activate when a threat is detected from behind.The Ultraviolette X47 Venom gets a 7-inch TFT touchscreen with front and rear cameras. Mappls navigation, rear-camera park assist, cruise control and software updates are also on offer, along with VIOLETTE AI alerts for movement, falls, towing and crashes.Colour options are Afterburner Yellow, Turbo Red, Cosmic Black and Stellar White. Ultraviolette also announced the reusable B-MAX safety vest, which claims 86 per cent force attenuation and can be reused up to five times. Extendable warranty coverage is promised up to 8,00,000 km.   Ω Ω                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   í?ÅR!5Å5+1ÇA üs95148821122026-10-22T11:30:04ZTiger Shroff firing: Two women among four accused sent to police custody till Oct 26Hindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/mumbai-news/tiger-shroff-firing-two-women-among-four-accused-sent-to-police-custody-till-oct-26-101792668281375.htmlengIndiaø·qqqqqrMumbai, A court here on Thursday remanded four accused, including two women, held in Delhi in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff to police custody till October 26.They have been identified as Kunal and Sumit , both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha and Babita , both from Uttar Pradesh.The accused were produced before the magistrate court after being brought to the city from the national capital.Police sought their remand, saying they have active participation in the conspiracy along with the previously arrested accused.Police said these accused supplied weapons to the shooters, which were used in the crime.The defence, represented by Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi, opposed their remand, saying that there was no material against them and they have been arrested on the basis of mere suspicion.Hence, their custodial interrogation is unwarranted and the accused should be remanded to judicial custody, they said.After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused to custody till October 26.According to the police, two of these accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women smuggled the firearms by train to Mumbai, handing them over directly to the attackers.At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. A motorcycle, allegedly used by the shooters, was found abandoned in Andheri.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.A total of 10 persons have been arrested in the case so far.Of them, the court on Wednesday remanded three accused- Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, to police custody till October 31.   ≥ ≥                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         úIÅS!5y7!Ås µ95148820622026-10-22T11:30:01ZPolice Custody For Four Accused In Tiger Shroff FiringRediff.com India Ltd.rediff.comhttps://www.rediff.com/news/report/four-accused-in-tiger-shroff-firing-case-remanded-to-police-custody/20261022.htmengIndiaø›]]]]]]Mumbai Police have remanded four more accused, including two women, to custody until October 26 for their alleged role in supplying weapons for the firing incident at actor Tiger Shroff's car.IMAGE: This is an AI-generated image and has been used only for representational purposes.Key Points* Four accused, including two women, were remanded to police custody till October 26 in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff's car.* The arrested individuals, identified as Kunal, Sumit, Radha, and Babita, were apprehended in Delhi and brought to Mumbai.* Police allege the accused supplied weapons to the shooters, with two men procuring them from Amritsar and the two women smuggling them by train to Mumbai.* The incident involved gunshots fired at Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening, injuring his driver and a bystander.* A total of 10 persons have been arrested in the case so far, with three others previously remanded to custody till October 31.A court here on Thursday remanded four accused, including two women, held in Delhi in connection with the firing at actor Tiger Shroff to police custody till October 26.They have been identified as Kunal (21) and Sumit (19), both residents of Haryana's Sonipat district, and Radha (23) and Babita (23), both from Uttar Pradesh.The accused were produced before the magistrate court after being brought to the city from the national capital.Allegations And Defence ArgumentsPolice sought their remand, saying they have active participation in the conspiracy along with the previously arrested accused.Police said these accused supplied weapons to the shooters, which were used in the crime.The defence, represented by Ajinkya Mirgul and Satyavrat Joshi, opposed their remand, saying that there was no material against them and they have been arrested on the basis of mere suspicion.Hence, their custodial interrogation is unwarranted and the accused should be remanded to judicial custody, they said.After hearing both sides, the court remanded the four accused to custody till October 26.Weapon Procurement And Incident DetailsAccording to the police, two of these accused had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while the two women smuggled the firearms by train to Mumbai, handing them over directly to the attackers.At least two men fired gunshots at Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.According to Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. A motorcycle, allegedly used by the shooters, was found abandoned in Andheri.The Mumbai Police have registered a case under the provisions of attempt to murder and the Arms Act.A total of 10 persons have been arrested in the case so far.Of them, the court on Wednesday remanded three accused- Rehan alias Sukka, from Sonipat in Haryana; Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, originally from Begusarai in Bihar and living in Mumbai; and Phool Singh from Haryana, to police custody till October 31.Disclaimer: News content is sourced from the stated source. Headlines, summaries, section headers, and images are automatically generated or selected using AI/algorithms and may not always be fully accurate. Readers are advised to refer to the full article for complete context.    x  x                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       