946704 ≤%b-9514945438 ≥%b-9514934199 µ%b-9514931143 ∂%b-9514917866 ª%b-9514911202 æ%b-9514896371 …%b-9514893422 Ã%b-9514882543 –%b-9514872456 ÷%b-9514865560 €%b-9514434419 ¥!	9515724380!9515718561!9515716792!9515707114!9515707109!9515706701!9515703452 !9515703450!9515701000	!9515693825!9515693511!9515692721!9515691840!9515689285!9515688934!9515684483!9515679624!9515679011!9515678127!9515669896!9515626620!9515603684!9515584703!9515566316!9515538418!9515537772 !9515513822!!9515509592"!9515478754#!9515471734$!9515465118%!9515462132&!9515456563'!9515453697(!9515452009)!9515450927*!9515444915+!9515443924,!9515443922.!9515443917-!9515443914/!95154314981!95154263212!95154252683!95154205414!95154205406!95154205355!95154202617!95154130878!95154065089!9515393219;!9515388287<!9515388278=!9515385187>!9515377731@!9515377476A!9515375680B!9515372214C!9515362011D!9515362008F!9515362001E!9515358824H!9515358819G!9515352217I!9515350257J!9515341853L!9515334435N!9515331967O!9515330676P!9515328206Q!9515319273S!9515319267T!9515319263U!9515318345V!9515315919W!9515314232X!9515311297Y!9515304651Z!9515304577[    clutch-less upshift (quickshifter) function and a 5-inch TFT display. These are substantial mechanical and equipment changes for a motorcycle that otherwise looks much like the existing N250.The N250SS is now the more expensive of the two versions. It retains the 249.07cc single-cylinder, air- and oil-cooled engine layout, but its new four-valve cylinder head lifts output to approximately 25PS and 22Nm. The regular two-valve N250 produces about 24.5PS and 21.5Nm. The increases are small, so buyers should expect the transmission and electronics to make a bigger difference than the extra power.Six Gears: The Biggest Mechanical UpgradeThe earlier N250 used a five-speed gearbox, making the new sixth ratio one of the most useful changes for riders who travel regularly on highways. It could allow the engine to run at lower revs while cruising, although Bajaj has not published a direct comparison of sixth-gear cruising speeds and engine rpm. Whether it makes the new bike quieter or more economical will need testing.Bajaj has also added what it calls the Sports Shifter, allowing clutchless upshifts. That is an unusual feature at this price and should make quick acceleration through the gears easier. However, the presence of a quickshifter does not automatically mean every shift will be equally smooth at low speeds. Riders will need to try it in stop-start traffic as well as on an open road.The electronic throttle body allows selectable riding modes, supplementing the ABS settings and traction control available on the N250. The benefits depend on how noticeably each mode changes throttle response. That matters more to everyday riders than the small rise in peak power.The Display Is A Proper Step-upThe 5-inch colour TFT replaces the regular N250's LCD instrument panel and supports Google Maps mirroring through a connected phone. For riders who use navigation frequently, seeing a map on the instrument display is more convenient than fitting a separate mobile holder. Adjustable hand levers, a USB Type-C charging socket, hazard lights and a Panic Brake Alert function complete the equipment additions.The motorcycle retains the familiar naked-bike design, with updated graphics and colour choices separating the SS from the standard version. Its underlying chassis layout remains familiar too, with an upside-down front fork, a rear monoshock, 17-inch alloy wheels and disc brakes at both ends. Bajaj has not claimed a wholesale change in suspension geometry or braking performance.How Does It Compare With Other 250cc Bikes?At ‚Çπ1.59 lakh, the N250SS remains cheaper than the Hero Xtreme 250R, starting at approximately ‚Çπ1.84 lakh, and the Suzuki Gixxer 250, priced around ‚Çπ1.85 lakh. Hero Xtreme 250R offers a significantly stronger 30 PS and 25 Nm from its liquid-cooled engine. Suzuki's Gixxer delivers 26.5 PS and 22.2 Nm. The Bajaj therefore does not lead this group on engine output, but it offers a six-speed transmission, quickshifter and TFT navigation at a lower purchase price.For someone buying primarily for outright acceleration, the Hero's substantial power advantage deserves attention. For riders replacing a smaller commuter or using one motorcycle for office journeys and weekend highway trips, the N250SS makes a different case. The extra ‚Çπ14,136 buys practical upgrades that are difficult to add later.The regular N250 still makes sense for buyers who want the same basic riding position and strong low-cost 250cc performance without paying for electronic features. The N250SS is the more complete option on paper, but its sixth-gear gearing, quickshifter behaviour and ride modes are the key additions that call for a test ride before buying.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Û Û                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ä	Åh!5m!)Å; êi95148286112026-10-22T10:50:55ZUltraviolette X47 Venom Launched At Rs 2.65 Lakhcarandbikecarandbike.comhttps://www.carandbike.com/news/ultraviolette-x47-venom-launched-at-rs-265-lakh-3222432engIndia?úSits on the new VX-100 platform and features the SRB-11 battery system.Ultraviolette has launched the X47 Venom at Rs 2.65 lakh. The electric motorcycle is based on the brand's all-new VX-100 platform and is 20 kg lighter than before. It claims an IDC range of 343 km and is the first motorcycle to use the new platform.On the powertrain front, the motorcycle features an 11 kWh battery pack paired with an electric motor that produces 39.5 bhp and 550 Nm of peak wheel torque. It has a claimed top speed of 155 km/h and can accelerate from 0 to 100 km/h in 5.9 seconds.With the new VX-100 platform, the X47 Venom weighs 180 kg. It is equipped with the SRB-11 battery system, which supports DC fast charging at up to 12 kW.In terms of features, the electric motorcycle gets a 7-inch TFT touchscreen display paired with front and rear cameras. It also features a suite of advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS), including Blind Spot Monitoring, Lane Change Assist, Rear Collision Warning and Overtake Alert.This is a developing story, stay tuned for updates.    S  S                                                                         ü)Åi!5Å	%Q ª95148263342026-10-22T10:48:57ZNew Ultraviolette X-47 Venom Launch Price Rs 2.65 Lakh OnwardsRushLanerushlane.comhttps://www.rushlane.com/?p=559248engIndia?ƒîîîîîòThe first motorcycle on Ultraviolette's new VX-100 platform brings lower weight, rear radar, a 7-inch touchscreen and a claimed range of up to 343 km.Ultraviolette has launched the new X-47 Venom in India at an introductory starting price of Rs 2.65 lakh for the first 5,000 units. The regular starting price is Rs 3 lakh, translating into an introductory benefit of Rs 35,000. These starting prices apply to the 7 kWh version, while pricing for the 11 kWh option and the complete variant lineup is awaited.Bookings open at 4 pm today, October 22, with deliveries scheduled to begin in November 2026. The X-47 Venom introduces Ultraviolette's next-generation VX-100 architecture, which will also support future products.New VX-100 Platform Reduces WeightThe new 100V platform brings changes to the battery, motor and controller, aimed at improving efficiency and reducing weight. The motorcycle is quoted at 180 kg, making it up to 20 kg lighter than the previous generation.Ultraviolette says the new battery pack is 15% lighter and offers 25% higher energy density. An axial cooling arrangement replaces the earlier radial setup, with the company claiming twice the cooling performance.The new Light Fury motor operates at up to 9,000 rpm and uses soft magnetic components. According to Ultraviolette, motor weight has been reduced by 25-30%, while rare-earth material usage is down by 50%. The controller is also more compact and 40% lighter than the current-generation unit.Two Battery Options, Up To 343 Km RangeThe X-47 Venom will be available with 7 kWh and 11 kWh battery packs. The larger SRB-11 pack offers 11 kWh of usable capacity and a claimed IDC range of 343 km. Range for the entry-level 7 kWh version has not been detailed yet.Motor output of 30 kW, or approximately 40 bhp, and 550 Nm of torque at the wheel. Ultraviolette claims acceleration from 0-60 km/h in 2.7 seconds and 0-100 km/h in 5.9 seconds, along with a top speed of 155 km/h. The new platform supports DC fast charging at up to 12 kW, while an onboard charger adds convenience.Revised Regeneration And Battery ProtectionUltraviolette has also expanded the operating window of its performance features. Ballistic mode remains available down to 10% battery charge, while regenerative braking can operate from full charge, instead of becoming available only below 90%.Battery protection includes a pyro-fuse designed to isolate the circuit within microseconds if a critical fault is detected. This works alongside the battery management system and cell-level fuses. The battery enclosure carries an IP67 rating for protection against dust and water ingress.Rear Radar And New 7-Inch TouchscreenThe X-47 Venom features Ultraviolette's Hypersense system, using a 77 GHz rear radar with a claimed monitoring distance of up to 200 metres. Its functions include blind-spot monitoring, lane-change assistance, overtake alerts and rear-collision warnings. Hazard lights can activate when a threat is detected from behind.A new 7-inch touchscreen running Interface X forms the centre of the cockpit. The announced equipment includes onboard Mappls navigation, rear-camera park assist and cruise control. Connected features include software updates and VIOLETTE AI alerts for movement, falls, towing and crashes.Colours, Warranty And B-MAX Safety VestThe X-47 Venom will be offered in Afterburner Yellow, Turbo Red, Cosmic Black and Stellar White. Ultraviolette has also announced extendable warranty coverage of up to 8,00,000 km, with detailed terms and eligibility still to be clarified.Alongside the motorcycle, the company showcased its B-MAX safety vest. Ultraviolette claims 86% force attenuation and says the vest can be reused up to five times. Pricing for the vest has not been specified in the information available.   π π                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ñCÅj!5Å'%Å{ ®i95148253202026-10-22T10:48:04ZDucati Hypermotard V2 SP Price in India, Specifications and Features RevealedLatestLYlatestly.comhttps://www.latestly.com/auto/ducati-hypermotard-v2-sp-price-in-india-specifications-and-features-revealed-7653259.htmlengIndia?µDucati Hypermotard V2, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Price in India, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Specifications, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Features, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Launch, Ducati Hypermotard V2 890cc Engine, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Mileage, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Bookings, Ducati Bikes in India, Ducati Hypermotard V2 Price, Ducati Hypermotard V2 RedDucati has officially introduced the fourth-generation iteration of its high-performance supermotard range in India, bringing the track-focused Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP to enthusiast riders across the country. The updated model builds upon the manufacturer's iconic supermoto lineage, offering focused hardware upgrades designed for track usability and high-speed precision.The motorcycle features aggressive supermotard styling with an upright riding position, high-mounted wide handlebars, lightweight forged aluminium wheels, and a carbon-fibre front fender. Alongside its sharp visual design, the bike brings notable upgrade features, including a significantly reduced overall weight, a new variable intake valve timing system for stronger low-end torque, and a fully adjustable race-spec suspension layout. Ducati Hypermotard V2 Price in India, Specifications and Features Revealed.Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP Specifications and FeaturesThe Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP is powered by a new 890cc liquid-cooled V-twin engine with Intake Variable Timing (IVT), producing 120 hp at 10,750 rpm and 94 Nm of peak torque at 8,250 rpm, paired with a six-speed gearbox featuring Ducati Quick Shift 2.0.The chassis relies on an aluminium monocoque frame using the engine as a structural element, suspended by fully adjustable Ohlins 48mm NIX30 upside-down front forks and an Ohlins STX46 rear monoshock. Stopping power is delivered by dual front disc brakes with Brembo M50 monobloc callipers, backed by a six-axis inertial measurement unit operating cornering ABS, traction control, wheelie control, and engine brake control.Additional hardware includes forged aluminium wheels wrapped in Pirelli Diablo Rosso IV Corsa tyres, a 5-inch full-TFT display, a lightweight lithium-ion battery, a pit limiter, Ducati Power Launch, and dedicated riding modes including Race, Sport, Road, and Wet. The motorcycle has a dry kerb weight of 177 kg and a seat height of 880mm. Kawasaki Z300 Price in India, Specifications and Features Revealed.Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP Price in IndiaThe Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP carries an ex-showroom price of INR 20,78,000 in India. Pre-bookings for the track-focused supermotard are now open across authorised Ducati dealerships nationwide.    º 	( º                                                                                                                                                                                êhÅl%5Å]Å#'Åe úb-95148142452026-10-22T10:39:45ZTwo Odisha Sprinters Die in Road Accident; CM Mohan Charan Majhi Expresses Condolences - Yes Punjab NewsYesPunjab ‚Äì No.1 News-Portal. Latest News from Punjab, India & the World.yespunjab.comhttps://yespunjab.com/two-odisha-sprinters-die-in-road-accident-cm-mohan-charan-majhi-expresses-condolences/engIndiaøÃúúúúúùBhubaneswar, October 22, 2026 (Yes Punjab News)Two Odisha sprinters, Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malaya Barik, died in a road accident on National Highway 16 near Phulnakhara in Cuttack district late Wednesday night, triggering grief across the state's sporting fraternity.Dondapati, who hailed from Kalahandi district, was among India's fastest under-23 sprinters in 2025. Barik was from Bargarh district. Both athletes were training at the High Performance Centres (HPCs) at the Kalinga Stadium Sports Complex in Bhubaneswar.According to reports, a group comprising three athletes and a swimming coach was travelling on two two-wheelers towards Cuttack to attend a Sambalpuri Melody orchestra during the Durga Puja celebrations.Astik Pradhan, who recently won a silver medal in the men's 400-metre event at the U23 National Championships in Jaipur, was reportedly travelling on a separate two-wheeler about 50 metres behind the other members of the group.Reports said the two deceased athletes lost control of their vehicle and crashed into roadside barricades on the National Highway near Phulnakhara. They were rushed to SCB Medical College and Hospital, where doctors declared them dead.Odisha Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi, Sports Minister Suryabanshi Suraj and members of the sporting fraternity across the state and country expressed deep sorrow over the deaths.In a post on X, Chief Minister Majhi said, "Deeply saddened by the tragic demise of athletes Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malaya Barik in a road accident. Their untimely passing is a profound loss to Odisha's sporting fraternity. My heartfelt condolences to their bereaved families. May Mahaprabhu Shri Jagannath grant them strength in this difficult time and eternal peace to the departed souls."çTÅk%5Å9/Ç	 ñob-95148243282026-10-22T10:47:12ZShillong Tense After Fresh Petrol Bomb Attack Targets ED OfficeThe Sentinel Newspapersentinelassam.comhttps://www.sentinelassam.com/north-east-india-news/assam-news/shillong-tense-after-fresh-petrol-bomb-attack-targets-ed-officeengIndiaø≈ïïïïïîSecurity Tightened Across Capital as Masked Attackers Flee Scene; Police Analyze CCTV Footage After Spate of Government TargetingsTensions soared across Meghalaya's capital on Thursday after two masked assailants on a scooter hurled a petrol bomb at the Enforcement Directorate (ED) office in Shyiap, marking a critical escalation in a series of targeted attacks against government establishments.The incident occurred at approximately 12:05 AM at the ED office premises in the Langkyrding Mihngi locality. According to the East Khasi Hills Police, the on-duty security guard was positioned inside the building and did not notice the assault until morning.Official sources confirmed that while the incendiary device caused a fire scare, no injuries were reported, and the building sustained no major structural damage.This latest strike follows back-to-back arson attempts during recent festivities, including attacks on the Directorate of Employment and Craftsmen Training on Keating Road and the state Pollution Control Board. The shifting focus to a central government agency has forced the district administration to significantly step up vigil.Superintendent of Police Vivek Syiem stated that specialized teams are actively scanning local CCTV networks to unmask the perpetrators and identify the scooter's registration details. Meanwhile, intensive night patrolling has been deployed to secure central and state institutions across the city.   ’ ’                                                                                                                        