ontrol, Wheelie Control, and Engine Brake Control. The motorcycle carries a dry weight of 180 kg without fuel, a seat height of 880mm, and selectable riding modes including Road, Road Pro, and Track. BSA Gold Star 650 New Variants Launched in India; Check Price, Specs.Ducati Hypermotard V2 Price in IndiaThe Ducati Hypermotard V2 is priced at INR 16,53,000 (ex-showroom) for the standard variant in India. Bookings are officially open across Ducati dealerships nationwide, with the bike available in the classic Ducati Red colour scheme.     and warehouse space absorption also rose 9.1% to 3.6 million sq. ft. during the period, reflecting continued occupier demand. With manufacturing and 3PL companies fueling demand, locations such as Hoskote and Tumkur Road are emerging as key industrial and logistics hubs in Bengaluru.Bengaluru Industrial and Logistics Market: Top 5 Micro-MarketsBengaluru's industrial and logistics activity is concentrated in five major micro-markets: Hoskote, Tumkur Road, Hosur Road, Bellary Road and Mysore Road.HoskoteHoskote is emerging as a key industrial and logistics hub in eastern Bengaluru, supported by connectivity to NH 75 and the wider Narsapura industrial belt. Companies operating across this industrial region include Tata Electronics, Honda Motorcycle, Volvo, Aisin Automotive, Bando and Exedy Clutch, spanning electronics, automotive and engineering manufacturing.Hoskote registered two major industrial leasing transactions in H1 2026, covering 222,235 sq. ft. for a third-party logistics (3PL) operator and 208,000 sq. ft. for a manufacturing company. Together, the transactions spanned 430,235 sq. ft. of leased space. Grade-A industrial and logistics rents stood at approximately ‚Çπ30 per sq. ft. per month, compared with ‚Çπ28 in H1 2025. The combination of manufacturing activity, warehouse demand and road connectivity continues to enhance Hoskote's position in Bengaluru's industrial property market.Tumkur RoadTumkur Road is one of Bengaluru's preferred industrial and logistics micro-markets, supported by highway connectivity, established industrial clusters and the availability of Grade-A facilities. The corridor registered two major leasing transactions in H1 2026: 140,000 sq. ft. leased by a third-party logistics (3PL) operator and 110,000 sq. ft. by an FMCG/FMCD occupier. Together, the transactions spanned 250,000 sq. ft. of industrial and logistics space.Grade-A rental values for industrial and logistics space in Tumkur Road stood at approximately ‚Çπ29 per sq. ft. per month in H1 2026, compared with ‚Çπ28 in H1 2025. Grade-B rentals were around ‚Çπ24 per sq. ft. per month, against ‚Çπ22 a year earlier. The corridor's industrial ecosystem and connectivity to major highways continue to fuel demand from logistics operators and consumer goods companies.Hosur RoadHosur Road is an important industrial corridor in southern Bengaluru, connecting manufacturing clusters in Bommasandra, Jigani and Attibele with Hosur in Tamil Nadu. 100,000 sq. ft. of industrial space was leased in the Hosur Road micro-market during H1 2026, underscoring demand for manufacturing facilities.As a rental benchmark, Cushman & Wakefield reported warehouse rents of ‚Çπ24-27 per sq. ft. per month across Hosur Road, including Jigani and Attibele, in H1 2025, with annual growth of 3-4%. Industrial land prices ranged from ‚Çπ70 lakh to ‚Çπ1.2 crore per acre, registering year-on-year growth of 9-10%. The corridor's connectivity to Tamil Nadu and Bengaluru's manufacturing ecosystem supports industrial activity, warehousing and goods movement.Bellary RoadBellary Road is an important industrial and logistics corridor in north Bengaluru, benefiting from connectivity to Kempegowda International Airport and industrial areas in Devanahalli. Its location supports logistics operations, manufacturing and the movement of goods across Bengaluru and surrounding districts. 110,000 sq. ft. of industrial space was leased on Bellary Road in H1 2026.The micro-market also has an established industrial base. Savills' H1 2025 report recorded 423,312 sq. ft. of manufacturing-related absorption on Bellary Road, accounting for 20% of Bengaluru's total industrial and logistics absorption during that period. This provides historical evidence of the corridor's role in manufacturing-led demand. Airport conn                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   x ix                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ¢ZÅv!5Ç)EÉ) æM95147994112026-10-22T10:27:32ZFirst terrorism, then Naxalism, now drugs: By 2029, Amit Shah sets hard deadline to wipe out India's narcotics menace & Punjab crisisEconomic Timeseconomictimes.indiatimes.comhttps://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/new-updates/first-terrorism-then-naxalism-now-drugs-by-2029-amit-shah-sets-hard-deadline-to-wipe-out-indias-narcotics-menace-punjab-crisis/articleshow/135115193.cmsengIndiaøÀõõõõõõUnion home minister Amit Shah has set December    ŸìÅu!5Å913Å °Q95147995502026-10-22T10:27:42ZWATCH: Leopard Spotted In Kanifnath Ghat On Beed-Ahilyanagar Highway; Video Goes ViralFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/pune/watch-leopard-spotted-in-kanifnath-ghat-on-beed-ahilyanagar-highway-video-goes-viralengIndia?™!Forest Department steps up vigilance, advises motorists and farmers to exercise cautionBeed: Commuters travelling along the Beed-Ahilyanagar Highway at night were in for a startling encounter when a fully grown leopard was spotted roaming near the road in the historic Kanifnath Ghat at Pimpri (Ghata) village in Ashti tehsil, about 110 km from the district headquarters, on Monday night.According to sources, a motorist passing through the ghat captured the leopard on his mobile phone while driving along a bend in the hilly stretch. The video, showing the animal moving near the road, has since gone viral on social media, triggering concern among motorists, farmers and livestock owners in the area.Watch Video:The motorist noticed the animal near the roadside, apparently searching for prey. As the leopard's eyes reflected the vehicle's headlights, the driver slowed down and recorded the animal from inside his car.The leopard reportedly moved around the road for a while before disappearing into dense bushes along the hillside.Hundreds of two-wheelers and four-wheelers pass through Kanifnath Ghat every day. Several agricultural settlements are also located near the foothills, where farmers and their families live alongside livestock. The sighting has raised concerns about the safety of residents, particularly those travelling on two-wheelers at night.Following the sighting, the Forest Department has stepped up vigilance in the area. Farmers have been advised to keep their livestock in secure cattle sheds instead of leaving them tied in open areas.Motorists, particularly two-wheeler riders, have been urged to exercise caution while passing through the ghat at night and avoid stopping their vehicles unnecessarily.Ashti Range Forest Officer Amol Munde confirmed that a leopard had been reported in the Daulwadgaon area of Ashti tehsil. The animal was captured on CCTV footage at a farmer's house on the night of Oct 17. He said forest staff were keeping a watch on the location.Munde appealed to residents and farmers to avoid venturing into forested and hilly areas late at night and early in the morning.    31, 2029, as the target to make India drug-free, saying the Centre will focus on tackling the narcotics menace after its fight against terrorism and armed Naxalism. Speaking on Police Commemoration Day, Shah also credited security forces for their role in LWE-affected regions. Around 7,000 people from 126 districts affected by left-wing extremism will attend the Ekta Diwas parade in Gujarat on October 31.After terrorism and decades of armed Naxalism, the Centre is turning its attention to India's drug menace, with Union home minister Amit Shah setting December 31, 2029, as the target date to make the country narcotics-free. Addressing an event in New Delhi on Wednesday to mark Police Commemoration Day, Shah said peace had been established in three major conflict-hit regions, Jammu and Kashmir, the Northeast and areas affected by left-wing extremism (LWE). He said the government would now focus on tackling drug trafficking and substance abuse, calling on police forces across the country to participate in the implementation of the 'Nasha Mukt Bharat' roadmap.Shah also described 2026 as a significant year for Indian police forces, saying they had brought an end to the decades-old threat of violent Naxalism.Amit Shah sets December 31, 2029, deadline for a drug-free IndiaThe home minister said the remaining part of 2026 and the following three years would be dedicated to freeing India from the drug menace.Read more - Driving licence new rules: 75% pass mark, 15-day deadline for name & address changes, some online services may be free; check what could change soonHe urged police forces nationwide to take an active role in implementing the government's anti-drug roadmap, signalling that tackling narcotics would be a major priority for the Union home ministry after its focus on terrorism and left-wing extremism.Shah also flagged off a nationwide motorcycle rally carrying the message of a 'fight against drugs'. Five riders each from 36 states and Union territories, along with nine Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs), are taking part in the rally.The riders will travel from different parts of the country to Kevadia in Gujarat, where they will join the Ekta Diwas parade on October 31.Amit Shah credits CRPF, CoBRA and Chhattisgarh Police in fight against NaxalismShah said an environment conducive to development had emerged in Jammu and Kashmir, the Northeast and LWE-affected areas following efforts to tackle violence and restore peace.Read more - When a 25-year-old woman went into labour aboard a train to Patna, railway officials sprang into action; baby boy born inside Ahmedabad-Barauni ExpressHe particularly thanked the Central Reserve Police Force (CRPF), its Commando Battalion for Resolute Action (CoBRA) and Chhattisgarh Police for their role in the fight against left-wing extremism.The Centre had set March 31, 2026, as the deadline to end armed Naxalism. The government plans to mark the end of armed Naxalism alongside the 150th anniversary of 'Vande Mataram' at this year's Rashtriya Ekta Diwas celebrations.7,000 people from Naxal-affected districts to attend Ekta Diwas paradeAround 7,000 people from 126 districts previously affected by left-wing extremism will participate in the Rashtriya Ekta Diwas parade and Bharat Parv in Kevadia, Gujarat, on October 31. They will attend as performers and spectators at the event, which will also be attended by Prime MinisterNarendra Modi.Around 5,000 additional local residents from these districts have also been invited."Their participation will underline the resilience of communities that have endured conflict and highlight the role of cultural expression in strengthening national integration," Union home secretary Govind Mohan said.The parade will also feature march-pasts by contingents of the CAPFs and state police forces that fought against LWE-related violence.Police Commemoration Day honours 36,852 personnelOn P                                                                                                                                              . .                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  °Åx!5w7!Å_ æM95147891142026-10-22T10:19:40ZHow Delhi Police Dismantled An Interstate Heroin RingRediff.com India Ltd.rediff.comhttps://www.rediff.com/news/report/delhi-police-busts-interstate-heroin-network-seizes-81-kg/20261022.htmengIndiaøƒîîîîîïDelhi Police have successfully dismantled a sophisticated interstate heroin manufacturing and supply network, arresting seven individuals and seizing over Rs 60 crore worth of contraband, highlighting a significant blow against drug traffic   €ó]Åw!5Ç!Çm ©=95147975772026-10-22T10:26:00ZPoor Girlfriend-Boyfriend Wanted To Marry, Stole Gold Chain From 60-Year-Old Woman To Fund Wedding In Hyderabad, But CCTV Changed The GameNewsXnewsx.comhttps://www.newsx.com/regionals/poor-girlfriend-boyfriend-wanted-to-marry-stole-gold-chain-from-60-year-old-woman-to-fund-wedding-in-hyderabad-but-cctv-changed-the-game-286074/engIndiaøø A young Andhra Pradesh couple was arrested in Hyderabad for allegedly snatching a 60-year-old temple worker's gold chain to fund their wedding plans. CCTV footage helped police trace the accused.A young couple from Andhra Pradesh has been arrested for allegedly snatching a gold chain of about three tolas from a 60-year-old woman at the Sri Rajarajeshwari temple in Vanasthalipuram, Hyderabad. According to police, the two wanted to get married but did not have the money. They were caught about two days after the incident with the help of CCTV footage and other leads.A Woman Alone At The TempleRamulamma, 60, works at the temple. On the morning of the incident, she was alone, going about her work in a place where few people were around at that hour.A young man and woman walked up to her. Police say they offered to help her. The offer was only a pretext.The SnatchingAccording to the police account, the couple pressed the woman's mouth shut so she could not call for help and pulled the gold chain, weighing about three tolas, from her neck. They then rode away on a two-wheeler before anyone could react.Who Are The Accused?Police have identified the accused as Durga Ramana Reddy, 23, from Macherla in Andhra Pradesh, and Tenka Varalakshmi, 24, from the Kakinada area. Police say the two had known each other for around a year and a half and wanted to marry. A lack of money, however, stood in the way of their plans.A Plan Built On WatchingThe investigation indicates that the couple did not act on impulse. Police say they kept an eye on the temple's routine and learnt that few people visit early in the morning. That quiet window, and an elderly woman working by herself, is what they allegedly chose to exploit.How CCTV Closed InAfter the incident, police went through CCTV footage from the area and traced the movements of the two. Leads gathered during the inquiry helped them narrow down the suspects. Both were picked up near Kamalanayak at around 9 am on October 20.Police AdvicePolice have asked women, particularly elderly women who go out alone, to stay alert. Officials said people should take care when wearing gold jewellery in isolated places. Patrolling and crime prevention teams will keep watch in the area to stop similar incidents.The Road AheadThe arrests have solved the case on the surface, but the investigation is still on. Police will need to establish whether the couple were involved in any other offences, and what became of the stolen chain. How the case proceeds in court will show how a plan made for a wedding ended in the arrest of both partners before they could marry.    king in the region.IMAGE: This is an AI-generated image and has been used only for representational purposes.Key Points* Delhi Police busted an alleged interstate heroin manufacturing and supply network, arresting seven persons on Thursday.* Over 8 kg of heroin, valued at around Rs 60 crore, along with chemicals, cash, and vehicles, were recovered.* The network allegedly sourced raw opium from Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh, processing it into heroin at a Lucknow unit.* Key arrests include an alleged raw opium supplier from Jharkhand's Chatra district and individuals involved in manufacturing and distribution.* The operation, which began on September 16, successfully dismantled the entire supply chain from cultivation to distribution.The Delhi Police has busted an alleged interstate heroin manufacturing and supply network spanning Delhi, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Jharkhand, arresting seven persons and recovering more than 8 kg of the contraband worth around Rs 60 crore in the illicit market, officials said on Thursday.The operation has led to the arrest of an alleged raw opium supplier from Jharkhand's Naxal-affected Chatra district, allegedly involved in illegal cultivation of poppy on his agricultural land, police said.Police have also seized nearly 3.3 kg of chemicals and other raw materials used in heroin-manufacture, Rs 12.81 lakh in cash, three SUVs, a motorcycle and equipment allegedly used in production of the contraband.Investigation has revealed that raw opium was allegedly sourced from Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh, processed into heroin at an illicit manufacturing unit in Lucknow and supplied through a network operating across Delhi-NCR and other states, police said.Initial Bust And SeizuresThe operation began on September 16 when a Delhi Police team, acting on specific inputs, intercepted an SUV in Sector 32 of north-west Delhi's Begumpur and apprehended Laxman Hooda, 58, who had allegedly arrived to deliver a heroin consignment.Police recovered 300 grams of heroin and Rs 3 lakh from the vehicle, which was seized.The next day, police apprehended an alleged supplier, Anil alias Bhola, 51, from Sonipat in Haryana and recovered 501 grams of heroin from his SUV.Anil has been previously involved in 12 criminal cases and was arrested in a narcotics case registered at Bhalswa Dairy police station in 2025. He allegedly failed to surrender after being granted interim bail and was subsequently declared a proclaimed offender by a court, police said.Key Arrests And Network UnravelledFurther investigation, aided by technical surveillance and human intelligence, led the team to a heroin manufacturing facility in Lucknow, where Bablu, 35, was apprehended on October 4.The raid resulted in the recovery of 6.275 kg of freshly manufactured heroin, along with 2.5 kg of sodium, 787 grams of acetic anhydride and equipment, including a gas cylinder, mixer-grinder, tub, utensils, an electronic weighing machine and other material allegedly used in the manufacturing process.Lucknow Manufacturing Unit RaidedActing on Bablu's disclosures, police traced and apprehended Ruksar Ali alias Raju, the alleged owner of the manufacturing facility, from Bareilly in Uttar Pradesh, officials said.On October 6, the team arrested Ajaj Ahmed, 38, from Bareilly with the help of technical surveillance. He allegedly supplied crude opium to Ruksar Ali. Police recovered 501 grams of heroin and a Royal Enfield motorcycle from him.The investigation subsequently led to the arrest of Mohammad Azhar, 20, from Badaun in Uttar Pradesh on October 16. He allegedly supplied heroin and crude opium to Ajaj Ahmed. Police recovered 551 grams of heroin, Rs 9.81 lakh in cash and an SUV from him.Tra                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Í Í                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                öÅy!5Å'-Åk ∞95147835222026-10-22T10:14:54ZBKT, Pirelli join hands to manufacture passenger car tyres in IndiaAutocar Indiaautocarindia.comhttps://www.autocarindia.com/industry/bkt-pirelli-join-hands-to-manufacture-passenger-car-tyres-in-india-441108engIndia? öööööòA new manufacturing plant is also being planned as part of the proposed joint venture.Indian tyre maker Balkrishna Industries (BKT) and Italian tyre maker Pirelli have signed a series of agreements to manufacture Pirelli-branded passenger car tyres in India, with plans to establish a 50/50 joint venture in a second phase. While the companies have signed a framework agreement, an offtake agreement, and a technical services agreement, a definitive joint venture agreement is yet to be signed.The partnership will combine Pirelli's expertise in high-calibre passenger car tyres with BKT's manufacturing capabilities and industrial presence in India. While Pirelli has a commercial presence in India, it does not currently operate a local tyre manufacturing facility. BKT, meanwhile, is primarily known for its off-highway tyres - used in applications like agriculture, mining, construction, and industrial - though it has been expanding into other segments, including passenger car tyres, commercial-vehicle radial tyres, and two-wheeler tyres.BKT-Pirelli tyre manufacturing partnership detailsUnder the initial phase of the partnership, BKT plans to manufacture up to 8,00,000 Pirelli-branded passenger car radial tyres in India by 2030. The tyres will be produced in line with Pirelli's technical and quality standards, and then supplied to the Italian brand and its affiliates for sale in India and overseas markets.The initial manufacturing arrangement will remain in place until December 31, 2031, unless the proposed joint venture can meet Pirelli's requirements earlier. It also includes minimum annual purchase commitments from Pirelli, matched by corresponding production capacity commitments from BKT. Both companies are targeting the incorporation of the joint venture by December 31, 2030, subject to the fulfilment of applicable conditions.New manufacturing facility planned for high-value passenger car tyresIn the second phase, the proposed joint venture will establish a dedicated manufacturing plant in India to produce high-value passenger car tyres under both the Pirelli and BKT brands, with the products catering to both domestic and international markets. However, Pirelli and BKT have not disclosed the proposed plant's location, investment, production capacity, or detailed product portfolio. The joint venture is expected to have a four-member board, with each company nominating two directors.Under a separate technical services arrangement, Pirelli will also support BKT's development of passenger car, SUV, and two-wheeler tyres sold under the Indian brand. This will include access to overseas testing facilities, proving grounds, and simulation equipment.Partnership targets India's growing premium tyre marketFor this partnership, Pirelli and BKT are banking on an expansion of demand for premium tyres in the Indian passenger vehicle market. The companies estimate that car registrations in India will grow by 5-7 percent annually until 2030, while the premium car tyre market could grow almost fivefold over the same period.   ú ú                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ú`Åz!5Å=+1ÇG ¥'95147824462026-10-22T10:13:58ZDelhi Police busts interstate heroin network, seizes 8.1 kg contraband worth ‚Çπ60 croreHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/delhi-news/delhi-police-busts-interstate-heroin-network-seizes-8-1-kg-contraband-worth-rs-60-crore-101792663876794.htmlengIndiaø›]]]]]]New Delhi, The Delhi Police has busted an alleged interstate heroin manufacturing and supply network spanning Delhi, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Jharkhand, arresting seven persons and recovering more than 8 kg of the contraband worth around ‚Çπ60 crore in the illicit market, officials said on Thursday.The operation has led to the arrest of an alleged raw opium supplier from Jharkhand's Naxal-affected Chatra district, allegedly involved in illegal cultivation of poppy on his agricultural land, police said.Police have also seized nearly 3.3 kg of chemicals and other raw materials used in heroin-manufacture, ‚Çπ12.81 lakh in cash, three SUVs, a motorcycle and equipment allegedly used in production of the contraband.Investigation has revealed that raw opium was allegedly sourced from Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh, processed into heroin at an illicit manufacturing unit in Lucknow and supplied through a network operating across Delhi-NCR and other states, police said.The operation began on September 16 when a Delhi Police team, acting on specific inputs, intercepted an SUV in Sector 32 of north-west Delhi's Begumpur and apprehended Laxman Hooda, 58, who had allegedly arrived to deliver a heroin consignment.Police recovered 300 grams of heroin and ‚Çπ3 lakh from the vehicle, which was seized.The next day, police apprehended an alleged supplier, Anil alias Bhola, 51, from Sonipat in Haryana and recovered 501 grams of heroin from his SUV.Anil has been previously involved in 12 criminal cases and was arrested in a narcotics case registered at Bhalswa Dairy police station in 2025. He allegedly failed to surrender after being granted interim bail and was subsequently declared a proclaimed offender by a court, police said.Further investigation, aided by technical surveillance and human intelligence, led the team to a heroin manufacturing facility in Lucknow, where Bablu, 35, was apprehended on October 4.The raid resulted in the recovery of 6.275 kg of freshly manufactured heroin, along with 2.5 kg of sodium, 787 grams of acetic anhydride and equipment, including a gas cylinder, mixer-grinder, tub, utensils, an electronic weighing machine and other material allegedly used in the manufacturing process.Acting on Bablu's disclosures, police traced and apprehended Ruksar Ali alias Raju, the alleged owner of the manufacturing facility, from Bareilly in Uttar Pradesh, officials said.On October 6, the team arrested Ajaj Ahmed, 38, from Bareilly with the help of technical surveillance. He allegedly supplied crude opium to Ruksar Ali. Police recovered 501 grams of heroin and a Royal Enfield motorcycle from him.The investigation subsequently led to the arrest of Mohammad Azhar, 20, from Badaun in Uttar Pradesh on October 16. He allegedly supplied heroin and crude opium to Ajaj Ahmed. Police recovered 551 grams of heroin, ‚Çπ9.81 lakh in cash and an SUV from him.The final link was traced to Chatra district of Jharkhand, where Prakash Kumar, 31, was arrested on October 18. He allegedly supplied raw opium to the accused and was involved in illegal cultivation of opium poppy on his agricultural land, police said.With these arrests, police claimed to have dismantled the alleged network spanning raw opium cultivation, procurement of raw materials, heroin manufacturing and distribution.   $ å$                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        ñdÅ|%5Å'Å- ™b-95147767462026-10-22T10:10:14ZNew Bajaj Pulsar N250SS Launched at Rs 1.59 Lakh | MotoroidsMotoroidsmotoroids.comhttps://www.motoroids.com/news/new-bajaj-pulsar-n250ss-launched-at-rs-1-59-lakh/engIndia?úFollowing its recent sighting at a dealership, Bajaj Auto has formally launched the Pulsar N250SS in India. The motorcycle is priced at Rs 1,59,406 (ex-showroom, Delhi) and costs around Rs 14,000 more than the standard Pulsar N250. It gets changes to the engine, gearbox and electronic equipment, along with a new instrument display.The update brings several features that were missing from the earlier model. These include a quickshifter, ride modes, Google Maps mirroring and adjustable levers.New Engine and Six-Speed GearboxThe Pulsar N250SS continues to use a 249cc, single-cylinder engine. However, Bajaj has changed the engine from a two-valve to a four-valve setup. This brings a small increase in power and torque.Here are the engine specifications:* Engine: 249cc, single-cylinder* Maximum power: 25 PS (24.6bhp)* Peak torque: 22 Nm* Gearbox: Six-speed* Quickshifter: Sports ShifterThe standard N250 produces 24.5 PS and 21.5 Nm of torque. The new version makes slightly more power and torque, while the additional sixth gear replaces the five-speed transmission.The six-speed gearbox should also help make highway rides more comfortable by providing an extra gear for cruising. The Sports Shifter allows clutchless gear changes under suitable riding conditions.TFT Display and New FeaturesAnother major change is the instrument console. Bajaj has replaced the standard motorcycle's LCD unit with a 5-inch TFT screen. The new display supports Google Maps mirroring, which can help riders follow navigation directions while travelling.The motorcycle also gets an electronic throttle body (ETB). This system works with ride modes to adjust the motorcycle's response according to the selected setting. The existing ABS modes are also available.Other additions include:* Adjustable brake and clutch levers* USB Type-C charging port* Hazard warning switch* Panic Brake Alert* 5-inch TFT instrument console* Google Maps mirroring* Electronic throttle body with ride modesThese features add to the motorcycle's equipment list without changing its basic engine capacity or overall mechanical layout.Bajaj Pulsar N250SS SpecificationsMassive Updates Across the Pulsar FamilyThis launch comes at a busy time for Bajaj, as the company celebrates the 25th anniversary of the Pulsar brand. The manufacturer has been aggressively updating its entire portfolio, rolling out feature-rich models across various engine capacities.Recent updates have included the N160, new-generation Pulsar 125 and Pulsar 150, along with the NS400Z TFT variant. The N250SS now brings similar attention to equipment and electronics to the quarter-litre N series.ÜpÅ{!5Å	5%Å5 ä95147783662026-10-22T10:10:54ZMan shot dead in Punjab's Tarn Taran hours afte... | UNI IndiaUnited News of Indiauniindia.comhttps://www.uniindia.com/north-india/crime-punjab-tarn-taran-gangster-rivalry/221735engIndiaøÈ˘˘˘˘˘˙Neeraj Bali Chandigarh, Oct 22 (UNI) A 40-year-old man was shot dead by two masked motorcycle-borne assailants in Punjab's Tarn Taran district on Wednesday evening, hours after being released from police custody, in what investigators suspect was a revenge killing linked to a deadly rivalry between criminal gangs, police said. The victim, identified as Kuldeep Singh, a house painter from Naushehra Pannuan village, was on his way to a barber's shop at around 6:30 p.m. when the attackers opened fire and fled. Gangsters identifying themselves as Landa Harike and Satta Naushehra claimed responsibility for the killing in a social media...    hra Pradesh State Election Commission to examine the YSRCP's complaints and decide where civic poll nominations should reopen. File Special Arrangement Special Arrangement https://th-i.thgim.com/public/news/national/8ktjfk/article71607297.ece/alternates/FREE_1200/6744_19_8_2025_16_15_17_2_18_08_2025_SUPREME_COURT04.jpgThe Supreme Court has asked the State Election Commission to decide where candidates were unable to file nominationsThe story so far:The YSR Congress Party (YSRCP)'s allegation of obstructions during the filing of nominations for elections to urban local bodies (ULBs) has landed the State Election Commission (SEC) in a tight spot, and the process has come under the Supreme Court's scrutiny. The focus has now shifted from political claims to the SEC's ability to establish a level playing field.https://www.thehindu.com/topic/yuvajana-sramika-rythu-congress-party/ https://www.thehindu.com/topic/andhra-pradesh-local-body-elections-2026/The question in Andhra Pradesh's municipal elections is no longer only who will win the civic bodies. It is also whether every eligible candidate gets a fair opportunity to enter the contest. The Supreme Court's intervention, following a petition by the YSRCP, has come at a critical stage of the electoral process.https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/ https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/andhra-pradesh-govt-issues-rules-paving-way-for-direct-election-of-mayors-municipal-chairpersons/article71432356.ece https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/supreme-court-finds-prima-facie-case-in-ysrcp-plea-for-more-time-to-file-nominations-in-andhra-civic-polls/article71606630.eceBy directing the Commission to examine complaints of alleged obstruction, consider extending nomination deadlines wherever it finds candidates were unable to file papers because of the law-and-order situation, and defer publication of the final candidates' list till October 25, the court has made it clear that adherence to an election calendar cannot, by itself, settle concerns about electoral fairness.https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/supreme-court-finds-prima-facie-case-in-ysrcp-plea-for-more-time-to-file-nominations-in-andhra-civic-polls/article71606630.eceSupreme Court defers AP municipal poll final list to October 25 on YSRCP plea, directs SEC to decide on nominationsSupreme Court defers AP municipal poll final list to October 25 on YSRCP plea, directs SEC to decide on nominationsThe court holds that the YSRCP has made out a prima facie case in its plea for more time to file nominationsAndhra Pradesh SEC halts election process for 100 ULBs after Supreme Court orderAndhra Pradesh SEC halts election process for 100 ULBs after Supreme Court orderSEC will issue an order on the ULB elections on October 22 after obtaining reports from Collectors, District Election and Police authoritiesLocal body polls in Andhra Pradesh: YSRCP welcomes Supreme Court directions, urges SEC to ensure free and fair electionsLocal body polls in Andhra Pradesh: YSRCP welcomes Supreme Court directions, urges SEC to ensure free and fair electionsSajjala urges the State Election Commissioner to ensure CCTV surveillance at the nomination centresThe court's directions do not establish the YSRCP's allegations as true. They do, however, require the authorities to examine whether any candidate was denied the opportunity to contest because of a breakdown in law and order.What does the YSRCP allege?The YSRCP approached the Supreme Court after the Andhra Pradesh High Court declined, on October 18, to extend the nomination deadline. The party had first approached the High Court before the nomination process began, seeking preventive measures over its apprehensions of violence. A single judge declin                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Û Û                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       êÅ~!5Å-3Ç õc95147640682026-10-22T10:01:43ZCourt Rejects Plea to Shift Mini Cooper Crash Accused to Central PrisonDeccan Chronicledeccanchronicle.comhttps://www.deccanchronicle.com/southern-states/kerala/court-rejects-plea-to-shift-mini-cooper-crash-accused-to-central-prison-1997853engIndiaøÀõõõõõõSuhail's admission to the Borstal School, which houses prisoners aged between 18 and 21, had earlier drawn criticismKochi: A court here on Thursday dismissed a petition by the superintendent of the Borstal School seeking to shift the prime accused in the Mini Cooper crash that killed three youngsters in Nedumbassery here, to a central prison. Angamaly Judicial First Class Magistrate Samyuktha M K dismissed the petition filed by the superintendent of the Borstal School in Kakkanad, which houses prisoners aged between 18 and 21, seeking Suhail's transfer to a central prison on security grounds.The petition cited security concerns over his continued stay at the facility.However, the magistrate dismissed it after examining the plea.Suhail's admission to the Borstal School had earlier drawn criticism.Suhail, 19, was allegedly driving the car when it rammed into a scooter carrying three youngsters on the airport road at Nedumbassery in the early hours of October 11.Three others who were travelling in the car were also arrested after police found that the occupants were heavily drunk and the vehicle was allegedly travelling at over 100 kmph.Meanwhile, a five-member investigation team visited the house of Devika, a native of Kalpetta in Wayanad and one of the three victims, on Thursday morning.The team recorded statements and interacted with her family for over an hour, officials said.After the accident, the family members told reporters that they are hopeful that justice would be delivered and that investigators have collected all crucial evidence in the case.Recently, the magistrate court had dismissed the bail petitions of the accused persons.They have filed fresh petitions at the Ernakulam District Principal Sessions Court.°iÅ}!5Å3%ÇU æM95147707502026-10-22T10:05:54ZWhy are Andhra Pradesh's civic poll nominations under the Supreme Court's scrutiny?The Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/why-are-andhra-pradeshs-civic-poll-nominations-under-the-supreme-courts-scrutiny-explained/article71610915.eceengIndia?◊◊◊◊◊◊◊Why are Andhra Pradesh's civic poll nominations under the Supreme Court's scrutiny? | Explained left The Supreme Court in New Delhi. The court has asked the And   ﬂ   ; ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 óAÅ!5É1CÑ ¶+95147487852026-10-22T09:49:21ZBengaluru's traffic takes a holiday: Google Maps shows just 21 minutes for 13 km from Silk Board to Marathahalli; commuter hilariously jokes that he can't blame traffic for being late anymoreThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/bengalurus-traffic-takes-a-holiday-google-maps-shows-just-21-minutes-for-13-km-from-silk-board-to-marathahalli-commuter-hilariously-jokes-that-he-cant-blame-traffic-for-being-late-anymore/articleshow/135114786.cmsengIndia?––––––œBengaluru is well known for its notorious traffic, which tests anybody's patience. Commuters often cite these traffic jams as spending immensely long hours in the vehicle lanes on the road.Regular commuters are well-versed with traffic woes, but recently during the festive season, the roads have seen a visible dip in traffic as many people have moved back to their hometowns to celebrate the festive season.A recent Instagram post has people smiling as he explained how two of Bengaluru's best-known traffic hotspots would take only 21 minutes to cover 13 kmBengaluru commuter shares how commute between Silk Board and Marathahalli took only 21 minutes to cover 13 kmsA man shared on Instagram that a two-wheeler ride from Silk Board to Marathahalli, two of Bengaluru's best-known traffic hotspots, would take only 21 minutes to cover 13 km.The short ride made him joke that employees could no longer blame traffic for being late. The text on his Google Maps screenshot read, "Guys, please come back, I can't use traffic as an excuse for showing up at 12 for a 9 AM shift."He posted the screenshot with the caption, "Bangalore is not Bangaloring, and the traffic is not trafficking," teasing the city for its reputation for frustrating jams.Social media users weigh inThe post quickly got attention online, and many people reacted with sarcasm and surprise.One user said, "I couldn't believe I have been reaching office in 35 min...usually it takes me 2 hrs...everytime during festivals I get to experience my old Bangalore." Another wrote, "Reached office in 20 mins 10km... N then came back collecting my gift in 20 mins. .. no one in office."A third person wrote, "I pray to God, let it be like this all the time." Another user wrote, "No no no.... Take more leave.... Enjoy your vacation.... Or work from where ever you are for some more time."Another user shared a prior experience, "Banglore is Bangloring, caption is wrong. When I was like 5 we could reach Whitefield from anywhere in max 45 min at any time this is real bengaluru. Traffic ruined it."Another wrote, "Just say Cab nahi mil rahi thi. And add 'Even cab drivers are gone because of long weekend.' It works"Someone else joked, "Just hang in there for few more days , we will be back soon."Another person said, "So infrastructure is actually not the problem... current infrastructure which is unable to handle the current population of our city Bangalore is the problem."   Â «÷Â                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       °_Ç!5Ç %)ÇW ΩY95147409982026-10-22T09:42:33ZBalkrishna Industries Q1 FY27: Net profit climbs 56% YoY on robust ‚Çπ3,455.27 Cr revenue backed by major Pirelli partnershipTrade Brainstradebrains.inhttps://tradebrains.in/indian-markets/balkrishna-industries-q1-fy27-net-profit-climbs-56-yoy-on-robust-345527-cr-revenue-backed-by-major-pirelli-partnership-12717036engIndia? öööööòBalkrishna Industries signed three agreements with Pirelli on 22 October, covering a 50:50 passenger car tyre jo   ‰ükÇ!5ÅaE=ÇS πg95147453262026-10-22T09:46:23ZWATCH: Jhansi Girl Chases Down and Catches Scooter-Borne Harasser in Fearless Street Act, Video Goes ViralAsianet News Network Pvt Ltdnewsable.asianetnews.comhttps://newsable.asianetnews.com/india/watch-jhansi-girl-chases-down-and-catches-scooter-borne-harasser-in-fearless-street-act-video-goes-viral-articleshow-omaei7lengIndiaø‘TTTTTTA young woman in Jhansi, Uttar Pradesh, chased down a man who allegedly slapped her while riding a scooter.   „é5Ç !5Å-%Ç	 ò995147471712026-10-22T09:48:12ZBengaluru Rains: Heavy Showers Hit City, IMD Issues Yellow Alert Till October 26Oneindiaoneindia.comhttps://www.oneindia.com/bengaluru/bengaluru-rains-heavy-showers-hit-city-imd-issues-yellow-alert-till-october-26-8241899.htmlengIndiaø≥Bengaluru witnessed a spell of heavy rain on Thursday afternoon, October 22, catching many people off guard. The showers brought down the temperature but also made travel difficult, with motorists, pedestrians and two wheeler riders struggling to get through the rain.Jayanagar and Lalbagh were among the areas that received heavy showers. Light to moderate rain was also reported in Corporation, KR Market, Shantinagar, Vidhana Soudha, Rajajinagar and Malleshwaram.As the rain picked up, people out on the roads rushed to find shelter. Two wheeler riders stopped under flyovers and outside roadside shops, while pedestrians walked through the rain holding umbrellas.The India Meteorological Department (IMD) has issued a yellow alert for Bengaluru and other southern interior districts of Karnataka until October 26. The department has forecast rain across several parts of the region over the next few days.Bengaluru Urban and Bengaluru Rural are among the districts likely to receive rainfall. In contrast, rain activity is expected to remain lower in the coastal and northern interior parts of Karnataka.The maximum temperature in Bengaluru is expected to be around 27¬∞C on Thursday, while the minimum is likely to be 21¬∞C. Cloudy skies and relatively cool weather are expected to continue.The IMD's seven day forecast also warns of thunderstorms, lightning and gusty winds in parts of Karnataka. The southern interior districts are likely to receive heavy rain between October 22 and 26, for which the department has issued a yellow alert.     After a viral video captured the confrontation, the accused was arrested by Premnagar police, who are searching for his two accomplices.In what is known as an act of immense courage and quick thinking, a victim reportedly chased down a two-wheeler perpetrator for over 50 metres after being assaulted and slapped in Jhansi, Uttar Pradesh, on Tuesday, October 20.In a video that went viral on social media, the girl was seen chasing the man for around 50 metres before catching him and pulling him off his scooter, as bystanders and onlookers watched the confrontation unfold. Shen then allegedly thrashed him as a crowd gathered at the spot.Since cases of street harassment and eve-teasing continue to pose significant safety concerns for women in public spaces, the girl's brave call to take the matter into her own hands to confront the alleged harasser has drawn attention online, with the video going viral on social media.Related ArticlesHow Did the Incident Unfold?The streets of Jhansi witnessed a dramatic confrontation near the Malgodam railway crossing in the Premnagar area, where a man allegedly harassed a woman riding a scooter. The accused was reportedly confronted by the woman after he allegedly slapped her and attempted to flee the scene on his two-wheeler.In a viral video on X (formerly Twitter), three men can be seen riding on a single scooter before one of them allegedly slaps the girl. Instead of remaining passive spectators, the woman took immediate action. She sprinted after the scooter, grabbed the alleged harasser, and forcefully dragged him off the moving vehicle.Immediately, the crowd began to gather around the accused as the confrontation escalated. Seeing the victim fearlessly stand her ground, several onlookers stepped in to ensure the suspect could not slip away again.Scroll to load tweet...Under pressure from the gathered crowd, who witnessed the girl chasing down the harasser, the suspect reportedly folded his hands, apologized repeatedly, and even touched the woman's feet to beg for forgiveness.The bystanders promptly informed local law enforcement about the confrontation. Officers from Premnagar Police Station arrived swiftly, took the accused into custody, and initiated formal legal proceedings based on the complaint and viral footage.What Action Did Police Take Against Alleged Harrasser?The Premnagar Police immediately arrived at the scene after the bystanders informed them of the incident, and then they took the accused into custody as part of the investigation into the alleged harassment in a public place.According to local reports, Premnagar police station in-charge Sher Singh has stated that legal action was initiated based on the formal complaint filed by the victim. The Jhansi Police administration instructed the Premnagar SHO to file a formal First Information Report (FIR) under relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) covering molestation, assault, and public harassment.Senior officials also stated that an investigation is currently underway to identify and question the two accomplices who were accompanying the accused on the two-wheeler when the assault occurred.With the rising cases of assault and eve-teasing in public spaces, incidents like this underline both the vulnerable reality women face on the streets and the powerful impact of refusing to remain silent.As the investigation progresses and authorities hunt for the remaining accomplices, the viral footage remains a striking testament to one woman's refusal to let harassment go unpunished.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              int venture, contract manufacturing at Bhuj and testing support.The off-highway tyre and carbon black maker Balkrishna Industries has stepped into a new chapter in passenger car tyres. A fresh tie-up with a leading global Italian tyre name could reshape its on-highway plans, while its latest quarter showed strong growth, as investors now weigh what comes next for shareholders.The Nifty 50 traded at 22,617, down 0.85%, while the Sensex fell 0.73% to 73,178 on Thursday. Following this the Shares of Balkrishna Industries Ltd are trading at Rs. 2,101.50, up 3.07 percent on Thursday. The stock touched the intraday high of Rs. 2,124.60 after opening at Rs. 2,039.60 before slipping to a low of Rs. 2,010.10. The company commands a market capitalization of Rs. 40,662.34 crore.BKT Signs Three Deals With PirelliBalkrishna Industries Limited, which sells tyres under the BKT brand, told the stock exchanges on 22 October 2026 that it has signed three agreements with Pirelli Tyre S.p.A. of Italy. The first is a Framework Agreement that lays out the plan for a 50:50 joint venture in India to make passenger car radial tyres, with the company to be incorporated by 31 December 2030. The second is an Offtake Agreement, under which BKT will make Pirelli-branded tyres at its Bhuj plant in Gujarat for Pirelli, valid up to 2031. The third is a Service Agreement, giving BKT access to Pirelli's testing grounds and simulation equipment for BKT-branded tyres.What the Deal Means for BKTFor BKT, the deal speeds up its entry into passenger car tyres. The Bhuj PCR plant gets a steady customer, since Pirelli has committed to a minimum yearly purchase at a price based on raw material cost plus conversion charges. Pirelli's testing support may also help BKT's own passenger car and two-wheeler tyres.There are limits, though. BKT cannot make competing tyres for other parties, and neither side can form a similar tyre venture in India with a third party, although BKT remains free to sell its own passenger car tyres. Pirelli is not a related party, and management control is unchanged.Financial PerformanceLooking at the quarterly results of Balkrishna Industries Limited, the company's consolidated revenue from operations increased by 25.19 percent YoY, from Rs. 2,760.02 crore in Q1 FY26 to Rs. 3,455.27 crore in Q1 FY27, and grew by 17.81 percent QoQ from Rs. 2,932.82 crore in Q4 FY26.Balkrishna Industries generated about 90 percent of its Q1 FY27 revenue from the off-highway tyre business and about 10 percent from carbon black, according to the company's investor presentation.In Q1 FY27, Balkrishna Industries' consolidated net profit increased by 56.35 percent YoY, reaching Rs. 450.77 crore compared to Rs. 288.30 crore during the same period last year. As compared to Q4 FY26, the net profit has increased by 50.53 percent, from Rs. 299.46 crore.The basic earnings per share increased by 56.40 percent and stood at Rs. 23.32 as against Rs. 14.91 recorded in the same quarter in the previous year, FY2026.Why the Tyre Market Looks PromisingIndia's rising incomes, growing vehicle ownership and demand for premium tyres support passenger car tyre growth, while global makers look for cost-efficient manufacturing bases. Deals like this fit that trend. Still, raw material swings, currency moves and trade uncertainty could affect margins, so execution and demand will matter for BKT.About Balkrishna IndustriesBalkrishna Industries Limited, founded in 1987, is an Indian maker of off-highway tyres for agriculture, construction, mining and industrial use. It sells in over 160 countries, runs four tyre plants and a carbon black facility, and offers over 3,600 products across applications. In FY26, it reported standalone revenue of Rs. 10,656 crore and profit after tax of Rs. 1,222 crore.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ˆ  gvˆ                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Ü|Ç!5Å!)ÅO ä95147314552026-10-22T09:34:31ZWild bison charges at tourists on bike, two injured at ValparaiOnManoramaonmanorama.comhttps://www.onmanorama.com/news/kerala/2026/10/22/valparai-wild-gaur-attack-tourists-injured.htmlengIndiaø¿êêêêêèPalakkad: Two tourists sustained minor injuries after a wild bison charged at their two-wheeler near Valparai. The incident occurred while a four-member group of tourists were returning on two motorbikes after visiting popular sightseeing spots in the Cinchona area.Quick intervention averts tragedyAccording to locals, the wild gaur rushed towards the riders as they reached an area locally designated as 2/3. As the animal charged, occupants of a car trailing behind the two-wheelers began honking and shouting loudly. The sudden commotion startled the animal, forcing it to retreat, enabling the young men to escape without severe injuries.°XÇ!5ÅE%)Ç æM95147364552026-10-22T09:38:53ZMaharashtra Scooters Q2; Profit Rises 10% to ‚Çπ293 Crore; Renewable Energy Added to CharterTrade Brainstradebrains.inhttps://tradebrains.in/indian-markets/maharashtra-scooters-q2-profit-rises-10-to-293-crore-renewable-energy-added-to-charter-12716989engIndia?ŒûûûûûûA quiet Pune holding company now has a new name, a cleaner charter and a fresh line of business to talk about. Its results depend on one big payday from group companies, and thi   ÊëÇ!5Å9))Ç ùK95147376072026-10-22T09:39:53ZBajaj Pulsar N250SS Launched At Rs 1.59 Lakh - 4V Engine, TFT Console & ETB Ride Modesdrivespark.comdrivespark.comhttps://www.drivespark.com/two-wheelers/2026/bajaj-pulsar-n250ss-launched-at-rs-1-59-lakh-gets-engine-gearbox-tech-upgrades-088397.htmlengIndia?∑The Bajaj Pulsar N250SS has been launched in India at Rs 1,59,406 (ex-showroom, Delhi). The N250SS is the new range-topping variant of the N250 and gets a host of upgrades including a a four-valve engine, six-speed gearbox, 5-inch TFT console and ETB ride modes.The SS is Rs 14,000 more expensive than the standard N250 and follows the same treatment Bajaj gave the Pulsar N160 earlier this year.. However, at Rs 1,59,406 (ex-showroom, Delhi), the Bajaj Pulsar N250SS is priced below the Suzuki Gixxer 250 at Rs 1.85 lakh and the recently launched Hero Xtreme 250R Carbon at Rs 1.98 lakh.Bajaj Pulsar N250SS - Engine, Gearbox and ElectronicsThe Bajaj Pulsar N250SS uses an updated 249cc air- and oil-cooled engine with a four-valve head, producing 25 PS and 22 Nm. The standard N250 makes 24.5 PS and 21.5 Nm.A six-speed gearbox replaces the earlier five-speed unit. A Sports Shifter, which is Bajaj-speak for a quickshifter for clutchless upshifts, is fitted as standard. The engine also features an Electronic Throttle Body (ETB) which brings ETB ride modes, which sit alongside the existing ABS modes.Bajaj Pulsar N250SS - Features, Price and RivalsThe new 5-inch TFT console on the Bajaj Pulsar N250SS replaces the LCD unit found on the standard N250 and adds Google Maps mirroring, the same feature Bajaj introduced on the N160SS. Adjustable levers, a USB Type-C port, Panic Brake Alert and a hazard switch are the other new additions on the Pulsar N250SS.Speaking on the launch, Sarang Kanade, Chief Business Officer, Two-wheeler Business Unit, Bajaj Auto Ltd., said,"With the N250SS, we are bringing a more advanced technology package to the quarter-litre segment. The combination of an upgraded powertrain and ETB ride modes strengthens the motorcycle's proposition, reflecting our focus on making technology a meaningful part of the performance riding experience."    s year that payday came in bigger. The more interesting question is where it might put that cash next.Group holding companies rarely make headlines. They sit on stakes in sister companies, collect dividends once or twice a year and pass a good part of it on to shareholders. Their earnings look lumpy because the income arrives in a single burst, so the real story is usually what they own and what they choose to do with surplus cash.The Nifty 50 was trading at 22,637.40, down 0.76%. Meanwhile, Sensex also fell 0.71% to 73,183.18 on Thursday. Meanwhile, Shares of Maharashtra Scooters Ltd. were trading at Rs. 12,244.00, up 2.04 percent from previous close of Rs. 11,999.00. The stock opened at Rs. 12,041.00 and reached an intraday high of Rs. 12,715.00 and low of Rs. 11,915.00. The company currently has a market capitalization of Rs. 13,953 crores.What's the NewsMaharashtra Scooters is now Bajaj Nivesh Limited, with the new name effective October 16. Three days later, the corporate affairs ministry registered changes to its charter, which shareholders had approved through a September 27 postal ballot. The scooter and automotive manufacturing clauses are gone, investment is now the principal object, and a new clause allows generation, sale and trading of renewable power, subject to approvals.For the September quarter, profit rose 10% to Rs. 293 crore from Rs. 267 crore, as dividend income grew 10% to Rs. 290 crore. Total income came to Rs. 297 crore. For the half year, profit slipped about 2% to Rs. 297 crore, because last year included a Rs. 7.7 crore tax write-back. The company also paid an interim dividend of Rs. 160 a share, about Rs. 183 crore, on October 13.Financial & Business AnalysisLooking at the quarterly results of Maharashtra Scooters Ltd., the company's consolidated revenue from operations increased by 9.72 percent YoY, from Rs. 271.02 crore in Q2 FY26 to Rs. 297.36 crore in Q2 FY27, and increased by 5,396.12 percent QoQ from Rs. 5.41 crore in Q1 FY27.In Q2 FY27 Maharashtra Scooters Ltd., consolidated net profit increased by 9.81 percent YoY, reaching Rs. 293.27 crore compared to Rs. 267.07 crore during the same period last year. As compared to Q1 FY27, the net profit increased by 8,731.63 percent, from Rs. 3.32 crore.The basic earnings per share stood at Rs. 256.61 as against Rs. 233.69 recorded in the same quarter in the previous year, FY2026. In Q1 FY27 Dividend Income is not there, so percentage changes are big when compared to Q2 FY27 and FY26.Bajaj Nivesh is a single-segment investment business, and its revenue mix shows it. About 97% of Q2 operating revenue was dividend income, with interest on surplus funds making up most of the rest. Its holdings are in Bajaj Auto, Bajaj Finance, Bajaj Finserv and Bajaj Holdings & Investment. Dividends mostly land in this quarter, so the June quarter earned almost nothing, and Q2 and the half-year are the numbers to read.There is no order book here, so the investment portfolio is the pipeline. Income depends on how the group's listed companies perform and what they choose to pay out. The new renewable energy clause adds a possible second leg, where surplus cash could eventually go into solar or wind projects. Management has said this can sit alongside investing without changing its unregistered core investment company status, but no project or spend has been announced, so for now it is flexibility rather than a plan.Industry ContextIndia's non-fossil power capacity crossed 300.5 GW on July 31, 2026, over 60% of the 500 GW target for 2030 and about 54% of total installed capacity of roughly 552 GW. Solar leads at 164.59 GW, followed by wind at 58.14 GW. India added a record 55.29 GW in FY26, of which 44.6 GW was solar.Reaching 500 GW needs close to 200 GW more, about four year                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                ô ô                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               öcÇ!5ÅgÇ9 ∞795147252752026-10-22T09:29:29ZAlia Bhatt Reacts To Post Defending Ranbir Kapoor Amid 'Ramayana' Speech Backlash, Reports Of Security ThreatNewsXnewsx.comhttps://www.newsx.com/entertainment/alia-bhatt-reacts-to-post-defending-ranbir-kapoor-amid-ramayana-speech-backlash-reports-of-security-threat-286047/engIndiaø±Alia Bhatt has reportedly liked a social media post defending Ranbir Kapoor amid trolling over his Dussehra speech. The development comes after reports that shooters involved in the Tiger Shroff firing case had conducted reconnaissance at Ranbir's Mumbai residence.Actor Alia Bhatt appears to have shown support for her husband, Ranbir Kapoor, amid online trolling over his recent Dussehra speech and reports that the shooters involved in the firing incident targeting Tiger Shroff had also conducted reconnaissance at Ranbir's residence in Mumbai. The actor reportedly liked a social media post defending Ranbir, although she has not issued a public statement on the matter.The development comes amid reports that the men arrested in connection with the firing incident involving Tiger's car in Juhu had allegedly surveyed Ranbir's residence in Bandra. According to India Today, police sources said the investigation had uncovered this additional detail. However, the reported reconnaissance does not by itself establish that Ranbir was the intended target of an attack.The social media post that Alia reportedly liked defended Ranbir for attending a public event despite the reported security concerns. It also criticised the online backlash against him over a verbal slip during his speech at a Dussehra celebration in Kolkata. Screenshots of the interaction were subsequently circulated by fan accounts.What Did Ranbir Kapoor Say At The Dussehra Event?Ranbir faced criticism after a video of his speech at a Dussehra celebration in Kolkata went viral. While speaking about the triumph of good over evil, the actor said, "Burai chahe kitni bhi taqatwar kyun naa ho, aakhir mein ant sacchai aur achchai ki hi hoga."His use of the word ant (end) instead of jeet (victory) prompted trolling, particularly as he is set to portray Lord Ram in Nitesh Tiwari's upcoming film Ramayana.On October 21, Ranbir addressed the controversy at a musical event for Ramayana in Chennai. Calling it a slip of the tongue, he apologised and clarified that he had intended to say that truth and goodness would ultimately triumph over evil.What Do We Know About The Tiger Shroff Firing Case?The firing incident took place in Mumbai's Juhu area on October 18, when motorcycle-borne assailants allegedly opened fire at Tiger Shroff's car. The actor escaped serious injury, while his driver and a bystander sustained gunshot injuries, according to reports.The Mumbai Crime Branch subsequently said Tiger was not the original target and that the accused had initially planned to target another prominent Bollywood celebrity. Separately, police sources told India Today that the men had conducted reconnaissance at Ranbir's Bandra residence. The identity of the initially intended target has not been independently established by the available reports.The investigation is ongoing, and the reported security threat has added another dimension to the controversy surrounding Ranbir. Alia's reported social media interaction has drawn attention, though she has not publicly commented on the claims.    3  3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ëIÇ %5Å?)Åg ûib-95147207522026-10-22T09:25:19ZTwo Odisha sprinter die in road accident, CM Majhi expresses condolencesBhaskar Live English Newsbhaskarlive.inhttps://bhaskarlive.in/others/two-odisha-sprinter-die-in-road-accident-cm-majhi-expresses-condolences-2155892engIndiaøÀõõõõõõBhubaneswar, Oct 22 (IANS) In a tragic incident, two Indian sprinters Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malaya Barik died in a fatal road accident on the National Highway 16 near Phulnakhara in Kataka district late on Wednesday night.Mrutyam, hailing from Kalahandi district, was among the country's fastest U23 sprinters in 2025. The deceased, Barik, was from the Baragada district. The duo was training at the High Performance Centres (HPCs) at the Kalinga Stadium Sports Complex in Bhubaneswar.According to reports, four people; three athletes and a swimming coach were travelling on two two-wheelers to Kataka city to watch Durga Puja on Thursday night. Sources also added that Astik Pradhan, who recently secured a silver medal in the men's 400-metre event at the U23 National Championships held in Jaipur, was reportedly riding a separate two-wheeler approximately 50 metres in the rear with the other member of the group.The group was reportedly travelling to attend a Sambalpuri Melody orchestra being held in Kataka on the occasion of Durga Puja festival on Thursday night when the deceased athletes lost control over their vehicle and rammed into the barricades along the roadside on the National Highway near Phulankhara on last night. They were immediately rushed to SCB medical college and hospital where the doctors declared them dead.Odisha Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi, Sports minister Suryabanshi Suraj and the sports fraternity across the state and country expressed deep grief over the tragic road mishap."Deeply saddened by the tragic demise of athletes Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malaya Barik in a road accident. Their untimely passing is a profound loss to Odisha's sporting fraternity. My heartfelt condolences to their bereaved families. May Mahaprabhu Shri Jagannath grant them strength in this difficult time and eternal peace to the departed souls," wrote CM Majhi on his X handle.Created On : &nbsp 22 Oct 2026 2:54 PM IST   A A                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       õ;Ç!5Å5/5Ç ≤95147202122026-10-22T09:24:47ZTiger Shroff resumes shooting of Lag Jaa Gale two days after firing incident: ReportBollywood Hungamabollywoodhungama.comhttps://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/tiger-shroff-resumes-shooting-of-lag-jaa-gale-two-days-after-firing-incident-report/engIndiaø‘TTTTTTTiger Shroff reportedly returned to work on October 20, two days after a firing incident outside a ground in Mumbai left the actor with minor injuries and his driver injured by a bullet. The incident took place on Sunday, October 18. While the investigation is ongoing, the three accused, including two gunmen and a motorcycle rider, have been arrested.Tiger Shroff resumes shooting of Lag Jaa Gale two days after firing incident: ReportAccording to a report by Times Now, Tiger resumed shooting for Dharma Productions' Lag Jaa Gale on Tuesday. The film also stars Janhvi Kapoor and Lakshya in key roles and is directed by Raj Mehta, who has previously helmed films such as Good Newwz, JugJugg Jeeyo and Selfiee.The reported return to the film's set came shortly after the firing incident. While further details about the investigation remain awaited, the arrests of the three accused marked a development in the case.A few months ago, pictures from the sets of Lag Jaa Gale surfaced on social media, drawing attention to the project. The film, which brings together Tiger Shroff, Janhvi Kapoor and Lakshya, has been described as a romantic action thriller.Lag Jaa Gale Release DateLag Jaa Gale was reportedly expected to arrive in theatres in 2026. However, delays in the shooting schedule led to a change in its release plans. The film has now been postponed to 2027 and is scheduled to release in cinemas on May 14, 2027.The project marks another collaboration between Tiger and Dharma Productions, with Raj Mehta directing the film.Tiger Shroff's Upcoming ProjectsApart from Lag Jaa Gale, Tiger has Remo D'Souza's next directorial venture in his lineup. The film is being produced by Vicky Jain, husband of actor Ankita Lokhande, and also features Nushrratt Bharuccha, Elvish Yadav, Abhishek Banerjee and Pashmina Roshan.Tiger has also reportedly been linked to an upcoming action film with Vidyut Jammwal. However, the project has not yet been officially announced.Following the firing incident involving Tiger, Vidyut shared a video addressing the broader issue of people witnessing harassment or assault without intervening. He captioned the video, "We know there's a lot happening in our country. Sometimes we can raise our voice, sometimes we can't, but WE do in our own way, But when we see someone being harassed or assaulted on the street (woman ), why do we stand by and watch? Why can't one of us step forward, not just as witnesses, but as human beings? We need fewer spectators and more heroes."Vidyut's message received praise from netizens, with several appreciating his decision to speak about the issue. Meanwhile, Tiger's reported return to the sets of Lag Jaa Gale has brought the film back into focus.More Pages: Lag Jaa Gale Box Office CollectionTags : Bollywood, Bollywood News, Firing Incident, Lag Jaa Gale, News, Resumes, Shooting, Tiger ShroffBOLLYWOOD NEWS - LIVE UPDATESCatch us for latest Bollywood News, New Bollywood Movies update, Box office collection, New Movies Release , Bollywood News Hindi, Entertainment News, Bollywood Live News Today & Upcoming Movies 2026 and stay updated with latest hindi movies only on Bollywood Hungama.   3 3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         õIÇ	!5Åy-É ± 95147192742026-10-22T09:23:54ZTiger Shroff Firing Case: Exclusive CCTV Shows Accused Leaving Andheri Hotel With Gun Inside Bag Minutes Before AttackTimesNowtimesnownews.comhttps://www.timesnownews.com/entertainment-news/bollywood/tiger-shroff-firing-case-exclusive-cctv-shows-accused-leaving-andheri-hotel-with-gun-inside-bag-minutes-before-attack-article-156384065engIndiaø“““““““Tiger Shroff shooting case: New CCTV footage shows three accused leaving an Andheri hotel for Juhu before undertaking the firing incidentExclusive CCTV footage obtained by Times Now reportedly shows three accused leaving a hotel in Mumbai's Andheri shortly before the October 18 firing incident involving actor Tiger Shroff. The footage captures one alleged accused carrying a blue bag believed to contain a pistol, while the other two are seen leaving on a yellow Pulsar motorcycle a minute later. According to the report, the three then headed towards a football ground in Juhu, where the shooting took place. The footage could offer investigators a crucial timeline as they piece together the events preceding the incident.Details of CCTV footageAccording to Times Now, the CCTV footage was recorded outside a hotel in Andheri on October 18, a little before the firing incident targeting Tiger Shroff, which left his driver and another man injured.The footage reportedly shows one of the accused leaving the hotel at 4:12 pm, carrying a blue bag believed to contain a pistol. The other two alleged accused are seen leaving at 4:13 pm on a yellow Pulsar motorcycle. The one-minute gap between the departures offers a timeline of the group's movements before the incident. However, the precise contents of the bag and the identities of the individuals seen in the footage would need to be established through the investigation.Andheri hotel to Juhu football groundAs per the report, the three individuals travelled from the Andheri hotel directly to the football ground in Juhu, where shots were fired on October 18. The incident reportedly took place as Tiger Shroff was leaving the football ground. The actor was unharmed, while his driver sustained a gunshot injury. The shooting triggered a police investigation into the alleged attackers, their movements and the vehicle used in the incident.The newly reported footage may help investigators reconstruct the sequence of events, including the accused's departure from the hotel and their reported journey to Juhu.Relevance of CCTV footageCCTV recordings can help investigators establish movements and timings, identify possible routes and compare visual evidence with witness accounts and other material collected during an investigation.In this case, the footage reportedly shows the blue bag and yellow Pulsar motorcycle as evidence and details that may be relevant as authorities examine the evidence.Mumbai Crime Branch took the three main accused from Kota in Rajasthan to Mumbai on Wednesday (October 21), reports said. A magistrate's court remanded them to police custody till October 31. The accused have been identified as Rehan alias Sukka from Sonipat in Haryana, Ritik Kurmi alias Roshan, a resident of Begusarai in Bihar and currently residing in Mumbai, and Phool Singh from Haryana.Police wanted 14 days' custody to recover the firearms used in the crime and to investigate the motive. Investigators also told the court that two mobile phones had been destroyed and call detail records and other electronic evidence needed to be collected.   – –                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ö,Ç!5Ç%Çu Æ[95147191592026-10-22T09:23:50ZOla Electric rights issue opens today: Who are the investors applying for 2.39 crore entitlements? Check details | Stock Market Newsmintlivemint.comhttps://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/ola-electric-rights-issue-opens-today-who-are-the-investors-applying-for-2-39-crore-entitlements-check-details-11792657152589.htmlengIndia?¬íííííêOla Electric Mobility rights issue: Ola Electric Mobility's rights issue came into focus on Thursday, October 22, after the company confirmed that two specific investors had submitted applications for a total of 2.39 crore rights entitlements on the opening day of the issue.In a regulatory filing dated October 22, 2026, the electric two-wheeler manufacturer said both investors had applied for all the rights entitlements transferred to them by the promoter-linked entities. The disclosure was made under Regulation 77B(2) of the Securities and Exchange Board of India's Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements Regulations, 2018, as amended.Motilal Oswal, Calliope Capital apply for 2.39 crore rights entitlementsAccording to the filing, ANI Technologies Private Limited, a member of Ola Electric's promoter group and the parent of Ola Cabs, renounced 1,28,33,054 rights entitlements in favour of Motilal Oswal Financial Services. The financial services company applied for the entire number of entitlements it received.Separately, Indus Trust, acting through its trustee Ankush Agarwal, renounced 1,10,22,422 rights entitlements in favour of Calliope Capital Advisors. Calliope Capital also applied for all the entitlements transferred to it.Together, the two investors applied for 2,38,55,476 rights entitlements, equivalent to approximately 2.39 crore. The filing confirmed the applications but did not specify the investors' reasons for applying.Ola Electric rights issue: Price, ratio and key datesThe Bhavish Aggarwal-led company had approved the issuance of partly paid-up equity shares through a rights issue of up to ‚Çπ1,000 crore on October 11, 2026.The issue opened on Thursday, October 22, and is scheduled to close on Friday, October 30. Ola Electric has fixed the rights issue price at ‚Çπ27 per share, comprising a face value of ‚Çπ10 and a premium of ‚Çπ17.The company's board approved the issuance of 37,02,72,665 rights equity shares, aggregating to ‚Çπ9,99,73,61,955, or approximately ‚Çπ1,000 crore.Ola Electric had fixed Tuesday, October 13, as the record date to determine shareholder eligibility. The rights issue ratio is two rights equity shares for every 25 fully paid-up equity shares held on the record date. This means eligible shareholders can subscribe to two additional shares for every 25 shares they held on October 13.Before the issue, the company had 4,62,84,08,313 outstanding equity shares. If the issue is fully subscribed, the number will rise to 4,99,86,80,978 shares.Ola Electric stock performance: Shares fall 5% in today's tradeOla Electric shares fell 5% to an intraday low of ‚Çπ31.31 in Thursday's trade. The stock has witnessed significant declines across several time frames, including a 10% fall in one week, 16% in one month, 14% in three months, 18% in six months and 41% over one year.The stock had touched a 52-week high of ‚Çπ53.47 in October 2025 and a 52-week low of ‚Çπ20.83 in March 2026.    ö 	 ö                                                                                                                                              êxÇ!5ÅC!Ç! ù95147126632026-10-22T09:18:42ZTiger Shroff Firing Case: Accused Practised Shooting Near Mumbai | Tiger Shroff Attack NewsNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/videos/india/tiger-shroff-firing-case-accused-practised-shooting-near-mumbai-tiger-shroff-attack-news-10392864.htmlengIndiaø¡ëëëëëëThe investigation into the firing incident involving actor Tiger Shroff has widened, with police continuing to trace the weapons used in the attack and reconstruct the accused's movements after the shooting.According to investigators, the alleged shooters fled Mumbai after firing at Shroff's car in Juhu. They reportedly abandoned a motorcycle, travelled towards Surat in Gujarat and boarded a train on which they were later apprehended in Kota, Rajasthan.Police have said the firearms used in the incident had not been recovered as of October 21. Investigators are examining the accused's escape route and questioning suspects to establish the source of the weapons, the wider conspiracy and the motive behind the attack.The case has also led to arrests of alleged weapon suppliers, while police investigate whether other people helped arrange or transport the firearms. Any claim that the weapons were deliberately dumped along the route remains subject to confirmation from investigators.Watch for the latest developments in the Tiger Shroff firing case, the search for the missing weapons and the ongoing police investigation. -news CNN-News18 is your trusted source for breaking news, updates, and in-depth analysis from around the world. CNN-News18 is dedicated to bringing you the latest news, trends, and insights, helping you stay informed and up-to-date. Subscribe Now and join our community of informed and engaged viewers. Follow Every Breaking Story LIVE üî¥Watch News18 LIVE 24x7: https://youtube.com/live/rfDx1HMvXbQFollow us on Google: news18.co/cn18gFollow CNN News18 on X: https://x.com/CNNnews18Follow CNN News18 on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/cnnnews18/Follow CNN News18 on Facebook: facebook.com/cnnnews18 with latest headlines on politics, sports and entertainment on news18.comNews18 Mobile App - https://onelink.to/desc-youtubeçfÇ%5Å9/Åk ó#b-95147128922026-10-22T09:18:51ZGuwahati: Nine Killed, 105 Injured in Road Accidents During Durga PujaThe Sentinel Newspapersentinelassam.comhttps://www.sentinelassam.com/breakingnews/guwahati-nine-killed-105-injured-in-road-accidents-during-durga-pujaengIndiaø””””””’Guwahati: Nine people were killed and 105 others injured in road accidents in Guwahati during the Durga Puja celebration from 16th October to 21st October , as per figures from Gauhati Medical College and Hospital (GMCH).The hospital treated 114 road accident victims during the six-day period, with nine succumbing to their injuries. The figures highlight road safety concerns during the festive season, when traffic movement increases as people visit puja pandals and attend celebrations.Of the 114 victims, 67 were men and 15 were women, while the available data did not specify the gender of the remaining patients. Around 20 per cent of the injured were reportedly in critical condition and continued to require medical attention.Two-wheeler accidents accounted for a significant proportion of the cases. However, the overall number of road accidents in Guwahati reportedly declined by 15 per cent compared with the corresponding period last year.Meanwhile, Assam Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma expressed concern over fatal road accidents across the state during and after Durga Puja, citing accident-prone stretches, road renovation work and unsafe driving practices."The accidents are surging and we are concerned about it," Sarma said, adding that driving under the influence of alcohol and not wearing helmets were among the factors contributing to crashes. He stressed the need for greater public awareness and corrective measures at accident-prone locations.    nues.A CCTV video has emerged in the firing case involving Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff, showing one of the accused leaving a hotel where he was allegedly staying to carry out the attack.The footage, said to be from October 18, shows the accused leaving the hotel at nearly 4.12 pm with a bag believed to be containing pistols. Two other accused are subsequently seen leaving on a motorcycle at 4.13 pm.The footage emerged as investigators probe the alleged movement and transportation of firearms used in the attack on Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area.The Mumbai Police has alleged that the firing was carried out at the behest of Anil Pandit, a member of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang.According to news agency PTI, two suspects had travelled to Amritsar to procure the weapons, while two women allegedly transported the firearms by train to Mumbai and handed them over to the attackers.The investigation is being conducted by the Anti-Extortion Cell of the Mumbai Crime Branch.Four Accused Arrested In DelhiThe Delhi Police arrested four people in connection with the firing incident, including two women identified as Radha, 23, from Uttar Pradesh's Sitapur district, and Babita, 23, from Azamgarh district.The two men arrested alongside them were identified as Kunal, 21, and Sumit, 19.According to PTI, the women were arrested at New Delhi Railway Station on Tuesday. Radha was apprehended along with Babita and the two men. Another accused, who allegedly stayed in Mumbai to provide logistical support to the shooters, was also arrested, the report said.An ANI report said the four accused arrested by the Delhi Police were brought to Mumbai's Anti-Extortion Cell on Thursday. The two women were kept at Azad Maidan police station.The Mumbai Police subsequently arrested seven more individuals from Haryana in connection with the firing incident, ANI reported. A total of 10 individuals were under police suspicion regarding the attack, according to the report.Investigators said leads gathered during the probe helped them identify and arrest additional suspects.Three Alleged Shooters Remanded In Police CustodyEarlier, the Mumbai Police produced three accused in connection with the firing before the Esplanade Court in Mumbai on Wednesday. The accused were brought from Kota in Rajasthan at around 3 am and presented before the court after undergoing medical examinations.The court remanded all three accused to police custody until October 31.The firing took place around 7 pm on Sunday in Mumbai's Juhu area, when two assailants allegedly opened fire at Shroff's car as he was leaving a football club.While the actor escaped relatively unhurt, his driver sustained injuries. A bystander was also injured.Families Of Two Women Claim They Are InnocentThe families of Radha and Babita have denied the allegations against them, claiming that the women have been falsely implicated in the case.Radha's mother, Maina Devi, told PTI that her daughter had moved to Haryana about a year ago in search of employment and was working at a factory for a monthly salary of Rs 15,000.Radha married a local man, Sunil, in 2015 and has a son. She left her matrimonial home around 2018, and Sunil has since remarried. He told PTI that he had not been in contact with Radha for several years.Babita's father, Ram Jatan Ram, said his daughter worked in a packaging unit in Sonipat, Haryana. He alleged that a girl known to the family had taken Babita to Mumbai on the pretext of sightseeing.Babita's sister, Neelam, said Babita had travelled to Mumbai with her friend Radha to visit religious places and fulfil a vow.According to the family, the two women were detained at a railway station while returning, and they were told that suspicious items had been found in Babita's bag.Babita also                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ¨ ù¨                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              †aÇ!5Å+%Q æM95146981632026-10-22T09:07:32ZTwo Wheeler Sales Sep 2026, Q3 - Hero, Honda, TVS, Bajaj, Royal Enfield, SuzukiRushLanerushlane.comhttps://www.rushlane.com/?p=559214engIndia?·qqqqqrHero led domestic sales in September, while Bajaj topped exports. TVS moved ahead of Honda in combined domestic and export volumes during July-September 2026, finishing close behind Hero.India's two-wheeler industry recorded combined domestic and export sales of 30,07,900 units in September 20   ÔÜnÇ%5Å)-Ç! â	b-95147076142026-10-22T09:14:42ZTwo-Wheeler Stocks Rebound, PSU Banks Gain Momentum | Analyst's Top PicksBusiness Todaybusinesstoday.inhttps://www.businesstoday.in/bt-tv/whats-hot/video/two-wheeler-stocks-rebound-psu-banks-gain-momentum-analysts-top-picks-563046-2026-10-22engIndia?ﬁ^^^^^`Two-wheeler stocks and PSU banks are emerging as potential opportunities amid recent market movements. After a correction, stocks such as Hero MotoCorp, Bajaj Auto and TVS Motor are showing signs of renewed strength. Aditya Agarwal, Head of Investment at Coheron Wealth, identifies Hero MotoCorp as his top pick from the two-wheeler segment with a potential target of ‚Çπ5,600 - ‚Çπ5,700. In the PSU banking space, Union Bank has broken out after consolidation and could move towards ‚Çπ195-‚Çπ200, while State Bank of India remains another large-cap banking stock to watch.°cÇ!5Åe!Ç! æM95147108422026-10-22T09:17:08ZTiger Shroff Firing Case: CCTV Shows Accused Leaving Hotel With Bag Allegedly Carrying Pistols Before AttackNews18news18.comhttps://www.news18.com/india/tiger-shroff-firing-case-cctv-shows-leaving-hotel-allegedly-carrying-weapons-before-attack-ws-l-10392681.htmlengIndiaø„333333CCTV footage in the Tiger Shroff firing case shows an accused carrying a blue bag before the attack. Police have arrested multiple suspects as the investigation conti   Ì    26, growing 15.70% over 25,99,662 units a year earlier. Domestic volumes increased 13.50% to 24,63,103 units, while exports grew faster at 26.83%, reaching 5,44,797 units. Top six manufacturers - Hero, Honda, TVS, Bajaj, Royal Enfield and Suzuki; together registered 28,37,799 units, up 15.45% year-on-year. Their combined volumes also improved 16.27% over August, supported primarily by higher domestic sales.Two Wheeler Sales Sep 2026Hero retained first position with domestic sales of 7,39,108 units, growing 14.13% over September 2025. Sales rose 36.29% compared to August, giving Hero the largest sequential volume increase among the six manufacturers. Honda followed with 6,36,768 units, up 25.92% year-on-year and 23.09% month-on-month. It delivered the strongest annual percentage growth in this group and added 1,31,075 units over September last year.TVS ranked third with 4,82,073 units, registering growth of 16.65% year-on-year and 11.13% month-on-month. Bajaj recorded 2,39,771 units, down 12.23% annually, although volumes recovered 18.76% over August. It was the only manufacturer among these six to report a domestic year-on-year decline.Royal Enfield recorded 1,21,326 units, growing 6.83% year-on-year and 6.24% month-on-month. Suzuki followed with 1,08,806 units, up 2.76% annually but down 4.50% sequentially. Together, the six manufacturers recorded domestic sales of 23,27,852 units, up 13.05% year-on-year and 21.02% month-on-month.Exports September 2026 - Bajaj And TVS DominateBajaj led exports with 2,11,723 units, growing 34.29% over September 2025. However, shipments declined 12.46% compared to August. TVS followed with 1,63,882 units, recording strong growth of 48.12% year-on-year and 3.96% month-on-month. Honda exported 69,498 units, up 11.25% annually and 12.40% sequentially. Hero recorded 27,330 units, declining 31.05% year-on-year, although exports improved 4.74% over August. Suzuki's exports rose 40.86% to 24,882 units, while Royal Enfield registered 12,632 units, up 17.45%.Top six-brand export total reached 5,09,947 units, growing 27.86% annually but falling 1.40% month-on-month. Bajaj and TVS together accounted for nearly three-fourths of exports within this group, underlining their importance to its overseas performance.Combined September Sales - All Six Brands GrowIncluding domestic sales and exports, Hero led with 7,66,438 units, up 11.53%. Honda ranked second with 7,06,266 units and growth of 24.31%, followed by TVS at 6,45,955 units, up 23.29%.Bajaj's export gains more than offset its domestic decline, lifting combined sales by 4.79% to 4,51,494 units. Royal Enfield recorded 1,33,958 units, up 7.75%, narrowly finishing ahead of Suzuki's 1,33,688 units, which represented 8.21% growth.Q3 2026 - TVS Closes In On HeroDuring July-September 2026, total industry volumes reached 80,75,631 units, growing 17.44% year-on-year. Domestic sales increased 15.05% to 64,21,284 units, while exports rose 27.70% to 16,54,347 units. The six manufacturers together contributed 76,07,876 units, up 16.68%. Hero retained the combined sales lead with 18,68,252 units, growing 10.50%. TVS ranked second with 18,40,530 units, registering the strongest growth among the six at 26.63%.Honda followed closely with 18,28,362 units, up 12.97%. Just 39,890 units separated the top three manufacturers, with TVS trailing Hero by 27,722 units and leading Honda by 12,168 units. Bajaj recorded 12,83,961 units, growing 20.11%. Suzuki ranked fifth with 4,08,102 units, up 12.56%, followed by Royal Enfield at 3,78,669 units, up 16.02%.Domestic Strength And Exports Shape Quarterly RankingsHero led Q3 domestic sales with 17,82,816 units, foll                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       ? ?                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     ï=Ç15ÅÅG ß32026-10-13189123882026-10-22T09:01:20ZDucati Hypermotard V2, V2 SP Launched In India; Check PricesNDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/auto/ducati-hypermotard-v2-v2-sp-launched-in-india-check-prices-12219267engIndia?Æ Ducati Hypermotard V2 and the V2 SP come with the 890cc V2 engine of the brand which produces 120 hp of power.Ducati has launched the fourth-generation Hypermotard in India in two flavours, the standard V2 at Rs 16.53 lakh and the track-focused V2 SP at Rs 20.78 lakh (both ex-showroom). Bookings are open across Ducati dealerships nationwide. The motorcycle joins the wide variety of models based on the V2 platform, including the Monster, Panigale, and others.Engine And ChassisBoth variants share a new 890cc Ducati V2 engine producing 120 hp at 10,750 rpm and 94 Nm at 8,250 rpm. At 54.4kg, Ducati claims it's the lightest twin-cylinder engine it has ever built, and the IVT variable intake valve timing system ensures 70 per cent of peak torque is available from 3,000 rpm.The new aluminium monocoque frame uses the engine as a structural element, paired with a double-sided aluminium swingarm. The standard V2 is 13 kg lighter than its predecessor, while the SP sheds 14 kg.Suspension And BrakesThe standard Hypermotard V2 runs on fully adjustable 46mm Kayaba USD forks and a Kayaba rear monoshock with preload and rebound adjustment, riding on cast alloy wheels and Pirelli Diablo Rosso IV tyres. Braking comes via Brembo M4.32 callipers.The V2 SP steps up with fully adjustable Ohlins NIX30 48mm USD forks and an Ohlins STX46 rear monoshock, forged aluminium wheels, Brembo M50 callipers and Pirelli Diablo Rosso IV Corsa tyres. It also gets a carbon-fibre front fender and a lithium battery, while the standard model uses a lead-acid unit.Electronics And Riding PositionBoth bikes carry a six-axis IMU-based electronics package with cornering ABS, Ducati Traction Control, Wheelie Control, Engine Brake Control and Ducati Quick Shift 2.0, all displayed on a 5-inch full-TFT screen.The SP adds Ducati Power Launch and a pit limiter as standard, features available as accessories on the regular V2. The electronics interface offers Road, Road Pro and Track modes, while the SP also lists Race, Sport, Road and Wet riding modes.Weight And ErgonomicsThe standard V2 weighs 180kg without fuel, while the SP comes in at 177kg. Both share an 880mm seat height and a supermotard-style riding position with wide handlebars and repositioned footpegs.Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the worldDucati Hypermotard V2, Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP, Ducati   x ix                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            °0Ç!5Å)-Åq æM95146788812026-10-22T08:53:45ZKanpur man's death: Family alleges murder, blocks highway with bodyThe Hans Indiathehansindia.comhttps://www.thehansindia.com/uttarpradesh/kanpur-mans-death-family-alleges-murder-blocks-highway-with-body-1134577engIndiaø——————“Kanpur: The death of 37-year-old Biru Singh Bhadauria in the Hanumant Vihar police station area of Uttar Pradesh's Kanpur has triggered a major controversy, as his family rejected the police account that he died in a    ÚôÇ%5ÅO3;Ç7 ¨ub-95146845072026-10-22T08:57:53Z2 days after surprise return from Australia, woman and childhood friend die in Kerala road mishapEnglish.Mathrubhumienglish.mathrubhumi.comhttps://english.mathrubhumi.com/news/kerala/2-days-after-surprise-return-from-australia-woman-and-childhood-friend-die-in-kerala-road-mishap-m2q3vvzeengIndiaøø On Wednesday morning at around half-past eight, a quiet stretch of the Kottayam-Kumily highway near Pampady in Kerala became the site of a heartbreaking tragedy. Two young childhood friends lost their lives in a sudden road accident at the 13th Mile junction near Edakkarapadi. Ashley Ann Thomas, aged 24, was riding her scooter towards Kanam, with her close friend Kripa Merin Kurian, also 24, riding pillion. The two young women were travelling from Pampady to visit a mutual friend when the fatal crash took place. Within moments, a normal morning journey ended in devastating grief for their families and neighbouring villages. Both women died on the spot.A surprise homecoming ends in heart-breakFor Kripa Merin Kurian, the trip back home to Kerala was supposed to be a joyful secret. She had completed her postgraduate studies in Australia. When her brother Kiran Jacob Kurian booked his flight home for a vacation, Kripa decided to join him as a surprise for her family. They arrived home in Kottayam just two days ago. Kripa had been looking forward to celebrating her 25th birthday on the 22nd of November. Instead, her unexpected return home ended in tragedy after just forty-eight hours. Upon arriving, she immediately reunited with her lifelong friend, Ashley. The two schoolmates had spent the past two days travelling together, catching up on lost time after years of studying in different places.How the collision occurred at PampadyThe fatal crash occurred on National Highway 183 near Kothala 13th Mile as the women rode towards Kanam. Police reported that a car travelling ahead of the scooter suddenly braked and swerved to avoid hitting a parked motorcycle and a pedestrian talking by the roadside. As the car slowed down abruptly, Ashley's scooter brushed past the vehicle and skidded out of control. The two-wheeler and its riders fell directly into the path of an oncoming private bus heading towards Kottayam on the Kattappana-Thankamany route. The impact was immediate, leaving no time for rescue. Local police from Pampady quickly arrived at the scene to manage the situation and complete legal formalities. Following an autopsy at the Government Medical College Hospital in Kottayam, the bodies were moved to a hospital mortuary at Manarcad.A sorrowful farewell for two bright futuresThe loss of Ashley and Kripa has left the communities of Pampady and Meenadom in deep mourning. Both young women were accomplished students with bright careers ahead. Ashley had recently completed her ACCA chartered accountancy qualifications after studying in Bengaluru, with her results announced earlier this week. She leaves behind her mother Mary Thomas and her brother Alvin V Thomas. Kripa, the daughter of Fr Kuriakose Kadavumbhagom and Anita Kurian, had completed her higher studies in Australia, with her convocation planned for March.    road accident and alleged instead that he was murdered.On Thursday, the family staged a protest by placing his body on the highway leading towards Hamirpur, demanding the immediate arrest of those allegedly responsible for his death.The case has taken a fresh turn after an eyewitness, identified as Rahul, questioned the police version of events and claimed that Biru's death was not accidental but the result of a deliberate act.According to the victim's family, Biru Singh Bhadauria worked as a salesman for a food products company. They alleged that he had a dispute a few days earlier with Rajveer and Mewalal, both residents of Khadepur Nai Basti, following which tensions had reportedly continued between the two sides.The family claimed that on Tuesday night, Biru was returning home after visiting a Dussehra fair when Mewalal arrived at the spot in a car.According to their account, three other men, including Rajveer, were also travelling in the vehicle. The group allegedly stopped Biru and assaulted him. When he attempted to escape, they hit him with the car. The family further alleged that the men then placed him on the roof of the vehicle and drove away.Speaking to IANS, the victim's wife rejected the suggestion that her husband had died in an accident, and said, "I am saying that it was not an accident. It was murder, committed by five people. They are saying it was an accident, but it was not an accident; it was murder committed by five people."Eyewitness Rahul has also challenged the police's account, alleging that the circumstances surrounding the incident point towards a deliberate act rather than a routine road accident. He claimed to have personally seen the men place Biru on the roof of the car before driving away."The police are misrepresenting the sequence of events. This was not a routine road accident, but a case of murder. I have personally witnessed individuals placing the man on the roof of the car and driving away," Rahul said.He further alleged that Biru's hands had become trapped in the openings of the car's front windows as the vehicle moved forward."Both of the man's hands were trapped inside the car's front window openings. The vehicle was driven forward, and the man was subsequently thrown off before the accused fled the scene," Rahul added.However, the allegations made by the family and the eyewitness remain to be established, and their veracity can only be determined through a thorough investigation by the police.Meanwhile, a video circulating on social media purportedly shows a car travelling at high speed. It is alleged that Rahul was pursuing the vehicle on a motorcycle at the time of the incident.CCTV footage related to the case has also emerged, with the family claiming that the entire sequence of events was captured by more than 12 surveillance cameras installed in the area.The family has alleged that despite the availability of potential evidence, the police initially registered the case as a death caused by an "unknown vehicle", treating it as a hit-and-run incident.They have expressed dissatisfaction with the initial handling of the matter and are demanding that the case be investigated from the perspective of murder, with strict legal action taken against all those found responsible.Following the incident, Biru was taken to a hospital, where doctors declared him dead at around 3 p.m. on Wednesday. His death subsequently led to demands from the family for a thorough investigation and action against the people they accuse of being involved.The family alleged that the police were not taking effective action, prompting them to block the highway with Biru's body in protest. During the demonstration, they remained firm on their demand for the immediate                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         6 6                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            óFÇ!5Å'Ç ™a95146753672026-10-22T08:50:57ZNikhil Kamath On What Indian Entrepreneurs Can Learn From 'Tech Bros' In WestNDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/india-news/ndtv-world-summit-nikhil-kamath-on-what-indian-entrepreneurs-can-learn-from-tech-bros-in-west-12219191engIndiaø¡ëëëëëëNikhil Kamath referenced China's Amnesty programme, where if an entrepreneur fails, he pays a fine and then the programme allows him to try again.Nikhil Kamath at NDTV World Summit 2026 in New DelhiThe billionaire tech bros in the west have a lot more risk capital at hand, to experiment and try different things, Nikhil Kamath, investor and entrepreneur, told NDTV, suggesting that Indian entrepreneurs take the cue and that failure should not be looked down upon."We do think Indian entrepreneurs should really be thinking about, or trying to, scale at that level. Culturally in a lot of places that are being very innovative, somehow when these guys fail society does not look down upon them. Maybe that's something we need to inculcate here," the 40-year-old Kamath, attending the NDTV World Summit in Delhi, said."If somebody were to raise a bunch of capital, attempt something huge, and not succeed along the way for whatever reason, it's not as easy here as it is for them in different pockets of the world where maybe more innovation is happening today. That's another thing I think we need to learn," he said.Elaborating on the same, the entrepreneur referenced China's Amnesty programme, where if an entrepreneur fails, he pays a fine and then the programme allows him to try again."In the '90s, when they (China) really took off, they had this Amnesty programme. When an entrepreneur tried something and failed, he kind of had to pay a fine and they got him back to start working right away and try again. They really pushed him to do it. I think culturally and more so from a policy standpoint, we need to inculcate that somewhere," the entrepreneur, who has lately been reading a lot of books on China, said.He underscored that he does not align with everything that China is saying, "but some things we can definitely pick up"."I was in China for a month earlier this year. They have a lot more capital, risk capital at hand, to experiment and try different things. I don't see how an Indian company, or for that matter any company outside of those two or three countries where there is that much risk capital, can have a fair shot at competing in that layer. It would be really hard. I think the odds are low," he said.Kamath, a school dropout, is best known as the co-founder of Zerodha, one of India's largest stockbroking firms. He has also invested in several businesses, including Licious, Nourish You, Pee Safe, Subko, and Ather, an electric scooter maker.Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the worldNikhil Kamath, NDTV World Summit 2026, Tech Bros                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       °/Ç%5Å?)ÅY æMb-95146734022026-10-22T08:48:54ZKanpur man's death: Family alleges murder, blocks highway with bodyBhaskar Live English Newsbhaskarlive.inhttps://bhaskarlive.in/others/kanpur-mans-death-family-alleges-murder-blocks-highway-with-body-2155875engIndiaø——————“Kanpur, Oct 22 (IANS) The death of 37-year-old Biru Singh Bhadauria in the Hanumant Vihar police station area of Uttar Pradesh's Kanpur has triggered a major controversy, as his family rejected the police account that    ıólÇ%5s''Å ¨=b-95146751122026-10-22T08:50:43Z2026 Ducati Hypermotard V2, V2 SP Launched in IndiaBikeAdvice.inbikeadvice.inhttps://bikeadvice.in/2026-ducati-hypermotard-v2-v2-sp-launched-in-india/engIndia?«óóóóóòThe 2026 Ducati Hypermotard V2 has been presented in Ducati Red colourway while the 2026 Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP has been rolled out in a dedicated SP liveryDucati India has launched the 2026 Hypermotard V2 and 2026 Hypermotard V2 SP at price points of Rs 16.53 lakh and Rs 20.78 lakh, respectively, in the country. Both the prices mentioned before are ex-showroom, India. The bookings for both the superbikes have commenced from today across all the company authorized dealerships in the Indian market. The 2026 Ducati Hypermotard V2 has been presented in Ducati Red colourway while the 2026 Ducati Hypermotard V2 SP has been rolled out in a dedicated SP livery.The Hypermotard V2 originally debuted at the EICMA 2005 and now over two decades later, it is presently in the fourth-generation. Some of the notable styling elements of the superbike are double-wing fuel tank, streamlined front end, commanding riding position, forward-set footpegs, wide handlebars and dual under-seat exhausts. The V2 SP, in particular, boasts of fully adjustable √ñhlins suspension, Brembo M50 calipers and forged aluminium wheels.Sitting on a monocoque frame, it comes with a new double-sided aluminium swingarm which has resulted in a weight reduction by 13 kg for the standard V2 and 14 kg for the SP version as compared to the preceding model. Additionally, the seat height has been optimized to 880 mm, making the motorcycle more accessible to a wider range of riders.Commenting on the launch, Mr. Bipul Chandra, Managing Director, Ducati India, said, "We are immensely proud to introduce the Hypermotard V2 and V2 SP to the Indian market. This motorcycle is a true testament to Ducati's commitment to pure riding emotion, bringing supermotard agility and thrilling performance directly to the streets. The new V2 engine, the incredibly light monocoque chassis and the advanced electronics are engineered for one purpose to offer an unparalleled, adrenaline-fueled experience."Both the 2026 Hypermotard V2 and 2026 Hypermotard V2 SP are powered by a new 890 cc Ducati V2 engine which is claimed to be the lightest twin-cylinder ever produced by Ducati, weighing just 54.4 kg. It generates max power of 118.3 bhp at 10,750 rpm and peak torque of 94 Nm at 8,250 rpm. The brand states that 70 percent of the maximum torque is available at just 3,000 rpm.Needless to mention, both the Ducati superbikes come loaded with a plethora of bells and whistles in the form of Cornering ABS with a "Slide by Brake" function, Ducati Traction Control (DTC), Ducati Wheelie Control (DWC), Engine Brake Control (EBC), Ducati Quick Shift (DQS) 2.0 and the new 5-inch full-TFT instrument cluster featuring three specific Info Modes: Road, Road Pro, and Track. The 2026 Hypermotard V2 SP further gets Ducati Power Launch and a Pit Limiter as standard fitment.    he died in a road accident and alleged instead that he was murdered.On Thursday, the family staged a protest by placing his body on the highway leading towards Hamirpur, demanding the immediate arrest of those allegedly responsible for his death.The case has taken a fresh turn after an eyewitness, identified as Rahul, questioned the police version of events and claimed that Biru's death was not accidental but the result of a deliberate act.According to the victim's family, Biru Singh Bhadauria worked as a salesman for a food products company. They alleged that h