ly shows a car travelling at high speed. It is alleged that Rahul was pursuing the vehicle on a motorcycle at the time of the incident.CCTV footage related to the case has also emerged, with the family claiming that the entire sequence of events was captured by more than 12 surveillance cameras installed in the area.The family has alleged that despite the availability of potential evidence, the police initially registered the case as a death caused by an "unknown vehicle", treating it as a hit-and-run incident.They have expressed dissatisfaction with the initial handling of the matter and are demanding that the case be investigated from the perspective of murder, with strict legal action taken against all those found responsible.Following the incident, Biru was taken to a hospital, where doctors declared him dead at around 3 p.m. on Wednesday. His death subsequently led to demands from the family for a thorough investigation and action against the people they accuse of being involved.The family alleged that the police were not taking effective action, prompting them to block the highway with Biru's body in protest. During the demonstration, they remained firm on their demand for                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          " ∏"                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ëÇ!5k'-ÅG ûg95146726012026-10-22T08:48:13ZUpcoming Kawasaki KLE650 teased ahead of revealAutocar Indiaautocarindia.comhttps://www.autocarindia.com/bike-news/upcoming-kawasaki-kle650-teased-ahead-of-reveal-441107engIndiaø¢The bigger sibling for the KLE500 is expected to be launched next yearKawasaki has already revived the KLE name in the global markets with its new KLE500 in 2026, but a few days ago Australian type-approval listings were spotted suggesting a larger motorcycle. Now a new teaser video from Kawasaki UK seems to show a new upcoming adventure bike and we believe this is the new KLE650.* Gets green tubular trellis frame like the KLE500* Features dual front discs, different engine casing to KLE 500* Crash bars and auxiliary light matching the KLE silhouetteTwin front disc brakes hint at a bigger engineAs the teaser offered only glimpses, here is what we could make out from it. Firstly, let's start with the chassis, the bike shown in the video uses a tubular trellis frame finished in Kawasaki's signature metallic green colour, like on the KLE500. Another thing we can see, is likely a new engine, the right-side clutch cover is distinctly different from the KLE500's and the gap between the frame and the engine is far less on the bike in the video.The next hint that is clearly visible is the crash bars, indicators, and auxiliary lights. In which the crash bar seemingly is identical to the ones found on the KLE500. Lastly, we can see a dual-disc brake setup at the front, unlike the single disc offered on the KLE500. All of which suggests the upcoming bike that will likely have more performance and equipment than the existing KLE500.Kawasaki's venerable 649cc, twin-cylinder engine powers just about every form factor of motorcycle from a low-slung cruiser to a tall road-biased tourer and even a neo-retro machine. What has been lacking all these years is a properly off-road capable machine and given Kawasaki's renewed focus on that genre with the recently updated KLX300 range and KLE500 SmartRide SE, it stands to reason that now Kawasaki is shifting its attention to a larger segment. Stay tuned for more developments on this story.ÜDÇ!5Å)-Åy ào95146729662026-10-22T08:48:40ZAP Home Minister Anita Helps injured students in accident in VizagThe Hans Indiathehansindia.comhttps://www.thehansindia.com/andhra-pradesh/ap-home-minister-anita-helps-injured-students-in-accident-in-vizag-1134575engIndiaøÆ Home Minister Vangalapudi Anita stopped to help two students seriously injured in a road accident on BRTS Road in Health City, Arilova, Visakhapatnam.The students were travelling by scooter from Visakhapatnam towards Payakaraopeta when a Bolero collided with them. Anita, who was travelling along the same route, noticed the crash and went to their aid.She arranged for the students to be taken to hospital and instructed medical staff to provide them with the best possible care. She also directed the police to take legal action against the Bolero driver.   Û Û                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         î	Ç!5Å;%Ç £A95146707462026-10-22T08:46:37ZKakinada Accident: 4 Bhavani Devotees Killed by Speeding SUV While Walking to Tea StallLatestLYlatestly.comhttps://www.latestly.com/india/news/kakinada-accident-4-bhavani-devotees-killed-by-speeding-suv-while-walking-to-tea-stall-7653118.htmlengIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿAmaravati, October 22: At least four Bhavani devotees were killed when a speeding SUV rammed into them in Andhra Pradesh's Kakinada district on Thursday, police said. Another devotee was also injured in the accident that occurred near Kathipudi in Prathipadu constituency. According to police, the accident occurred when the devotees were crossing the road to have tea after the bus in which they were travelling broke down.The bus, carrying devotees from Vizianagaram district, was on its way to Vijayawada. They were heading to Vijayawada for 'darshan' at Sri Kanaka Durga Temple. As the vehicle had stopped due to some technical problem, a few devotees got down and headed to a nearby tea stall. In the meantime, a speeding vehicle coming from Etcherla in Srikakulam district rammed into the devotees. Gujarat Accident: 3 Killed, 1 Injured as Motorcycle Plunges 50 Feet From Bridge in Surat.Three of them died on the spot, while another devotee was injured. The deceased were identified as C. Yerraiah (38), L. Sitaram (45), T. Shivaprasad (40) and B.R. Sattibabu (40). Police rushed to the spot and shifted the injured to a local hospital. The bodies of the deceased were taken to a government hospital for post-mortem examination. Deputy Chief Minister Pawan Kalyan has expressed grief over the accident in which four Bhavani devotees lost their lives.He stated that it is heartbreaking that devotees who had completed their vow and were on their way to have darshan of Kanaka Durga lost their lives midway. He conveyed deep condolences to the families of the deceased. The Deputy Chief Minister spoke with the Kakinada District Collector over the phone and gathered details about the incident. 2 Dead, 10 Injured in Udhampur Road Accident: Union Minister Jitendra Singh.The District Collector explained that the accident occurred when a vehicle came speeding from behind, hitting the devotees after they all got down from the bus that had stopped near Ravikampadu Junction and were heading to a nearby hotel. Pawan Kalyan directed that a full-scale investigation be conducted into the incident and that the injured be provided the best medical treatment. He assured that the coalition government will extend all support to the families of the deceased.           ¢Ç!5Åu!)ÇC æM95146588662026-10-22T08:37:25ZKochi Mini Cooper crash: Court rejects Borstal School's plea to move Suhail to Viyyur jail over threat to his safetyOnManoramaonmanorama.comhttps://www.onmanorama.com/news/kerala/2026/10/22/kochi-mini-cooper-crash-court-rejects-borstal-school-plea-move-suhail-viyyur-jail-over-threat-safety.htmlengIndiaøÂuuuuuvKochi: The Judicial First Class Magistrate Court in Angamaly has rejected a plea by the superintendent of Kakkanad Borstal School to    ˘õzÇ!5ÅÇ ≥Y95146677312026-10-22T08:44:15Z"CEO Chief Ministers": Nikhil Kamath On What India Can Learn From ChinaNDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/world-news/ndtv-world-summit-ceo-chief-ministers-nikhil-kamath-on-one-thing-india-can-learn-from-china-12219351engIndia?∑NDTV World Summit: Nikhil Kamath said that India has the opportunity to build a great tech company, but what it lacks is the "risk capital" similar to the US and China.Nikhil Kamath at NDTV World SummitNDTV PhotoNew Delhi:"Why can't chief ministers of Indian states be like CEOs of corporations and compete with each other?" That's what investor and entrepreneur Nikhil Kamath believes India needs to learn from China to make big things happen.Speaking to NDTV CEO and Editor-in-Chief Rahul Kanwal at the NDTV World Summit, Kamath said that India has the opportunity to build a great tech company, but what it lacks is the "risk capital" similar to the US and China."I've been spending a fair amount of time around the frontier model guys. They have a lot more capital, risk capital at hand, to experiment and try different things. I don't see how an Indian company, or for that matter any company outside of those two or three countries where there is that much risk capital, can have a fair shot at competing in that layer. It would be really hard. I think the odds are low."He, however, pointed out that the cost of setting up a company is much cheaper in India than in many places."The one thing people don't take cognizance of when it comes to India is that the cost of putting on a megawatt is probably 30-40% cheaper than it is in the West. Somebody who's doing the plumbing and the piping around a data center in America gets paid $300,000. The same person here makes a lot less money. We also don't take cognizance of the fact that power in India is actually significantly cheaper than in many geographies in the world," he said.Nikhil Kamath with Rahul Kanwal At NDTV World SummitPhoto Credit: NDTV PhotoTo the question of what China has figured out about building an AI ecosystem that India hasn't been able to, Kamath pointed out that India can learn from competition between Chinese provinces which is almost like corporate rivalry."China claims not to be capitalist but when I'm in China it almost feels like the state is capitalist in itself. Every municipality or the mayor of each province competes with another province like he were a capitalistic organization," the Zerodha founder noted.He continued: "The one thing that maybe we can change and learn from China is to allow for different provinces or states to compete with one another like they were a capitalistic organization itself? Maybe the chief minister of a state could operate like the CEO of the state."Kamath, a school dropout, is best known as the co-founder of Zerodha, one of India's largest stockbroking firms. He has also invested in several businesses, including Licious, Nourish You, Pee Safe, Subko, and Ather, an electric scooter maker. In 2025, he bought a 5 per cent stake in D'yavol Spirits, a company founded by actor Shah Rukh Khan and his son Aryan Khan.Kamath is also involved in philanthropy and environmental work. He has signed the Giving Pledge, an initiative started by Bill Gates and Warren Buffett, and has promised to donate at least 50 per cent of his wealth to charitable causes.Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the world    transfer 19-year-old Suhail Sajeev, the prime accused in the Nedumbassery fatal Mini Cooper crash, to Viyyur Central Prison, citing concerns over his safety amid fears of a possible attack by fellow inmates.The application sought Suhail's transfer to the Central Prison in Viyyur on the grounds that the intense public attention surrounding the case and its sensational nature could put his life at risk at the Borstal School.However, Judicial First Class Magistrate Samyuktha M K held that an adolescent accused with no prior criminal antecedents could not be shifted to a conventional prison for adult offenders based solely on unsubstantiated apprehensions about his safety.The court referred to Section 39(4) of the Kerala Prisons and Correctional Services (Management) Act, 2010, and the Borstal Schools Act, 1961, observing that the statutory framework envisages the detention of adolescent offenders in Borstal Schools even after conviction.Underlining the impropriety of transferring an accused whose trial is pending to a prison housing adult offenders, the court observed "... when the law contemplates the detention of even an adolescent offender found guilty of an offence in a Borstal School, it would be inappropriate to direct the detention of an adolescent accused, whose trial is pending, in a sub-jail where adult and hardened offenders are detained."The court also scrutinised the facilities available at Viyyur Central Prison. Although the prison authorities had indicated that arrangements could be made to accommodate Suhail, their report did not establish that separate lodging facilities for adolescent offenders were currently operational.The court further noted the severe overcrowding at the prison. According to official figures placed before it, Viyyur Central Prison has a sanctioned capacity of 553 inmates but was accommodating 1,227 at the time of the report, more than twice its designated capacity.The magistrate also found no factual basis to conclude that Suhail faced an immediate threat from other inmates. No report of an actual threat, unrest or physical attempt against him by fellow inmates had been recorded. The court noted that Suhail had not raised any complaint about his safety when he was produced before it on a production warrant.The court said ensuring the safety and security of inmates fell within the administrative responsibility of prison authorities. It noted that the authorities were empowered under the applicable prison rules to implement necessary protective measures without seeking a specific judicial direction.While rejecting the transfer application, the court clarified that the prison authorities could seek administrative approval from the Director General of Prisons and Correctional Services if necessary. They could also approach the court again if a specific and tangible security threat emerged and suitable segregation facilities were available at another institution.Borstal remand, haircut controversyThe order comes amid continued public scrutiny of the high-profile Nedumbassery crash, in which a speeding Mini Cooper driven by Suhail collided with a two-wheeler, killing three young students.Following Suhail's arrest, the magistrate's initial decision to remand him to Kakkanad Borstal School drew widespread criticism on social media and other public platforms. Several people alleged that the wealthy youngster was receiving preferential treatment because of his background.Legal officials subsequently clarified that the law categorises persons aged 18 to 21 as adolescent offenders for the purposes of the applicable detention framework, requiring their segregation from adult convicts and under-trial prisoners. Kakkanad Borstal School was identified as the only designated facility for such detainees in the district.The case subsequently triggered                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     m m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ïÇ!5Å[Ç' •-95146577212026-10-22T08:36:40ZCaught On CCTV: Pump Operator Attacked With Iron Rods At Petrol Pump In Maharashtra, Three Accused FleeNewsXnewsx.comhttps://www.newsx.com/regionals/caught-on-cctv-pump-operator-attacked-with-iron-rods-at-petrol-pump-in-maharashtra-three-accused-flee-286027/engIndiaø‡000000CCTV footage shows three men allegedly attacking a 35-year-old pump operator at a petrol pump near Umarga in Maharashtra's Dharashiv district. The victim was seriously injured, and police are examining the footage to identify the accused.A CCTV recording taken from a petrol pump in the Dharashiv district of Maharashtra reveals an attack on a petrol pump attendant by three unknown men. This event is said to have occurred on Wednesday, October 21 near Umarga, which is on the Solapur-Hyderabad National Highway.In the video, the incident is seen happening at the petrol pump where the attendant was attacked. The man got badly injured due to the attack, while the attackers reportedly ran away from the place.What Does The CCTV Footage Show?The video evidence shows the alleged assault carried out at the petrol pump. According to the report, three men were seen to come on a motorcycle and assault the attendant. It is alleged that they used iron rods in carrying out the assault before their escape.What happened before the attack is not yet known. The identities of the accused and the motive for the attack are still unknown. The video will enable the police to look into the movements of the men. But the motive for the attack is not yet known.Who Is The Injured Pump Operator?The victim has been identified in a report by regional outlet Pudhari as Wasim Abdul Rahim Attar, 35. He was reportedly taken to Umarga Sub-District Hospital following the attack and later shifted to a private hospital for further treatment.Further details about his condition have not been independently confirmed by NewsX.Police Examine Footage To Identify AccusedIt was reported that the police have already inspected the crime scene and are analyzing the CCTV footage as part of the investigation process. The footage will help understand the order of the events and gather information regarding the suspects.It is reported that the suspects were wearing face masks while committing the crime and that the motorbike they were using did not have a number plate. This may make it difficult to identify the suspects, but the police can analyze the footage and gather any other evidence. The names of the three men, their locations, and their motives are still unknown. The case has shed light on the importance of CCTV footage in recording crimes and helping in investigations.    v  v                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ëÇ!5É%1CÑ5 ô95146578692026-10-22T08:36:37ZBhopal newspaper hawker arranging papers on his scooter at 5am suffers severe leg injury after speeding SUV rams parked sedan, pushing it into his scooter; CCTV captures driver and woman passenger fleeingThe Times of Indiatimesofindia.indiatimes.comhttps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/bhopal/bhopal-newspaper-hawker-arranging-papers-on-his-scooter-at-5am-suffers-severe-leg-injury-after-speeding-suv-rams-parked-sedan-pushing-it-into-his-scooter-cctv-captures-driver-and-woman-passenger-fleeing/articleshow/135112132.cmsengIndiaø‡∞∞∞∞∞∞BHOPAL: A 36-year-old newspaper hawker suffered a severe injury in his left leg after a speeding SUV rammed into a parked sedan, pushing it into his scooter while he was arranging newspapers in DK-2 Danish Kunj under Kolar police station limits around 5am on Thursday. The collision also damaged another scooter parked alongside his vehicle.The incident was captured on CCTV footage from a shop opposite the accident spot. The footage reportedly shows the SUV driver and a woman passenger getting out of the vehicle and leaving the scene after the crash.According to the complaint, the driver abandoned the black SUV and fled. The injured hawker also alleged that the driver was under the influence of alcohol.The complainant, Rajkumar Malviya, a resident of Baba Nagar in Shahpura, told police that he reaches Danish Kunj around 4.30am daily to collect newspapers of different publications for distribution.Around 5am on Thursday, he was loading newspapers onto his scooter when the SUV approached from the Jain temple side at high speed and allegedly rammed into a parked sedan. The impact pushed the sedan backwards into Malviya's scooter and another two-wheeler parked beside it, damaging both and injuring his left knee badly.Malviya's colleague, Gaman, took him to a private hospital, where he was undergoing treatment when police recorded his statement in the emergency ward around 9am.Kolar police registered a case under the BNS for rash and negligent driving and an act endangering life and public safety. Police are investigating the crash and the allegations against the driver.   √ √                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         í9Ç!5Å51/Åu †/95146553612026-10-22T08:35:07ZBengaluru garment worker murders wife over infidelity suspicion, dumps body in drainThe Indian Expressindianexpress.comhttps://indianexpress.com/article/cities/bangalore/bengaluru-wife-murder-case-mohammed-irfaz-ruksana-drain-10932024/engIndiaø÷VVVVVUThank you for your feedback.Your feedback has been reported succesfully.The Bengaluru police have arrested a 22-year-old man for allegedly murdering his wife, Ruksana, following a domestic dispute and dumping her body in a stormwater drain on October 10.The body was found on October 13, three days after the alleged murder, the police said on Thursday.The accused, Mohammed Irfaz, and Ruksana, 25 -- both natives of Bihar -- had married last year and moved to Bengaluru around six months ago, the police said. The two were working at a garment factory.The couple met and fell in love while working as balloon sellers in Bihar before getting married. Ruksana was previously married and had a child from her first marriage.The police revealed that the couple argued frequently due to domestic disputes, with Irfaz suspecting Ruksana of infidelity because she often spent time talking on the phone.On October 10, during one such dispute, Irfaz allegedly killed Ruksana with a stone and then stuffed a veil into her mouth, the police said.How the crime was covered upAccording to the police, Irfaz allegedly broke the handle lock of a motorcycle belonging to an unidentified person to dispose of the body. He placed Ruksana's body inside a bag, loaded it onto the motorcycle and pushed the vehicle to a stormwater drain, where he dumped the body.Initially, the police were unable to establish the woman's identity or identify the accused."More than 10 teams conducted door-to-door enquiries while gathering information about missing persons," a police officer said. During the investigation, local people told the police that a woman who lived with her husband in Gopalapura had gone missing.When questioned, Irfaz allegedly told the police that Ruksana had returned to Bihar and was not using her mobile phone. Suspicious of his account, the police took him into custody for further questioning.During interrogation, he allegedly confessed to murdering his wife, said the police, adding that they have registered a murder case against Irfaz.   n än                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  äÇ!5Å-%Ç7 èO95146483352026-10-22T08:29:20ZMan dies after Erode Collector's vehicle hits two-wheeler near GobichettipalayamThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/man-dies-after-erode-collectors-vehicle-hits-two-wheeler-near-gobichettipalayam/article71610620.eceengIndiaø–PPPPPPA 52-year-old man died after the two-wheeler he was riding was hit by the official vehicle of Erode Collector S. Kandasamy near Gobichettipalayam here on Thursday (October 22, 2026).The deceased, Shanmugam of Vellankovil, had visited the Regional Transport Office (RTO) in Gobichettipalayam to renew his driving licence. He was returning home after completing the formalities when the accident occurred near Vellalapalayam Pirivu.The Collector's vehicle, which was proceeding towards Erode from Gobichettipalayam, hit Shanmugam's two-wheeler as he attempted to cross the road. He was thrown off the vehicle and sustained severe injuries. The Collector, members of the public, and security personnel present at the spot rushed to his aid and arranged to take him to the Gobichettipalayam Government Hospital. However, doctors declared him dead on arrival.The Gobichettipalayam police are investigating the accident. They are also questioning Vinoth, the driver of the Collector's vehicle.írÇ!5y-Ç °_95146549632026-10-22T08:34:42ZTwo Promising Athletes Killed In Cuttack Road Accidentenglishnews.abplive.comhttps://news.abplive.com/sports/cuttack-road-accident-kills-odisha-athletes-mrutyam-dondapati-malay-barik-killed-cm-post-1872667engIndiaøÿÿÿÿÿÿÿOdisha athletes Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malay Barik died in a road accident on the Cuttack highway. CM Mohan Charan Majhi expressed grief.Two young athletes from Odisha, Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malay Barik, have died in a road accident on the Cuttack highway, cutting short their sporting ambitions. The incident took place late Wednesday night and has prompted an outpouring of grief, including from Odisha Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi, who offered condolences to their families.Dondapati had emerged as one of India's fastest under-23 sprinters in 2025, while Barik competed in the 400-metre race. Their deaths have come as a major loss to Odisha's athletics community, with both athletes pursuing careers in competitive sport.How Did The Cuttack Highway Accident Happen?Preliminary reports indicate that a group of four people, including three athletes and a swimming coach, were travelling on two two-wheelers when the accident occurred.Dondapati and Barik were reportedly on the same motorcycle. Athlete Astik Pradhan was travelling on a scooter with the other members of the group, approximately 50 metres behind them. The available information does not establish further details about how the collision occurred.Who Is Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati?Dondapati was gaining recognition in India's under-23 sprinting circuit. His performances in 2025 placed him among the country's fastest sprinters in that age category, highlighting his potential to progress further in athletics.His rise had made him a promising name in Odisha's sporting circles. His death has brought an abrupt end to a career that was still developing.Who is Malay Barik?Barik pursued the 400-metre event, a discipline that tests both sprinting speed and the ability to sustain pace over one lap of the track. He was working to establish himself in competitive athletics.The loss of Barik and Dondapati has left the state's sporting community grieving two young athletes whose careers were still taking shape.Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi expressed his grief following their deaths and conveyed his condolences to the bereaved families.   Ó &Ó                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  å4Ç!!5Å995Ç5 ìS95146373672026-10-22T08:19:51ZWest Bengal police seize explosives, banned chemicals; two-wheeler showroom owner heldThe New Indian Expressnewindianexpress.comhttps://www.newindianexpress.com/states/west-bengal/2026/Oct/22/west-bengal-police-seize-explosives-banned-chemicals-two-wheeler-showroom-owner-heldengIndiaø√ìììììíAccording to preliminary findings cited by sources, the explosives and banned chemicals may have been intended for transport to a location in Kolkata to carry out subversive activities.KOLKATA: West Bengal Police seized large quantities of explosives and banned chemicals from a car in Duttapukur, North 24 Parganas district, on Wednesday night, triggering tension in the area.Three teams from the National Security Guard (NSG), National Investigation Agency (NIA) and the state police's Special Task Force (STF) have launched a joint operation. Rakibul Islam, owner of a two-wheeler showroom in the area, has been arrested by the investigating agencies.M Marsy, superintendent of police of Barasat police district, told reporters on Thursday that a thorough investigation was underway to determine the nature and potency of the explosives."Using scientific procedures, we are identifying the nature of the explosives and how powerful they are. One person has already been arrested, and we are questioning him to gather more details about the case," Marsy said.Acting on a tip-off, the STF searched the car at Tentultala in Duttapukur on Wednesday night and seized it. The STF and district police had been monitoring the vehicle's movements.ãVÇ %5Å9/Åo í}b-95146400582026-10-22T08:22:02ZSilchar: 60-Year-Old Pedestrian Killed by Speeding Motorcycle on NH-306The Sentinel Newspapersentinelassam.comhttps://www.sentinelassam.com/breakingnews/silchar-60-year-old-pedestrian-killed-by-speeding-motorcycle-on-nh-306engIndiaø€€€€€€€Guwahati: A 60-year-old pedestrian was killed after being hit by a speeding motorcycle on National Highway 306 near Aulia Bazar in Uttar Krishnapur, Silchar on Bijoy Dashami's evening. The motorcycle rider allegedly fled the scene leaving the vehicle.The deceased has been identified as Zakir Hussain Mazumdar, a resident of Barhali in Sonai. As per people nearby, the accident occurred at around 7 pm when Mazumdar was attempting to cross the road. The impact of the collision was reportedly fatal, and he died on the spot.After the accident, the motorcycle rider allegedly abandoned the vehicle and fled, leaving the victim at the scene. Police from Rangirkhari reached the spot around an hour after the incident, recovered the body and sent it to the mortuary of Silchar Medical College and Hospital for a post-mortem examination.As per people's statement, Sonai Police arrived around two hours after the accident. Residents gathered at the scene criticised the police over the alleged delay in reaching the spot.The exact age and whereabouts of Zakir Mazumdar's family is not yet confirmed, Mazumdar worked as a night watchman at a local workshop situated in front of which the accident occurred.   E E                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           è7Ç"!5ÅG#Ç ö#95146340342026-10-22T08:16:52ZBihar man arrested for abducting toddler for alleged human sacrifice in Rajasthan; child safeThePrinttheprint.inhttps://theprint.in/india/bihar-man-arrested-for-abducting-toddler-for-alleged-human-sacrifice-in-rajasthan-child-safe/3078245/engIndiaø≈ïïïïïîThe accused, identified as Vivek Kumar Kushwaha, a resident of Sasaram in Bihar's Rohtas district, was arrested after the child was rescued from a Kali temple in Kavar village near Mathura's Kosi Kalan.According to preliminary investigations, Kushwaha had turned to superstition following personal setbacks, including separation from his wife and unsuccessful relationships, and allegedly believed that sacrificing a child would help him attain supernatural powers.Jaipur Range Inspector General of Police Rahul Prakash said Kushwaha allegedly kidnapped Krishna while he was playing outside his house on October 18.The accused travelled through several locations for nearly 50 hours, searching for a secluded temple where he could allegedly sacrifice the child, police said.The child was rescued after a local sadhu heard him crying inside the temple and alerted police. When questioned, Kushwaha initially claimed to be the child's father, they said.However, verification of his motorcycle revealed that it had been stolen from Shahpura, raising suspicion.Neemrana SHO Surendra Yadav said eight police teams were formed following the kidnapping, and footage from around 300 to 350 CCTV cameras was examined to trace the accused.Police said the accused had travelled through Shahjahanpur, Bawal, Rewari and Faridabad before reaching Mathura.A brass trident, a packet of wheat, bangles and two metal rings were recovered from his possession. The child was allegedly found seated on a ritual platform inside the temple.The IG said Uttar Pradesh police personnel involved in the rescue would be awarded commendation certificates for their alertness. PTI AG SHS    •  •                                                                                                                                                           ûWÇ#!5Å%Ås π+95146299662026-10-22T08:13:40ZDrugs Worth Rs 60 Crore Seized, 7 Arrested: Interstate Heroin Network BustedNDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/india-news/drugs-worth-rs-60-crore-seized-7-arrested-interstate-heroin-network-busted-12218890engIndiaøﬁ^^^^^^Delhi Police busts heroin supply network arresting seven and recovering 8.128 kg heroin.NDTVNew Delhi:An interstate heroin supply and manufacturing network spanning Delhi, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Jharkhand has been busted, with seven accused arrested and 8.128 kg of heroin worth approximately Rs 60 crore in the international market recovered, according to the Delhi Police.According to the police, the operation also led to the recovery of Rs 12,81,700 in cash, 3.291 kg of chemicals and other materials allegedly used to manufacture heroin, three SUVs and a Royal Enfield motorcycle.The investigation took off on September 16, when a Special Staff team intercepted a Maruti Suzuki Grand Vitara in Sector 32, Begumpur, and arrested Laxman Hooda, 58, a resident of Rohtak, Haryana. Police recovered 300 grams of heroin and Rs 3 lakh in cash from the vehicle. Hooda had previously been involved in a murder case, according to the Delhi police.On September 17, investigators arrested Anil alias Bhola, 51, a resident of Raghubir Nagar, Delhi, from Sonipat, Haryana. They recovered 501 grams of heroin from his Mahindra XUV700. Police identified him as a source supplier and said he had been involved in 12 cases. Anil had also been declared a proclaimed offender in an NDPS case registered at Bhalswa Dairy police station after allegedly failing to surrender following interim bail.On October 4, the investigating team raided an alleged heroin manufacturing facility in Sita Colony, Jankipuram, Lucknow, and arrested Bablu, 35, a resident of Bareilly, Uttar Pradesh. Police recovered 6.275 kg of freshly manufactured heroin, 2.504 kg of sodium, 787 grams of acetic anhydride and equipment allegedly used in the manufacturing process, including a gas cylinder, mixer-grinder, utensils, an electronic weighing machine and other materials. Police said Bablu had previously been involved in an NDPS case.Acting on information provided by Bablu during interrogation, the investigating team traced and arrested Ruksar Ali alias Raju in Bareilly. He was identified as the alleged main source supplier and owner of the manufacturing facility. Police said he had previously been involved in three NDPS cases.On October 6, police arrested Ajaj Ahmed, 38, a resident of Mujhiyana village in Badaun, Uttar Pradesh. He allegedly supplied crude opium to Ruksar Ali. Police recovered 501 grams of heroin and a Royal Enfield motorcycle from him. He had previously been involved in an NDPS case, according to police.Mohammad Azhar, 20, a resident of Badaun, was arrested on October 16. Police alleged that he supplied heroin and crude opium to Ajaj Ahmed. They recovered 551 grams of heroin, Rs 9,81,700 in cash and a Hyundai Creta from him. The police document lists no previous criminal involvement for Azhar.The investigation led police to Chatra district in Jharkhand on October 18, where Prakash Kumar was arrested. Police alleged that he supplied raw opium to the other accused and was involved in the illegal cultivation of opium poppy on his agricultural land, establishing another link in the interstate supply chain.Police said the arrests had helped expose the alleged network's supply chain, from opium cultivation and raw material supply to heroin manufacturing and distribution across states.The operation was conducted by a Special Staff team led by Inspector Sandeep Godara under the supervision of ACP Ajmer Singh.Further investigation is underway.Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the world   S S                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ì)Ç$!5Å%Åi ¢Y95146299642026-10-22T08:13:40ZTiger Shroff Firing Case Accused To Be Tried Under Organised Crime Act MCOCANDTVndtv.comhttps://www.ndtv.com/india-news/accused-in-tiger-shroff-firing-case-to-be-tried-under-stringent-mcoca-12218955engIndiaø‹\\\\\]At least two men fired gunshots at Tiger Shroff's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on SundayMumbai:All those arrested, 10 so far, in connection with the Tiger Shroff firing case will be charged under the stringent Maharashtra Control of Organised Crime Act, or MCOCA, the police said.According to sources, the police have begun gathering evidence and completing the necessary documentation to invoke MCOCA.At least two men fired gunshots at the 36-year-old actor's car in Mumbai's Juhu area on Sunday evening before speeding away on a motorcycle. The actor escaped relatively unhurt, while his driver and a bystander were injured.According to the Mumbai Police, five to six rounds were fired at the car. A motorcycle, allegedly used by the shooters, was found abandoned in Andheri. Anil Pandit, a member of the Lawrence Bishnoi gang, claimed responsibility for the murder attempt.The three shooters had been arrested in Rajasthan's Kota. They were attempting to escape to Nepal via Delhi.The Anti-Extortion Cell (AEC) of the Mumbai Crime Branch is investigating the case.Police sources have told NDTV that the gang wanted to target another high-profile personality. As they couldn't do so because of heavy security, they improvised."After checking out areas frequented by this individual, the shooters realised that they would not be able to get to the person. This was when they shifted their target to Tiger Shroff after learning - through reels posted by his fans - that the actor did not have police protection," the source said.Among the 10 arrested, there are also two women who allegedly supplied weapons to the accused who fired shots at the actor's car.On Tuesday, Tiger Shroff's team issued a stern warning against the circulation of fabricated stories, unauthorised statements and AI-generated videos falsely attributed to the actor, urging media organisations and social media platforms to verify information before publishing it.(With inputs from Ruttik Ganakwar)Got a follow‚Äëup question on this article? Go onHow may i help you todayShow full articleTrack Latest News Live on NDTV.com and get news updates from India and around the worldMCOCA, Tiger Shroff, Mumbai Police    ó  ó                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             êeÇ%!5Å-=Åu ù95146295882026-10-22T08:13:12ZCourt rejects plea to shift Mini Cooper crash accused to central prisonmetrovaartha.comenglish.metrovaartha.comhttps://english.metrovaartha.com/news/kerala/court-rejects-plea-to-shift-mini-cooper-crash-accused-to-central-prisonengIndiaøÀõõõõõõA court here dismissed a petition by superintendent of the Borstal School seeking to shift the prime accused in the Mini Cooper crash that killed three youngsters in Nedumbassery here, to a central prisonKochi | A court here on Thursday dismissed a petition by the superintendent of the Borstal School seeking to shift the prime accused in the Mini Cooper crash that killed three youngsters in Nedumbassery here, to a central prison.Angamaly Judicial First Class Magistrate Samyuktha M K dismissed the petition filed by the superintendent of the Borstal School in Kakkanad, which houses prisoners aged between 18 and 21, seeking Suhail's transfer to a central prison on security grounds.The petition cited security concerns over his continued stay at the facility.However, the magistrate dismissed it after examining the plea.Suhail's admission to the Borstal School had earlier drawn criticism.Suhail, 19, was allegedly driving the car when it rammed into a scooter carrying three youngsters on the airport road at Nedumbassery in the early hours of October 11.Three others who were travelling in the car were also arrested after police found that the occupants were heavily drunk and the vehicle was allegedly travelling at over 100 kmph.Meanwhile, a five-member investigation team visited the house of Devika, a native of Kalpetta in Wayanad and one of the three victims, on Thursday morning.The team recorded statements and interacted with her family for over an hour, officials said.After the accident, the family members told reporters that they are hopeful that justice would be delivered and that investigators have collected all crucial evidence in the case.Recently, the magistrate court had dismissed the bail petitions of the accused persons.They have filed fresh petitions at the Ernakulam District Principal Sessions Court.    ¸                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               °jÇ'!5Å775Ç+ æM95146283002026-10-22T08:12:18ZNavratri auto retail hits 11.23 lk units: Tata Motors, Maruti gear up for Diwali rushThe Financial Expressfinancialexpress.comhttps://www.financialexpress.com/business/industry-navratri-auto-retail-hits-11-23-lk-units-tata-motors-maruti-gear-up-for-diwali-rush-4366871/engIndia?›]]]]][With more festive days including Dhanteras and Diwali around the corner, dealerships are gearing up for another wave of purchases."As we enter the Dhanteras-  î Ç&!5Åq13Ç= ¢595146288802026-10-22T08:12:50ZWho Were Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati And Malay Barik? Two Promising Odisha Sprinters Killed In Cuttack Road AccidentFree Press Journalfreepressjournal.inhttps://www.freepressjournal.in/sports/who-were-mrutyam-jayaram-dondapati-and-malay-barik-two-promising-odisha-sprinters-killed-in-cuttack-road-accidentengIndiaøÃúúúúúùDondapati was among India's fastest under-23 sprinters in 2025, while Barik competed in the 400-metre event. Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi expressed grief over their deaths and offered condolences to their bereaved families.Two promising Odisha athletes, Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati and Malay Barik, were killed in a road accident on the Cuttack highway late Wednesday night. Their deaths have left the state's sporting community in mourning. While Dondapati was one of India's fastest under-23 sprinters in 2025, Barik competed in the 400-metre event.Who Was Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati?Mrutyam Jayaram Dondapati was an emerging sprinter from Odisha who gained recognition in the under-23 category. In 2025, he was counted among India's fastest sprinters in his age group. His performances highlighted his potential in Indian athletics.Who Was Malay Barik?Malay Barik was a 400-metre runner from Odisha who was working to establish himself in athletics. The event requires a combination of speed, stamina and endurance. He was among the young athletes pursuing their ambitions in competitive sport.What Happened In The Road Accident?According to preliminary reports, four people, including three athletes and a swimming coach, were travelling on two two-wheelers when the accident occurred. Dondapati and Barik were reportedly riding a motorcycle, while athlete Astik Pradhan was travelling on a scooter with the other members of the group around 50 metres behind them.The group was reportedly heading to Cuttack to attend a Sambalpuri Melody orchestra when the tragedy occurred. They were taken to SCB Medical College and Hospital in Cuttack, where doctors declared them dead on arrival. Further details about the circumstances of the accident have not been independently confirmed.Odisha Chief Minister Expresses GriefOdisha Chief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi expressed grief over the deaths in a social media post. He described their untimely passing as a profound loss to Odisha's sporting community and offered condolences to their families. He also prayed to Mahaprabhu Shri Jagannath to give the bereaved families strength and grant eternal peace to the departed souls.    to-Diwali wave, we remain cautiously optimistic: affordability is strong, aspiration is rising, and auto retail continues to mirror the enduring momentum of the India Growth Story," FADA President Sai Giridhar said.Navratri 2026 Auto Sales Fall 6.52% from 2025Vehicle retail sales rose nearly 27% compared with Navratri 2024, when Indian customers brought 8.86 lakh vehicles. However, vehicle retail sales declined 6.52% year-on-year compared to the 12.01 lakh units sold during Navratri 2025.However, FADA says, the comparison is not like-for-like as Navratri lasted 11 days last year, compared with 10 days this year. The festive period in 2025 also coincided with the rollout of GST 2.0, which brought forward pent-up demand.Tata Motors delivers over 50,000 vehicles during NavratriTata Motors Passenger Vehicles said the company is seeing strong festive cheer resulting in robust demand across our multi-powertrain portfolio of cars & SUVs, with improved customer sentiment driving higher showroom walk-ins, enquiries, bookings and deliveries."The response during Navratri has been particularly encouraging, with over 50,000 vehicles delivered during this festive period, including more than 10,000 on Dussehra alone," Amit Kamat, Chief Commercial Officer of Tata Motors Passenger Vehicles said."As families across the country celebrate and welcome new beginnings, we are working hard to ensure that more customers can bring home the Tata car of their choice. We have stepped up production and sharpened logistics to improve availability of high-demand models and variants. With a healthy booking pipeline and the celebrations building towards Diwali, we look forward to carrying this strong momentum through the festive season," Kamat added.Maruti Suzuki expects double-digit festive growth till DiwaliMaruti Suzuki India also had an encouraging festive season with strong customer demand through Navratri."Between Ganesh Chaturthi and Dussehra, our retail sales grew by 35%, with small-car retail increasing by around 16% and SUV retail doubling. Our retail sales during the Navratri period is almost the same as last year," said Partho Banerjee, Senior Executive Officer, Marketing and Sales, Maruti Suzuki."We began October with pending bookings of around 2 lakh units, which have increased to 2.7 lakh units after Dussehra. We are making every effort to maximise deliveries and serve our customers. With this strong demand momentum, we expect the positive trend to continue and anticipate double-digit growth for the whole festive period till Diwali," Banerjee added.Two-wheeler sales rise 32%, passenger vehicles grow 10%Two-wheeler retail sales stood at 8.34 lakh units during Navratri 2026, registering a 32.41% increase from 6.29 lakh units in Navratri 2024. However, sales declined 2.79% from 8.58 lakh units in the corresponding period last year.Overall passenger vehicle (PV) retail sales increased 10.39% to 1.82 lakh units from 1.65 lakh units in Navratri 2024. On a year-on-year basis, however, sales fell 21.91% from 2.34 lakh units in Navratri 2025.Commercial vehicle (CV) retail sales rose 16.47% to 35,618 units from 30,580 units in Navratri 2024. Compared with last year, sales increased 1.12%.Three-wheeler retail sales grew 19.04% year-on-year over Navratri 2024 to 45,735 units. However, sales declined 7.51% compared with 49,450 units in Navratri 2025.Retail sales of tractors increased 20.21% to 22,690 units from 18,875 units in Navratri 2024. Sales were marginally higher than the 22,489 units recorded in Navratri 2025.EV retail sales jump 83% over Navratri 2024Electric vehicle (EV) retail sales continued to grow across categories during Navratri 2026. Total EV sales increased 26.78% year-on-year to 1.17 lakh units from 92,628 units in Navratri 2025. Compared with Na                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Q Q                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       ó+Ç(!5Å9+1Ç3 ©U95146190002026-10-22T08:04:54ZLuLu leases hypermarket space at Greater Noida Mall for 15 years at nearly ‚Çπ51 croreHindustan Timeshindustantimes.comhttps://www.hindustantimes.com/real-estate/lulu-leases-hypermarket-space-at-greater-noida-mall-for-15-years-at-nearly-51-crore-101792647397267.htmlengIndia?¡ëëëëëëLuLu International Shopping Malls Private Limited has leased approximately 62,035 sq ft of carpet area on the lower-ground floor of I-Thums Galleria in Greater Noida for 15 years, at a total rent of nearly ‚Çπ51 crore, according to documents accessed by Propstack.The documents show that the lease provides for a monthly rent of ‚Çπ45 per sq ft for the retail area and ‚Çπ20 per sq ft for the back-of-house area, taking the initial monthly rent to approximately ‚Çπ26.41 lakh.The leased premises comprise 56,035 sq ft of retail carpet area and 6,000 sq ft of back-of-house area. The premises were scheduled to be handed over by March 31, 2026, with rent commencing after a 240-day fit-out period or on the store's opening date, whichever is earlier.The documents showed the company has deposited ‚Çπ1.585 crore as a security deposit, equivalent to six months of the initial lease rent.The lease provides for a 9% rent escalation every three years. It also includes 10 car parking spaces and 100 two-wheeler parking spaces at no additional cost.The agreement specifies a three-year lock-in period for the lessee and a 15-year lock-in period for the lessor. In addition to rent, the company will pay monthly common area maintenance (CAM) charges of approximately ‚Çπ12.11 lakh to the maintenance company, the documents showed.Earlier this week, LuLu Group announced the opening of a new 1-lakh-sq-ft hypermarket in Greater Noida, strengthening its presence in Uttar Pradesh and the Delhi-NCR region. Company sources told Hindustan Times that the 1-lakh-sq-ft figure refers to the hypermarket's larger, super built-up area, which includes common areas, while the registered lease covers 62,035 sq ft of carpet area.The UAE-based retailer is targeting an investment of ‚Çπ2,500 crore to establish 25 outlets across Delhi-NCR by 2030. The expansion will include a mix of hypermarkets and smaller daily-concept stores, depending on the catchment and population of each location, a senior company executive told Hindustan Times.Raja Seetharaman, co-founder of Propstack, said LuLu Group's entry into Greater Noida reflected the growing interest of institutional and large-format retailers in NCR's expanding suburban markets."Anchor commitments of this scale reflect sustained confidence in organised physical retail, especially in high-density residential corridors where consumer spending is maturing rapidly," he said.With operations across more than 35 countries, a network of over 285 retail stores and 24 shopping malls, LuLu continues to expand its presence in India through shopping malls and hypermarkets, the company said in a statement.   #  #                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       °jÇ*!5ÅAc'Ç æM95146115452026-10-22T07:59:44ZTiger Shroff likes Instagram post featuring Heropanti scene two days after firing incidentInternational Business Times, India Editionibtimes.co.inhttps://www.ibtimes.co.in/tiger-shroff-likes-instagram-post-featuring-heropanti-scene-two-days-after-firing-incident-907728engIndiaø«óóóóóòDays after a reported firing incident in Mumbai's Juhu area, Tiger Shroff liked an Instagram video featuring his Heropanti song Raat Bhar. The clip showed him    ëhÇ)!5Å/-Åq ü+95146150562026-10-22T08:02:38ZGMCH records 114 road accident cases during Durga Puja, nine brought deadThe Assam Tribuneassamtribune.comhttps://assamtribune.com/guwahati/gmch-records-114-road-accident-cases-during-durga-puja-nine-brought-dead-1620889engIndiaøŸYYYYY[Guwahati, Oct 22: More than 100 road traffic accident cases were recorded at Gauhati Medical College and Hospital (GMCH) during the Durga Puja festivities, with 114 people brought to its emergency ward between October 16 and October 21.Of them, 82 were admitted for treatment, while nine were brought dead, GMCH Superintendent Dr Devajit Choudhury said.Among the 82 patients admitted, 67 were men and 15 were women. The nine people brought dead included eight men and one woman."From October 16 to October 21, we recorded 114 road traffic accident cases in our emergency ward. Of these, 82 patients were admitted, while nine people were brought dead," Choudhury said.He said the number of road accident cases had declined by 15% compared to the corresponding period last year."Most of the cases are from Guwahati and its adjoining areas. A few patients are referred to us from other places, including Tezpur and Jorhat," he said.According to Choudhury, around 20% of the admitted patients are in critical condition and are being closely monitored."We are examining them every day and conducting repeat CT scans as well. Around 70% of the cases involve motorcycle accidents, while car accidents account for the remaining 30%," he said.The figures come amid broader concerns over road safety in the state. On October 20, Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma expressed concern over the number of road crashes, citing accident-prone stretches, ongoing road renovation work and unsafe driving practices as contributing factors."The accidents are surging and we are concerned about it. In some places the situation has improved but in others, it's a matter of concern, especially in areas where roads are being revamped. There are also red points and we are trying to correct them," Sarma told reporters.He also stressed the need for greater road safety awareness, identifying driving under the influence of alcohol and failure to wear helmets among the factors contributing to accidents    riding a bike with Kriti Sanon.Tiger Shroff narrowly escaped death on Sunday, with many considering it a blessing and divine intervention that he remained unharmed despite the attackers allegedly trying to shoot at him at point-blank range. Their gun jammed, and the crowd started screaming.The viral clip also shows the attackers pulling at the car door where Tiger was seated, but they could not open it. The driver was injured and is now being treated at a hospital.Within minutes, the attackers identified themselves on social media as Anil Pandit and Harman Sandhu. They also issued a warning to Bollywood at large, while specifically targeting people associated with their main target, Salman Khan. They announced that nobody would be spared. The wording was ominous and unambiguous. In the recording, Anil openly threatened Salman Khan and his family with complete annihilation. Not even a kutta ( dog) inside their home would be left alive, the alleged attacker boasted.However, on Monday morning, a headline in a leading publication read, "Tiger Zinda Hai", while reporting on the alleged murderous attack on Bollywood star Tiger Shroff. Not just media outlets, but the internet was also seen mocking and making memes about Tiger Shroff's firing incident. Many made highly insensitive and nasty comments, such as saying that had he been shot, it would have been "Ek Tha Tiger".Some also said that Tiger is harmless and has not been embroiled in controversies. He plays football shirtless, plays cricket in his underwear, and is friendly with kids. Many even lauded his bravery and the way he did not panic, handled the situation and drove his injured driver home.Amid the memes and insensitive comments online, Tiger, who is now doing well, has liked a meme about his own firing incident.Tiger liked an Instagram post shared on October 20, marking his first known social media interaction since the firing incident.The post featured his song "Raat Bhar" from his debut film, Heropanti, playing in the background. The video showed Tiger riding a bike with his co-star Kriti Sanon seated behind him in a scene from the film, accompanied by the text, "Bhai, raat bhar ke liye kya, zindagi bhar ke liye gayab ho jata."The timing of the interaction has drawn attention, given that it came shortly after the firing incident. However, it remains unclear whether Tiger liked the post intentionally or whether the interaction was accidental.While the actor has not issued a statement since the incident, his latest social media activity has caught attention.What the statement saysTiger's team has issued a strong warning against the spread of fake news and AI-generated content falsely linked to the actor. In a statement, the team clarified that Tiger has not made any public comments or released videos about the recent incident and warned that those responsible for spreading misleading content could face legal action.The statement comes amid concerns over social media pages and digital platforms using fabricated material to create confusion and spread unverified claims. Team Tiger has urged people to rely on official sources instead of believing or sharing content without checking its authenticity."We would like to categorically clarify that Tiger Shroff has made no statements, released no videos, and authorised no communication regarding the recent incident or any related developments," the statement read.The statement also raised concerns about the misuse of artificial intelligence and the circulation of misleading stories online. According to the team, several platforms have been sharing "fabricated stories, AI-generated videos and scripted narratives, falsely attributed to Tiger". It described such material as "completely false, unauthorised and intended to mislead the public".Team                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               " "                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        ìZÇ+%5Å=!/ÅQ £b-95146104912026-10-22T07:58:57ZSleeping Pills, Broken Bottle, WhatsApp Updates: Wife's Murder Plot Exposed - NorthlinesNorthlinesthenorthlines.comhttps://thenorthlines.com/sleeping-pills-broken-bottle-whatsapp-updates-wifes-murder-plot-exposed/engIndiaø’UUUUUWBAGHPAT, OCT 22: A woman and her alleged lover have been arrested for conspiring to murder her husband in Uttar Pradesh's Baghpat district, with police investigations reportedly uncovering WhatsApp exchanges detailing plans to drug the victim and avoid CCTV cameras.The accused, identified as Urmila and Sikandar, allegedly plotted to kill Pramod so they could move to Dehradun and start a new life together, police said.Pramod's body was found near a tubewell in his agricultural field on October 18, bearing severe injuries to his face. He had left home saying he was going to watch a Ramlila performance but never returned.During the investigation, police traced the alleged conspiracy to Urmila and Sikandar, a motorcycle mechanic who had rented a shop owned by Pramod. According to investigators, the two had developed a romantic relationship and continued communicating over the phone even after Urmila's son learnt about their affair.Police said Urmila allegedly called Sikandar to her compound on October 18 and handed him two sleeping pills, instructing him to mix them with Pramod's liquor. Sikandar allegedly gave Pramod a quarter bottle of liquor near the village primary school before proceeding towards the tubewell through agricultural fields to avoid CCTV cameras, following Urmila's instructions.When Pramod began becoming intoxicated, Sikandar allegedly attempted to knock him down. After Pramod resisted, Sikandar repeatedly struck him on the head with the liquor bottle and continued attacking him with the broken glass, police said.He allegedly dragged Pramod's unconscious body to a nearby sugarcane field and left after confirming his death. He later went to watch the Ramlila performance.Investigators said Urmila repeatedly sought updates from Sikandar through WhatsApp during the alleged killing. After receiving confirmation, she reportedly told him she would block his number and contact him herself if required.Sikandar had allegedly saved screenshots of some WhatsApp conversations before the messages could be deleted. The exchanges, along with other evidence, helped police reconstruct the alleged conspiracy.Both accused have been arrested, and further legal proceedings are underway. (Agencies)   • •                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           îWÇ,!5Åe%Çg £e95146097262026-10-22T07:58:13ZNedumbassery car crash: Court rejects plea to shift prime accused from Borstal School to Viyyur Central jailThe Hinduthehindu.comhttps://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/nedumbassery-car-crash-court-rejects-plea-to-shift-prime-accused-from-borstal-school-to-viyyur-central-jail/article71610556.eceengIndiaø⁄ZZZZZZMagistrate court points out there is no specific evidence currently to show the accused is facing safety threats at the facilityThe Judicial First Class Magistrate Court-I, Angamaly, on Thursday (October 22, 2026) rejected a request by the authorities of the Borstal School at Kakkanad to shift 19-year-old Suhail Sajeev, the prime accused in the Nedumbassery drunk-driving case that claimed three lives, to the Viyyur Central jail citing security concerns.The court pointed out that there is no specific evidence currently to show that the accused is facing safety threats at the facility. It stated that the accused has also not raised any concern over his safety at the Borstal School.The court had rejected the bail applications of all four accused in the case on Saturday (October 17, 2026). The Nedumbassery police had earlier arrested Suhail, who allegedly drove the luxury car under the influence of alcohol, and three co-passengers, Ninav, 19; Ameer, 20; and Joel, 20.The accident occurred around 1.45 a.m. on October 11, 2026 on the Airport Road near Athani. The three deceased, who had been working part-time at a commercial store, were returning after dinner when the speeding car hit their scooter. The luxury car was allegedly speeding at over 165 km per hour while ramming the two-wheeler from behind.The victims included Gopika, 21, daughter of Pradeep Kumar and Sajitha of Mullankuzhi House, Edakurissi, Mannarkkad, Devika, 21, also known as Kukku, daughter of Santhosh Kumar and Saritha of Madakkimala, Kalpetta; and Iyas, 21, son of Ibrahim and Rukiya from Sullia, Karnataka.The families of the victims had questioned the decision to send Suhail to the Borstal School, a detention facility for offenders aged 18 to 21, instead of a regular prison.The Ernakulam Rural Police had denied allegations of preferential treatment to the accused, while pointing out that the court's order specifically directed that the accused be remanded in the Borstal School.They had cited Section 324 of the Kerala Prison Rules, which stipulates that steps should be taken to transfer prisoners below 21 years of age to Borstal Schools in order to prevent their character from being adversely influenced through association with prisoners belonging to other categories.